('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם עוֹטֵר יִשְׂרָאֵל בְּתִפְאָרָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy our God, King of the Universe, Who crowns Israel with glory.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:22:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','transliteration','bah-rookh ah-tah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo meh-lehkh hah-oh-lahm oh-tehr yees-rah-ehl be-teef-ah-rah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם הַנּוֹתֵן לַיָּעֵף כֹּֽחַ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy our God, King of the Universe, Who gives strength to the weary.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:23:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','transliteration','bah-rookh ah-tah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo meh-lehkh hah-oh-lahm hah-noh-tehn lah-yah-ehf koh-ahkh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם הַמַּעֲבִיר שֵׁנָה מֵעֵינָי וּתְנוּמָה מֵעַפְעַפָּי: וִיהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ שֶׁתַּרְגִּילֵֽנוּ בְּתוֹרָתֶֽךָ וְדַבְּ֒קֵֽנוּ בְּמִצְוֹתֶֽיךָ, וְאַל תְּבִיאֵֽנוּ לֹא לִידֵי חֵטְא וְלֹא לִידֵי עֲבֵרָה וְעָוֹן וְלֹא לִידֵי נִסָּיוֹן וְלֹא לִידֵי בִזָּיוֹן וְאַל יִשְׁלֹט בָּֽנוּ יֵֽצֶר הָרָע וְהַרְחִיקֵֽנוּ מֵאָדָם רָע וּמֵחָבֵר רָע וְדַבְּ֒קֵֽנוּ בְּיֵֽצֶר הַטּוֹב וּבְמַעֲשִׂים טוֹבִים וְכוֹף אֶת יִצְרֵֽנוּ לְהִשְׁתַּעְבֶּד־לָךְ וּתְנֵֽנוּ הַיּוֹם וּבְכָל יוֹם לְחֵן וּלְחֶֽסֶד וּלְרַחֲמִים בְּעֵינֶֽיךָ וּבְעֵינֵי כָל רוֹאֵֽינוּ וְתִגְמְ֒לֵֽנוּ חֲסָדִים טוֹבִים: בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה הַגּוֹמֵל חֲסָדִים טוֹבִים לְעַמּוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy our God, King of the Universe, Who removes sleep from my eyes and slumber from my eyelids. And may it be Your will Adonoy, our God And God of our fathers, to make us study Torah regularly, and hold fast to Your commandments. Do not bring us into the grasp of sin, nor into the grasp of transgression or iniquity. Do not cause us to be tested, or brought to disgrace. Let us not be ruled over by the Evil Inclination. Keep us far from an evil person, and from an evil companion. Make us hold fast to the Good Inclination, and to good deeds, and compel our Evil Inclination to be subservient to You. Grant us this day and every day favor, kindness, and compassion in Your eyes and in the eyes of all who see us, and bestow bountiful kindness upon us, Blessed are You, Adonoy, Who bestows bountiful kindness upon His people Israel.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:24:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','transliteration','bah-rookh ah-tah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo meh-lehkh hah-oh-lahm hah-mah-ah-veer sheh-nah meh-ey-nahy oo-te-noo-mah meh-ahf-ah-pahy: vee-hee rah-tsohn mee-LE-fah-ney-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo veh-loh-hey ah-voh-tey-noo sheh-tahr-gee-leh-noo be-toh-rah-teh-khah ve-dah-BE-keh-noo be-meets-voh-tey-khah, ve-ahl te-vee-eh-noo loh lee-dey kheht ve-loh lee-dey ah-veh-rah ve-ah-vohn ve-loh lee-dey nee-sah-yohn ve-loh lee-dey vee-zah-yohn ve-ahl yeesh-loht bah-noo yeh-tsehr hah-rah ve-hahr-khee-keh-noo meh-ah-dahm rah oo-meh-khah-vehr rah ve-dah-BE-keh-noo be-yeh-tsehr hah-tohv oo-ve-mah-ah-seem toh-veem ve-khohf eht yeets-reh-noo le-heesh-tah-behd lahkh oo-te-neh-noo hah-yohm oo-ve-khohl yohm le-khehn oo-le-kheh-sehd oo-le-rah-khah-meem be-ey-ney-khah oo-ve-ey-ney khohl roh-ey-noo ve-teeg-ME-leh-noo khah-sah-deem toh-veem: bah-rookh ah-tah ah-doh-NAI hah-goh-mehl khah-sah-deem toh-veem le-ah-moh yees-rah-ehl:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:25:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','he','יְהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהַי וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתַי שֶׁתַּצִּילֵֽנִי הַיּוֹם וּבְכָל יוֹם מֵעַזֵּי פָנִים וּמֵעַזּוּת פָּנִים מֵאָדָם רָע וּמֵחָבֵר רָע וּמִשָּׁכֵן רָע וּמִפֶּֽגַע רָע מֵעַֽיִן הָרָע, מִלָּשׁוֹן הָרָע, מִמַּלְשִׁינוּת. מֵעֵדוּת שֶֽׁקֶר, מִשִּׂנְאַת הַבְּ֒רִיּוֹת, מֵעֲלִילָה, מִמִּיתָה מְשׁוּנָה, מֵחֳלָיִם רָעִים, וּמִמִּקְרִים רָעִים וּמִשָּׂטָן הַמַּשְׁחִית מִדִּין קָשֶׁה וּמִבַּֽעַל דִּין קָשֶׁה, בֵּין שֶׁהוּא בֶן בְּרִית וּבֵין שֶׁאֵינוֹ בֶן בְּרִית, וּמִדִּינָהּ שֶׁל גֵּיהִנֺּם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:25:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','en','May it be Your will, Adonoy, my God and God of my fathers, to save me today and every day from arrogant men and from arrogance; from an evil man, from an evil companion, from an evil neighbor; from an evil mishap from an evil eye, from a malicious tongue, from slander, from false testimony, from hatred from scandal, from unnatural death, from harsh disease, and from misfortune, and from the destructive Satan; from a difficult judgment and a difficult opponent, whether he is a fellow Jew or not a fellow Jew and from the retribution of Gehinnom.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:25:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','transliteration','ye-hee rah-tsohn mee-LE-fah-ney-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hahy veh-loh-hey ah-voh-tahy sheh-tah-tsee-leh-nee hah-yohm oo-ve-khohl yohm meh-ah-zey fah-neem oo-meh-ah-zoot pah-neem meh-ah-dahm rah oo-meh-khah-vehr rah oo-mee-shah-khehn rah oo-mee-peh-gah rah meh-ah-yeen hah-rah, mee-lah-shohn hah-rah, mee-mahl-shee-noot. meh-eh-doot sheh-kehr, mee-seen-aht hah-BE-ree-yoht, meh-ah-lee-lah, mee-mee-tah me-shoo-nah, meh-khoh-lah-yeem rah-eem, oo-mee-meek-reem rah-eem oo-mee-sah-tahn hah-mahsh-kheet mee-deen kah-sheh oo-mee-bah-ahl deen kah-sheh, beyn sheh-hoo vehn be-reet oo-veyn sheh-ey-noh vehn be-reet, oo-mee-dee-nahh shehl gey-hee-nohm:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','he','אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ זָכְ֒רֵֽנוּ בְּזִכָּרוֹן טוֹב לְפָנֶֽיךָ וּפָקְ֒דֵֽנוּ בִּפְקֻדַּת יְשׁוּעָה וְרַחֲמִים מִשְּׁ֒מֵי שְׁמֵי קֶֽדֶם וּזְכָר לָֽנוּ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ אַהֲבַת הַקַּדְמוֹנִים אַבְרָהָם יִצְחָק וְיִשְׂרָאֵל עֲבָדֶֽיךָ אֶת הַבְּ֒רִית וְאֶת הַחֶֽסֶד וְאֶת הַשְּׁ֒בוּעָה שֶׁנִּשְׁבַּֽעְתָּ לְאַבְרָהָם אָבִֽינוּ בְּהַר הַמֹּרִיָּה וְאֶת הָעֲקֵדָה שֶׁעָקַד אֶת יִצְחָק בְּנוֹ עַל גַּבֵּי הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ כַּכָּתוּב בְּתוֹרָתֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','en','Our God and God of our fathers, remember us favorably before You and be mindful of us for deliverance and compassion from the eternal high heavens. Remember in our behalf, Adonoy, our God: the love of our ancestors, Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, Your servants; the covenant, the kindness, and the oath which You swore to our father Abraham on Mount Moriah, and the binding of Isaac, his son on the altar, as it is written in Your Torah.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','transliteration','eh-loh-hey-noo veh-loh-hey ah-voh-tey-noo zah-KHE-reh-noo be-zee-kah-rohn tohv le-fah-ney-khah oo-fah-KE-deh-noo beef-koo-daht ye-shoo-ah ve-rah-khah-meem mee-SHE-mey she-mey keh-dehm oo-ze-khahr lah-noo ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo ah-hah-vaht hah-kahd-moh-neem ahv-rah-hahm yeets-khahk ve-yees-rah-ehl ah-vah-dey-khah eht hah-BE-reet ve-eht hah-kheh-sehd ve-eht hah-SHE-voo-ah sheh-neesh-bah-e-tah le-ahv-rah-hahm ah-vee-noo be-hahr hah-moh-ree-yah ve-eht hah-ah-keh-dah sheh-ah-kahd eht yeets-khahk be-noh ahl gah-bey hah-meez-beh-ahkh kah-kah-toov be-toh-rah-teh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','he','וַיְהִי אַחַר הַדְּ֒בָרִים הָאֵֽלֶּה וְהָאֱלֹהִים נִסָּה אֶת־אַבְרָהָם וַיֹּֽאמֶר אֵלָיו אַבְרָהָם וַיֹּֽאמֶר הִנֵּֽנִי: וַיֹּֽאמֶר קַח־נָא אֶת־בִּנְךָ אֶת־יְחִידְ֒ךָ אֲשֶׁר־אָהַֽבְתָּ אֶת־יִצְחָק וְלֶךְ־לְךָ אֶל־אֶֽרֶץ הַמֹּרִיָּה וְהַעֲלֵֽהוּ שָׁם לְעֹלָה עַל אַחַד הֶהָרִים אֲשֶׁר אֹמַר אֵלֶֽיךָ: וַיַּשְׁכֵּם אַבְרָהָם בַּבֹּֽקֶר וַיַּחֲבשׁ אֶת־חֲמֹרוֹ וַיִּקַּח אֶת־שְׁנֵי נְעָרָיו אִתּוֹ וְאֵת יִצְחָק בְּנוֹ וַיְבַקַּע עֲצֵי עֹלָה וַיָּֽקָם וַיֵּֽלֶךְ אֶל־הַמָּקוֹם אֲשֶׁר־אָֽמַר־לוֹ הָאֱלֹהִֽים: בַּיּוֹם הַשְּׁ֒לִישִׁי וַיִּשָּׂא אַבְרָהָם אֶת־עֵינָיו וַיַּרְא אֶת־הַמָּקוֹם מֵרָחֹק: וַיֹּֽאמֶר אַבְרָהָם אֶל־נְעָרָיו שְׁבוּ־לָכֶם פֹּה עִם־הַחֲמוֹר וַאֲנִי וְהַנַּֽעַר נֵלְ֒כָה עַד־כֹּה וְנִשְׁתַּחֲוֶה וְנָשֽׁוּבָה אֲלֵיכֶם: וַיִּקַּח אַבְרָהָם אֶת־עֲצֵי הָעֹלָה וַיָּֽשֶׂם עַל־יִצְחָק בְּנוֹ וַיִּקַּח בְּיָדוֹ אֶת־הָאֵשׁ וְאֶת־הַמַּאֲכֶֽלֶת וַיֵּלְ֒כוּ שְׁנֵיהֶם יַחְדָּו: וַיֹּֽאמֶר יִצְחָק אֶל־אַבְרָהָם אָבִיו וַיֹּֽאמֶר אָבִי וַיֹּֽאמֶר הִנֶּֽנִּי בְנִי וַיֹּֽאמֶר הִנֵּה הָאֵשׁ וְהָעֵצִים וְאַיֵּה הַשֶּׂה לְעֹלָֽה: וַיֹּֽאמֶר אַבְרָהָם אֱלֹהִים יִרְאֶה־לּוֹ הַשֶּׂה לְעֹלָה בְּנִי וַיֵּלְ֒כוּ שְׁנֵיהֶם יַחְדָּו: וַיָּבֹֽאוּ אֶל־הַמָּקוֹם אֲשֶׁר אָֽמַר־לוֹ הָאֱלֹהִים וַיִּֽבֶן שָׁם אַבְרָהָם אֶת־הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ וַיַּעֲרֹךְ אֶת־הָעֵצִים וַיַּעֲקֹד אֶת־יִצְחָק בְּנוֹ וַיָּֽשֶׂם אֹתוֹ עַל־הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ מִמַּֽעַל לָעֵצִים: וַיִּשְׁלַח אַבְרָהָם אֶת־יָדוֹ וַיִּקַּח אֶת־הַמַּאֲכֶֽלֶת לִשְׁחֹט אֶת־בְּנוֹ: וַיִּקְרָא אֵלָיו מַלְאַךְ יְהֹוָה מִן־הַשָּׁמַֽיִם וַיֹּֽאמֶר אַבְרָהָם אַבְרָהָם וַיֹּֽאמֶר הִנֵּֽנִי: וַיֹּֽאמֶר אַל־תִּשְׁלַח יָֽדְ֒ךָ אֶל־הַנַּֽעַר וְאַל־תַּֽעַשׂ לוֹ מְאוּמָה כִּי עַתָּה יָדַֽעְתִּי כִּי־יְרֵא אֱלֹהִים אַֽתָּה וְלֹא חָשַֽׂכְתָּ אֶת־בִּנְךָ אֶת־יְחִידְ֒ךָ מִמֶּֽנִּי: וַיִּשָּׂא אַבְרָהָם אֶת־עֵינָיו וַיַּרְא וְהִנֵּה־אַֽיִל אַחַר נֶאֱחַז בַּסְּ֒בַךְ בְּקַרְנָיו וַיֵּֽלֶךְ אַבְרָהָם וַיִּקַּח אֶת־הָאַֽיִל וַיַּעֲלֵֽהוּ לְעֹלָה תַּֽחַת בְּנוֹ: וַיִּקְרָא אַבְרָהָם שֵׁם־הַמָּקוֹם הַהוּא יְהֹוָה יִרְאֶה אֲשֶׁר יֵאָמֵר הַיּוֹם בְּהַר יְהֹוָה יֵרָאֶה: וַיִּקְרָא מַלְאַךְ יְהֹוָה אֶל־אַבְרָהָם שֵׁנִית מִן־הַשָּׁמָֽיִם: וַיֹּאמֶר בִּי נִשְׁבַּֽעְתִּי נְאֻם־יְהֹוָה כִּי יַֽעַן אֲשֶׁר עָשִֽׂיתָ אֶת־הַדָּבָר הַזֶּה וְלֹא חָשַֽׂכְתָּ אֶת־בִּנְךָ אֶת־יְחִידֶֽךָ: כִּי־בָרֵךְ אֲבָרֶכְ֒ךָ וְהַרְבָּה אַרְבֶּה אֶת־זַרְעֲךָ כְּכוֹכְ֒בֵי הַשָּׁמַֽיִם וְכַחוֹל אֲשֶׁר עַל־שְׂפַת הַיָּם וְיִרַשׁ זַרְעֲךָ אֵת שַֽׁעַר אֹיְ֒בָיו: וְהִתְבָּרְ֒כוּ בְזַרְעֲךָ כֹּל גּוֹיֵי הָאָֽרֶץ עֵֽקֶב אֲשֶׁר שָׁמַֽעְתָּ בְּקֹלִי: וַיָּֽשָׁב אַבְרָהָם אֶל־נְעָרָיו וַיָּקֻֽמוּ וַיֵּלְ֒כוּ יַחְדָּו אֶל־בְּאֵר שָֽׁבַע וַיֵּֽשֶׁב אַבְרָהָם בִּבְאֵר שָֽׁבַע:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','en','After these events, God tested Abraham and said to him, "Abraham!" and he [Abraham] said, "Here I am." He said, "Please, take your son, your only one, whom you love—Isaac— and go to the land of Moriah, and bring him up as a burnt-offering on one of the mountains which I will designate to you. Abraham awoke early in the morning, saddled his donkey, and took his two attendants with him, and also his son Isaac. He split the wood of the burnt-offering, and rose up, and went to the place that God had designated to him. On the third day, Abraham lifted his eyes and saw the place from afar. Abraham said to his attendants, You stay here with the donkey, and I and the boy will go to that place. We will prostrate ourselves [in worship] and return to you." And Abraham took the wood of the burnt-offering and placed it on his son Isaac. In his hand he took the fire and the knife, and they both went together. Isaac spoke to Abraham his father and said, "Father," and he said, "Here I am my son." He said, "Here are the fire and the wood, but where is the lamb for the burnt-offering?" Abraham said, God Himself will show the lamb for a burnt offering, my son." And the two of them went together. They came to the place that God had designated to him, and Abraham built the altar there, and arranged the wood, and bound his son Isaac, and placed him on the altar, on top of the wood. Abraham reached out his hand and took the knife to slaughter his son. An angel of Adonoy called to him from heaven and said, "Abraham! Abraham!" and he said, "Here I am." He [God] said, Do not harm the boy, nor do anything to him; for now I know that you are one who fears God and have not withheld your son, your only one, from Me." Abraham raised his eyes and beheld a ram after it had been caught in the thicket by its horns; and Abraham went and took the ram, and brought it up as a burnt-offering instead of his son. Abraham called the name of that place, Adonoy will see; as it is said [to] this day On Adonoy''s mountain, He will be seen. An angel of Adonoy called to Abraham a second time from heaven, and said, ‘I have sworn by Myself,'' declares Adonoy, ‘that because you performed this deed, and did not withhold your only son, I will greatly bless you and make your descendants as numerous as the stars of the sky and like the sand on the seashore, and your descendants will inherit the gate of their enemies. Through your children, will be blessed all the nations of the world, because you heeded My voice.''" Abraham returned to his attendants, and they rose and went together to Beer Sheva, and Abraham dwelt in Beer Sheva.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','transliteration','vah-ye-hee ah-khahr hah-DE-vah-reem hah-eh-leh ve-hah-eh-loh-heem nee-sah eht ahv-rah-hahm vah-yoh-mehr eh-lahv ahv-rah-hahm vah-yoh-mehr hee-neh-nee: vah-yoh-mehr kahkh nah eht been-khah eht ye-khee-DE-khah ah-shehr ah-hah-ve-tah eht yeets-khahk ve-lehkh le-khah ehl eh-rehts hah-moh-ree-yah ve-hah-ah-leh-hoo shahm le-oh-lah ahl ah-khahd heh-hah-reem ah-shehr oh-mahr eh-ley-khah: vah-yahsh-kehm ahv-rah-hahm bah-boh-kehr vah-yah-khahvsh eht khah-moh-roh vah-yee-kahkh eht she-ney ne-ah-rahv ee-toh ve-eht yeets-khahk be-noh vah-ye-vah-kah ah-tsey oh-lah vah-yah-kahm vah-yeh-lehkh ehl hah-mah-kohm ah-shehr ah-mahr loh hah-eh-loh-heem: bah-yohm hah-SHE-lee-shee vah-yee-sah ahv-rah-hahm eht ey-nahv vah-yahr eht hah-mah-kohm meh-rah-khohk: vah-yoh-mehr ahv-rah-hahm ehl ne-ah-rahv she-voo lah-khehm pohh eem hah-khah-mohr vah-ah-nee ve-hah-nah-ahr neh-LE-khah ahd kohh ve-neesh-tah-khah-veh ve-nah-shoo-vah ah-ley-khehm: vah-yee-kahkh ahv-rah-hahm eht ah-tsey hah-oh-lah vah-yah-sehm ahl yeets-khahk be-noh vah-yee-kahkh be-yah-doh eht hah-ehsh ve-eht hah-mah-ah-kheh-leht vah-yeh-LE-khoo she-ney-hehm yahkh-dahv: vah-yoh-mehr yeets-khahk ehl ahv-rah-hahm ah-veev vah-yoh-mehr ah-vee vah-yoh-mehr hee-neh-nee ve-nee vah-yoh-mehr hee-neh hah-ehsh ve-hah-eh-tseem ve-ah-yeh hah-seh le-oh-lah: vah-yoh-mehr ahv-rah-hahm eh-loh-heem yeer-eh loh hah-seh le-oh-lah be-nee vah-yeh-LE-khoo she-ney-hehm yahkh-dahv: vah-yah-voh-oo ehl hah-mah-kohm ah-shehr ah-mahr loh hah-eh-loh-heem vah-yee-vehn shahm ahv-rah-hahm eht hah-meez-beh-ahkh vah-yah-ah-rohkh eht hah-eh-tseem vah-yah-ah-kohd eht yeets-khahk be-noh vah-yah-sehm oh-toh ahl hah-meez-beh-ahkh mee-mah-ahl lah-eh-tseem: vah-yeesh-lahkh ahv-rah-hahm eht yah-doh vah-yee-kahkh eht hah-mah-ah-kheh-leht leesh-khoht eht be-noh: vah-yeek-rah eh-lahv mahl-ahkh ah-doh-NAI meen hah-shah-mah-yeem vah-yoh-mehr ahv-rah-hahm ahv-rah-hahm vah-yoh-mehr hee-neh-nee: vah-yoh-mehr ahl teesh-lahkh yah-DE-khah ehl hah-nah-ahr ve-ahl tah-ahs loh me-oo-mah kee ah-tah yah-dah-e-tee kee ye-reh eh-loh-heem ah-tah ve-loh khah-sah-khe-tah eht been-khah eht ye-khee-DE-khah mee-meh-nee: vah-yee-sah ahv-rah-hahm eht ey-nahv vah-yahr ve-hee-neh ah-yeel ah-khahr neh-eh-khahz bah-SE-vahkh be-kahr-nahv vah-yeh-lehkh ahv-rah-hahm vah-yee-kahkh eht hah-ah-yeel vah-yah-ah-leh-hoo le-oh-lah tah-khaht be-noh: vah-yeek-rah ahv-rah-hahm shehm hah-mah-kohm hah-hoo ah-doh-NAI yeer-eh ah-shehr yeh-ah-mehr hah-yohm be-hahr ah-doh-NAI yeh-rah-eh: vah-yeek-rah mahl-ahkh ah-doh-NAI ehl ahv-rah-hahm sheh-neet meen hah-shah-mah-yeem: vah-yoh-mehr bee neesh-bah-e-tee ne-oom ah-doh-NAI kee yah-ahn ah-shehr ah-see-tah eht hah-dah-vahr hah-zeh ve-loh khah-sah-khe-tah eht been-khah eht ye-khee-deh-khah: kee vah-rehkh ah-vah-REHKH-khah ve-hahr-bah ahr-beh eht zahr-ah-khah ke-khoh-KHE-vey hah-shah-mah-yeem ve-khah-khohl ah-shehr ahl se-faht hah-yahm ve-yee-rahsh zahr-ah-khah eht shah-ahr oh-YE-vahv: ve-heet-bah-RE-khoo ve-zahr-ah-khah kohl goh-yey hah-ah-rehts eh-kehv ah-shehr shah-mah-e-tah be-koh-lee: vah-yah-shahv ahv-rah-hahm ehl ne-ah-rahv vah-yah-koo-moo vah-yeh-LE-khoo yahkh-dahv ehl be-ehr shah-vah vah-yeh-shehv ahv-rah-hahm beev-ehr shah-vah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','he','ביום שאין אומרים תחנון אין אומרים זה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','en','On a day when Tachanun is not said, the following paragraph is omitted.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','he','רִבּוֹנוֹ שֶׁל עוֹלָם כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּבַשׁ אַבְרָהָם אָבִינוּ אֶת רַחֲמָיו לַעֲשׂוֹת רְצוֹנְ֒ךָ בְּלֵבָב שָׁלֵם, כֵּן יִכְבְּ֒שׁוּ רַחֲמֶיךָ אֶת כַּעַסְךָ מֵעָלֵינוּ, וְיָגֺֽלּוֹ רַחֲמֶֽיךָ עַל מִדּוֹתֶֽיךָ: וְתִתְנַהֵג עִמָּֽנוּ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ בְּמִדַּת הַחֶֽסֶד וּבְמִדַּת הָרַחֲמִים, וּבְטוּבְ֒ךָ הַגָּדוֹל יָשׁוּב חֲרוֹן אַפְּ֒ךָ מֵעַמְּ֒ךָ וּמֵעִירְ֒ךָ וּמֵאַרְצְ֒ךָ וּמִנַחֲלָתֶֽךָ: וְקַיֶם לָֽנוּ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ אֶת הַדָּבָר שֶׁהִבְטַחְתָּֽנוּ בְּתוֹרָתֶֽךָ, עַל יְדֵי משֶׁה עַבְדֶּֽךָ כָּאָמוּר. וְזָכַרְתִּי אֶת בְּרִיתִי יַעֲקוֹב וְאַף אֶת בְּרִיתִי יִצְחָק, וְאַף אֶת בְּרִיתִי אַבְרָהָם אֶזְכֹּר וְהָאָֽרֶץ אֶזְכֹּר: וְנֶאֱמַר, וְאַף גַּם זֹאת בִּהְיוֹתָם בְּאֶֽרֶץ אֹיְ֒בֵיהֶם לֹא מְאַסְתִּים וְלֹא גְעַלְתִּים לְכַלּוֹתָם לְהָפֵר בְּרִיתִי אִתָּם כִּי אֲנִי יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵיהֶם: וְנֶאֱמַר וְזָכַרְתִּי לָהֶם בְּרִית רִאשֺׁנִים אֲשֶׁר הוֹצֵֽאתִי אֹתָם מֵאֶֽרֶץ מִצְרַֽיִם, לְעֵינֵי הַגּוֹיִם לִהְיוֹת לָהֶם לֵאלֹהִים, אֲנִי יְהֹוָה. וְנֶאֶמַר וְשָׁב יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ אֶת שְׁבוּתְ֒ךָ וְרִחֲמֶֽךָ, וְשָׁב וְקִבֶּצְךָ מִכָּל הָעַמִּים, אֲשֶׁר הֱפִיצְ֒ךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ שָֽׁמָּה. אִם יִהְיֶה נִדַּחֲךָ בִּקְצֵה הַשָּׁמָֽיִם מִשָּׁם יְקַבֶּצְךָ יְהֹוָה אֶלֹהֶֽיךָ וּמִשָּׁם יִקָּחֶֽךָ: וְנֶאֶמַר וֶהֱבִיאֲךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ אֶל הָאָֽרֶץ אֲשֶׁר יָרְ֒שׁוּ אֲבֹתֶֽיךָ וִירִשְׁתָּהּ וְהֵיטִבְ֒ךָ וְהִרְבְּ֒ךָ מֵאֲבֹתֶֽיךָ: וְנֶאֱמַר עַל יְדֵי נְבִיאֶֽךָ, יְהֹוָה חָנֵֽנוּ, לְךָ קִוִּֽינוּ הֱיֵה זְרוֹעָם לַבְּ֒קָרִים, אַף יְשׁוּעָתֵֽנוּ בְּעֵת צָרָה: וְנֶאֱמַר, וְעֵת צָרָה הִיא לְיַעֲקֹב וּמִמֶּֽנָּה יִוָּשֵֽׁעַ: וְנֶאֱמַר בְּכָל־צָרָתָם לוֹ צָר וּמַלְאַךְ פָּנָיו הוֹשִׁיעָם, בְּאַהֲבָתוֹ וּבְחֶמְלָתוֹ הוּא גְאָלָם וַיְנַטְּ֒לֵם וַיְנַשְּׂ֒אֵם כָּל־יְמֵי עוֹלָם: וְנֶאֱמַר, מִי אֵל כָּמֽוֹךָ נֹשֵׂא עָוֺן וְעֹבֵר עַל־פֶּֽשַׁע, לִשְׁאֵרִית נַחֲלָתוֹ לֹא־הֶחֱזִיק לָעַד אַפּוֹ, כִּי חָפֵץ חֶֽסֶד הוּא: יָשׁוּב יְרַחְמֵֽנוּ יִכְבּוֹשׁ עֲוֺנוֹתֵֽינוּ, וְתַשְׁלִיךְ בִּמְצוּלוֹת יָם כָּל־חַטֹּאתָם: תִּתֵּן אֱמֶת לְיַעֲקֹב חֶֽסֶד לְאַבְרָהָם אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּֽעְתָּ לַאֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ מִֽימֵי קֶֽדֶם: וְנֶאֱמַר, וַהֲבִיאוֹתִים אֶל־הַר קָדְשִׁי וְשִׂמַּחְתִּים בְּבֵית תְּפִלָּתִי עוֹלוֹתֵיהֶם וְזִבְחֵיהֶם לְרָצוֹן עַל מִזְבְּחִי, כִּי בֵיתִי בֵּית־תְּפִלָּה, יִקָּרֵא לְכָל הָעַמִּים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','en','Master of the Universe! just as our father, Abraham suppressed his compassion to do Your will with his whole heart, so may your compassion suppress your anger against us; and may your compassion prevail over your [other] attributes. Act with us Adonoy, our God, kindly and with compassion. In your great goodness turn away your fierce anger from your people, and from your city, from your land and from your territorial heritage. Fulfill for us, Adonoy, our God, the promise you made in your Torah, through your servant, Moses, as it says, I will recall my covenant with Jacob, also my covenant with Isaac, and also my covenant with Abraham will I recall; and I will recall the land. And it is said: "And even then when they are in the land of their enemies I will not abhor them nor sparn them to destroy them— to annul my covenant with them; for I am Adonoy, their God." And it is said: And I will recall for them the covenant with their ancestors whom I took out from the land of Egypt before the eyes of the nations, to be their God, I am Adonoy. And it is said: "And Adonoy, Your God, will return your exiles and have compassion upon you, and will again gather you from [among] all the nations where Adonoy, your God, has scattered you. Even if your dispersed will be scattered to the ends of the world, from there Adonoy, your God, will gather you, and from there He will fetch you. And it is said: And Adonoy, your God will bring you into the land your forefathers inherited. And you will inherit it; And He will do good to you and multiply you more than your forefathers. And it is said by Your prophets: Adonoy, be gracious to us, [for] we put our hope in You; be their strength every morning; also our deliverance in time of distress. And it is said: It is a time of trouble for Jacob, but he will be delivered from it And it is said: In all their affliction, He is afflicted, and the angel of His Presence delivered them; in His love and in His pity, He redeemed them, and bore them and carried them forever. and it is said: Who is an Almighty like You, forbearer of iniquity and forgiver of transgression for the remnant of his heritage? He does not maintain His wrath forever, for He desires to do kindness. He will again show us compassion, He will suppress our iniquities; And you will cast into the depths of the sea all their sins. You will grant truth to Jacob, kindliness to Abraham as You swore to our fathers from the days of old. And it is said: And I will bring them to My holy moutain; and make them joyful in My House of Prayer; their burnt-offerings and sacrifices will be accepted with favor on My Altar, for My House will be called a House of Prayer for all peoples.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','transliteration','ree-boh-noh shehl oh-lahm ke-moh sheh-kah-vahsh ahv-rah-hahm ah-vee-noo eht rah-khah-mahv lah-ah-soht re-tsoh-NE-khah be-leh-vahv shah-lehm, kehn yeekh-BE-shoo rah-khah-mey-khah eht kah-ahs-khah meh-ah-ley-noo, ve-yah-goh-loh rah-khah-mey-khah ahl mee-doh-tey-khah: ve-teet-nah-hehg ee-mah-noo ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo be-mee-daht hah-kheh-sehd oo-ve-mee-daht hah-rah-khah-meem, oo-ve-too-VE-khah hah-gah-dohl yah-shoov khah-rohn ah-PE-khah meh-ah-ME-khah oo-meh-ee-RE-khah oo-meh-ahr-TSE-khah oo-mee-nah-khah-lah-teh-khah: ve-kah-yehm lah-noo ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo eht hah-dah-vahr sheh-heev-tahkh-tah-noo be-toh-rah-teh-khah, ahl ye-dey m-sheh ahv-deh-khah kah-ah-moor. ve-zah-khahr-tee eht be-ree-tee yah-ah-kohv ve-ahf eht be-ree-tee yeets-khahk, ve-ahf eht be-ree-tee ahv-rah-hahm ehz-kohr ve-hah-ah-rehts ehz-kohr: ve-neh-eh-mahr, ve-ahf gahm zoht beeh-yoh-tahm be-eh-rehts oh-YE-vey-hehm loh me-ahs-teem ve-loh ge-ahl-teem le-khah-loh-tahm le-hah-fehr be-ree-tee ee-tahm kee ah-nee ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-hehm: ve-neh-eh-mahr ve-zah-khahr-tee lah-hehm be-reet ree-shoh-neem ah-shehr hoh-tseh-tee oh-tahm meh-eh-rehts meets-rah-yeem, le-ey-ney hah-goh-yeem leeh-yoht lah-hehm leh-loh-heem, ah-nee ah-doh-NAI. ve-neh-eh-mahr ve-shahv ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-khah eht she-voo-TE-khah ve-ree-khah-meh-khah, ve-shahv ve-kee-behts-khah mee-kohl hah-ah-meem, ah-shehr heh-fee-TSE-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-khah shah-mah. eem yeeh-yeh nee-dah-khah-khah beek-tseh hah-shah-mah-yeem mee-shahm ye-kah-behts-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-khah oo-mee-shahm yee-kah-kheh-khah: ve-neh-eh-mahr veh-heh-vee-ah-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-khah ehl hah-ah-rehts ah-shehr yah-RE-shoo ah-voh-tey-khah vee-reesh-tahh ve-hey-TEEV-khah ve-heer-BE-khah meh-ah-voh-tey-khah: ve-neh-eh-mahr ahl ye-dey ne-vee-eh-khah, ah-doh-NAI khah-neh-noo, le-khah kee-vee-noo heh-yeh ze-roh-ahm lah-BE-kah-reem, ahf ye-shoo-ah-teh-noo be-eht tsah-rah: ve-neh-eh-mahr, ve-eht tsah-rah hee le-yah-ah-kohv oo-mee-meh-nah yee-vah-sheh-ah: ve-neh-eh-mahr be-khohl tsah-rah-tahm loh tsahr oo-mahl-ahkh pah-nahv hoh-shee-ahm, be-ah-hah-vah-toh oo-ve-khehm-lah-toh hoo ge-ah-lahm vah-ye-nah-TE-lehm vah-ye-nah-SE-ehm kohl ye-mey oh-lahm: ve-neh-eh-mahr, mee ehl kah-moh-khah noh-seh ah-vohn ve-oh-vehr ahl peh-shah, leesh-eh-reet nah-khah-lah-toh loh heh-kheh-zeek lah-ahd ah-poh, kee khah-fehts kheh-sehd hoo: yah-shoov ye-rahkh-meh-noo yeekh-bohsh ah-voh-noh-tey-noo, ve-tahsh-leekh beem-tsoo-loht yahm kohl khah-toh-tahm: tee-tehn eh-meht le-yah-ah-kohv kheh-sehd le-ahv-rah-hahm ah-shehr neesh-bah-e-tah lah-ah-voh-tey-noo mee-mey keh-dehm: ve-neh-eh-mahr, vah-hah-vee-oh-teem ehl hahr kohd-shee ve-see-mahkh-teem be-veyt te-fee-lah-tee oh-loh-tey-hehm ve-zeev-khey-hehm le-rah-tsohn ahl meez-be-khee, kee vey-tee beyt te-fee-lah, yee-kah-reh le-khohl hah-ah-meem:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','he','לְעוֹלָם יְהֵא אָדָם יְרֵא שָׁמַֽיִם בַּסֵּֽתֶר וּבַגָּלוּי וּמוֹדֶה עַל הָאֱמֶת וְדוֹבֵר אֱמֶת בִּלְבָבוֹ וְיַשְׁכֵּם וְיֹאמַר:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','en','A person should always be in fear of God, privately as well as openly, [he should] admit the truth, and speak truth in his heart, and rise early and proclaim:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','transliteration','le-oh-lahm ye-heh ah-dahm ye-reh shah-mah-yeem bah-seh-tehr oo-vah-gah-looy oo-moh-deh ahl hah-eh-meht ve-doh-vehr eh-meht beel-vah-voh ve-yahsh-kehm ve-yoh-mahr:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','he','רִבּוֹן כָּל הָעוֹלָמִים וַאֲדוֹנֵי הָאֲדוֹנִים, לֹא עַל צִדְקוֹתֵֽינוּ אֲנַֽחְנוּ מַפִּילִים תַּחֲנוּנֵֽינוּ לְפָנֶֽיךָ כִּי עַל רַחֲמֶֽיךָ הָרַבִּים, מָה אָֽנוּ מֶה חַיֵּֽינוּ מֶה חַסְדֵּֽנוּ, מַה צִּדְקוֹתֵֽינוּ, מַה יְּשׁוּעָתֵֽנוּ, מַה כֹּחֵֽנוּ מַה גְּבוּרָתֵֽנוּ, מַה נֹּאמַר לְפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ הֲלֹא כָּל הַגִּבּוֹרִים כְּאַֽיִן לְפָנֶֽיךָ וְאַנְשֵׁי הַשֵּׁם כְּלֹא הָיוּ וַחֲכָמִים כִּבְלִי מַדָּע וּנְבוֹנִים כִּבְלִי הַשְׂכֵּל כִּי רוֹב מַעֲשֵׂיהֶם תֹּֽהוּ וִימֵי חַיֵּיהֶם הֶֽבֶל לְפָנֶֽיךָ, וּמוֹתַר הָאָדָם מִן הַבְּ֒הֵמָה אָֽיִן כִּי הַכֹּל הָֽבֶל: לְבַד הַנְשָׁמָה הַטְּ֒הוֹרָה שֶׁהִיא עֲתִידָה לִתֵּן דִּין וְחֶשְׁבּוֹן לִפְנֵי כִסֵּא כְבוֹדֶֽךָ וְכָל הַגּוֹיִם כְּאַֽיִן נֶגְדֶּֽךָ שֶׁנֶּאֶמַר הֵן גּוֹיִם כְּמַר מִדְּ֒לִי וּכְשַֽׁחַק מֹאזְ֒נַֽיִם נֶחְשָֽׁבוּ הֵן אִיִּים כַּדַּק יִטּוֹל:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','en','Lord of all the worlds and Master of masters! Not on account of our righteousness do we offer our supplications before You, but on account of Your abundant mercy. What are we? What is our life? What are our acts of kindness? What is our righteousness? What is our deliverance? What is our strength? What is our might? What can we say before You, Adonoy, our God and God of our fathers? Are not all the mighty men as nothing before You? Famous men as though they had never been? The wise as if they were without knowledge? And men of understanding, as if they were devoid of intelligence? For most of their actions are a waste, and the days of their life are trivial in Your presence. The superiority of man over the beast is nil, for all is futile. Except the pure soul which is destined to give an accounting before the Throne of Your Glory. All the nations are as nothing before you, as it is written: The nations are as a drop of a bucket— no more than dust upon the scales are they considered! Behold, the isles are like the flying dust.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','transliteration','ree-bohn kohl hah-oh-lah-meem vah-ah-doh-ney hah-ah-doh-neem, loh ahl tseed-koh-tey-noo ahnah-khe-noo mah-pee-leem tah-khah-noo-ney-noo le-fah-ney-khah kee ahl rah-khah-mey-khah hah-rah-beem, mah ah-noo meh khah-yey-noo meh khahs-deh-noo, mahh tseed-koh-tey-noo, mahh ye-shoo-ah-teh-noo, mahh koh-kheh-noo mahh ge-voo-rah-teh-noo, mahh noh-mahr le-fah-ney-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo veh-loh-hey ah-voh-tey-noo hah-loh kohl hah-gee-boh-reem ke-ah-yeen le-fah-ney-khah ve-ahn-shey hah-shehm ke-loh hah-yoo vah-khah-khah-meem keev-lee mah-dah oo-ne-voh-neem keev-lee hahs-kehl kee rohv mah-ah-sey-hehm toh-hoo vee-mey khah-yey-hehm heh-vehl le-fah-ney-khah, oo-moh-tahr hah-ah-dahm meen hah-BE-heh-mah ah-yeen kee hah-kohl hah-vehl: le-vahd hahn-shah-mah hah-TE-hoh-rah sheh-hee ah-tee-dah lee-tehn deen ve-khehsh-bohn leef-ney khee-seh khe-voh-deh-khah ve-khohl hah-goh-yeem ke-ah-yeen nehg-deh-khah sheh-neh-eh-mahr hehn goh-yeem ke-mahr mee-DE-lee oo-khe-shah-khahk moh-ZE-nah-yeem nehkh-shah-voo hehn ee-yeem kah-dahk yee-tohl:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','he','אֲבָל אֲנַֽחְנוּ עַמְּ֒ךָ בְּנֵי בְרִיתֶֽךָ, בְּנֵי אַבְרָהָם אֹהַבְךָ שֶׁנִּשְׁבַּֽעְתָּ לּוֹ בְּהַר הַמֹּרִיָּה, זֶֽרַע יִצְחָק יְחִידוֹ שֶׁנֶּעֱקַד עַל גַּבֵּי הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ, עֲדַת יַעֲקֹב בִּנְךָ בְּכוֹרֶֽךָ שֶׁמֵּאַהֲבָתְ֒ךָ שֶׁאָהַֽבְתָּ אוֹתוֹ וּמִשִּׂמְחָתְ֒ךָ שֶׁשָּׂמַֽחְתָּ בּוֹ קָרָֽאתָ אֶת שְׁמוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל וִישֻׁרוּן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','en','However, we are Your people, children of Your covenant, children of Abraham, Your beloved, to whom You swore on Mount Moriah; the seed of Isaac, his only son, who was bound on top of the altar; the community of Jacob, Your firstborn, [whom]—because of Your love for him and Your joyous delight in him— You named him Yisrael and Yeshurun.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','transliteration','ah-vahl ahnah-khe-noo ah-ME-khah be-ney ve-ree-teh-khah, be-ney ahv-rah-hahm oh-hahv-khah sheh-neesh-bah-e-tah loh be-hahr hah-moh-ree-yah, zeh-rah yeets-khahk ye-khee-doh sheh-neh-eh-kahd ahl gah-bey hah-meez-beh-ahkh, ah-daht yah-ah-kohv been-khah be-khoh-reh-khah sheh-meh-ah-hah-vah-TE-khah sheh-ah-hah-ve-tah oh-toh oo-mee-seem-khah-TE-khah sheh-sah-mah-khe-tah boh kah-rah-tah eht she-moh yees-rah-ehl vee-shoo-roon:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','he','לְפִיכָךְ אֲנַֽחְנוּ חַיָּבִים לְהוֹדוֹת לְךָ וּלְשַׁבֵּחֲךָ וּלְפָאֶרְךָ וּלְבָרֵךְ וּלְקַדֵּשׁ וְלִתֵּן שֶֽׁבַח וְהוֹדָיָה לִשְׁמֶֽךָ: אַשְׁרֵֽינוּ מַה טּוֹב חֶלְקֵֽנוּ וּמַה נָּעִים גּוֹרָלֵֽנוּ וּמַה יָּפָה יְרֻשָּׁתֵֽנוּ: אַשְׁרֵֽינוּ כְּשֶׁאָֽנוּ מַשְׁכִּימִים וּמַעֲרִיבִים בְּבָתֵּי כְנֵסִיּוֹת וּבְבָתֵּי מִדְרָשׁוֹת וּמְיַחֲדִים שִׁמְךָ בְּכָל־יוֹם תָּמִיד וְאוֹמְ֒רִים פַּעֲמַֽיִם בְּאַהֲבָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','en','Therefore, we are obligated to thank You, to praise You, and to glorify You; to bless, to sanctify, and to offer praise and thanks to Your Name. We are fortunate! How good is our portion! How pleasant is our destiny! How beautiful is our heritage! We are fortunate we who rise early and stay late in synagogues and houses of study, and unify Your Name each day—always and lovingly say twice:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','transliteration','le-fee-khahkh ahnah-khe-noo khah-yah-veem le-hoh-doht le-khah oo-le-shah-beh-khah-khah oo-le-fah-ehr-khah oo-le-vah-rehkh oo-le-kah-dehsh ve-lee-tehn sheh-vahkh ve-hoh-dah-yah leesh-meh-khah: ahsh-rey-noo mahh tohv khehl-keh-noo oo-mahh nah-eem goh-rah-leh-noo oo-mahh yah-fah ye-roo-shah-teh-noo: ahsh-rey-noo ke-sheh-ah-noo mahsh-kee-meem oo-mah-ah-ree-veem be-vah-tey khe-neh-see-yoht oo-ve-vah-tey meed-rah-shoht oo-me-yah-khah-deem sheem-khah be-khohl yohm tah-meed ve-oh-ME-reem pah-ah-mah-yeem be-ah-hah-vah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','he','שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ יְהֹוָה אֶחָד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','en','"Hear Israel, Adonoy is our God, Adonoy is One."','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','transliteration','she-mah yees-rah-ehl ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo ah-doh-NAI eh-khahd:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','he','ויאמר בלחש:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','en','The following line is to be said silently','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','he','בָּרוּךְ שֵׁם כְּבוֹד מַלְכוּתוֹ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','en','Blessed [is His] Name, Whose glorious kingdom is forever and ever.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','transliteration','bah-rookh shehm ke-vohd mahl-khoo-toh le-oh-lahm vah-ehd:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','he','וְאָהַבְתָּ אֵת יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ בְּכָל֯־לְ֯בָבְךָ וּבְכָל־נַפְשְׁךָ וּבְכָל־מְאֹדֶֽךָ: וְהָיוּ הַדְּ֒בָרִים הָאֵֽלֶּה אֲשֶׁר֯ אָ֯נֹכִי מְצַוְּךָ הַיּוֹם עַל֯־לְ֯בָבֶֽךָ: וְשִׁנַּנְתָּם לְבָנֶֽיךָ וְדִבַּרְתָּ בָּם בְּשִׁבְתְּ֒ךָ בְּבֵיתֶֽךָ וּבְלֶכְתְּ֒ךָ בַדֶּֽרֶךְ וּבְשָׁכְבְּ֒ךָ וּבְקוּמֶֽךָ: וּקְשַׁרְתָּם לְאוֹת עַל֯־יָ֯דֶֽךָ וְהָיוּ לְטֹטָפֹת בֵּין עֵינֶֽיךָ: וּכְתַבְתָּם עַל־מְזֻזוֹת בֵּיתֶֽךָ וּבִשְׁעָרֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','en','And you shall love Adonoy your God with all your heart and with all your soul and with all your possessions. And these words which I command you today, shall be upon your heart. And you shall teach them sharply to your children. And you shall discuss them when you sit in your house, and when you travel on the road, and when you lie down and when you rise. And you shall bind them for a sign upon your hand, and they shall be for totafos between your eyes. And you shall write them upon the doorposts of your house and upon your gateways.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','transliteration','ve-ah-hahv-tah eht ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-khah be-khahl le-vah-ve-KHAH oo-ve-khohl nahf-she-khah oo-ve-khohl me-oh-deh-khah: ve-hah-yoo hah-DE-vah-reem hah-eh-leh ah-SHEHR ah-noh-KHEE me-tsah-ve-khah hah-yohm ahl le-vah-veh-KHAH: ve-shee-nahn-tahm le-vah-ney-khah ve-dee-bahr-tah bahm be-sheev-TE-khah be-vey-teh-khah oo-ve-lehkh-TE-khah vah-deh-rehkh oo-ve-shah-khe-BE-khah oo-ve-koo-meh-khah: oo-ke-shahr-tahm le-oht ahl yah-deh-KHAH ve-hah-yoo le-toh-tah-foht beyn ey-ney-khah: oo-khe-tahv-tahm ahl me-zoo-zoht bey-teh-khah oo-veesh-ah-rey-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','he','אַתָּה הוּא עַד שֶׁלֹּא נִבְרָא הָעוֹלָם, אַתָּה הוּא מִשֶּׁנִּבְרָא הָעוֹלָם, אַתָּה הוּא בָּעוֹלָם הַזֶּה וְאַתָּה הוּא לָעוֹלָם הַבָּא, קַדֵּשׁ אֶת שִׁמְךָ עַל מַקְדִּישֵׁי שְׁמֶֽךָ וְקַדֵּשׁ אֶת שִׁמְךָ בְּעֺלָמֶֽךָ, וּבִישׁוּעָתְ֒ךָ תָּרוּם וְתַגְבִּֽיהַּ קַרְנֵֽנוּ לְמַֽעְלָה, וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ בְּקָרוֹב לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ. בָּרוּךְ הַמְקַדֵּשׁ שְׁמוֹ בָּרַבִּים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','en','You existed before the world was created. You exist [in the same way] now that the world has been created. You exist in this world, and You will exist in the World-to-Come. Sanctify Your Name upon those who hallow Your Name, and sanctify Your Name in Your world. And through Your deliverance You will be exalted and You will uplift our power, and deliver us speedily for the sake of Your Name. Blessed is He who sanctifies His Name among the multitudes.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','transliteration','ah-tah hoo ahd sheh-loh neev-rah hah-oh-lahm, ah-tah hoo mee-sheh-neev-rah hah-oh-lahm, ah-tah hoo bah-oh-lahm hah-zeh ve-ah-tah hoo lah-oh-lahm hah-bah, kah-dehsh eht sheem-khah ahl mahk-dee-shey she-meh-khah ve-kah-dehsh eht sheem-khah be-oh-lah-meh-khah, oo-vee-shoo-ah-TE-khah tah-room ve-tahg-bee-ahh kahr-neh-noo le-mah-e-lah, ve-hoh-shee-eh-noo be-kah-rohv le-mah-ahn she-meh-khah. bah-rookh hah-me-kah-dehsh she-moh bah-rah-beem:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','he','אַתָּה הוּא יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם וּבָאָֽרֶץ וּבִשְׁמֵי הַשָּׁמַֽיִם הָעֶלְיוֹנִים, אֱמֶת אַתָּה הוּא רִאשׁוֹן וְאַתָּה הוּא אַחֲרוֹן וּמִבַּלְעָדֶֽיךָ אֵין אֱלֹהִים: קַבֵּץ נְפוּצוֹת קֺוֶֽיךָ מֵאַרְבַּע כַּנְ֒פוֹת הָאָֽרֶץ, יַכִּֽירוּ וְיֵדְ֒עוּ כָּל בָּאֵי עוֹלָם כִּי אַתָּה הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים לְבַדְּ֒ךָ עֶלְיוֹן לְכֹל מַמְלְ֒כוֹת הָאָֽרֶץ, אַתָּה עָשִֽׂיתָ אֶת הַשָּׁמַֽיִם וְאֶת הָאָֽרֶץ אֶת הַיָּם וְאֶת כָּל אֲשֶׁר בָּם וּמִי בְּכָל מַעֲשֵׂה יָדֶֽיךָ בָּעֶלְיוֹנִים אוֹ בַתַּחְתּוֹנִים שֶׁיֹּאמַר לְךָ מַה תַּעֲשֶׂה, ומַה תִּפְעָל אָבִינוּ שֶׁבַּשָּׁמַֽיִם חַי וְקַיָם עֲשֵׂה עִמָּֽנוּ צְדָקָה וָחֶֽסֶד בַּעֲבוּר שִׁמְךָ הַגָּדוֹל הַגִּבּוֹר וְהַנּוֹרָא שֶׁנִּקְרָא עָלֵֽינוּ וְקַיֶּם־לָֽנוּ יְהֺוָה אֶלֹהֵֽינוּ מַה־שֶּׁכָּתוּב, אֶת הַדָבָר שֶׁהִבְטַחְתָּֽנוּ עַל יְדֵי צְפַנְיָה חוֹזָךְ כָּאָמוּר, בָּעֵת הַהִיא אָבִיא אֶתְכֶם וּבָעֵת קַבְּ֒צִי אֶתְכֶם כִּי־אֶתֵּן אֶתְכֶם לְשֵׁם וְלִתְהִלָּה בְּכֹל עַמֵּי הָאָֽרֶץ בְּשׁוּבִי אֶת־שְׁבוּתֵיכֶם לְעֵינֵיכֶם אָמַר יְהֹוָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','en','You are Adonoy, our God, in heaven and on earth, and in the highest heavens. In truth, You are First, and You are Last. And besides You there is no God. Gather the scattered who hope in You from the four corners of the earth. Let all mankind recognize and know that You alone are the God over all the kingdoms of the earth. You made the heavens, the earth, the sea, and all that is in them. Who is there among all Your handiwork, among the heavenly or earthly creatures, that can say to You, "What are You doing?" and what are you making Our father in Heaven, living and eternal [One] deal graciously and kindly with us for the sake of your great name [which is] mighty and awesome which is called upon us and fulfill for us, Adonoy, our God that which is written: the promise you made to us through Zephaniah, your prophet as it is said: ‘At that time, I will bring you in and at that time, I will gather you: for I will make you renowned and praised among all the peoples of the earth, when I bring back your captivity before your eyes,'' said Adonoy.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-prayer','transliteration','ah-tah hoo ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo bah-shah-mah-yeem oo-vah-ah-rehts oo-veesh-mey hah-shah-mah-yeem hah-ehl-yoh-neem, eh-meht ah-tah hoo ree-shohn ve-ah-tah hoo ah-khah-rohn oo-mee-bahl-ah-dey-khah eyn eh-loh-heem: kah-behts ne-foo-tsoht koh-vey-khah meh-ahr-bah KAHN-foht hah-ah-rehts, yah-kee-roo ve-yeh-DE-oo kohl bah-ey oh-lahm kee ah-tah hoo hah-eh-loh-heem le-vah-DE-khah ehl-yohn le-khohl mahm-LE-khoht hah-ah-rehts, ah-tah ah-see-tah eht hah-shah-mah-yeem ve-eht hah-ah-rehts eht hah-yahm ve-eht kohl ah-shehr bahm oo-mee be-khohl mah-ah-seh yah-dey-khah bah-ehl-yoh-neem oh vah-tahkh-toh-neem sheh-yoh-mahr le-khah mahh tah-ah-seh, v-mahh teef-ahl ah-vee-noo sheh-bah-shah-mah-yeem khahy ve-kah-yahm ah-seh ee-mah-noo tse-dah-kah vah-kheh-sehd bah-ah-voor sheem-khah hah-gah-dohl hah-gee-bohr ve-hah-noh-rah sheh-neek-rah ah-ley-noo ve-kah-yehm lah-noo ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo mahh sheh-kah-toov, eht hah-dah-vahr sheh-heev-tahkh-tah-noo ahl ye-dey tse-fahn-yah khoh-zahkh kah-ah-moor, bah-eht hah-hee ah-vee eht-khehm oo-vah-eht kah-BE-tsee eht-khehm kee eh-tehn eht-khehm le-shehm ve-leet-hee-lah be-khohl ah-mey hah-ah-rehts be-shoo-vee eht she-voo-tey-khehm le-ey-ney-khehm ah-mahr ah-doh-NAI:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Prayer'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','אמרו חכמים (מנחות קי.) מאי דכתיב זאת תורת החטאת וזאת תורת האשם. כל העוסק בתורת חטאת כאילו הקריב חטאת וכל העוסק בתורת אשם כאילו הקריב אשם. ולכן אין די באמירת הפסוקים לבד אלא יתבונן בטעמי הקרבנות ובדיניהם כפי השגתו.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','The Talmud (Maseches Menachos 110a) states: Rabbi Isaac asked, "Why does it say (Leviticus 6:18; 7:1) This is the law of the sin-offering, this is the law of the guilt-offering? To teach us that when one studies the law of the sin-offering, it is considered as though he had actually brought it on the Altar, and when one studies the law of the guilt-offering, it is as though he actually brought it on the Altar." Rather than merely recite the following portions, study them and attempt to learn about the laws and significance of the various sacrifices.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','וַיְדַבֵּר יְהֹוָה אֶל־משֶׁה לֵּאמֹר: וְעָשִֽׂיתָ כִּיּוֹר נְחֽשֶׁת וְכַנּוֹ נְחֽשֶׁת לְרָחְצָה וְנָתַתָּ אֹתוֹ בֵּין־אֹֽהֶל מוֹעֵד וּבֵין הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ וְנָתַתָּ שָֽׁמָּה מָֽיִם: וְרָחֲצוּ אַהֲרֹן וּבָנָיו מִמֶּֽנּוּ אֶת־יְדֵיהֶם וְאֶת־רַגְלֵיהֶם: בְּבֹאָם אֶל־אֹֽהֶל מוֹעֵד יִרְחֲצוּ־מַֽיִם וְלֹא יָמֻֽתוּ אוֹ בְגִשְׁתָּם אֶל־הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ לְשָׁרֵת לְהַקְטִיר אִשֶּׁה לַיהוָֹה: וְרָחֲצוּ יְדֵיהֶם וְרַגְלֵיהֶם וְלֹא יָמֻֽתוּ וְהָיְ֒תָה לָהֶם חָק־עוֹלָם לוֹ וּלְזַרְעוֹ לְדֹרֹתָם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','(Exodus 30:17-21) And Adonoy spoke to Moses to say: Make a copper laver and a copper base, for washing; and place it between the Tent of Meeting and the Altar, and put water in it. Aaron and his sons will wash from it, their hands and their feet. Upon entering the Tent of Meeting they will wash with water that they not die, or whenever they approach the Altar to serve, to burn a fire-offering to Adonoy. They will wash their hands and feet that they not die; and this is for them a perpetual statute for him [Aaron], and his descendants for all their generations.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','vah-ye-dah-behr ah-doh-NAI ehl m-sheh leh-mohr: ve-ah-see-tah kee-yohr ne-kh-sheht ve-khah-noh ne-kh-sheht le-rah-khe-tsah ve-nah-tah-tah oh-toh beyn oh-hehl moh-ehd oo-veyn hah-meez-beh-ahkh ve-nah-tah-tah shah-mah mah-yeem: ve-rah-khah-tsoo ah-hah-rohn oo-vah-nahv mee-meh-noo eht ye-dey-hehm ve-eht rahg-ley-hehm: be-voh-ahm ehl oh-hehl moh-ehd yeer-khah-tsoo mah-yeem ve-loh yah-moo-too oh ve-geesh-tahm ehl hah-meez-beh-ahkh le-shah-reht le-hahk-teer ee-sheh lah-ah-doh-NAI: ve-rah-khah-tsoo ye-dey-hehm ve-rahg-ley-hehm ve-loh yah-moo-too ve-hah-YE-tah lah-hehm khohk oh-lahm loh oo-le-zahr-oh le-doh-roh-tahm:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','תרומת הדשן קודמת לכל עבודות לפיכך יאמר פרשת תרומת הדשן קודם פרשת התמיד. ואומרה אף שלא האיר היום.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','The following Scripture section describes the removal of the ashes which had accumulated on the Altar from the daily burnt-offering of the previous afternoon. This removal was performed prior to the daily morning burnt-offering. The passage below also describes the ritual of maintaining the wood pyres which were always burning on the Altar.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','וַיְדַבֵּר יְהֹוָה אֶל־משֶׁה לֵּאמֹר: צַו אֶת־אַהֲרֹן וְאֶת־בָּנָיו לֵאמֹר זֹאת תּוֹרַת הָעֹלָה הִוא הָעֹלָה עַל מוֹקְ֒דָה עַל־הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ כָּל־הַלַּֽיְלָה עַד־הַבֹּֽקֶר וְאֵשׁ הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ תּוּקַד בּוֹ: וְלָבַשׁ הַכֹּהֵן מִדּוֹ בַד וּמִכְנְ֒סֵי־בַד יִלְבַּשׁ עַל־בְּשָׂרוֹ וְהֵרִים אֶת־הַדֶּֽשֶׁן אֲשֶׁר תֹּאכַל הָאֵשׁ אֶת הָעֹלָה עַל־הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ וְשָׂמוֹ אֵֽצֶל הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ: וּפָשַׁט אֶת־בְּגָדָיו וְלָבַשׁ בְּגָדִים אֲחֵרִים וְהוֹצִיא אֶת־הַדֶּֽשֶׁן אֶל־מִחוּץ לַמַּחֲנֶה אֶל־מָקוֹם טָהוֹר: וְהָאֵשׁ עַל־הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ תּֽוּקַד־בּוֹ לֹא תִכְבֶּה וּבִעֵר עָלֶֽיהָ הַכֹּהֵן עֵצִים בַּבֹּֽקֶר בַּבֹּֽקֶר וְעָרַךְ עָלֶֽיהָ הָעֹלָה וְהִקְטִיר עָלֶֽיהָ חֶלְבֵי הַשְּׁ֒לָמִים: אֵשׁ תָּמִיד תּוּקַד עַל־הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ לֹא תִכְבֶּה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','(Leviticus 6:1) And Adonoy spoke to Moses to say: Command Aaron and his sons to say, this is the law of the burnt-offering. This is the burnt-offering [which must remain] on its pyre, upon the Altar all night, until morning, and the fire of the Altar will be kept burning on it. The Kohein will don his linen garment, and linen breeches upon his flesh, and he will remove the ashes when the fire consumes the burnt-offering on the Altar; and he will place them beside the Altar. He will remove his garments and don other garments, and carry the ashes outside the camp to an undefiled place. The fire upon the altar will be kept burning, it may not be extinguished. And the Kohein will burn wood on it every morning, and arrange on it the burnt-offering, and burn on it the fats of the peace-offerings. A constant fire will be kept burning on the Altar, it may not be extinguished.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','vah-ye-dah-behr ah-doh-NAI ehl m-sheh leh-mohr: tsahv eht ah-hah-rohn ve-eht bah-nahv leh-mohr zoht toh-raht hah-oh-lah heev hah-oh-lah ahl moh-KE-dah ahl hah-meez-beh-ahkh kohl hah-lah-ye-lah ahd hah-boh-kehr ve-ehsh hah-meez-beh-ahkh too-kahd boh: ve-lah-vahsh hah-koh-hehn mee-doh vahd oo-meekh-NE-sey VAHD yeel-bahsh ahl be-sah-roh ve-heh-reem eht hah-deh-shehn ah-shehr toh-khahl hah-ehsh eht hah-oh-lah ahl hah-meez-beh-ahkh ve-sah-moh eh-tsehl hah-meez-beh-ahkh: oo-fah-shaht eht be-gah-dahv ve-lah-vahsh be-gah-deem ah-kheh-reem ve-hoh-tsee eht hah-deh-shehn ehl mee-khoots lah-mah-khah-neh ehl mah-kohm tah-hohr: ve-hah-ehsh ahl hah-meez-beh-ahkh too-kahd boh loh teekh-beh oo-vee-ehr ah-ley-hah hah-koh-hehn eh-tseem bah-boh-kehr bah-boh-kehr ve-ah-rahkh ah-ley-hah hah-oh-lah ve-heek-teer ah-ley-hah khehl-vey hah-SHE-lah-meem: ehsh tah-meed too-kahd ahl hah-meez-beh-ahkh loh teekh-beh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','אומרים פרשת התמיד. ואם אי אפשר לאומרה בצבור יכול לאומרה בביתו ולחזור לקרותה עם הצבור. ויכוין בפעם השנייה כקורא בתורה (טור). יש מי שמצריך לעמוד בשעת אמירת הקרבנות, דהקרבת קרבן אינו אלא בעמידה (מגן אברהם).','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','The Tamid-offerings, two daily offerings of one lamb at a time, were offered once in the morning and once in the afternoon. The former was the first public-offering brought on the Altar each day. And the latter terminated the day''s offerings. These animals were purchased from the annual half-shekel gifts of the people and were offered on behalf of the entire Jewish People. Before reading this passage we offer a brief prayer.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','יש שאין אומרים ''יהי רצון'' בשבת ויום טוב','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','Some do not say the following prayer on Sabbath and Yom Tov.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','יְהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ, יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ, שֶׁתְּ֒רַחֵם עָלֵֽינוּ וְתִמְחָל לָֽנוּ עַל כָּל חַטֹּאתֵֽינוּ וּתְכַפֶּר לָֽנוּ אֶת כָּל עֲוֹנוֹתֵֽינוּ וְתִסְלַח לָֽנוּ עַל־כָּל פְּשָׁעֵֽינוּ וְשֶׁתִּבְנֶה בֵּית הַמִּקְדָּשׁ בִּמְהֵרָה בְיָמֵֽינוּ וְנַקְרִיב לְפָנֶֽיךָ קָרְבַּן הַתָּמִיד שֶׁיְּ֒כַפֵּר בַּעֲדֵֽנוּ כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתַֽבְתָּ עָלֵֽינוּ בְּתוֹרָתֶֽךָ, עַל יְדֵי משֶׁה עַבְדֶּֽךָ, מִפִּי כְבוֹדֶֽךָ כָּאָמוּר:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','May it be Your will, Adonoy, our God and God of our fathers, to have compassion on us, to forgive us all our sins, [done unknowingly], to atone all our iniquities, [done knowingly], to pardon all our [malicious] transgressions, and may You build the Holy Temple quickly, in our days, that we may offer, before You, the daily burnt-offering to atone for us, as You wrote for us in Your Torah by the hand of Moses, Your servant, from the mouth of Your Reverence, as it is said:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','ye-hee rah-tsohn mee-LE-fah-ney-khah, ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo veh-loh-hey ah-voh-tey-noo, sheh-TE-rah-khehm ah-ley-noo ve-teem-khahl lah-noo ahl kohl khah-toh-tey-noo oo-te-khah-pehr lah-noo eht kohl ah-voh-noh-tey-noo ve-tees-lahkh lah-noo ahl kohl pe-shah-ey-noo ve-sheh-teev-neh beyt hah-meek-dahsh beem-heh-rah ve-yah-mey-noo ve-nahk-reev le-fah-ney-khah kohr-bahn hah-tah-meed sheh-YE-khah-pehr bah-ah-deh-noo ke-moh sheh-kah-tah-ve-tah ah-ley-noo be-toh-rah-teh-khah, ahl ye-dey m-sheh ahv-deh-khah, mee-pee khe-voh-deh-khah kah-ah-moor:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','וַיְדַבֵּר יְהֹוָה אֶל־משֶׁה לֵּאמֹר: צַו אֶת־בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאָמַרְתָּ אֲלֵהֶם אֶת־קָרְבָּנִי לַחְמִי לְאִשַּׁי רֵֽיחַ נִיחֹחִי תִּשְׁמְ֒רוּ לְהַקְרִיב לִי בְּמוֹעֲדוֹ: וְאָמַרְתָּ לָהֶם זֶה הָאִשֶּׁה אֲשֶׁר תַּקְרִֽיבוּ לַיהוָֹה כְּבָשִׂים בְּנֵי־שָׁנָה תְמִימִם שְׁנַֽיִם לַיּוֹם עֹלָה תָמִיד: אֶת־הַכֶּֽבֶשׂ אֶחָד תַּעֲשֶׂה בַבֹּֽקֶר וְאֵת הַכֶּֽבֶשׂ הַשֵּׁנִי תַּעֲשֶׂה בֵּין הָעַרְבָּֽיִם: וַֽעֲשִׂירִית הָאֵיפָה סֹֽלֶת לְמִנְחָה בְּלוּלָה בְּשֶֽׁמֶן כָּתִית רְבִיעִת הַהִין: עֹלַת תָּמִיד הָעֲשֻׂיָה בְּהַר סִינַי לְרֵֽיחַ נִיחֹֽחַ אִשֶּׁה לַיהוָֹה: וְנִסְכּוֹ רְבִיעִת הַהִין לַכֶּֽבֶשׂ הָאֶחָד בַּקֹּֽדֶשׁ הַסֵּךְ נֶֽסֶךְ שֵׁכָר לַיהוָֹה: וְאֵת הַכֶּֽבֶשׂ הַשֵּׁנִי תַּעֲשֶׂה בֵּין הָעַרְבָּֽיִם כְּמִנְחַת הַבֹּֽקֶר וּכְנִסְכּוֹ תַּעֲשֶׂה אִשֵּׁה רֵֽיחַ נִיחֹֽחַ לַיהוָֹה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','(Numbers 28:1-8) And Adonoy spoke to Moses to say: Command the Children of Israel, and say to them: My offering, My food, to be consumed by My fires, a pleasing odor to Me, You shall be diligent to bring unto Me, at its fixed time. And you will say to them: This is the fire-offering that you will bring unto Adonoy: [male] lambs, in their first year, without blemish, two [of them] each day, as a constant burnt-offering. Offer one lamb in the morning, and the second lamb, offer in the afternoon. And a tenth of an ephah of fine flour as a meal-offering, mixed with oil of crushed [olives] measuring one-fourth of a hin. [This is] a constant burnt-offering as offered at Mount Sinai for a pleasing odor, a fire-offering to Adonoy. And its libation will be a fourth of a hin for the one lamb; in the Holy [Sanctuary] you will pour out a drink-offering of strong wine to Adonoy. And the second lamb you will offer in the afternoon; as the meal-offering of the morning [together] with its libation, you shall offer a fire-offering of pleasing odor to Adonoy.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','vah-ye-dah-behr ah-doh-NAI ehl m-sheh leh-mohr: tsahv eht be-ney yees-rah-ehl ve-ah-mahr-tah ah-leh-hehm eht kohr-bah-nee lahkh-mee le-ee-shahy rey-ahkh nee-khoh-khee teesh-ME-roo le-hahk-reev lee be-moh-ah-doh: ve-ah-mahr-tah lah-hehm zeh hah-ee-sheh ah-shehr tahk-ree-voo lah-ah-doh-NAI ke-vah-seem be-ney shah-nah te-mee-meem she-nah-yeem lah-yohm oh-lah tah-meed: eht hah-keh-vehs eh-khahd tah-ah-seh vah-boh-kehr ve-eht hah-keh-vehs hah-sheh-nee tah-ah-seh beyn hah-ahr-bah-yeem: vah-ah-see-reet hah-ey-fah soh-leht le-meen-khah be-loo-lah be-sheh-mehn kah-teet re-vee-eet hah-heen: oh-laht tah-meed hah-ah-soo-yah be-hahr see-nahy le-rey-ahkh nee-khoh-ahkh ee-sheh lah-ah-doh-NAI: ve-nees-koh re-vee-eet hah-heen lah-keh-vehs hah-eh-khahd bah-koh-dehsh hah-sehkh neh-sehkh sheh-khahr lah-ah-doh-NAI: ve-eht hah-keh-vehs hah-sheh-nee tah-ah-seh beyn hah-ahr-bah-yeem ke-meen-khaht hah-boh-kehr oo-khe-nees-koh tah-ah-seh ee-sheh rey-ahkh nee-khoh-ahkh lah-ah-doh-NAI:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','וְשָׁחַט אֹתוֹ עַל יֶֽרֶךְ הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ צָפֹֽנָה לִפְנֵי יְהֹוָה וְזָרְקוּ בְּנֵי אַהֲרֹן הַכֹּהֲנִים אֶת־דָּמוֹ עַל־הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ סָבִיב:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','(Leviticus 1:11) And he will slaughter it on the north side of the Altar, before Adonoy; and Aaron''s sons, the Kohanim, will sprinkle its blood all around the Altar.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','ve-shah-khaht oh-toh ahl yeh-rehkh hah-meez-beh-ahkh tsah-foh-nah leef-ney ah-doh-NAI ve-zah-re-koo be-ney ah-hah-rohn hah-koh-hah-neem eht dah-moh ahl hah-meez-beh-ahkh sah-veev:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','יְהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ, יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ, שֶׁתְּ֒הֵא אֲמִירָה זוּ, חֲשׁוּבָה וּמְקֻבֶּֽלֶת, וּמְרֻצָּה לְפָנֶֽיךָ, כְּאִלּוּ הִקְרַֽבְנוּ קָרְבַּן הַתָּמִיד בְּמוֹעֲדוֹ, וּבִמְ֒קוֹמוֹ וּכְהִלְכָתוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','May it be Your will, Adonoy, our God and God of our fathers, that this recitation be important, acceptable and desirable before You, as if we sacrificed the daily burnt-offering at its proper time, in its proper place and according to its laws.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','ye-hee rah-tsohn mee-LE-fah-ney-khah, ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo veh-loh-hey ah-voh-tey-noo, sheh-TE-heh ah-mee-rah zoo, khah-shoo-vah oo-me-koo-beh-leht, oo-me-roo-tsah le-fah-ney-khah, ke-ee-loo heek-rah-ve-noo kohr-bahn hah-tah-meed be-moh-ah-doh, oo-VEEM-koh-moh oo-khe-heel-khah-toh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','אַתָּה הוּא יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ שֶׁהִקְטִֽירוּ אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ לְפָנֶֽיךָ אֶת קְטֹֽרֶת הַסַּמִּים בִּזְמַן שֶׁבֵּית הַמִּקְדָּשׁ הָיָה קַיָּם כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוִּיתָ אוֹתָם עַל יְדֵי משֶׁה נְבִיאֶֽךָ כַּכָּתוּב בְּתוֹרָתֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','You are Adonoy, our God, before Whom our fathers burned the incense of spices when the Holy Temple was standing, as You commanded them by the hand of Moses Your prophet, as it is written in Your Torah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','ah-tah hoo ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo sheh-heek-tee-roo ah-voh-tey-noo le-fah-ney-khah eht ke-toh-reht hah-sah-meem beez-mahn sheh-beyt hah-meek-dahsh hah-yah kah-yahm kah-ah-shehr tsee-vee-tah oh-tahm ahl ye-dey m-sheh ne-vee-eh-khah kah-kah-toov be-toh-rah-teh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','וַיֹּֽאמֶר יְהֹוָה אֶל־משֶׁה קַח־לְךָ סַמִּים נָטָף וּשְׁחֵֽלֶת וְחֶלְבְּנָה סַמִּים וּלְבֹנָה זַכָּה בַּד בְּבַד יִהְיֶה: וְעָשִֽׂיתָ אֹתָהּ קְטֹֽרֶת רֹֽקַח מַעֲשֵׂה רוֹקֵֽחַ מְמֻלָּח טָהוֹר קֹֽדֶשׁ: וְשָׁחַקְתָּ מִמֶּֽנָּה הָדֵק וְנָתַתָּה מִמֶּֽנָּה לִפְנֵי הָעֵדֻת בְּאֹֽהֶל מוֹעֵד אֲשֶׁר אִוָּעֵד לְךָ שָֽׁמָּה קֹֽדֶשׁ קָדָשִׁים תִּהְיֶה לָכֶם: וְנֶאֱמַר','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','(Exodus 30:34-36) And Adonoy said to Moses, Take for yourself spices— stacte, onycha, and galbanum— spices, and pure frankincense, [they] shall be in equal weights. You will make it into incense, a compound mixed by a compounder, salted, undefiled, and holy. You will pulverize some of it very fine, and place it before the [Ark of] Testimony in the Tent of Meeting, where I will meet with you; it will be to you holy of holies." It is also written:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','vah-yoh-mehr ah-doh-NAI ehl m-sheh kahkh le-khah sah-meem nah-tahf oo-she-kheh-leht ve-khehl-be-nah sah-meem oo-le-voh-nah zah-kah bahd be-vahd yeeh-yeh: ve-ah-see-tah oh-tahh ke-toh-reht roh-kahkh mah-ah-seh roh-keh-ahkh me-moo-lahkh tah-hohr koh-dehsh: ve-shah-khahk-tah mee-meh-nah hah-dehk ve-nah-tah-tah mee-meh-nah leef-ney hah-eh-doot be-oh-hehl moh-ehd ah-shehr ee-vah-ehd le-khah shah-mah koh-dehsh kah-dah-sheem teeh-yeh lah-khehm: ve-neh-eh-mahr','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','וְהִקְטִיר עָלָיו אַהֲרֹן קְטֹֽרֶת סַמִּים בַּבֹּֽקֶר בַּבֹּֽקֶר בְּהֵיטִיבוֹ אֶת־הַנֵּרֹת יַקְטִירֶֽנָּה: וּבְהַעֲלֹת אַהֲרֹן אֶת־הַנֵּרֹת בֵּין הָֽעַרְבַּֽיִם יַקְטִירֶֽנָּה קְטֹֽרֶת תָּמִיד לִפְנֵי יְהֹוָה לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','(Exodus 30:7-8) And Aaron shall burn upon it [the Altar] incense of spices every morning; when he cleans the lamps he will burn it. And when Aaron lights the lamps in the afternoon, he will burn it; a constant incense-offering before Adonoy throughout your generations.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','ve-heek-teer ah-lahv ah-hah-rohn ke-toh-reht sah-meem bah-boh-kehr bah-boh-kehr be-hey-tee-voh eht hah-neh-roht yahk-tee-reh-nah: oo-ve-hah-ah-loht ah-hah-rohn eht hah-neh-roht beyn hah-ahr-bah-yeem yahk-tee-reh-nah ke-toh-reht tah-meed leef-ney ah-doh-NAI le-doh-roh-tey-khehm:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','תָּנוּ רַבָּנָן פִּטּוּם הַקְּ֒טֹֽרֶת כֵּיצַד שְׁלֹש מֵאוֹת וְשִׁשִּׁים וּשְׁמוֹנָה מָנִים הָיוּ בָהּ, שְׁלֹש מֵאוֹת וְשִׁשִּׁים וַחֲמִשָּׁה כְּמִנְיַן יְמוֹת הַחַמָּה מָנֶה לְכָל יוֹם, פְּרַס בַּשַּׁחֲרִית וּפְרַס בֵּין הָעַרְבָּֽיִם, וּשְׁלשָׁה מָנִים יְתֵרִים שֶׁמֵּהֶם מַכְנִיס כֹּהֵן גָּדוֹל מְלֹא חָפְנָיו בְּיוֹם הַכִּפּוּרִים, וּמַחֲזִירָן לְמַכְתֶּֽשֶׁת בְּעֶֽרֶב יוֹם הַכִּפּוּרִים, וְשׁוֹחֲקָן יָפֶה יָפֶה כְּדֵי שֶׁתְּ֒הֵא דַקָּה מִן הַדַּקָּה, וְאַחַד עָשָׂר סַמָּנִים הָֽיוּ בָהּ, וְאֵֽלּוּ הֵן הַצֳּרִי וְהַצִּפֹּֽרֶן הַחֶלְבְּנָה וְהַלְּ֒בוֹנָה מִשְׁקַל שִׁבְעִים שִׁבְעִים מָנֶה, מוֹר וּקְצִיעָה שִׁבֹּֽלֶת נֵרְדְּ וְכַרְכֹּם מִשְׁקַל שִׁשָּׁה עָשָׂר שִׁשָּׁה עָשָׂר מָנֶה, הַקּשְׁטְ שְׁנֵים עָשָׂר וְקִלּוּפָה שְׁלשָׁה וְקִנָּמוֹן תִּשְׁעָה, בֹּרִית כַּרְשִׁינָה תִּשְׁעָה קַבִּין, יֵין קַפְרִיסִין סְאִין תְּלָתָא וְקַבִּין תְּלָתָא, וְאִם אֵין לוֹ יֵין קַפְרִיסִין מֵבִיא חֲמַר חִוַּרְיָן עַתִּיק, מֶֽלַח סְדוֹמִית רֹֽבַע הַקָּב, מַעֲלֶה עָשָׁן כָּל שֶׁהוּא, רַבִּי נָתָן הַבַּבְלִי אוֹמֵר אַף כִּפַּת הַיַּרְדֵּן כָּל שֶׁהוּא, וְאִם נָֽתַן בָּהּ דְּבַשׁ פְּסָלָהּ וְאִם חִסַּר אַחַת מִכָּל סַמָּנֶֽיהָ חַיָּב מִיתָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','(Maseches Kreisos 6a; Jerusalem Talmud, Maseches Yoma 4:5) The Rabbis taught: How was the incense compounded? Three hundred and sixty-eight manim were comprised therein, three hundred and sixty-five corresponding to the number of days in the solar year, one maneh for each day— half in the morning and half in the afternoon. From the three remaining manim the Kohein Gadol brought two handfuls [into the Holy of Holies] on Yom Kippur; [for which purpose] they were put back into the mortar on the eve of Yom Kippur, and ground [again] very thoroughly, in order to make them very fine. Eleven kinds of spices were used for it. They were: 1) balm, 2) onycha, 3) galbanum, 4) frankincense— by weight, seventy maneh of each; 5) myrrh, 6) cassia, 7) spikenard and 8) saffron— in weight sixteen maneh of each; 9) twelve maneh of costus, 10) three of aromatic bark, and 11) nine of cinnamon. [Also used in the incense compound were:] Nine kabin of Carshina lye, Cyprus wine [measuring] three s''in and three kabin— if he had no Cyprus wine, he could use strong white wine— a fourth of a kab of Sodom salt, and a minute quantity of maaleh ashan. Rabbi Nosson of Babylonia says, Jordan amber was added of a minute quantity, and if one added honey, it (the incense) became unfit; and if one omitted any of its spices he was liable to the death penalty."','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','tah-noo rah-bah-nahn pee-toom hah-KE-toh-reht key-tsahd she-lohsh meh-oht ve-shee-sheem oo-she-moh-nah mah-neem hah-yoo vahh, she-lohsh meh-oht ve-shee-sheem vah-khah-mee-shah ke-meen-yahn ye-moht hah-khah-mah mah-neh le-khohl yohm, pe-rahs bah-shah-khah-reet oo-fe-rahs beyn hah-ahr-bah-yeem, oo-she-l-shah mah-neem ye-teh-reem sheh-meh-hehm mahkh-nees koh-hehn gah-dohl me-loh khohf-nahv be-yohm hah-kee-poo-reem, oo-mah-khah-zee-rahn le-mahkh-teh-sheht be-eh-rehv yohm hah-kee-poo-reem, ve-shoh-khah-kahn yah-feh yah-feh ke-dey sheh-TE-heh dah-kah meen hah-dah-kah, ve-ah-khahd ah-sahr sah-mah-neem hah-yoo vahh, ve-eh-loo hehn hah-tsoh-ree ve-hah-tsee-poh-rehn hah-khehl-be-nah ve-hah-LE-voh-nah meesh-kahl sheev-eem sheev-eem mah-neh, mohr oo-ke-tsee-ah shee-boh-leht nehrd ve-khahr-kohm meesh-kahl shee-shah ah-sahr shee-shah ah-sahr mah-neh, hahksht she-neym ah-sahr ve-kee-loo-fah she-l-shah ve-kee-nah-mohn teesh-ah, boh-reet kahr-shee-nah teesh-ah kah-been, yeyn kahf-ree-seen se-een te-lah-tah ve-kah-been te-lah-tah, ve-eem eyn loh yeyn kahf-ree-seen meh-vee khah-mahr khee-vahr-yahn ah-teek, meh-lahkh se-doh-meet roh-vah hah-kahv, mah-ah-leh ah-shahn kohl sheh-hoo, rah-bee nah-tahn hah-bahv-lee oh-mehr ahf kee-paht hah-yahr-dehn kohl sheh-hoo, ve-eem nah-tahn bahh de-vahsh pe-sah-lahh ve-eem khee-sahr ah-khaht mee-kohl sah-mah-ney-hah khah-yahv mee-tah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','רַבָּן שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן גַּמְלִיאֵל אוֹמֵר הַצֳּרִי אֵינוֹ אֶלָּא שְׂרָף הַנּוֹטֵף מֵעֲצֵי הַקְּ֒טָף, בֹּרִית כַּרְשִׁינָה שֶׁשָׁפִין בָּה אֶת הַצִפֹּרֶן כִּדֵי שֶׁתְּ֒הֵא נָאָה יֵין קַפְרִיסִין שֶׁשׁוֹרִין בּוֹ אֶת הַצִפֹּרֶן כְּדֵי שֶׁתְּ֒הֵא עַזָּה, וַהֲלֹא מֵי רַגְלַֽיִם יָפִין לָהּ אֶלָּא שֶׁאֵין מַכְנִיסִין מֵי רַגְלַֽיִם בַּמִּקְדָּשׁ מִפְּנֵי הַכָּבוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','Rabbi Shimon ben Gamliel says: The balm is nothing but sap which drips from the balsam tree. the lye of Carshina was used for rubbing the onycha in order to refine its appearance. The Cyprus wine was used to soak the onycha to give it a pungent odor. Though the water of Raglayim was well suited for that purpose, they did not bring the water of Raglayim into the Temple because it would be disrespectful.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','rah-bahn sheem-ohn behn gahm-lee-ehl oh-mehr hah-tsoh-ree ey-noh eh-lah se-rahf hah-noh-tehf meh-ah-tsey hah-KE-tahf, boh-reet kahr-shee-nah sheh-shah-feen bah eht hah-tsee-poh-rehn kee-dey sheh-TE-heh nah-ah yeyn kahf-ree-seen sheh-shoh-reen boh eht hah-tsee-poh-rehn ke-dey sheh-TE-heh ah-zah, vah-hah-loh mey rahg-lah-yeem yah-feen lahh eh-lah sheh-eyn mahkh-nee-seen mey rahg-lah-yeem bah-meek-dahsh mee-pe-ney hah-kah-vohd:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','תַּנְיָא רַבִּי נָתָן אוֹמֵר כְּשֶׁהוּא שׁוֹחֵק אוֹמֵר הָדֵק הֵיטֵב הֵיטֵב הָדֵק מִפְּ֒נֵי שֶׁהַקּוֹל יָפֶה לַבְּ֒שָׂמִים, פִּטְּ֒מָהּ לַחֲצָאִין כְּשֵׁרָה לִשְׁלִישׁ וְלִרְבִֽיעַ לֹא שָׁמַֽעְנוּ: אָמַר רַבִּי יְהוּדָה זֶה הַכְּ֒לָל אִם כְּמִדָּתָהּ כְּשֵׁרָה לַחֲצָאִין וְאִם חִסַּר אַחַת מִכָּל סַמָּנֶֽיהָ חַיָּב מִיתָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','It was taught in a Boraysa: Rabbi Nosson says, While [the Kohein] ground [the incense] he would say, ‘Hodeik heiteiv, heiteiv hodeik,'' because the sound is good for the spices. If half the quantity of incense was prepared it was acceptable, but if only a third or a fourth [of it was prepared] we have not heard [whether it was acceptable."] Rabbi Yehuda said, This is the general rule: If [it was prepared with all its ingredients] in the correct proportion, it is acceptable even if only half was prepared; but if he left out any of its spices, he was liable for the death penalty.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','tahn-yah rah-bee nah-tahn oh-mehr ke-sheh-hoo shoh-khehk oh-mehr hah-dehk hey-tehv hey-tehv hah-dehk mee-PE-ney sheh-hah-kohl yah-feh lah-BE-sah-meem, pee-TE-mahh lah-khah-tsah-een ke-sheh-rah leesh-leesh ve-leer-vee-ah loh shah-mah-e-noo: ah-mahr rah-bee ye-hoo-dah zeh hah-KE-lahl eem ke-mee-dah-tahh ke-sheh-rah lah-khah-tsah-een ve-eem khee-sahr ah-khaht mee-kohl sah-mah-ney-hah khah-yahv mee-tah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','תַּנְיָא בַּר קַפָּרָא אוֹמֵר אַחַת לְשִׁשִּׁים אוֹ לְשִׁבְעִים שָׁנָה הָיְ֒תָה בָאָה שֶׁל שִׁירַֽיִם לַחֲצָאִין: וְעוֹד תָּנֵי בַּר קַפָּרָא אִלּוּ הָיָה נוֹתֵן בָּהּ קוֹרְ֒טוֹב שֶׁל דְּבַשׁ אֵין אָדָם יָכוֹל לַעֲמֹד מִפְּ֒נֵי רֵיחָהּ וְלָֽמָּה אֵין מְעָרְ֒בִין בָּהּ דְּבַשׁ מִפְּ֒נֵי שֶׁהַתּוֹרָה אָמְ֒רָה כִּי כָל־שְׂאֹר וְכָל־דְּבַשׁ לֹא־תַקְטִֽירוּ מִמֶּֽנּוּ אִשֶּׁה לַיהוָֹה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','It was taught in a Boraysa: Bar Kappara says, Once in sixty or seventy years the accumulated surplus was sufficient to provide half [the yearly quantity of incense."] Bar Kappara also taught, If he would have put into it a minute quantity of honey, no one could have withstood [resisted] the scent. Why was no honey mixed with it? Because the Torah says, (Leviticus 2:11) For any leaven or honey, do not burn from them, [as] a fire-offering to Adonoy.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:16:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','tahn-yah bahr kah-pah-rah oh-mehr ah-khaht le-shee-sheem oh le-sheev-eem shah-nah hah-YE-tah vah-ah shehl shee-rah-yeem lah-khah-tsah-een: ve-ohd tah-ney bahr kah-pah-rah ee-loo hah-yah noh-tehn bahh koh-RE-tohv shehl de-vahsh eyn ah-dahm yah-khohl lah-ah-mohd mee-PE-ney rey-khahh ve-lah-mah eyn me-ah-RE-veen bahh de-vahsh mee-PE-ney sheh-hah-toh-rah ah-ME-rah kee khohl se-ohr ve-khohl de-vahsh loh tahk-tee-roo mee-meh-noo ee-sheh lah-ah-doh-NAI:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','אומר ג'' פעמים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','Recite each of these verses three times:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת עִמָּֽנוּ מִשְׂגַּב־לָֽנוּ אֱלֹהֵי יַעֲקֹב סֶֽלָה: יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת אַשְׁרֵי אָדָם בֹּטֵֽחַ בָּךְ: יְהֹוָה הוֹשִֽׁיעָה הַמֶּֽלֶךְ יַעֲנֵֽנוּ בְיוֹם־קָרְאֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','Adonoy of Hosts is with us, a stronghold for us is the God of Jacob, Selah! Adonoy of Hosts, fortunate is the man who trusts in You. Adonoy, deliver [us]! The King will answer us on the day we call.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:18:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','ah-doh-NAI tse-vah-oht ee-mah-noo mees-gahv lah-noo eh-loh-hey yah-ah-kohv seh-lah: ah-doh-NAI tse-vah-oht ahsh-rey ah-dahm boh-teh-ahkh bahkh: ah-doh-NAI hoh-shee-ah hah-meh-lehkh yah-ah-neh-noo ve-yohm kah-re-eh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','אַתָּה סֵֽתֶר לִי מִצַּר תִּצְּ֒רֵֽנִי רָנֵּי פַלֵּט תְּסוֹבְ֒בֵֽנִי סֶֽלָה: וְעָרְ֒בָה לַיהוָֹה מִנְחַת יְהוּדָה וִירוּשָׁלָֽםִ כִּימֵי עוֹלָם וּכְשָׁנִים קַדְמֹנִיּוֹת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','You are my shelter; from distress You preserve me; with glad song of rescue, You envelop me, Selah! Let Adonoy be pleased with the offerings of Judah and Jerusalem, as in the days of old and in earlier years.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','ah-tah seh-tehr lee mee-tsahr tee-TSE-reh-nee rah-ney fah-leht te-soh-VE-veh-nee seh-lah: ve-ah-RE-vah lah-ah-doh-NAI meen-khaht ye-hoo-dah vee-roo-shah-lah-mee kee-mey oh-lahm oo-khe-shah-neem kahd-moh-nee-yoht:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','אַבַּיֵּי הֲוָה מְסַדֵּר סֵֽדֶר הַמַּעֲרָכָה מִשְּׁ֒מָא דִגְמָרָא וְאַלִּבָּא דְאַבָּא שָׁאוּל, מַעֲרָכָה גְדוֹלָה קוֹדֶֽמֶת לְמַעֲרָכָה שְׁנִיָּה שֶׁל קְטֹֽרֶת, וּמַעֲרָכָה שְׁנִיָּה שֶׁל קְטֹֽרֶת קוֹדֶֽמֶת לְסִדּוּר שְׁנֵי גִזְרֵי עֵצִים, וְסִדּוּר שְׁנֵי גִזְרֵי עֵצִים קֽוֹדֶם לְדִשּׁוּן מִזְבֵּֽחַ הַפְּ֒נִימִי, וְדִשּׁוּן מִזְבֵּֽחַ הַפְּ֒נִימִי קֽוֹדֶם לְהַטָּבַת חָמֵשׁ נֵרוֹת, וְהַטָּבַת חָמֵשׁ נֵרוֹת קוֹדֶֽמֶת לְדַם הַתָּמִיד, וְדַם הַתָּמִיד קֽוֹדֶם לְהַטָּבַת שְׁתֵּי נֵרוֹת, וְהַטָּבַת שְׁתֵּי נֵרוֹת קוֹדֶֽמֶת לִקְטֹֽרֶת, וּקְטֹֽרֶת קוֹדֶֽמֶת לְאֵבָרִים, וְאֵבָרִים לְמִנְחָה, וּמִנְחָה לַחֲבִתִּין, וַחֲבִתִּין לִנְסָכִין, וּנְסָכִין לְמוּסָפִין, וּמוּסָפִין לְבָזִיכִין, וּבָזִיכִין קוֹדְ֒מִין לְתָמִיד שֶׁל בֵּין הָעַרְבָּֽיִם, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר וְעָרַךְ עָלֶֽיהָ הָעֹלָה וְהִקְטִיר עָלֶֽיהָ חֶלְבֵי הַשְּׁ֒לָמִים, עָלֶֽיהָ הַשְׁלֵם כָּל הַקָּרְבָּנוֹת כֻּלָּם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','Abbaye listed the order of the [daily] Altar service based on tradition, and according to the opinion of Abba Shaul: the [arranging on the Altar of the] great Pyre precedes the second pyre [from which live coals are taken] for the incense-offering; the second pyre of the incense-offering [is arranged] before the placement of two logs [on the large pyre] the placement of the two logs precedes the removal of the ashes from the inner Altar; the removal of the ashes from the inner Altar precedes the cleaning of five lamps [of the Menorah]; the cleaning of the five lamps precedes [sprinkling] the blood of the daily-offering; the blood of the daily-offering precedes the cleaning of the [remaining] two lamps; the cleaning of the two lamps precedes the incense-offering; the incense-offering precedes [burning] the limbs [of the daily-offering]; burning the limbs [precedes] the meal-offering; the meal-offering [precedes] the baking-pan-offering; the baking-pan-offerings [precede] the wine libations; the wine-libations [precede] the Mussaf-offering; the Mussaf-offering [precedes] the two bowls of frankincense; and the two bowls of frankincense precede the daily afternoon-offering, for it is said, (Leviticus 6:5) And [the Kohein] shall arrange on it the burnt-offering, and burn on it the fat of the peace-offerings. Therewith complete all the offerings [of the day.]','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:20:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','ah-bah-yey hah-vah me-sah-dehr seh-dehr hah-mah-ah-rah-khah mee-SHE-mah deeg-mah-rah ve-ah-lee-bah de-ah-bah shah-ool, mah-ah-rah-khah ge-doh-lah koh-deh-meht le-mah-ah-rah-khah she-nee-yah shehl ke-toh-reht, oo-mah-ah-rah-khah she-nee-yah shehl ke-toh-reht koh-deh-meht le-see-door she-ney geez-rey eh-tseem, ve-see-door she-ney geez-rey eh-tseem koh-dehm le-dee-shoon meez-beh-ahkh hah-PE-nee-mee, ve-dee-shoon meez-beh-ahkh hah-PE-nee-mee koh-dehm le-hah-tah-vaht khah-mehsh neh-roht, ve-hah-tah-vaht khah-mehsh neh-roht koh-deh-meht le-dahm hah-tah-meed, ve-dahm hah-tah-meed koh-dehm le-hah-tah-vaht she-tey neh-roht, ve-hah-tah-vaht she-tey neh-roht koh-deh-meht leek-toh-reht, oo-ke-toh-reht koh-deh-meht le-eh-vah-reem, ve-eh-vah-reem le-meen-khah, oo-meen-khah lah-khah-vee-teen, vah-khah-vee-teen leen-sah-kheen, oo-ne-sah-kheen le-moo-sah-feen, oo-moo-sah-feen le-vah-zee-kheen, oo-vah-zee-kheen koh-DE-meen le-tah-meed shehl beyn hah-ahr-bah-yeem, sheh-neh-eh-mahr ve-ah-rahkh ah-ley-hah hah-oh-lah ve-heek-teer ah-ley-hah khehl-vey hah-SHE-lah-meem, ah-ley-hah hahsh-lehm kohl hah-kah-re-bah-noht koo-lahm:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','ואח"כ יאמר תפלת רבי נחוניא בן הקנה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','The following is the prayer of Rabbi Nechunya ben Hakanah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','אָֽנָּא בְּכֹֽחַ גְּדֻלַּת יְמִינְ֒ךָ תַּתִּיר צְרוּרָה: קַבֵּל רִנַּת עַמְּ֒ךָ שַׂגְּ֒בֵֽנוּ טַהֲרֵֽנוּ נוֹרָא: נָא גִבּוֹר דּוֹרְ֒שֵׁי יִחוּדְ֒ךָ כְּבָבַת שָׁמְ֒רֵם: בָּרְ֒כֵם טַהֲרֵם רַחֲמֵם צִדְקָתְ֒ךָ תָּמִיד גָּמְ֒לֵם: חֲסִין קָדוֹשׁ בְּרֹב טוּבְ֒ךָ נַהֵל עֲדָתֶֽךָ: יָחִיד גֵּאֶה לְעַמְּ֒ךָ פְּנֵה, זוֹכְ֒רֵי קְדֻשָּׁתֶֽךָ: שַׁוְעָתֵֽנוּ קַבֵּל וּשְׁמַע צַעֲקָתֵֽנוּ יוֹדֵֽעַ תַּעֲלוּמוֹת: בָּרוּךְ שֵׁם כְּבוֹד מַלְכוּתוֹ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','Please, by the force of Your great right hand, release the bound one. Accept the prayer of Your people; strengthen us, purify us, Awesome One! Please! Mighty One, those who seek Your Unity, preserve them like the pupil [of Your eye]. Bless them, purify them, have compassion on them; Your benevolent righteousness [may You] always bestow upon them. Mighty, Holy One, in Your abundant goodness, lead Your community. Unique One, Exalted, turn to Your people who are mindful of Your holiness. Accept our prayer and hear our cry, [You] Who knows hidden thoughts. Blessed [is His] Name, Whose glorious kingdom is forever and ever.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:22:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','ah-nah be-khoh-ahkh ge-doo-laht ye-mee-NE-khah tah-teer tse-roo-rah: kah-behl ree-naht ah-ME-khah sah-GE-veh-noo tah-hah-reh-noo noh-rah: nah gee-bohr doh-RE-shey yee-khoo-DE-khah ke-vah-vaht shah-ME-rehm: bah-RE-khehm tah-hah-rehm rah-khah-mehm tseed-kah-TE-khah tah-meed gah-ME-lehm: khah-seen kah-dohsh be-rohv too-VE-khah nah-hehl ah-dah-teh-khah: yah-kheed geh-eh le-ah-ME-khah pe-neh, zoh-KHE-rey ke-doo-shah-teh-khah: shahv-ah-teh-noo kah-behl oo-she-mah tsah-ah-kah-teh-noo yoh-deh-ah tah-ah-loo-moht: bah-rookh shehm ke-vohd mahl-khoo-toh le-oh-lahm vah-ehd:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','רִבּוֹן הָעוֹלָמִים אַתָּה צִוִּיתָֽנוּ לְהַקְרִיב קָרְבַּן הַתָּמִיד בְּמוֹעֲדוֹ וְלִהְיוֹת כֹּהֲנִים בַּעֲבוֹדָתָם וּלְוִיִּם בְּדוּכָנָם וְיִשְׂרָאֵל בְּמַעֲמָדָם, וְעַתָּה בַּעֲוֹנוֹתֵֽינוּ חָרַב בֵּית הַמִּקְדָּשׁ וּבֻטַּל הַתָּמִיד וְאֵין לָֽנוּ לֹא כֹהֵן בַּעֲבוֹדָתוֹ וְלֹא לֵוִי בְּדוּכָנוֹ וְלֹא יִשְׂרָאֵל בְּמַעֲמָדוֹ. לָכֵן יְהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ שֶׁיְּ֒הֵא שִֽׂיחַ שִׂפְתוֹתֵֽינוּ חָשׁוּב וּמְקֻבָּל וּמְרֻצֶּה לְפָנֶֽיךָ כְּאִלּוּ הִקְרַֽבְנוּ קָרְבַּן הַתָּמִיד בְּמוֹעֲדוֹ וְעָמַֽדְנוּ עַל מַעֲמָדוֹ. כְּמָה שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר וּנְשַׁלְּ֒מָה פָרִים שְׂפָתֵֽינוּ: וְנֶאֶמַר וְשָׁחַט אֹתוֹ עַל יֶֽרֶךְ הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ צָפֹֽנָה לִפְנֵי יְהֹוָה וְזָרְ֒קוּ בְּנֵי אַהֲרֹן הַכֹּהֲנִים אֶת־דָּמוֹ עַל־הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ סָבִיב: וְנֶאֱמַר זֹאת הַתּוֹרָה לָעֹלָה לַמִּנְחָה וְלַחַטָּאת וְלָאָשָׁם וְלַמִּלּוּאִים וּלְזֶֽבַח הַשְּׁ֒לָמִים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','Master of the Worlds, You commanded us to bring the Daily offering at its appointed time; and have the Kohanim perform their service, and the Levites [sing and play music] on the platform, and the Israelites [attend] at their Ma''amad. And now, because of our sins, the Holy Temple is destroyed, and the Daily offering discontinued; we have neither a Kohein at his service, nor a Levite on his platform, nor an Israelite at his Ma''amad. Therefore let it be Your will Adonoy, our God, and God of our fathers, that the prayer of our lips be considered, and accepted and regarded favorably before You, as if we had offered the Daily offering at its appointed time, and stood in attendance at its service, as it has been said, Let the offering of our lips replace bullocks. And it is said, And he will slaughter it on the north side of the Altar, before Adonoy; and Aaron''s sons, the Kohanim, will sprinkle its blood all around the Altar. And it is said, This is the law of the burnt-offering, the meal-offering, the sin-offering, the guilt-offering, the inauguration-offerings and the peace-offerings.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:23:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','ree-bohn hah-oh-lah-meem ah-tah tsee-vee-tah-noo le-hahk-reev kohr-bahn hah-tah-meed be-moh-ah-doh ve-leeh-yoht koh-hah-neem bah-ah-voh-dah-tahm oo-le-vee-yeem be-doo-khah-nahm ve-yees-rah-ehl be-mah-ah-mah-dahm, ve-ah-tah bah-ah-voh-noh-tey-noo khah-rahv beyt hah-meek-dahsh oo-voo-tahl hah-tah-meed ve-eyn lah-noo loh khoh-hehn bah-ah-voh-dah-toh ve-loh leh-vee be-doo-khah-noh ve-loh yees-rah-ehl be-mah-ah-mah-doh. lah-khehn ye-hee rah-tsohn mee-LE-fah-ney-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo veh-loh-hey ah-voh-tey-noo sheh-YE-heh see-ahkh seef-toh-tey-noo khah-shoov oo-me-koo-bahl oo-me-roo-tseh le-fah-ney-khah ke-ee-loo heek-rah-ve-noo kohr-bahn hah-tah-meed be-moh-ah-doh ve-ah-mah-de-noo ahl mah-ah-mah-doh. ke-mah sheh-neh-eh-mahr oo-ne-shah-LE-mah fah-reem se-fah-tey-noo: ve-neh-eh-mahr ve-shah-khaht oh-toh ahl yeh-rehkh hah-meez-beh-ahkh tsah-foh-nah leef-ney ah-doh-NAI ve-zah-RE-koo be-ney ah-hah-rohn hah-koh-hah-neem eht dah-moh ahl hah-meez-beh-ahkh sah-veev: ve-neh-eh-mahr zoht hah-toh-rah lah-oh-lah lah-meen-khah ve-lah-khah-taht ve-lah-ah-shahm ve-lah-mee-loo-eem oo-le-zeh-vahkh hah-SHE-lah-meem:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','בראש חודש מוסיפים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','On Rosh Chodesh add:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:25:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','וּבְרָאשֵׁי חָדְשֵׁיכֶם תַּקְרִֽיבוּ עֹלָה לַיהוָֹה פָּרִים בְּנֵי־בָקָר שְׁנַֽיִם וְאַֽיִל אֶחָד כְּבָשִׂים בְּנֵי־שָׁנָה שִׁבְעָה תְּמִימִם: וּשְׁלשָׁה עֶשְׂרֹנִים סֹֽלֶת מִנְחָה בְּלוּלָה בַשֶּֽׁמֶן לַפָּר הָאֶחָד וּשְׁ֒נֵי עֶשְׂרֹנִים סֹֽלֶת מִנְחָה בְּלוּלָה בַשֶּֽׁמֶן לָאַֽיִל הָאֶחָד: וְעִשָּׂרֹן עִשָּׂרוֹן סֹֽלֶת מִנְחָה בְּלוּלָה בַשֶּֽׁמֶן לַכֶּֽבֶשׂ הָאֶחָד עֹלָה רֵֽיחַ נִיחֹֽחַ אִשֶּׁה לַיהוָֹה: וְנִסְכֵּיהֶם חֲצִי הַהִין יִהְיֶה לַפָּר וּשְׁלִישִׁת הַהִין לָאַֽיִל וּרְבִיעִת הַהִין לַכֶּֽבֶשׂ יָֽיִן זֹאת עֹלַת חֹֽדֶשׁ בְּחָדְשׁוֹ לְחָדְשֵׁי הַשָּׁנָה: וּשְׂעִיר עִזִּים אֶחָד לְחַטָּאת לַיהוָֹה עַל עֹלַת הַתָּמִיד יֵעָשֶׂה וְנִסְכּוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:25:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','And on your Rosh Chodesh days you shall bring a burnt-offering to Adonoy. Two young bullocks, one ram, seven male yearling lambs without blemish. And three-tenths [of an epha] of fine flour for a meal-offering mixed with the [olive] oil, for each bullock; and two-tenths of fine flour for a meal-offering mixed with the [olive] oil, for the one ram. And one-tenth of fine flour each for a meal-offering mixed with the [olive] oil, for each lamb; a burnt-offering of pleasing savor, a fire-offering to Adonoy. Their libations shall be: half a hin for [each] bullock, a third of a hin for the ram, and a fourth of a hin for each lamb—wine; this is the burnt-offering of Rosh Chodesh, each Rosh Chodesh, for [all] the Rosh Chodesh days of the year. And one he-goat for a sin-offeing to Adonoy, in addition to the daily burnt-offering and its libation.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:25:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','oo-ve-rah-shey khohd-shey-khehm tahk-ree-voo oh-lah lah-ah-doh-NAI pah-reem be-ney vah-kahr she-nah-yeem ve-ah-yeel eh-khahd ke-vah-seem be-ney shah-nah sheev-ah te-mee-meem: oo-she-l-shah ehs-roh-neem soh-leht meen-khah be-loo-lah vah-sheh-mehn lah-pahr hah-eh-khahd oo-SHE-ney ehs-roh-neem soh-leht meen-khah be-loo-lah vah-sheh-mehn lah-ah-yeel hah-eh-khahd: ve-ee-sah-rohn ee-sah-rohn soh-leht meen-khah be-loo-lah vah-sheh-mehn lah-keh-vehs hah-eh-khahd oh-lah rey-ahkh nee-khoh-ahkh ee-sheh lah-ah-doh-NAI: ve-nees-key-hehm khah-tsee hah-heen yeeh-yeh lah-pahr oo-she-lee-sheet hah-heen lah-ah-yeel oo-re-vee-eet hah-heen lah-keh-vehs yah-yeen zoht oh-laht khoh-dehsh be-khohd-shoh le-khohd-shey hah-shah-nah: oo-se-eer ee-zeem eh-khahd le-khah-taht lah-ah-doh-NAI ahl oh-laht hah-tah-meed yeh-ah-seh ve-nees-koh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:26:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','קבעו לשנות אחר פרשת התמיד פרק איזהו מקומן וברייתא דרבי ישמעאל כדי שיזכה כל אדם ללמוד בכל יום מקרא משנה וגמרא. דברייתא דרבי ישמעאל הוי במקום גמרא, שהמדרש כגמרא: (שו"ע או"ח נ, א)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:26:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','The following sequence of Mishnayos and the selection from Sifra "Rabbi Yishmael Says," were inserted after the Scriptural selections dealing with daily-offerings in order to give every Jew the opportunity to study/recite daily, the minimum of selections from Scripture, Mishnah, and Talmud. Even though Sifra is not actually a Talmudic tractate, it is a Tanaitic expansion of Mishnah. (See Shulchan Aruch, Orach Chaim 50:1).','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:27:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','הא דתקינו לשנות פרק ''איזהו מקומן'', לפי שאין בכל אותו פרק מחלוקת והיא משנה ברורה למשה מסיני. (ב"י)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:27:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','(The following are Mishnayos found in the fifth chapter of Maseches Zevachim.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:28:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','משנה א אֵיזֶהוּ מְקוֹמָן שֶׁל זְבָחִים קָדְשֵׁי קָדָשִׁים שְׁחִיטָתָן בַּצָּפוֹן פָּר וְשָׂעִיר שֶׁל יוֹם הַכִּפּוּרִים שְׁחִיטָתָן בַּצָּפוֹן וְקִבּוּל דָּמָן בִּכְלִי שָׁרֵת בַּצָּפוֹן וְדָמָן טָעוּן הַזָּיָה עַל בֵּין הַבַּדִּים וְעַל הַפָּרֹֽכֶת וְעַל מִזְבַּח הַזָּהָב מַתָּנָה אַחַת מֵהֶן מְעַכָּֽבֶת: שְׁיָרֵי הַדָּם הָיָה שׁוֹפֵךְ עַל יְסוֹד מַעֲרָבִי שֶׁל מִזְבֵּֽחַ הַחִיצוֹן אִם לֹא נָתַן לֹא עִכֵּב:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:28:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','MISHNAH I Where are the offerings slaughtered [in the Holy Temple?] The holiest of offerings are slaughtered on the north side [of the Altar]. The bullock and he-goat of Yom Kippur are slaughtered on the north side, and their blood is received in a sacred vessel, on the north side. Their blood must be thrown between the poles [of the Ark], and in front of the curtain and upon the Gold Altar; [omission of] any one of these applications prevents [atonement]. The remainder of the blood [in the vessel] he [the Kohein] would pour on the western base of the Outer Altar; [but] if he did not do so, it did not prevent [atonement].','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:28:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','mshnh ey-zeh-hoo me-koh-mahn shehl ze-vah-kheem kohd-shey kah-dah-sheem she-khee-tah-tahn bah-tsah-fohn pahr ve-sah-eer shehl yohm hah-kee-poo-reem she-khee-tah-tahn bah-tsah-fohn ve-kee-bool dah-mahn beekh-lee shah-reht bah-tsah-fohn ve-dah-mahn tah-oon hah-zah-yah ahl beyn hah-bah-deem ve-ahl hah-pah-roh-kheht ve-ahl meez-bahkh hah-zah-hahv mah-tah-nah ah-khaht meh-hehn me-ah-kah-veht: she-yah-rey hah-dahm hah-yah shoh-fehkh ahl ye-sohd mah-ah-rah-vee shehl meez-beh-ahkh hah-khee-tsohn eem loh nah-tahn loh ee-kehv:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:29:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','משנה ב פָּרִים הַנִּשְׂרָפִים וּשְׂעִירִים הַנִּשְׂרָפִים שְׁחִיטָתָן בַּצָּפוֹן וְקִבּוּל דָּמָן בִּכְלִי שָׁרֵת בַּצָּפוֹן וְדָמָן טָעוּן הַזָּיָה עַל הַפָּרֹֽכֶת וְעַל מִזְבַּח הַזָּהָב מַתָּנָה אַחַת מֵהֶן מְעַכָּֽבֶת: שְׁיָרֵי הַדָּם הָיָה שׁוֹפֵךְ עַל יְסוֹד מַעֲרָבִי שֶׁל מִזְבֵּֽחַ הַחִיצוֹן אִם לֹא נָתַן לֹא עִכֵּב אֵֽלּוּ וָאֵֽלּוּ נִשְׂרָפִין בְּבֵית הַדָּֽשֶׁן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:29:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','MISHNAH II The bullocks that are burned entirely, and the he-goats that are burned entirely, are slaughtered on the north side, and their blood is received in a sacred vessel, on the north side; their blood must be thrown in front of the curtain and upon the Gold Altar; [omission of] any one of these applications prevents [atonement]. The remainder of the blood [in the vessel] he [the Kohein] would pour on the western base of the Outer Altar; [but] if he did not do so, it did not prevent [atonement]. These [offerings] and those are burned at the place where the ashes were put.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:29:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','mshnh v pah-reem hah-nees-rah-feem oo-se-ee-reem hah-nees-rah-feem she-khee-tah-tahn bah-tsah-fohn ve-kee-bool dah-mahn beekh-lee shah-reht bah-tsah-fohn ve-dah-mahn tah-oon hah-zah-yah ahl hah-pah-roh-kheht ve-ahl meez-bahkh hah-zah-hahv mah-tah-nah ah-khaht meh-hehn me-ah-kah-veht: she-yah-rey hah-dahm hah-yah shoh-fehkh ahl ye-sohd mah-ah-rah-vee shehl meez-beh-ahkh hah-khee-tsohn eem loh nah-tahn loh ee-kehv eh-loo vah-eh-loo nees-rah-feen be-veyt hah-dah-shehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:30:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','משנה ג חַטֹּאת הַצִּבּוּר וְהַיָּחִיד אֵֽלּוּ הֵן חַטֹּאת הַצִּבּוּר שְׂעִירֵי רָאשֵׁי חֳדָשִׁים וְשֶׁל מוֹעֲדוֹת שְׁחִיטָתָן בַּצָּפוֹן וְקִבּוּל דָּמָן בִּכְלִי שָׁרֵת בַּצָּפוֹן וְדָמָן טָעוּן אַרְבַּע מַתָּנוֹת עַל אַרְבַּע קְרָנוֹת, כֵּיצַד עָלָה בַכֶּֽבֶשׁ וּפָנָה לַסּוֹבֵב וּבָא לוֹ לְקֶֽרֶן דְּרוֹמִית מִזְרָחִית, מִזְרָחִית צְפוֹנִית, צְפוֹנִית מַעֲרָבִית, מַעֲרָבִית דְּרוֹמִית, שְׁיָרֵי הַדָּם הָיָה שׁוֹפֵךְ עַל יְסוֹד דְּרוֹמִי וְנֶאֱכָלִין לִפְנִים מִן הַקְּ֒לָעִים לְזִכְרֵי כְהֻנָּה בְּכָל מַאֲכָל לְיוֹם וָלַֽיְלָה עַד חֲצוֹת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:30:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','MISHNAH III The communal and individual sin-offerings— these are the communal sin-offerings: The he-goats offered on Rosh Chodesh and on the Festivals are slaughtered on the north side, and their blood must be received in a sacred vessel, on the north side; their blood requires four applications [one] on each of the four corners. How [was this done]? He [the Kohein] went up the ramp [of the Altar] and turned to the ledge [bordering the Altar]; he came to the southeast corner, the northeast corner, the northwest corner, the southwest corner. He poured the rest of the blood at the southern base [of the Altar]. These offerings were eaten within the Temple Courtyard by the male Kohanim, prepared in any fashion, on that day and [the following] night until midnight.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:30:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','mshnh g khah-toht hah-tsee-boor ve-hah-yah-kheed eh-loo hehn khah-toht hah-tsee-boor se-ee-rey rah-shey khoh-dah-sheem ve-shehl moh-ah-doht she-khee-tah-tahn bah-tsah-fohn ve-kee-bool dah-mahn beekh-lee shah-reht bah-tsah-fohn ve-dah-mahn tah-oon ahr-bah mah-tah-noht ahl ahr-bah ke-rah-noht, key-tsahd ah-lah vah-keh-vehsh oo-fah-nah lah-soh-vehv oo-vah loh le-keh-rehn de-roh-meet meez-rah-kheet, meez-rah-kheet tse-foh-neet, tse-foh-neet mah-ah-rah-veet, mah-ah-rah-veet de-roh-meet, she-yah-rey hah-dahm hah-yah shoh-fehkh ahl ye-sohd de-roh-mee ve-neh-eh-khah-leen leef-neem meen hah-KE-lah-eem le-zeekh-rey khe-hoo-nah be-khohl mah-ah-khahl le-yohm vah-lah-ye-lah ahd khah-tsoht:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:31:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','יְהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ אִם נִתְחַיַּֽבְתִּי חַטָּאת שֶּׁתְּ֒הֵא אֲמִֽירָה זוּ מְרֻצָּה לְפָנֶֽיךָ כְּאִֽלּוּ הִקְרַֽבְתִּי חַטָּאת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:31:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','May it be Your will Adonoy, our God, and God of our fathers, if I have committed a sin which requires, the bringing of a sin-offering, that this recitation be acceptable before you as if I had brought a sin-offering.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:31:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','ye-hee rah-tsohn mee-LE-fah-ney-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo veh-loh-hey ah-voh-tey-noo eem neet-khah-yah-ve-tee khah-taht sheh-TE-heh ah-mee-rah zoo me-roo-tsah le-fah-ney-khah ke-ee-loo heek-rah-ve-tee khah-taht:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:32:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','משנה ד הָעוֹלָה קֹֽדֶשׁ קָדָשִׁים שְׁחִיטָתָהּ בַּצָּפוֹן וְקִבּוּל דָּמָהּ בִּכְלִי שָׁרֵת בַּצָּפוֹן וְדָמָהּ טָעוּן שְׁתֵּי מַתָּנוֹת שֶׁהֵן אַרְבַּע וּטְעוּנָה הֶפְשֵׁט וְנִתּֽוּחַ וְכָלִיל לָאִשִּׁים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:32:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','MISHNAH IV The burnt-offering is one of the holiest offerings. It is slaughtered on the north side and its blood is received in a sacred vessel on the north side; its blood requires two applications which are [like] four. It must be skinned, severed into parts, and totally consumed by the fire.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:32:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','mshnh d hah-oh-lah koh-dehsh kah-dah-sheem she-khee-tah-tahh bah-tsah-fohn ve-kee-bool dah-mahh beekh-lee shah-reht bah-tsah-fohn ve-dah-mahh tah-oon she-tey mah-tah-noht sheh-hehn ahr-bah oo-te-oo-nah hehf-sheht ve-nee-too-ahkh ve-khah-leel lah-ee-sheem:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:33:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','יְהִי רָצוֹן כְּאִֽלּוּ הִקְרַֽבְתִּי עוֹלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:33:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','May it be Your will as if I had brought a burnt-offering.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:33:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','ye-hee rah-tsohn ke-ee-loo heek-rah-ve-tee oh-lah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:34:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','משנה ה זִבְחֵי שַׁלְמֵי צִבּוּר וַאֲשָׁמוֹת, אֵֽלּוּ הֵן אֲשָׁמוֹת אֲשַׁם גְּזֵלוֹת אֲשַׁם מְעִילוֹת אֲשַׁם שִׁפְחָה חֲרוּפָה אֲשַׁם נָזִיר אֲשַׁם מְצוֹרָע אָשָׁם תָּלוּי, שְׁחִיטָתָן בַּצָּפוֹן וְקִבּוּל דָּמָן בִּכְלִי שָׁרֵת בַּצָּפוֹן, וְדָמָן טָעוּן שְׁתֵּי מַתָּנוֹת שֶׁהֵן אַרְבַּע, וְנֶאֱכָלִין לִפְנִים מִן הַקְּ֒לָעִים לְזִכְרֵי כְהֻנָּה בְּכָל מַאֲכָל לְיוֹם וָלַֽיְלָה עַד חֲצוֹת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:34:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','MISHNAH V Communal peace-offerings and guilt-offerings. These are the guilt-offerings: the guilt-offering for robbery, the guilt-offering for unauthorized use of sacred objects, the guilt-offering for violating a betrothed handmaiden, the guilt-offering of a Nazirite, the guilt-offering of a metzora, the guilt-offering for suspension. These are slaughtered on the north side and their blood received in a sacred vessel on the north side; their blood requires two applications which are [like] four. These [offerings] were eaten within the Courtyard by the male Kohanim, prepared for eating in any fashion. On that day and [the following] night until midnight.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:34:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','mshnh h zeev-khey shahl-mey tsee-boor vah-ah-shah-moht, eh-loo hehn ah-shah-moht ah-shahm ge-zeh-loht ah-shahm me-ee-loht ah-shahm sheef-khah khah-roo-fah ah-shahm nah-zeer ah-shahm me-tsoh-rah ah-shahm tah-looy, she-khee-tah-tahn bah-tsah-fohn ve-kee-bool dah-mahn beekh-lee shah-reht bah-tsah-fohn, ve-dah-mahn tah-oon she-tey mah-tah-noht sheh-hehn ahr-bah, ve-neh-eh-khah-leen leef-neem meen hah-KE-lah-eem le-zeekh-rey khe-hoo-nah be-khohl mah-ah-khahl le-yohm vah-lah-ye-lah ahd khah-tsoht:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:35:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','יְהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ אִם נִתְחַיַּֽבְתִּי אָשָׁם שֶּׁתְּ֒הֵא אֲמִֽירָה זוּ מְרֻצָּה לְפָנֶֽיךָ כְּאִֽלּוּ הִקְרַֽבְתִּי אָשָׁם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:35:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','May it be Your will Adonoy, our God, and God our our fathers, if I have committed a sin which requires the bringing of a guilt-offering that this recitation be acceptable before You as if I had brought a guilt-offering.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:35:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','ye-hee rah-tsohn mee-LE-fah-ney-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo veh-loh-hey ah-voh-tey-noo eem neet-khah-yah-ve-tee ah-shahm sheh-TE-heh ah-mee-rah zoo me-roo-tsah le-fah-ney-khah ke-ee-loo heek-rah-ve-tee ah-shahm:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:36:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','משנה ו הַתּוֹדָה וְאֵיל נָזִיר קָדָשִׁים קַלִּים שְׁחִיטָתָן בְּכָל־מָקוֹם בָּעֲזָרָה וְדָמָן טָעוּן שְׁתֵּי מַתָּנוֹת שֶׁהֵן אַרְבַּע, וְנֶאֱכָלִין בְּכָל־הָעִיר לְכָל־אָדָם בְּכָל־מַאֲכָל לְיוֹם וָלַֽיְלָה עַד־חֲצוֹת, הַמּוּרָם מֵהֶם כַּיּוֹצֵא בָהֶם אֶלָּא שֶׁהַמּוּרָם נֶאֱכָל לַכֹּהֲנִים לִנְשֵׁיהֶם וְלִבְנֵיהֶם וּלְעַבְדֵיהֶם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:36:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','MISHNAH VI The thanksgiving-offering and the ram of the Nazirite are of lesser sanctity. They are slaughtered anywhere in the Temple Courtyard, and their blood requires two applications which are [like] four; they may be eaten anywhere in the city by anyone, and prepared for eating in any fashion, [and may be eaten] on that day and the following night until midnight. The portion given to the Kohanim, has the same rule, but may be eaten only by the Kohanim, their wives, children, and slaves.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:36:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','mshnh v hah-toh-dah ve-eyl nah-zeer kah-dah-sheem kah-leem she-khee-tah-tahn be-khohl mah-kohm bah-ah-zah-rah ve-dah-mahn tah-oon she-tey mah-tah-noht sheh-hehn ahr-bah, ve-neh-eh-khah-leen be-khohl hah-eer le-khohl ah-dahm be-khohl mah-ah-khahl le-yohm vah-lah-ye-lah ahd khah-tsoht, hah-moo-rahm meh-hehm kah-yoh-tseh vah-hehm eh-lah sheh-hah-moo-rahm neh-eh-khahl lah-koh-hah-neem leen-shey-hehm ve-leev-ney-hehm oo-le-ahv-dey-hehm:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:37:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','יְהִי רָצוֹן כְּאִֽלּוּ הִקְרַֽבְתִּי תּוֹדָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:37:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','May it be Your will as if I brought a thanksgiving-offering.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:37:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','ye-hee rah-tsohn ke-ee-loo heek-rah-ve-tee toh-dah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:38:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','משנה ז שְׁלָמִים קָדָשִׁים קַלִּים שְׁחִיטָתָן בְּכָל מָקוֹם בָּעֲזָרָה וְדָמָן טָעוּן שְׁתֵּי מַתָּנוֹת שֶׁהֵן אַרְבַּע, וְנֶאֱכָלִין בְּכָל הָעִיר לְכָל אָדָם בְּכָל מַאֲכָל לִשְׁנֵי יָמִים וְלַֽיְלָה אֶחָד: הַמּוּרָם מֵהֶם כַּיּוֹצֵא בָהֶם אֶלָּא שֶׁהַמּוּרָם נֶאֱכָל לַכֹּהֲנִים לִנְשֵׁיהֶם וְלִבְנֵיהֶם וּלְעַבְדֵיהֶם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:38:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','MISHNAH VII The peace-offerings are [also] of lesser sanctity. They are slaughtered anywhere in the Courtyard, and their blood requires two applications which are [like] four. They may be eaten anywhere in the city by anyone, and prepared for eating in any fashion, for two days and one night. The portion given to the Kohanim has the same rule, but may be eaten only by the Kohanim, their wives, children, and slaves.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:38:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','mshnh z she-lah-meem kah-dah-sheem kah-leem she-khee-tah-tahn be-khohl mah-kohm bah-ah-zah-rah ve-dah-mahn tah-oon she-tey mah-tah-noht sheh-hehn ahr-bah, ve-neh-eh-khah-leen be-khohl hah-eer le-khohl ah-dahm be-khohl mah-ah-khahl leesh-ney yah-meem ve-lah-ye-lah eh-khahd: hah-moo-rahm meh-hehm kah-yoh-tseh vah-hehm eh-lah sheh-hah-moo-rahm neh-eh-khahl lah-koh-hah-neem leen-shey-hehm ve-leev-ney-hehm oo-le-ahv-dey-hehm:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:39:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','יְהִי רָצוֹן כְּאִֽלּוּ הִקְרַֽבְתִּי שְׁלָמִים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:39:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','May it be Your will as if I brought a peace-offering.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:39:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','ye-hee rah-tsohn ke-ee-loo heek-rah-ve-tee she-lah-meem:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:40:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','he','משנה ח הַבְּ֒כוֹר וְהַמַּעֲשֵׂר וְהַפֶּֽסַח קָדָשִׁים קַלִּים שְׁחִיטָתָן בְּכָל מָקוֹם בָּעֲזָרָה וְדָמָן טָעוּן מַתָּנָה אֶחָת וּבִלְבָד שֶׁיִּתֵּן כְּנֶֽגֶד הַיְסוֹד, שִׁנָּה בַאֲכִילָתָן הַבְּ֒כוֹר נֶאֱכָל לַכֹּהֲנִים וְהַמַּעֲשֵׂר לְכָל אָדָם, וְנֶאֱכָלִין בְּכָל הָעִיר בְּכָל מַאֲכָל לִשְׁנֵי יָמִים וְלַֽיְלָה אֶחָד: הַפֶּֽסַח אֵינוֹ נֶאֱכָל אֶלָּא בַלַּֽיְלָה וְאֵינוֹ נֶאֱכָל אֶלָּא עַד חֲצוֹת וְאֵינוֹ נֶאֱכָל אֶלָּא לִמְנוּיָו וְאֵינוֹ נֶאֱכָל אֶלָּא צָלִי:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:40:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','en','MISHNAH VIII Firstborn animals, the tithe of cattle and the Passover-offering (Pascal lamb) are [also] of lesser sanctity. They are slaughtered anywhere in the Temple Courtyard, and their blood requires one application provided that it is applied above the base (of the Altar). They differ in their consumption: The firstborn is eaten only by Kohanim, while the tithe may be eaten by any person. They may be eaten anywhere in the city, and prepared for eating in any fashion, and may be eaten for two days and one night. The Pascal lamb must be eaten only at night and only until midnight; and it may not be eaten except by those registered for it, and it may only be eaten when spit-roasted.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot:40:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-korbanot','transliteration','mshnh kh hah-BE-khohr ve-hah-mah-ah-sehr ve-hah-peh-sahkh kah-dah-sheem kah-leem she-khee-tah-tahn be-khohl mah-kohm bah-ah-zah-rah ve-dah-mahn tah-oon mah-tah-nah eh-khaht oo-veel-vahd sheh-yee-tehn ke-neh-gehd hah-ye-sohd, shee-nah vah-ah-khee-lah-tahn hah-BE-khohr neh-eh-khahl lah-koh-hah-neem ve-hah-mah-ah-sehr le-khohl ah-dahm, ve-neh-eh-khah-leen be-khohl hah-eer be-khohl mah-ah-khahl leesh-ney yah-meem ve-lah-ye-lah eh-khahd: hah-peh-sahkh ey-noh neh-eh-khahl eh-lah vah-lah-ye-lah ve-ey-noh neh-eh-khahl eh-lah ahd khah-tsoht ve-ey-noh neh-eh-khahl eh-lah leem-noo-yahv ve-ey-noh neh-eh-khahl eh-lah tsah-lee:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','he','רַבִּי יִשְׁמָעֵאל אוֹמֵר בִּשְׁלשׁ עֶשְׂרֵה מִדּוֹת הַתּוֹרָה נִדְרֶֽשֶׁת בָּהֵן: מִקַּל וָחֹֽמֶר, וּמִגְּ֒זֵרָה שָׁוָה, מִבִּנְיַן אָב מִכָּתוּב אֶחָד, וּמִבִּנְיַן אָב מִשְּׁ֒נֵי כְתוּבִים, מִכְּ֒לָל וּפְרָט, וּמִפְּ֒רָט וּכְלָל, כְּלָל וּפְרָט וּכְלָל אִי אַתָּה דָן אֶלָּא כְּעֵין הַפְּ֒רָט, מִכְּ֒לָל שֶׁהוּא צָרִיךְ לִפְרָט וּמִפְּ֒רָט שֶׁהוּא צָרִיךְ לִכְלָל, כָּל דָּבָר שֶׁהָיָה בִּכְלָל וְיָצָא מִן הַכְּ֒לָל לְלַמֵּד לֹא לְלַמֵּד עַל עַצְמוֹ יָצָא אֶלָּא לְלַמֵּד עַל הַכְּ֒לָל כֻּלּוֹ יָצָא, כָּל דָּבָר שֶׁהָיָה בִּכְלָל וְיָצָא לִטְעֹן טֹֽעַן אֶחָד שֶׁהוּא כְעִנְיָנוֹ יָצָא לְהָקֵל וְלֹא לְהַחֲמִיר, כָּל דָּבָר שֶׁהָיָה בִּכְלָל וְיָצָא לִטְעֹן טֹֽעַן אַחֵר שֶׁלֹּא כְעִנְיָנוֹ יָצָא לְהָקֵל וּלְהַחֲמִיר, כָּל דָּבָר שֶׁהָיָה בִּכְלָל וְיָצָא לִדּוֹן בַּדָּבָר הֶחָדָשׁ אִי אַתָּה יָכוֹל לְהַחֲזִירוֹ לִכְלָלוֹ עַד שֶׁיַּחֲזִירֶֽנּוּ הַכָּתוּב לִכְלָלוֹ בְּפֵרוּשׁ, דָּבָר הַלָּמֵד מֵעִנְיָנוֹ וְדָבָר הַלָּמֵד מִסּוֹפוֹ, וְכֵן שְׁנֵי כְתוּבִים הַמַּכְחִישִׁים זֶה אֶת זֶה עַד שֶׁיָּבֹא הַכָּתוּב הַשְּׁ֒לִישִׁי וְיַכְרִֽיעַ בֵּינֵיהֶם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','en','Rabbi Yishmael says: through thirteen methods the Torah is expounded: 1) A conclusion drawn from a minor or lenient law, to a major or more strict one. 2) A clarification based on identical words or terms in the Biblical text. 3) A principle derived from one Biblical text or from two Biblical texts. 4) A rule followed by a detail. 5) A detail followed by a rule. 6) A rule followed by a detail, which is in turn followed by a rule, may infer only what is similar to the detail. 7) When a general rule requires an explicit rule; when an explicit rule requires generalization. 8) Something included in a general rule, which was singled out to teach— was not singled out to teach about itself, but to teach (something new) concerning the rule as a whole. 9) Something that was included in a rule and was singled out in a case similar to its rule, —it was singled out to lessen not to increase the severity of the case. 10) Something that was included in a rule and was singled out in a case which is not similar to its rule, —it was singled out either to lessen or to increase the severity of the case. 11) Something that was included in a rule and was singled out for a new stipulation— does not revert to its rule unless Scripture restores it to its rule expressly. 12) A matter deduced from its context, or from a subsequent expression. 13) Also, two passages that contradict each other until a third passage reconciles them.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','transliteration','rah-bee yeesh-mah-ehl oh-mehr beeshlsh ehs-reh mee-doht hah-toh-rah need-reh-sheht bah-hehn: mee-kahl vah-khoh-mehr, oo-mee-GE-zeh-rah shah-vah, mee-been-yahn ahv mee-kah-toov eh-khahd, oo-mee-been-yahn ahv mee-SHE-ney khe-too-veem, mee-KE-lahl oo-fe-raht, oo-mee-PE-raht oo-khe-lahl, ke-lahl oo-fe-raht oo-khe-lahl ee ah-tah dahn eh-lah ke-eyn hah-PE-raht, mee-KE-lahl sheh-hoo tsah-reekh leef-raht oo-mee-PE-raht sheh-hoo tsah-reekh leekh-lahl, kohl dah-vahr sheh-hah-yah beekh-lahl ve-yah-tsah meen hah-KE-lahl le-lah-mehd loh le-lah-mehd ahl ahts-moh yah-tsah eh-lah le-lah-mehd ahl hah-KE-lahl koo-loh yah-tsah, kohl dah-vahr sheh-hah-yah beekh-lahl ve-yah-tsah leet-ohn toh-ahn eh-khahd sheh-hoo khe-een-yah-noh yah-tsah le-hah-kehl ve-loh le-hah-khah-meer, kohl dah-vahr sheh-hah-yah beekh-lahl ve-yah-tsah leet-ohn toh-ahn ah-khehr sheh-loh khe-een-yah-noh yah-tsah le-hah-kehl oo-le-hah-khah-meer, kohl dah-vahr sheh-hah-yah beekh-lahl ve-yah-tsah lee-dohn bah-dah-vahr heh-khah-dahsh ee ah-tah yah-khohl le-hah-khah-zee-roh leekh-lah-loh ahd sheh-yah-khah-zee-reh-noo hah-kah-toov leekh-lah-loh be-feh-roosh, dah-vahr hah-lah-mehd meh-een-yah-noh ve-dah-vahr hah-lah-mehd mee-soh-foh, ve-khehn she-ney khe-too-veem hah-mahkh-khee-sheem zeh eht zeh ahd sheh-yah-voh hah-kah-toov hah-SHE-lee-shee ve-yahkh-ree-ah bey-ney-hehm:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','he','יְהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ שֶׁיִּבָּנֶה בֵּית הַמִּקְדָּשׁ בִּמְהֵרָה בְיָמֵֽינוּ וְתֵן חֶלְקֵֽנוּ בְּתוֹרָתֶֽךָ: וְשָׁם נַעֲבָדְךָ בְּיִרְאָה כִּימֵי עוֹלָם וּכְשָׁנִים קַדְמוֹנִיּוֹת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','en','May it be Your will Adonoy, our God and God of our fathers, that the Holy Temple be rebuilt speedily in our days: and grant us our share in Your Torah. And there we will serve You reverently as in the days of old, and in earlier years.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','transliteration','ye-hee rah-tsohn mee-LE-fah-ney-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo veh-loh-hey ah-voh-tey-noo sheh-yee-bah-neh beyt hah-meek-dahsh beem-heh-rah ve-yah-mey-noo ve-tehn khehl-keh-noo be-toh-rah-teh-khah: ve-shahm nah-ah-vah-de-khah be-yeer-ah kee-mey oh-lahm oo-khe-shah-neem kahd-moh-nee-yoht:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','he','מה שאנו אומרין הקדיש בלשון תרגום, יש אומרים מפני המלאכים שלא יתקנאו בנו שאנו משבחים שבח נאה כזה ואם יבינו המלאכים זה יקטרגו עלינו, על כן אומרים אותו בלשון שלא יבינו, שאינן מכירין ארמית. ויש מפרשים הטעם לפי שהיו רגילין לומר אותו אחר הדרשה והיו שם עמי הארץ שאינן מכירין אלא ארמית שהוא לשונם לכן נהגו לאומרו בלשון שהכל מבינין בו (ע"פ טור או"ח נו)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','en','Kaddish is not the name generally given to this prayer in the Talmud. It is referred to there as "May His great Name...", because the congregational response beginning with these words is the heart of this prayer. Only in one minor tractate, (Maseches Soferim 16, 19, and 21) is it referred to as Kaddish. Composed primarily in Aramaic, the language spoken and understood by most Jews in the Second Temple period (See Tosafos to Maseches Berachos 3a), nevertheless, several Hebrew phrases, which were familiar even to the unschooled, were also incorporated in the prayer. This particular form of Kaddish d''Rabanan, is so named because of the insertion of the paragraph which begins with the words "Upon Israel and upon our Sages, etc." This Kaddish is recited following the study of Talmud or Midrash and invokes God''s blessings on the Sages of Jewry, the transmitters of the Oral Torah.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְ֒מָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְקָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ. בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming of His Mashiach. In your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','transliteration','yeet-gah-dahl ve-yeet-kah-dahsh she-meh rah-bah be-ah-LE-mah dee ve-rah kheer-oo-teh ve-yahm-leekh mahl-khoo-teh ve-yahts-mahkh poo-re-kah-neh vee-kah-rehv (kehts) me-shee-kheh. be-khah-yey-khohn oo-ve-yoh-mey-khohn oo-ve-khah-yey de-khahl beyt yees-rah-ehl, bah-ah-gah-lah oo-veez-mahn kah-reev ve-eem-roo ah-mehn','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','transliteration','ye-heh she-meh rah-bah me-vah-rahkh le-ah-lahm oo-le-ah-LE-mey ah-LE-mah-yah','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְעֵֽלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְ֒מָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','transliteration','yeet-bah-rahkh ve-yeesh-tah-bahkh ve-yeet-pah-ahr ve-yeet-roh-mahm ve-yeet-nah-seh ve-yeet-hah-dahr ve-yeet-ah-leh ve-yeet-hah-lahl she-meh de-koo-de-shah, be-reekh hoo le-eh-lah (vshyt" oo-le-eh-lah mee-kahl) meen kohl beer-khah-tah ve-shee-rah-tah, toosh-be-khah-tah ve-neh-kheh-mah-tah, dah-ah-mee-rahn be-ah-LE-mah, ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','he','עַל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְעַל רַבָּנָן וְעַל תַלְמִידֵיהוֹן וְעַל כָּל תַּלְמִידֵי תַלְמִידֵיהוֹן, וְעַל כָּל מָאן דְּעָסְ֒קִין בְּאוֹרַיְתָא, דִּי בְאַתְרָא הָדֵין וְדִי בְכָל אֲתַר וַאֲתַר, יְהֵא לְהוֹן וּלְכוֹן שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא חִנָּא וְחִסְדָּא וְרַחֲמִין וְחַיִּין אֲרִיכִין וּמְזוֹנָא רְוִיחֵי וּפוּרְקָנָא מִן קֳדָם אֲבוּהוֹן דְבִשְׁמַיָּא וְאַרְעָא וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','en','Upon Israel, and upon our Sages, and upon their disciples, and upon all the disciples of their disciples, and upon all those who engage in Torah study in this land and in every land. May there be unto them and unto you abundant peace, favor, kindness, compassion, long life, ample sustenance and redemption from their Father Who is in heaven and on earth, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','transliteration','ahl yees-rah-ehl ve-ahl rah-bah-nahn ve-ahl tahl-mee-dey-hohn ve-ahl kohl tahl-mee-dey tahl-mee-dey-hohn, ve-ahl kohl mahn de-ah-SE-keen be-oh-rahy-tah, dee ve-aht-rah hah-deyn ve-dee ve-khahl ah-tahr vah-ah-tahr, ye-heh le-hohn oo-le-khohn she-lah-mah rah-bah khee-nah ve-khees-dah ve-rah-khah-meen ve-khah-yeen ah-ree-kheen oo-me-zoh-nah re-vee-khey oo-foo-re-kah-nah meen koh-dahm ah-voo-hohn de-veesh-mah-yah ve-ahr-ah ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','he','יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים טוֹבִים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','en','May there be abundant peace from heaven and a good life for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','transliteration','ye-heh she-lah-mah rah-bah meen she-mah-yah ve-khah-yeem toh-veem ah-ley-noo ve-ahl kohl yees-rah-ehl ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','he','עוֹשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם (בעשי"ת הַשָּׁלוֹם) בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא בְּרַחֲמָיו יַעֲשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','en','He Who makes peace (Ten Days of Penitence: the peace) in His high heavens may He, in His mercy, make peace for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-b-raita-d-rabi-yishmael','transliteration','oh-seh shah-lohm (vshyt" hah-shah-lohm) beem-roh-mahv hoo be-rah-khah-mahv yah-ah-seh shah-lohm ah-ley-noo ve-ahl kohl yees-rah-ehl ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, B''raita d''Rabi Yishmael'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','דרש ר'' שמלאי לעולם יסדר אדם שבחו של מקום ואחרי כן יתפלל. לפיכך תקנו לומר ''פסוקי דזמרה'' קודם תפלה. וקבעו ברכה אחת לפניהם ואחת לאחריהם, והן ברכות ''ברוך שאמר'' ו''ישתבח''. וצריך ליזהר שלא להפסיק ביניהם בדיבור. ויש מקומות שנוהגין לומר ''הודו לה'' קראו בשמו'' כאשר הוא כתוב בדברי הימים, לפי שדוד קבעו לאומרו בכל יום לפני הארון. ויש שמוסיפים עוד פסוקים אחרים, וכל מקום ומקום כמנהגו (ע"פ טור או"ח נ"א)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','The following sequence of prayers until Yishtabach is called Pesukei Dezimrah (verses of praise). These selected Scriptural passages were arranged by the Gaonim of the ninth century, in fulfillment of the Talmudic statement (Maseches Berachos 32a), "A person should always praise God first and make his requests [offer his prayers] afterwards." Beginning with the following prayer, it is forbidden to interrupt your prayer with conversation until after the Shemoneh Esrei. You are permitted to answer Amein, respond to Barechu, Kaddish and to say Kedushah even though you are in the midst of Pesukei Dezimrah. You are also permitted to say Modim d''Rabbonon and the first verse of the Shema together with the congregation. If you are concerned that the saying of Kerias Shema will not be within the proper time should you follow the regular order of prayers, you are permitted to recite the entire Kerias Shema during the Pesukei Dezimrah. The first 28 verses of this section are taken from 1 Chronicles 16:8-36, and the first 15 are almost identical with the first fifteen verses of Psalms 105. These prayers are mentioned in Maseches Soferim.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','הוֹדוּ לַיהוָֹה קִרְאוּ בִשְׁמוֹ הוֹדִֽיעוּ בָעַמִּים עֲלִילֹתָיו: שִֽׁירוּ לוֹ זַמְּ֒רוּ־לוֹ שִֽׂיחוּ בְּכָל־נִפְלְ֒אוֹתָיו: הִתְהַלְּ֒לוּ בְּשֵׁם קָדְשׁוֹ יִשְׂמַח לֵב מְבַקְשֵׁי יְהֹוָה: דִּרְשׁוּ יְהֹוָה וְעֻזּוֹ בַּקְּ֒שׁוּ פָנָיו תָּמִיד: זִכְרוּ נִפְלְ֒אֹתָיו אֲשֶׁר עָשָׂה מֹפְ֒תָיו וּמִשְׁפְּ֒טֵי־פִֽיהוּ: זֶֽרַע יִשְׂרָאֵל עַבְדּוֹ בְּנֵי יַעֲקֹב בְּחִירָיו: הוּא יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ בְּכָל־הָאָֽרֶץ מִשְׁפָּטָיו: זִכְרוּ לְעוֹלָם בְּרִיתוֹ דָּבָר צִוָּה לְאֶֽלֶף דּוֹר: אֲשֶׁר כָּרַת אֶת־אַבְרָהָם וּשְׁבוּעָתוֹ לְיִצְחָק: וַיַּעֲמִידֶֽהָ לְיַעֲקֹב לְחֹק לְיִשְׂרָאֵל בְּרִית עוֹלָם: לֵאמֹר לְךָ אֶתֵּן אֶֽרֶץ־כְּנָעַן חֶֽבֶל נַחֲלַתְכֶם: בִּהְיוֹתְ֒כֶם מְתֵי מִסְפָּר כִּמְעַט וְגָרִים בָּהּ: וַיִּתְהַלְּ֒כוּ מִגּוֹי אֶל־גּוֹי וּמִמַּמְלָכָה אֶל־עַם אַחֵר: לֹא־הִנִּֽיחַ לְאִישׁ לְעָשְׁקָם וַיּֽוֹכַח עֲלֵיהֶם מְלָכִים: אַל־תִּגְּ֒עוּ בִּמְשִׁיחָי וּבִנְבִיאַי אַל־תָּרֵֽעוּ: שִֽׁירוּ לַיהוָֹה כָּל־הָאָֽרֶץ בַּשְּׂ֒רוּ מִיּוֹם־אֶל־יוֹם יְשׁוּעָתוֹ: סַפְּ֒רוּ בַגּוֹיִם אֶת־כְּבוֹדוֹ בְּכָל־הָעַמִּים נִפְלְאֹתָיו: כִּי גָדוֹל יְהֹוָה וּמְהֻלָּל מְאֹד וְנוֹרָא הוּא עַל־כָּל־אֱלֹהִים: כִּי כָּל־אֱלֹהֵי הָעַמִּים אֱלִילִים וַיהוָֹה שָׁמַֽיִם עָשָׂה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','Give thanks to Adonoy, proclaim His Name; make His deeds known among the nations. Sing to Him, compose songs to Him, speak of all His wonders. Take pride in [uttering] His holy Name, let the heart rejoice of those who seek Adonoy. Search for Adonoy and His might, seek His presence continually. Remember the wonders He has performed, His miracles, and the laws from His mouth. [You,] the seed of Israel His servant, children of Jacob, His chosen ones. He is Adonoy our God; the entire earth is governed by His laws. Remember His covenant forever— the word He commanded to a thousand generations— which He made as a treaty with Abraham, and [which was] His oath to Isaac. He established it for Jacob as a statute, for Israel as an everlasting covenant. Saying, To you I will give the Land of Canaan, the portion of your inheritance. When you were only few in number— very few, and strangers in it. They wandered from nation to nation, and from one kingdom to another people. He permitted no one to oppress them, and admonished kings for their sakes. Do not touch My anointed ones, and do not harm My prophets." Sing to Adonoy all the earth, proclaim His deliverance from day to day. Recount His glory among the nations, His wonders among all the peoples. For Adonoy is great and most extolled; Awesome is He above all gods. For all the gods of the peoples are idols, whereas Adonoy made the heavens.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','hoh-doo lah-ah-doh-NAI keer-oo veesh-moh hoh-dee-oo vah-ah-meem ah-lee-loh-tahv: shee-roo loh zah-ME-roo LOH see-khoo be-khohl neef-LE-oh-tahv: heet-hah-LE-loo be-shehm kohd-shoh yees-mahkh lehv me-vahk-shey ah-doh-NAI: deer-shoo ah-doh-NAI ve-oo-zoh bah-KE-shoo fah-nahv tah-meed: zeekh-roo neef-LE-oh-tahv ah-shehr ah-sah moh-FE-tahv oo-meesh-PE-tey fee-HOO: zeh-rah yees-rah-ehl ahv-doh be-ney yah-ah-kohv be-khee-rahv: hoo ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo be-khohl hah-ah-rehts meesh-pah-tahv: zeekh-roo le-oh-lahm be-ree-toh dah-vahr tsee-vah le-eh-lehf dohr: ah-shehr kah-raht eht ahv-rah-hahm oo-she-voo-ah-toh le-yeets-khahk: vah-yah-ah-mee-deh-hah le-yah-ah-kohv le-khohk le-yees-rah-ehl be-reet oh-lahm: leh-mohr le-khah eh-tehn eh-rehts ke-nah-ahn kheh-vehl nah-khah-laht-khehm: beeh-yoh-TE-khehm me-tey mees-pahr keem-aht ve-gah-reem bahh: vah-yeet-hah-LE-khoo mee-gohy ehl gohy oo-mee-mahm-lah-khah ehl ahm ah-khehr: loh hee-nee-ahkh le-eesh le-ah-she-kahm vah-yoh-khahkh ah-ley-hehm me-lah-kheem: ahl tee-GE-oo beem-shee-khahy oo-veen-vee-ahy ahl tah-reh-oo: shee-roo lah-ah-doh-NAI kohl hah-ah-rehts bah-SE-roo mee-yohm ehl yohm ye-shoo-ah-toh: sah-PE-roo vah-goh-yeem eht ke-voh-doh be-khohl hah-ah-meem neef-le-oh-tahv: kee gah-dohl ah-doh-NAI oo-me-hoo-lahl me-ohd ve-noh-rah hoo ahl kohl eh-loh-heem: kee kohl eh-loh-hey hah-ah-meem eh-lee-leem vah-ah-doh-NAI shah-mah-yeem ah-sah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','הוֹד וְהָדָר לְפָנָיו עֹז וְחֶדְוָה בִּמְקֹמוֹ: הָבוּ לַיהוָֹה מִשְׁפְּ֒חוֹת עַמִּים הָבוּ לַיהוָֹה כָּבוֹד וָעֹז: הָבוּ לַיהוָֹה כְּבוֹד שְׁמוֹ שְׂאוּ מִנְחָה וּבֹֽאוּ לְפָנָיו הִשְׁתַּחֲווּ לַיהוָֹה בְּהַדְרַת־קֹֽדֶשׁ: חִֽילוּ מִלְּ֒פָנָיו כָּל־הָאָֽרֶץ אַף־תִּכּוֹן תֵּבֵל בַּל־תִּמּוֹט: יִשְׂמְחוּ הַשָּׁמַֽיִם וְתָגֵל הָאָֽרֶץ וְיֹאמְ֒רוּ בַגּוֹיִם יְהֹוָה מָלָךְ: יִרְעַם הַיָּם וּמְלוֹאוֹ יַעֲלֹץ הַשָּׂדֶה וְכָל־אֲשֶׁר־בּוֹ: אָז יְרַנְּ֒נוּ עֲצֵי הַיָּעַר מִלִּפְנֵי יְהֹוָה כִּי־בָא לִשְׁפּוֹט אֶת־הָאָֽרֶץ: הוֹדוּ לַיהוָֹה כִּי טוֹב כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ: וְאִמְרוּ הוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׁעֵֽנוּ וְקַבְּ֒צֵֽנוּ וְהַצִּילֵֽנוּ מִן־הַגּוֹיִם לְהוֹדוֹת לְשֵׁם קָדְשֶֽׁךָ לְהִשְׁתַּבֵּֽחַ בִּתְהִלָּתֶֽךָ: בָּרוּךְ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל מִן־הָעוֹלָם וְעַד הָעֹלָם וַיֹּאמְ֒רוּ כָל־הָעָם אָמֵן וְהַלֵּל לַיהוָֹה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','Beauty and splendor are before Him, strength and joy are in His presence. Give to Adonoy families of peoples— give to Adonoy glory and might. Give to Adonoy the glory due His Name, bring an offering and come before Him, prostrate yourselves before Adonoy in the splendor of holiness. Tremble before Him all [peoples of] the earth, for He established the inhabited world so that it cannot be moved. The heavens will rejoice, the earth will exult, and they will proclaim among the nations: Adonoy has begun His reign. The sea and its fullness will roar; the field and all that is in it will jubilate. Then the trees of the forest will sing with joy, [receding] before Adonoy when He comes to judge the earth. Give thanks to Adonoy, for He is good, for His kindness is everlasting. And say, "Deliver us, God of our deliverance; gather us and save us from the nations, to give thanks to Your holy Name, to be extolled in Your praise." Blessed is Adonoy, the God of Israel for all eternity, and all the people said: "Amein" and [they] praised Adonoy."','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','hohd ve-hah-dahr le-fah-nahv ohz ve-khehd-vah beem-koh-moh: hah-voo lah-ah-doh-NAI meesh-PE-khoht ah-meem hah-voo lah-ah-doh-NAI kah-vohd vah-ohz: hah-voo lah-ah-doh-NAI ke-vohd she-moh se-oo meen-khah oo-voh-oo le-fah-nahv heesh-tah-khah-voo lah-ah-doh-NAI be-hahd-raht koh-dehsh: khee-loo mee-LE-fah-nahv kohl hah-ah-rehts ahf tee-kohn teh-vehl bahl tee-moht: yees-me-khoo hah-shah-mah-yeem ve-tah-gehl hah-ah-rehts ve-yoh-ME-roo vah-goh-yeem ah-doh-NAI mah-lahkh: yeer-ahm hah-yahm oo-me-loh-oh yah-ah-lohts hah-sah-deh ve-khohl ah-shehr boh: ahz ye-rah-NE-noo ah-tsey hah-yah-ahr mee-leef-ney ah-doh-NAI kee vah leesh-poht eht hah-ah-rehts: hoh-doo lah-ah-doh-NAI kee tohv kee le-oh-lahm khahs-doh: ve-eem-roo hoh-shee-eh-noo eh-loh-hey yeesh-eh-noo ve-kah-BE-tseh-noo ve-hah-tsee-leh-noo meen hah-goh-yeem le-hoh-doht le-shehm kohd-sheh-khah le-heesh-tah-beh-ahkh beet-hee-lah-teh-khah: bah-rookh ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey yees-rah-ehl meen hah-oh-lahm ve-ahd hah-oh-lahm vah-yoh-ME-roo khohl hah-ahm ah-mehn ve-hah-lehl lah-ah-doh-NAI:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','רוֹמְ֒מוּ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וְהִשְׁתַּחֲווּ לַהֲדֹם רַגְלָיו קָדוֹשׁ הוּא: רוֹמְ֒מוּ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וְהִשְׁתַּחֲווּ לְהַר קָדְשׁוֹ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','Exalt Adonoy, our God, and prostrate yourselves at His footstool. Holy is He! Exalt Adonoy, our God, and prostrate yourselves at His holy mountain, for Adonoy our God is holy.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','roh-ME-moo ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo ve-heesh-tah-khah-voo lah-hah-dohm rahg-lahv kah-dohsh hoo: roh-ME-moo ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo ve-heesh-tah-khah-voo le-hahr kohd-shoh kee kah-dohsh ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','וְהוּא רַחוּם יְכַפֵּר עָוֹן וְלֹא־יַשְׁחִית וְהִרְבָּה לְהָשִׁיב אַפּוֹ וְלֹא־יָעִיר כָּל־חֲמָתוֹ: אַתָּה יְהֹוָה לֹא־תִכְלָא רַחֲמֶֽיךָ מִמֶּֽנִּי חַסְדְּ֒ךָ וַאֲמִתְּ֒ךָ תָּמִיד יִצְּ֒רֽוּנִי: זְכֹר רַחֲמֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה וַחֲסָדֶֽיךָ כִּי מֵעוֹלָם הֵֽמָּה: תְּנוּ עֹז לֵאלֹהִים עַל־יִשְׂרָאֵל גַּאֲוָתוֹ וְעֻזּוֹ בַּשְּׁ֒חָקִים: נוֹרָא אֱלֹהִים מִמִּקְדָּשֶֽׁיךָ אֵל יִשְׂרָאֵל הוּא נֹתֵן עֹז וְתַעֲצֻמוֹת לָעָם בָּרוּךְ אֱלֹהִים: אֵל־נְקָמוֹת יְהֹוָה אֵל נְקָמוֹת הוֹפִֽיעַ: הִנָּשֵׂא שֹׁפֵט הָאָֽרֶץ הָשֵׁב גְּמוּל עַל־גֵּאִים: לַיהוָֹה הַיְשׁוּעָה עַל־עַמְּ֒ךָ בִרְכָתֶֽךָ סֶּֽלָה: יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת עִמָּנוּ מִשְׂגָּב לָֽנוּ אֱלֹהֵי יַעֲקֹב סֶֽלָה: יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת אַשְׁרֵי אָדָם בֹּטֵֽחַ בָּךְ: יְהֹוָה הוֹשִֽׁיעָה הַמֶּֽלֶךְ יַעֲנֵֽנוּ בְיוֹם־קָרְאֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','And He, the Merciful One, atones iniquity and does not destroy; He frequently withdraws His anger and does not arouse all His rage. You, Adonoy, withhold not Your mercy from me; may Your kindness and Your truth always protect me. Remember Your mercies Adonoy and kindnesses, for they are from the beginning of the world. Give might to God, His pride (majesty) hovers over Israel, and His might is in the clouds. You are awesome, God, from Your Sanctuaries, Almighty of Israel— He grants might and power to the people; blessed is God. Almighty of vengeance, Adonoy, Almighty of vengeance, reveal Yourself. Arise, Judge of the earth! Repay the arrogant their just reward. Deliverance is Adonoy''s. Upon Your people is Your blessing. Selah. Adonoy of Hosts is with us, a stronghold for us is the God of Jacob. Selah. Adonoy of Hosts! Fortunate is the man who trusts in You. Adonoy, deliver [us]. The King will answer us on the day we call.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','ve-hoo rah-khoom ye-khah-pehr ah-vohn ve-loh yahsh-kheet ve-heer-bah le-hah-sheev ah-poh ve-loh yah-eer kohl khah-mah-toh: ah-tah ah-doh-NAI loh teekh-lah rah-khah-mey-khah mee-meh-nee khahs-DE-khah vah-ah-mee-TE-khah tah-meed yee-TSE-roo-nee: ze-khohr rah-khah-mey-khah ah-doh-NAI vah-khah-sah-dey-khah kee meh-oh-lahm heh-mah: te-noo ohz leh-loh-heem ahl yees-rah-ehl gah-ah-vah-toh ve-oo-zoh bah-SHE-khah-keem: noh-rah eh-loh-heem mee-meek-dah-shey-khah ehl yees-rah-ehl hoo noh-tehn ohz ve-tah-ah-tsoo-moht lah-ahm bah-rookh eh-loh-heem: ehl ne-kah-moht ah-doh-NAI ehl ne-kah-moht hoh-fee-ah: hee-nah-seh shoh-feht hah-ah-rehts hah-shehv ge-mool ahl geh-eem: lah-ah-doh-NAI hah-ye-shoo-ah ahl ah-ME-khah veer-khah-teh-khah seh-lah: ah-doh-NAI tse-vah-oht ee-mah-noo mees-gahv lah-noo eh-loh-hey yah-ah-kohv seh-lah: ah-doh-NAI tse-vah-oht ahsh-rey ah-dahm boh-teh-ahkh bahkh: ah-doh-NAI hoh-shee-ah hah-meh-lehkh yah-ah-neh-noo ve-yohm kah-re-eh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','הוֹשִֽׁיעָה אֶת־עַמֶּֽךָ וּבָרֵךְ אֶת־נַחֲלָתֶֽךָ וּרְעֵם וְנַשְּׂ֒אֵם עַד־הָעוֹלָם: נַפְשֵֽׁנוּ חִכְּ֒תָה לַיהוָֹה עֶזְרֵֽנוּ וּמָגִנֵּֽנוּ הוּא: כִּי־בוֹ יִשְׂמַח לִבֵּֽנוּ כִּי בְשֵׁם קָדְשׁוֹ בָטָֽחְנוּ: יְהִי־חַסְדְּ֒ךָ יְהֹוָה עָלֵֽינוּ כַּאֲשֶׁר יִחַֽלְנוּ לָךְ: הַרְאֵֽנוּ יְהֹוָה חַסְדֶּֽךָ וְיֶשְׁעֲךָ תִּֽתֶּן־לָֽנוּ: קֽוּמָה עֶזְרָֽתָה לָּנוּ וּפְ֒דֵֽנוּ לְמַֽעַן חַסְדֶּֽךָ: אָנֹכִי יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ הַמַּעַלְךָ מֵאֶֽרֶץ מִצְרָֽיִם הַרְחֶב־פִּֽיךָ וַאֲמַלְאֵֽהוּ: אַשְׁרֵי הָעָם שֶׁכָּֽכָה לּוֹ אַשְׁרֵי הָעָם שֶׁיְהֹוָה אֱלֹהָיו: וַאֲנִי בְּחַסְדְּ֒ךָ בָטַֽחְתִּי יָגֵל לִבִּי בִּישׁוּעָתֶֽךָ אָשִֽׁירָה לַיהוָֹה כִּי גָמַל עָלָי:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','Deliver Your people and bless Your inheritance, tend them and uplift them forever. Our soul yearned for Adonoy, our help and our shield is He. For in Him our hearts will rejoice, for in His holy Name we trusted. May Your kindness, Adonoy, be upon us, as we have waited for You. Show us Your kindness, Adonoy, and grant us Your deliverance. Arise—come to our aid, and redeem us for the sake of Your kindness. I am Adonoy, Your God, Who brought you up from the land of Egypt; open your mouth wide, and I will fill it. Fortunate is the people whose lot is thus, fortunate is the people for whom Adonoy is their God. In Your loving kindness I trust, My heart will exult in Your deliverance; I will sing to Adonoy, for He dealt kindly with me.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','hoh-shee-ah eht ah-meh-khah oo-vah-rehkh eht nah-khah-lah-teh-khah oo-re-ehm ve-nah-SE-ehm ahd hah-oh-lahm: nahf-sheh-noo khee-KE-tah lah-ah-doh-NAI ehz-reh-noo oo-mah-gee-neh-noo hoo: kee voh yees-mahkh lee-beh-noo kee ve-shehm kohd-shoh vah-tah-khe-noo: ye-hee khahs-DE-khah ah-doh-NAI ah-ley-noo kah-ah-shehr yeekhah-le-noo lahkh: hahr-eh-noo ah-doh-NAI khahs-deh-khah ve-yehsh-ah-khah tee-tehn lah-noo: koo-mah ehz-rah-tah lah-noo oo-FE-deh-noo le-mah-ahn khahs-deh-khah: ah-noh-khee ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-khah hah-mah-ahl-khah meh-eh-rehts meets-rah-yeem hahr-khehv pee-khah vah-ah-mahl-eh-hoo: ahsh-rey hah-ahm sheh-kah-khah loh ahsh-rey hah-ahm shehy-ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hahv: vah-ah-nee be-khahs-DE-khah vah-tah-khe-tee yah-gehl lee-bee bee-shoo-ah-teh-khah ah-shee-rah lah-ah-doh-NAI kee gah-mahl ah-lahy:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','מזמור זה אמרו שלמה בשעה שהכניס הארון לבית קודש הקודשים, ולא נענה עד שהזכיר זכות דוד. ולפי שכל פסוקי דזמרה הם פסוקי דוד המלך, לפיכך הקדימו מקודם מזמור זה שבו נגלה צדקתו (ערוה"ש נ, ד)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','Psalm 30, once used to inaugurate the Holy Temple, is used today to inaugurate our daily prayers, for the synagogue is a "Holy Temple in miniature" and our prayers take the place of the sacrifices. It is both a prayer for success and a declaration of thanksgiving.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','מִזְמוֹר שִׁיר־חֲנֻכַּת הַבַּֽיִת לְדָוִד: אֲרוֹמִמְךָ יְהֹוָה כִּי דִלִּיתָֽנִי וְלֹא־שִׂמַּֽחְתָּ אֹיְ֒בַי לִי: יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהָי שִׁוַּעְתִּי אֵלֶֽיךָ וַתִּרְפָּאֵֽנִי: יְהֹוָה הֶעֱלִֽיתָ מִן־שְׁאוֹל נַפְשִׁי חִיִּיתַֽנִי מִיָּרְ֒דִי־בוֹר: זַמְּ֒רוּ לַיהוָֹה חֲסִידָיו וְהוֹדוּ לְזֵֽכֶר קָדְשׁוֹ: כִּי רֶֽגַע בְּאַפּוֹ חַיִּים בִּרְצוֹנוֹ בָּעֶֽרֶב יָלִין בֶּֽכִי וְלַבֹּֽקֶר רִנָּה: וַאֲנִי אָמַֽרְתִּי בְשַׁלְוִי בַּל־אֶמּוֹט לְעוֹלָם: יְהֹוָה בִּרְצוֹנְ֒ךָ הֶעֱמַֽדְתָּה לְהַרְרִי עֹז הִסְתַּֽרְתָּ פָנֶֽיךָ הָיִֽיתִי נִבְהָל: אֵלֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֶקְרָא וְאֶל־אֲדֹנָי אֶתְחַנָּן: מַה־בֶּֽצַע בְּדָמִי בְּרִדְתִּי אֶל שָֽׁחַת הֲיוֹדְ֒ךָ עָפָר הֲיַגִּיד אֲמִתֶּֽךָ: שְׁמַע יְהֹוָה וְחָנֵּֽנִי יְהֹוָה הֱיֵה־עֹזֵר לִי: הָפַֽכְתָּ מִסְפְּדִי לְמָחוֹל לִי פִּתַּחְתָּ שַׂקִּי וַתְּ֒אַזְּ֒רֵֽנִי שִׂמְחָה: לְמַֽעַן יְזַמֶּרְךָ כָבוֹד וְלֹא יִדֹּם יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהַי לְעוֹלָם אוֹדֶֽךָּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','A Psalm, a song for the inauguration of the Temple, by David. I will exalt You, Adonoy, for You have upheld me, and not let my foes rejoice over me. Adonoy, my God, I cried out to You, and You healed me. Adonoy, You have raised my soul from the lower world. You have kept me alive, lest I descend to the Pit. Sing to Adonoy, [you,] His pious ones, and give thanks to His holy Name. For His anger lasts only a moment, but there is [long] life, in His conciliation. In the evening, one retires weeping, but in the morning there is [a cry of] joy! I said, in my serenity, I would never be moved. [But,] Adonoy, it was Your will [alone] that established my mountain as a stronghold. When You concealed Your Presence, I was terrified. To You, Adonoy, I called, and my Master I beseeched. What gain is there in [the shedding of] my blood? In my going down to destruction? Will the dust acknowledge You? Will it proclaim Your truth? Hear [me] Adonoy, and be gracious to me, Adonoy, be a help to me. You have turned my mourning into dancing, You have loosened my sackcloth and supported me with joy. In order that my soul might sing to You and not be stilled, Adonoy, my God, forever will I thank You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','meez-mohr sheer khah-noo-kaht hah-bah-yeet le-dah-veed: ah-roh-meem-khah ah-doh-NAI kee dee-lee-tah-nee ve-loh see-mah-khe-tah oh-YE-vahy lee: ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hahy shee-vah-tee eh-ley-khah vah-teer-pah-eh-nee: ah-doh-NAI heh-eh-lee-tah meen she-ohl nahf-shee khee-yee-tah-nee mee-yah-RE-dee VOHR: zah-ME-roo lah-ah-doh-NAI khah-see-dahv ve-hoh-doo le-zeh-khehr kohd-shoh: kee reh-gah be-ah-poh khah-yeem beer-tsoh-noh bah-eh-rehv yah-leen beh-khee ve-lah-boh-kehr ree-nah: vah-ah-nee ah-mah-re-tee ve-shahl-vee bahl eh-moht le-oh-lahm: ah-doh-NAI beer-tsoh-NE-khah heh-ehmah-de-tah le-hahr-ree ohz hees-tah-re-tah fah-ney-khah hah-yee-tee neev-hahl: eh-ley-khah ah-doh-NAI ehk-rah ve-ehl ah-doh-nahy eht-khah-nahn: mahh beh-tsah be-dah-mee be-reed-tee ehl shah-khaht hah-yoh-DE-khah ah-fahr hah-yah-geed ah-mee-teh-khah: she-mah ah-doh-NAI ve-khah-neh-nee ah-doh-NAI heh-yeh oh-zehr lee: hah-fah-khe-tah mees-pe-dee le-mah-khohl lee pee-tahkh-tah sah-kee vah-TE-ah-ZE-reh-nee seem-khah: le-mah-ahn ye-zah-mehr-khah khah-vohd ve-loh yee-dohm ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hahy le-oh-lahm oh-deh-kah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','יְהוָֹה מֶֽלֶךְ, יְהוָֹה מָלָֽךְ, יְהוָֹה יִמְלֹךְ, לְעֹלָם וָעֶד: יְהוָֹה מֶֽלֶךְ, יְהוָֹה מָלָֽךְ, יְהוָֹה יִמְלֹךְ, לְעֹלָם וָעֶד: וְהָיָה יְהוָֹה לְמֶֽלֶךְ עַל־כָּל־הָאָֽרֶץ, בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא יִהְיֶה יְהוָֹה אֶחָד, וּשְׁמוֹ אֶחָד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','Adonoy is King, Adonoy was King Adonoy will be King forever and ever. Adonoy is King, Adonoy was King Adonoy will be King forever and ever. And Adonoy will be King over the whole earth; on that day Adonoy will be One and His Name One.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','ah-doh-NAI meh-lehkh, ah-doh-NAI mah-lahkh, ah-doh-NAI yeem-lohkh, le-oh-lahm vah-ehd: ah-doh-NAI meh-lehkh, ah-doh-NAI mah-lahkh, ah-doh-NAI yeem-lohkh, le-oh-lahm vah-ehd: ve-hah-yah ah-doh-NAI le-meh-lehkh ahl kohl hah-ah-rehts, bah-yohm hah-hoo yeeh-yeh ah-doh-NAI eh-khahd, oo-she-moh eh-khahd:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','הֽוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ יְהוָֹה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ, וְקַבְּ֒צֵֽנוּ מִן־הַגּוֹיִם לְהוֹדוֹת לְשֵׁם קָדְשֶֽׁךָ, לְהִשְׁתַּבֵּֽחַ בִּתְהִלָּתֶֽךָ: בָּרוּךְ יְהוָֹה אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל, מִן־הָֽעוֹלָם וְעַד הָֽעוֹלָם, וְאָמַר כָּל־הָעָם אָמֵן, הַֽלְ֒לוּיָהּ: כֹּל הַנְּ֒שָׁמָה תְּהַלֵּל יָהּ, הַֽלְ֒לוּיָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','Deliver us Adonoy, our God, and gather us from among the nations, to give thanks to Your holy Name— to be extolled in Your praise. Blessed is Adonoy, God of Israel from the world till the next world and all the people said: "Amen, Praise God." Let every soul praise God. Praise God.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','hoh-shee-eh-noo ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo, ve-kah-BE-tseh-noo meen hah-goh-yeem le-hoh-doht le-shehm kohd-sheh-khah, le-heesh-tah-beh-ahkh beet-hee-lah-teh-khah: bah-rookh ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey yees-rah-ehl, meen hah-oh-lahm ve-ahd hah-oh-lahm, ve-ah-mahr kohl hah-ahm ah-mehn, hah-LE-loo-yahh: kohl hah-NE-shah-mah te-hah-lehl yahh, hah-LE-loo-yahh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','לַמְנַצֵּֽחַ בִּנְגִינֹת מִזְמוֹר שִׁיר: אֱלֹהִים יְחָנֵּֽנוּ וִיבָרְ֒כֵֽנוּ יָאֵר פָּנָיו אִתָּֽנוּ סֶֽלָה: לָדַֽעַת בָּאָֽרֶץ דַּרְכֶּֽךָ בְּכָל־גּוֹיִם יְשׁוּעָתֶֽךָ: יוֹדֽוּךָ עַמִּים אֱלֹהִים יוֹדֽוּךָ עַמִּים כֻּלָּם: יִשְׂמְחוּ וִירַנְּ֒נוּ לְאֻמִּים כִּי־תִשְׁפֹּט עַמִּים מִישֹׁר וּלְאֻמִּים בָּאָֽרֶץ תַּנְחֵם סֶֽלָה: יוֹדֽוּךָ עַמִּים אֱלֹהִים יוֹדוּךָ עַמִּים כֻּלָּם: אֶֽרֶץ נָתְ֒נָה יְבוּלָהּ יְבָרְ֒כֵֽנוּ אֱלֹהִים אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ: יְבָֽרְ֒כֵֽנוּ אֱלֹהִים וְיִירְ֒אוּ אוֹתוֹ כָּל־אַפְסֵי־אָֽרֶץ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','To the Chief Musician: a Psalm with instrumental music, a song. [May] God favor us and bless us, [may He] cause His countenance to shine among us Selah; [So] that Your way become known on earth, [and] Your deliverance among all nations. Peoples will thank You, God, all the peoples will thank You. Nations will rejoice and sing when You judge the peoples justly, and lead the nations upon the earth Selah. Peoples will thank You, God, all the peoples will thank You. The earth will have yielded its produce; God, our God, will have blessed us. God will bless us, and they will fear Him— all [men even from] the ends of the earth.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','lahm-nah-tseh-ahkh been-gee-noht meez-mohr sheer: eh-loh-heem ye-khah-neh-noo vee-vah-RE-kheh-noo yah-ehr pah-nahv ee-tah-noo seh-lah: lah-dah-aht bah-ah-rehts dahr-keh-khah be-khohl goh-yeem ye-shoo-ah-teh-khah: yoh-doo-khah ah-meem eh-loh-heem yoh-doo-khah ah-meem koo-lahm: yees-me-khoo vee-rah-NE-noo le-oo-meem kee teesh-poht ah-meem mee-shohr oo-le-oo-meem bah-ah-rehts tahn-khehm seh-lah: yoh-doo-khah ah-meem eh-loh-heem yoh-doo-khah ah-meem koo-lahm: eh-rehts nah-TE-nah ye-voo-lahh ye-vah-RE-kheh-noo eh-loh-heem eh-loh-hey-noo: ye-vah-RE-kheh-noo eh-loh-heem ve-yee-RE-oo oh-toh kohl ahf-sey ah-rehts:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','ברוך שאמר צריך לאומרו בניגון ובנעימה כי הוא שיר נאה ונחמד. וכתב בספר היכלות שיש בו פ"ז תיבות וסי'' ראשו כתם פז (טור או"ח נא)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','This blessing introduces the Pesukei Dezimrah . It was mentioned by Rabbi Isaac Alfasi (Rif) over 800 years ago in his commentary to Maseches Berachos 32. The Taz (Orach Chaim 51:1) states that this prayer was instituted by the "Men of the Great Assembly." The blessing contains eighty-seven words suggesting the numerical value of פָּז poz, refined gold.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','בָּרוּךְ שֶׁאָמַר וְהָיָה הָעוֹלָם, בָּרוּךְ הוּא, בָּרוּךְ עֹשֶׂה בְרֵאשִׁית, בָּרוּךְ אוֹמֵר וְעוֹשֶׂה, בָּרוּךְ גּוֹזֵר וּמְקַיֵּם, בָּרוּךְ מְרַחֵם עַל הָאָֽרֶץ, בָּרוּךְ מְרַחֵם עַל הַבְּ֒רִיּוֹת, בָּרוּךְ מְשַׁלֵּם שָׂכָר טוֹב לִירֵאָיו, בָּרוּךְ חַי לָעַד וְקַיָּם לָנֶֽצַח, בָּרוּךְ פּוֹדֶה וּמַצִּיל, בָּרוּךְ שְׁמוֹ: בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם הָאֵל הָאָב הָרַחֲמָן הַמְּ֒הֻלָּל בְּפֶה עַמּוֹ מְשֻׁבָּח וּמְפֹאָר בִּלְשׁוֹן חֲסִידָיו וַעֲבָדָיו וּבְשִׁירֵי דָוִד עַבְדֶּֽךָ, נְהַלֶּלְךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ בִּשְׁבָחוֹת וּבִזְמִירוֹת נְגַדֶּלְךָ וּנְשַׁבֵּחֲךָ וּנְפָאֶרְךָ וְנַזְכִּיר שִׁמְךָ וְנַמְלִיכְךָ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ, יָחִיד, חֵי הָעוֹלָמִים מֶֽלֶךְ מְשֻׁבָּח וּמְפֹאָר עֲדֵי עַד שְׁמוֹ הַגָּדוֹל: בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה מֶֽלֶךְ מְהֻלָּל בַּתִּשְׁבָּחוֹת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','Blessed is He Who spoke, and the world came into being, blessed is He; blessed is He Who maintains the creation; blessed is He Who says and does; blessed is He Who decrees and fulfills; blessed is He Who has compassion on the earth; blessed is He Who has compassion on the creatures; blessed is He Who rewards well those who fear Him, blessed is He Who lives forever and exists eternally; blessed is He Who redeems and saves blessed is His Name. Blessed are You, Adonoy, our God, King of the Universe, the Almighty, the merciful Father, Who is verbally extolled by His people, praised and glorified by the tongue of His pious ones, and His servants, and through the songs of David Your servant. We will extoll You, Adonoy our God, with praises and psalms; we will exalt, praise, and glorify You; we will mention Your Name, and proclaim You—our King, our God. Unique One, Life of the worlds, King, praised and glorified forever is His great Name. Blessed are You, Adonoy, King, Who is extolled with praises.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','bah-rookh sheh-ah-mahr ve-hah-yah hah-oh-lahm, bah-rookh hoo, bah-rookh oh-seh ve-reh-sheet, bah-rookh oh-mehr ve-oh-seh, bah-rookh goh-zehr oo-me-kah-yehm, bah-rookh me-rah-khehm ahl hah-ah-rehts, bah-rookh me-rah-khehm ahl hah-BE-ree-yoht, bah-rookh me-shah-lehm sah-khahr tohv lee-reh-ahv, bah-rookh khahy lah-ahd ve-kah-yahm lah-neh-tsahkh, bah-rookh poh-deh oo-mah-tseel, bah-rookh she-moh: bah-rookh ah-tah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo meh-lehkh hah-oh-lahm hah-ehl hah-ahv hah-rah-khah-mahn hah-ME-hoo-lahl be-feh ah-moh me-shoo-bahkh oo-me-foh-ahr beel-shohn khah-see-dahv vah-ah-vah-dahv oo-ve-shee-rey dah-veed ahv-deh-khah, ne-hah-lehl-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo beesh-vah-khoht oo-veez-mee-roht ne-gah-dehl-khah oo-ne-shah-beh-khah-khah oo-ne-fah-ehr-khah ve-nahz-keer sheem-khah ve-nahm-lee-khe-khah mahl-keh-noo eh-loh-hey-noo, yah-kheed, khey hah-oh-lah-meem meh-lehkh me-shoo-bahkh oo-me-foh-ahr ah-dey ahd she-moh hah-gah-dohl: bah-rookh ah-tah ah-doh-NAI meh-lehkh me-hoo-lahl bah-teesh-bah-khoht:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','מזמור לתודה יש לאומרו בנגינה שכל השירות עתידות ליבטל חוץ ממזמור לתודה (ראה ויק"ר ט,ז). ואין אומרים מזמור לתודה בשבת ויו"ט, או בימי פסח שאין תודה קריבה בהם משום חמץ, ולא בערב פסח.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','Psalm 100 was recited in the Temple only on those days when thank-offerings were offered on the Altar. It is therefore omitted on Shabbos, on Yom Tov, on the day before Yom Kippur, on the day before Pesach, and also on the intermediate days of Pesach, when only obligatory-offerings were offered. Our Sages declare (Midrash Rabbah Tzav, 9) "In the future, even though all things on earth will be in such an ideal state that there will be no more cause for prayers and offerings, prayers of gratitude, and offerings of thanksgiving will nevertheless not cease." Ordinarily, when a person is saved from a fatal illness, is released from captivity, or returns from a risky journey, he pronounces the special blessing Hagomeil. Our Sages, instituted psalm 100 in our daily prayers as an expression of thanks for the many unrecognized miracles God performs in our behalf every day.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','מִזְמוֹר לְתוֹדָה הָרִֽיעוּ לַיהוָֹה כָּל־הָאָֽרֶץ: עִבְדוּ אֶת יְהֹוָה בְּשִׂמְחָה בֹּֽאוּ לְפָנָיו בִּרְנָנָה: דְּעוּ כִּי־יְהֹוָה הוּא אֱלֹהִים הוּא עָשָֽׂנוּ וְלוֹ (וְלֹא) אֲנַֽחְנוּ עַמּוֹ וְצֹאן מַרְעִיתוֹ: בֹּֽאוּ שְׁעָרָיו בְּתוֹדָה חֲצֵרֹתָיו בִּתְהִלָּה הֽוֹדוּ לוֹ בָּרְ֒כוּ שְׁמוֹ: כִּי־טוֹב יְהֹוָה לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ וְעַד־דֹּר וָדֹר אֱמוּנָתוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','A psalm of thanksgiving: Shout for joy to Adonoy, everyone on earth. Serve Adony with joy, come before Him with exultation. Know that Adonoy is God, He has made us, and we are His, His people and the sheep of His pasturing. Enter His gates with thanksgiving, His courtyards with praise. Give thanks to Him, bless His Name for Adonoy is good, His loving kindness is eternal, and to every generation His faithfulness [extends.]','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','meez-mohr le-toh-dah hah-ree-oo lah-ah-doh-NAI kohl hah-ah-rehts: eev-doo eht ah-doh-NAI be-seem-khah boh-oo le-fah-nahv beer-nah-nah: de-oo kee ah-doh-NAI hoo eh-loh-heem hoo ah-sah-noo ve-loh (ve-loh) ahnah-khe-noo ah-moh ve-tsohn mahr-ee-toh: boh-oo she-ah-rahv be-toh-dah khah-tseh-roh-tahv beet-hee-lah hoh-doo loh bah-RE-khoo she-moh: kee tohv ah-doh-NAI le-oh-lahm khahs-doh ve-ahd dohr vah-dohr eh-moo-nah-toh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','שמונה עשר פסוקי יהי כבוד כנגד שמונה עשרה ברכות דשמונה עשרה. ולפיכך הכניסום בתוך פסוקי דזמרה. (ערוך השולחן, אורח חיים נ, ד)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','This prayer, mentioned in Maseches Sof''rim 17:11 is a collection of 18 verses from Psalms, Chronicles, and Proverbs, in which the Divine Name (הויה) is mentioned 18 times. Great care should be taken to pronounce the "Name" with the utmost concentration, keeping in mind that He is the Supreme Master of all that exists.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','יְהִי כְבוֹד יְהֹוָה לְעוֹלָם יִשְׂמַח יְהֹוָה בְּמַעֲשָׂיו: יְהִי שֵׁם יְהֹוָה מְבֹרָךְ מֵעַתָּה וְעַד־עוֹלָם: מִמִּזְרַח־שֶֽׁמֶשׁ עַד־מְבוֹאוֹ מְהֻלָּל שֵׁם יְהֹוָה: רָם עַל־כָּל־גּוֹיִם יְהֹוָה עַל הַשָּׁמַֽיִם כְּבוֹדוֹ: יְהֹוָה שִׁמְךָ לְעוֹלָם יְהֹוָה זִכְרְ֒ךָ לְדֹר־וָדֹר: יְהֹוָה בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם הֵכִין כִּסְאוֹ וּמַלְכוּתוֹ בַּכֹּל מָשָֽׁלָה: יִשְׂמְחוּ הַשָּׁמַֽיִם וְתָגֵל הָאָֽרֶץ וְיֹאמְ֒רוּ בַגּוֹיִם יְהֹוָה מָלָךְ: יְהֹוָה מֶֽלֶךְ יְהֹוָה מָלָךְ יְהֹוָה יִמְלֹךְ לְעֹלָם וָעֶד: יְהֹוָה מֶֽלֶךְ עוֹלָם וָעֶד אָבְ֒דוּ גוֹיִם מֵאַרְצוֹ: יְהֹוָה הֵפִיר עֲצַת־גּוֹיִם הֵנִיא מַחְשְׁבוֹת עַמִּים: רַבּוֹת מַחֲשָׁבוֹת בְּלֶב־אִישׁ וַעֲצַת יְהֹוָה הִיא תָקוּם: עֲצַת יְהֹוָה לְעוֹלָם תַּעֲמֹד מַחְשְׁבוֹת לִבּוֹ לְדֹר וָדֹר: כִּי הוּא אָמַר וַיֶּֽהִי הוּא־צִוָּה וַיַּעֲמֹד: כִּי בָחַר יְהֹוָה בְּצִיּוֹן אִוָּהּ לְמוֹשָׁב לוֹ: כִּי־יַעֲקֹב בָּחַר לוֹ יָהּ יִשְׂרָאֵל לִסְגֻלָּתוֹ: כִּי לֹא יִטּשׁ יְהֹוָה עַמּוֹ וְנַחֲלָתוֹ לֹא יַעֲזֹב: וְהוּא רַחוּם יְכַפֵּר עָוֹן וְלֹא־יַשְׁחִית וְהִרְבָּה לְהָשִׁיב אַפּוֹ וְלֹא־יָעִיר כָּל־חֲמָתוֹ: יְהֹוָה הוֹשִׁיעָה הַמֶּֽלֶךְ יַעֲנֵֽנוּ בְיוֹם־קָרְאֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','The glory of Adonoy will endure forever; Adonoy will rejoice in His works. The Name of Adonoy will be blessed from now forever. From the rising of the sun to its setting, praised is the Name of Adonoy. High above all nations is Adonoy, above the heavens is His glory. Adonoy, Your Name is forever, Adonoy, Your Mention is for generations. Adonoy has established His throne in heaven, [but] His dominion rules over all. The heavens will rejoice, the earth will exult, and they will proclaim among the nations: Adonoy has begun His reign. Adonoy is King, Adonoy was King; Adonoy will be King forever and ever." Adonoy will reign for all eternity [when] nations have perished from His earth. Adonoy annuls the counsel of nations, He disrupts the intention of peoples. Many thoughts are in the heart of man, but [only] Adonoy''s counsel will endure. The counsel of Adonoy will stand forever, the thoughts of His heart throughout all generations. For He spoke and it came to be; He commanded and it stood. For Adonoy has chosen Zion; He desired it for His dwelling place. For God chose Jacob to be His, Israel for His treasure. For Adonoy will not cast off His people, and His inheritance, He will not abandon. And He, the Merciful One, atones iniquity; and does not destroy. He frequently withdraws His anger and does not arouse all His rage. Adonoy, deliver [us!] The King will answer us on the day we call.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:16:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','ye-hee khe-vohd ah-doh-NAI le-oh-lahm yees-mahkh ah-doh-NAI be-mah-ah-sahv: ye-hee shehm ah-doh-NAI me-voh-rahkh meh-ah-tah ve-ahd oh-lahm: mee-meez-rahkh sheh-mehsh ahd me-voh-oh me-hoo-lahl shehm ah-doh-NAI: rahm ahl kohl goh-yeem ah-doh-NAI ahl hah-shah-mah-yeem ke-voh-doh: ah-doh-NAI sheem-khah le-oh-lahm ah-doh-NAI zeekh-RE-khah le-dohr vah-dohr: ah-doh-NAI bah-shah-mah-yeem heh-kheen kees-oh oo-mahl-khoo-toh bah-kohl mah-shah-lah: yees-me-khoo hah-shah-mah-yeem ve-tah-gehl hah-ah-rehts ve-yoh-ME-roo vah-goh-yeem ah-doh-NAI mah-lahkh: ah-doh-NAI meh-lehkh ah-doh-NAI mah-lahkh ah-doh-NAI yeem-lohkh le-oh-lahm vah-ehd: ah-doh-NAI meh-lehkh oh-lahm vah-ehd ah-VE-doo goh-yeem meh-ahr-tsoh: ah-doh-NAI heh-feer ah-tsaht goh-yeem heh-nee mahkh-she-voht ah-meem: rah-boht mah-khah-shah-voht be-lehv eesh vah-ah-tsaht ah-doh-NAI hee tah-koom: ah-tsaht ah-doh-NAI le-oh-lahm tah-ah-mohd mahkh-she-voht lee-boh le-dohr vah-dohr: kee hoo ah-mahr vah-yeh-hee hoo tsee-vah vah-yah-ah-mohd: kee vah-khahr ah-doh-NAI be-tsee-yohn ee-vahh le-moh-shahv loh: kee yah-ah-kohv bah-khahr loh yahh yees-rah-ehl lees-goo-lah-toh: kee loh yeetsh ah-doh-NAI ah-moh ve-nah-khah-lah-toh loh yah-ah-zohv: ve-hoo rah-khoom ye-khah-pehr ah-vohn ve-loh yahsh-kheet ve-heer-bah le-hah-sheev ah-poh ve-loh yah-eer kohl khah-mah-toh: ah-doh-NAI hoh-shee-ah hah-meh-lehkh yah-ah-neh-noo ve-yohm kah-re-eh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','צריך לכוין בתהלה לדוד דא"ר אלעזר כל האומר תהלה לדוד בכל יום ג"פ מובטח לו שהוא בן העולם הבא. ויותר יכוין בפסוק פותח את ידך, שעיקר מה שקבעוהו לומר בכל יום הוא בשביל אותו פסוק, שמזכיר בו שבחו של הקב"ה שמשגיח על בריותיו ומפרנסן. ונהגו לומר קודם לכן אשרי יושבי ביתך משום דילפינן מיניה שצריך אדם לישב שעה אחת קודם שיתפלל. ואחריו נהגו לומר ואנחנו נברך יה (טור, אורח חיים נ"א)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','Rav S.R. Hirsch writes that the six concluding chapters of the Book of Psalms are the most important gift of David''s Divinely-inspired hymns that Israel treasures so greatly. These six psalms, 145-150, are an essential component of our daily prayers. Our Sages attach much significance to Psalm 145 in particular, and stated: "Whoever recites ‘A praise by David'' three times a day is assuredly worthy of a share in the world to come" (Maseches Berachos 4b). When recited in prayer this psalm is always introduced with two verses from other Psalms (84:5 and 144:15). These verses contain the word fortunate three times, an allusion to this psalm being recited three times a day. These verses are so closely identified with Psalm 145 that it is commonly referred to as Ashrei (Fortunate).','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','אַשְׁרֵי יוֹשְׁ֒בֵי בֵיתֶֽךָ עוֹד יְהַלְ֒לֽוּךָ סֶּֽלָה: אַשְׁרֵי הָעָם שֶׁכָּֽכָה לּוֹ אַשְׁרֵי הָעָם שֶׁיְהֹוָה אֱלֹהָיו: תְּהִלָּה לְדָוִד אֲרוֹמִמְךָ אֱלוֹהַי הַמֶּֽלֶךְ וַאֲבָרְ֒כָה שִׁמְךָ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד: בְּכָל־יוֹם אֲבָרְ֒כֶֽךָּ וַאֲהַלְ֒לָה שִׁמְךָ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד: גָּדוֹל יְהֹוָה וּמְהֻלָּל מְאֹד וְלִגְדֻלָּתוֹ אֵין חֵֽקֶר: דּוֹר לְדוֹר יְשַׁבַּח מַעֲשֶׂיךָ וּגְבוּרֹתֶֽיךָ יַגִּֽידוּ: הֲדַר כְּבוֹד הוֹדֶֽךָ וְדִבְרֵי נִפְלְ֒אֹתֶֽיךָ אָשִֽׂיחָה: וֶעֱזוּז נוֹרְ֒אֹתֶֽיךָ יֹאמֵרוּ וּגְדֻלָּתְ֒ךָ אֲסַפְּ֒רֶֽנָּה: זֵֽכֶר רַב־טוּבְ֒ךָ יַבִּֽיעוּ וְצִדְקָתְ֒ךָ יְרַנֵּֽנוּ: חַנּוּן וְרַחוּם יְהֹוָה אֶֽרֶךְ אַפַּֽיִם וּגְדָל־חָֽסֶד: טוֹב־יְהֹוָה לַכֹּל וְרַחֲמָיו עַל־כָּל־מַעֲשָׂיו: יוֹדֽוּךָ יְהֹוָה כָּל־מַעֲשֶֽׂיךָ וַחֲסִידֶֽיךָ יְבָרְ֒כֽוּכָה: כְּבוֹד מַלְכוּתְ֒ךָ יֹאמֵרוּ וּגְבוּרָתְ֒ךָ יְדַבֵּֽרוּ: לְהוֹדִֽיעַ לִבְנֵי הָאָדָם גְּבוּרֹתָיו וּכְבוֹד הֲדַר מַלְכוּתוֹ: מַלְכוּתְ֒ךָ מַלְכוּת כָּל־עֹלָמִים וּמֶמְשַׁלְתְּ֒ךָ בְּכָל־דּוֹר וָדֹר: סוֹמֵךְ יְהֹוָה לְכָל־הַנֹּפְ֒לִים וְזוֹקֵף לְכָל־הַכְּ֒פוּפִים: עֵינֵי־כֹל אֵלֶֽיךָ יְשַׂבֵּֽרוּ וְאַתָּה נוֹתֵן־לָהֶם אֶת־אָכְלָם בְּעִתּוֹ: פּוֹתֵֽחַ אֶת־יָדֶֽךָ וּמַשְׂבִּֽיעַ לְכָל־חַי רָצוֹן: צַדִּיק יְהֹוָה בְּכָל־דְּרָכָיו וְחָסִיד בְּכָל־מַעֲשָׂיו: קָרוֹב יְהֹוָה לְכָל־קֹרְ֒אָיו לְכֹל אֲשֶׁר יִקְרָאֻֽהוּ בֶאֱמֶת: רְצוֹן־יְרֵאָיו יַעֲשֶׂה וְאֶת־שַׁוְעָתָם יִשְׁמַע וְיוֹשִׁיעֵם: שׁוֹמֵר יְהֹוָה אֶת־כָּל־אֹהֲבָיו וְאֵת כָּל־הָרְ֒שָׁעִים יַשְׁמִיד: תְּהִלַּת יְהֹוָה יְדַבֶּר פִּי וִיבָרֵךְ כָּל־בָּשָׂר שֵׁם קָדְשׁוֹ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד: וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ נְבָרֵךְ יָהּ מֵעַתָּה וְעַד־עוֹלָם הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','Fortunate are those who dwell in Your house; may they continue to praise You, Selah. Fortunate is the people whose lot is thus; fortunate is the people for whom Adonoy is their God. A praise by David! I will exalt You, my God, the King, and bless Your Name forever and ever. Every day I will bless You and extol Your Name forever and ever. Adonoy is great and highly extolled, and His greatness is unfathomable. One generation to another will praise Your works, and Your mighty acts they will declare. The splendor of Your glorious majesty, and the words of Your wonders I will speak. Of Your awesome might, they will speak, and Your greatness I will recount. Mention of Your bountifulness they will express, and in Your righteousness joyfully exult. Adonoy is gracious and merciful, slow to anger and great in kindliness. Adonoy is good to all, His mercy encompasses all His works. All Your works will thank You, Adonoy, and Your pious ones will bless You. Of the honor of Your kingship, they will speak, and Your might they will declare. To reveal to men His mighty acts, and the glorious splendor of His kingship. Your kingship is the kingship for all times, and Your dominion is in every generation. Adonoy supports all the fallen, and straightens all the bent. The eyes of all look expectantly to You, and You give them their food at its proper time. You open Your hand and satisfy the desire of every living being. Adonoy is just in all His ways and benevolent in all His deeds. Adonoy is near to all who call upon Him, to all who call upon Him in truth. The will of those who fear Him, He fulfills; He hears their cry and delivers them. Adonoy watches over all those who love Him, and will destroy all the wicked. Praise of Adonoy, my mouth will declare and all flesh will bless His holy Name forever and ever. And we will bless God from now forever. Praise God.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:18:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','ahsh-rey yoh-SHE-vey vey-teh-khah ohd ye-hah-LE-loo-khah seh-lah: ahsh-rey hah-ahm sheh-kah-khah loh ahsh-rey hah-ahm shehy-ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hahv: te-hee-lah le-dah-veed ah-roh-meem-khah eh-loh-hahy hah-meh-lehkh vah-ah-vah-RE-khah sheem-khah le-oh-lahm vah-ehd: be-khohl yohm ah-vah-RE-kheh-kah vah-ah-hah-LE-lah sheem-khah le-oh-lahm vah-ehd: gah-dohl ah-doh-NAI oo-me-hoo-lahl me-ohd ve-leeg-doo-lah-toh eyn kheh-kehr: dohr le-dohr ye-shah-bahkh mah-ah-sey-khah oo-ge-voo-roh-tey-khah yah-gee-doo: hah-dahr ke-vohd hoh-deh-khah ve-deev-rey neef-LE-oh-tey-khah ah-see-khah: veh-eh-zooz noh-RE-oh-tey-khah yoh-meh-roo oo-ge-doo-lah-TE-khah ah-sah-PE-reh-nah: zeh-khehr rahv too-VE-khah yah-bee-oo ve-tseed-kah-TE-khah ye-rah-neh-noo: khah-noon ve-rah-khoom ah-doh-NAI eh-rehkh ah-pah-yeem oo-ge-dahl khah-sehd: tohv ah-doh-NAI lah-kohl ve-rah-khah-mahv ahl kohl mah-ah-sahv: yoh-doo-khah ah-doh-NAI kohl mah-ah-sey-khah vah-khah-see-dey-khah ye-vah-RE-khoo-khah: ke-vohd mahl-khoo-TE-khah yoh-meh-roo oo-ge-voo-rah-TE-khah ye-dah-beh-roo: le-hoh-dee-ah leev-ney hah-ah-dahm ge-voo-roh-tahv oo-khe-vohd hah-dahr mahl-khoo-toh: mahl-khoo-TE-khah mahl-khoot kohl oh-lah-meem oo-mehm-shahl-TE-khah be-khohl dohr vah-dohr: soh-mehkh ah-doh-NAI le-khohl hah-noh-FE-leem ve-zoh-kehf le-khohl hah-KE-foo-feem: ey-ney khohl eh-ley-khah ye-sah-beh-roo ve-ah-tah noh-tehn lah-hehm eht ohkh-lahm be-ee-toh: poh-teh-ahkh eht yah-deh-khah oo-mahs-bee-ah le-khohl khahy rah-tsohn: tsah-deek ah-doh-NAI be-khohl de-rah-khahv ve-khah-seed be-khohl mah-ah-sahv: kah-rohv ah-doh-NAI le-khohl koh-RE-ahv le-khohl ah-shehr yeek-rah-oo-hoo veh-eh-meht: re-tsohn ye-reh-ahv yah-ah-seh ve-eht shahv-ah-tahm yeesh-mah ve-yoh-shee-ehm: shoh-mehr ah-doh-NAI eht kohl oh-hah-vahv ve-eht kohl hah-RE-shah-eem yahsh-meed: te-hee-laht ah-doh-NAI ye-dah-behr pee vee-vah-rehkh kohl bah-sahr shehm kohd-shoh le-oh-lahm vah-ehd: vah-ahnah-khe-noo ne-vah-rehkh yahh meh-ah-tah ve-ahd oh-lahm hah-LE-loo-yahh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','זה המזמור מעורר לאדם לעשות תשובה ומעשים טובים בחיים חיותו בעוד שיש נשמתו בו ואל יבטח בבני אדם שאינם יכולים להושיע לעצמם כי בפתע פתאום תצא רוחם מהם לכך מן הראוי לבטוח בהקב"ה שבידו לקיים מה שרוצה לעשות.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','This Psalm acclaims God''s loving care as experienced by each Jew in his own life.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ הַלְ֒לִי נַפְשִׁי אֶת־יְהֹוָה: אֲהַלְ֒לָה יְהֹוָה בְּחַיָּי אֲזַמְּ֒רָה לֵאלֹהַי בְּעוֹדִי: אַל־תִּבְטְחוּ בִנְדִיבִים בְּבֶן־אָדָם שֶׁאֵין לוֹ תְשׁוּעָה: תֵּצֵא רוּחוֹ יָשֻׁב לְאַדְמָתוֹ בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא אָבְ֒דוּ עֶשְׁתֹּנֹתָיו: אַשְׁרֵי שֶׁאֵל יַעֲקֹב בְּעֶזְרוֹ, שִׂבְרוֹ עַל־יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהָיו: עֹשֶׂה שָׁמַֽיִם וָאָֽרֶץ אֶת־הַיָּם וְאֶת־כָּל־אֲשֶׁר־בָּם, הַשֹּׁמֵר אֱמֶת לְעוֹלָם: עֹשֶׂה מִשְׁפָּט לַעֲשׁוּקִים נֹתֵן לֶֽחֶם לָרְ֒עֵבִים יְהֹוָה מַתִּיר אֲסוּרִים: יְהֹוָה פֹּקֵֽחַ עִוְרִים יְהֹוָה זֹקֵף כְּפוּפִים יְהֹוָה אֹהֵב צַדִּיקִים: יְהֹוָה שֹׁמֵר אֶת־גֵּרִים יָתוֹם וְאַלְמָנָה יְעוֹדֵד וְדֶֽרֶךְ רְשָׁעִים יְעַוֵּת: יִמְלֹךְ יְהֹוָה לְעוֹלָם אֱלֹהַֽיִךְ צִיּוֹן לְדֹר וָדֹר הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','Praise God! My soul, praise Adonoy. I will praise Adonoy with my life; I will sing to my God as long as I live. Do not place your trust [even] in noble men, in man who has no [power of] deliverance. [When] his spirit departs, he returns to his earth; on that day his plans come to naught. Fortunate [is he] when the Almighty of Jacob is his help, whose expectation is on Adonoy, his God. He makes heaven and earth, the sea and all that is in them; He keeps His promises faithfully forever. He performs justice for the oppressed; He gives bread to the hungry; Adonoy releases the imprisoned. Adonoy gives sight to the blind; Adonoy straightens the bent. Adonoy loves the righteous. Adonoy protects strangers; the orphan and widow He enables to stand firm; and the way of the wicked He thwarts. Adonoy will reign forever; your God, Zion, throughout all generations. Praise God.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:20:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','hah-LE-loo-yahh hah-LE-lee nahf-shee eht ah-doh-NAI: ah-hah-LE-lah ah-doh-NAI be-khah-yahy ah-zah-ME-rah leh-loh-hahy be-oh-dee: ahl teev-te-khoo veen-dee-veem be-vehn ah-dahm sheh-eyn loh te-shoo-ah: teh-tseh roo-khoh yah-shoov le-ahd-mah-toh bah-yohm hah-hoo ah-VE-doo ehsh-toh-noh-tahv: ahsh-rey sheh-ehl yah-ah-kohv be-ehz-roh, seev-roh ahl ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hahv: oh-seh shah-mah-yeem vah-ah-rehts eht hah-yahm ve-eh-t- -kohl ah-shehr bahm, hah-shoh-mehr eh-meht le-oh-lahm: oh-seh meesh-paht lah-ah-shoo-keem noh-tehn leh-khehm lah-RE-eh-veem ah-doh-NAI mah-teer ah-soo-reem: ah-doh-NAI poh-keh-ahkh eev-reem ah-doh-NAI zoh-kehf ke-foo-feem ah-doh-NAI oh-hehv tsah-dee-keem: ah-doh-NAI shoh-mehr eht geh-reem yah-tohm ve-ahl-mah-nah ye-oh-dehd ve-deh-rehkh re-shah-eem ye-ah-veht: yeem-lohkh ah-doh-NAI le-oh-lahm eh-loh-hah-yeekh tsee-yohn le-dohr vah-dohr hah-LE-loo-yahh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','המזמור הזה מדבר מן הגאולה העתידה במהרה בימינו','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','In this Psalm, David imparts the knowledge to sustain and uphold the Jewish People, during their bitter exile. He tells them of their special and enduring relationship with God and of their role as permanent messengers of the word of God to all mankind.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ כִּי־טוֹב זַמְּ֒רָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ, כִּי־נָעִים נָאוָה תְהִלָּה: בּוֹנֵה יְרוּשָׁלַֽםִ יְהֹוָה נִדְחֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל יְכַנֵּס: הָרוֹפֵא לִשְׁבֽוּרֵי לֵב וּמְחַבֵּשׁ לְעַצְּ֒בוֹתָם: מוֹנֶה מִסְפָּר לַכּוֹכָבִים לְכֻלָּם שֵׁמוֹת יִקְרָא: גָּדוֹל אֲדוֹנֵֽינוּ וְרַב־כֹּֽחַ לִתְבוּנָתוֹ אֵין מִסְפָּר: מְעוֹדֵד עֲנָוִים יְהֹוָה מַשְׁפִּיל רְשָׁעִים עֲדֵי־אָֽרֶץ: עֱנוּ לַיהוָֹה בְּתוֹדָה זַמְּ֒רוּ לֵאלֹהֵֽינוּ בְכִנּוֹר: הַמְכַסֶּה שָׁמַֽיִם בְּעָבִים הַמֵּכִין לָאָֽרֶץ מָטָר הַמַּצְמִֽיחַ הָרִים חָצִיר: נוֹתֵן לִבְהֵמָה לַחְמָהּ לִבְנֵי עֹרֵב אֲשֶׁר יִקְרָֽאוּ: לֹא בִגְבוּרַת הַסּוּס יֶחְפָּץ לֹא בְשׁוֹקֵי הָאִישׁ יִרְצֶה: רוֹצֶה יְהֹוָה אֶת־יְרֵאָיו אֶת־הַמְ֒יַחֲלִים לְחַסְדּוֹ: שַׁבְּ֒חִי יְרוּשָׁלַֽםִ אֶת יְהֹוָה הַלְ֒לִי אֱלֹהַֽיִךְ צִיּוֹן: כִּי־חִזַּק בְּרִיחֵי שְׁעָרָֽיִךְ בֵּרַךְ בָּנַֽיִךְ בְּקִרְבֵּךְ: הַשָּׂם־גְּבוּלֵךְ שָׁלוֹם חֵֽלֶב חִטִּים יַשְׂבִּיעֵךְ: הַשֹּׁלֵֽחַ אִמְרָתוֹ אָֽרֶץ עַד־מְהֵרָה יָרוּץ דְּבָרוֹ: הַנֹּתֵן שֶֽׁלֶג כַּצָּֽמֶר כְּפוֹר כָּאֵֽפֶר יְפַזֵּר: מַשְׁלִיךְ קַרְחוֹ כְפִתִּים לִפְנֵי קָרָתוֹ מִי יַעֲמֹד: יִשְׁלַח דְּבָרוֹ וְיַמְסֵם יַשֵּׁב רוּחוֹ יִזְּ֒לוּ־מָֽיִם: מַגִּיד דְּבָרָיו לְיַעֲקֹב חֻקָּיו וּמִשְׁפָּטָיו לְיִשְׂרָאֵל: לֹא עָֽשָׂה כֵן לְכָל־גּוֹי וּמִשְׁפָּטִים בַּל־יְדָעוּם הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','Praise God! for it is good to sing to our God; for [His] praise is pleasant, befitting. The builder of Jerusalem is Adonoy; the banished ones of Israel He will gather. [He is] the Healer of the broken-hearted and [also] binds up their wounds. He fixes the number of stars; He calls all of them by names. Great is our Master and abundant in power; His understanding is beyond reckoning. Adonoy causes the humble to stand firm; He casts down the wicked to the ground. Cry out to Adonoy in thanksgiving; sing to our God with the harp. [He] Who covers the heaven with clouds, Who prepares rain for the earth; Who causes grass to grow upon the hills. Who gives the animal its fodder; [also] to the young ravens which call. Not the power of the horse does He desire, nor the thighs of man does He want. Adonoy wants those who fear Him, those who hope for His kindliness. Jerusalem, praise Adonoy; Zion, extol your God. For He has fortified the bars of your gates; He has blessed your children in your midst. He established peace at your border; with prime wheat He satisfies you. He dispatches His command earthward; His word races swiftly. He provides snow like fleece, He scatters frost like ashes. He hurls His ice like crumbs; who can withstand His cold? He dispatches His word and melts them; He blows His wind, they flow as water. He declares His word to Jacob, His statutes and His laws to Israel. He did not do so to any [other] nation; and of His laws they were not informed. Praise God.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:22:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','hah-LE-loo-yahh kee tohv zah-ME-rah eh-loh-hey-noo, kee nah-eem nah-vah te-hee-lah: boh-neh ye-roo-shah-lah-mee ah-doh-NAI need-khey yees-rah-ehl ye-khah-nehs: hah-roh-feh leesh-voo-rey lehv oo-me-khah-behsh le-ah-TSE-voh-tahm: moh-neh mees-pahr lah-koh-khah-veem le-khoo-lahm sheh-moht yeek-rah: gah-dohl ah-doh-ney-noo ve-rahv koh-ahkh leet-voo-nah-toh eyn mees-pahr: me-oh-dehd ah-nah-veem ah-doh-NAI mahsh-peel re-shah-eem ah-dey ah-rehts: eh-noo lah-ah-doh-NAI be-toh-dah zah-ME-roo leh-loh-hey-noo ve-khee-nohr: hah-me-khah-seh shah-mah-yeem be-ah-veem hah-meh-kheen lah-ah-rehts mah-tahr hah-mahts-mee-ahkh hah-reem khah-tseer: noh-tehn leev-heh-mah lahkh-mahh leev-ney oh-rehv ah-shehr yeek-rah-oo: loh veeg-voo-raht hah-soos yehkh-pahts loh ve-shoh-key hah-eesh yeer-tseh: roh-tseh ah-doh-NAI eht ye-reh-ahv eht hah-ME-yah-khah-leem le-khahs-doh: shah-BE-khee ye-roo-shah-lah-mee eht ah-doh-NAI hah-LE-lee eh-loh-hah-yeekh tsee-yohn: kee khee-zahk be-ree-khey she-ah-rah-yeekh beh-rahkh bah-nah-yeekh be-keer-behkh: hah-sahm ge-voo-lehkh shah-lohm kheh-lehv khee-teem yahs-bee-ehkh: hah-shoh-leh-ahkh eem-rah-toh ah-rehts ahd me-heh-rah yah-roots de-vah-roh: hah-noh-tehn sheh-lehg kah-tsah-mehr ke-fohr kah-eh-fehr ye-fah-zehr: mahsh-leekh kahr-khoh khe-fee-teem leef-ney kah-rah-toh mee yah-ah-mohd: yeesh-lahkh de-vah-roh ve-yahm-sehm yah-shehv roo-khoh yee-ZE-loo mah-YEEM: mah-geed de-vah-rahv le-yah-ah-kohv khoo-kahv oo-meesh-pah-tahv le-yees-rah-ehl: loh ah-sah khehn le-khohl gohy oo-meesh-pah-teem bahl ye-dah-oom hah-LE-loo-yahh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','בפרק זה התחיל המשורר מעולם הגדול ועד עולם הקטן עיין נוראים מבריאת הקב"ה העליונים והתחתונים כולם עומדים בכוחו','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','In this psalm, David sings of the moment when all the world will be imbued with the knowledge of God''s all-embracing providence. All living creatures—from the infinite heights of heaven above (verses 1-7) down to the depths of the earth below (verses 7-12)—will join together in one great hymn of praise to their Creator, and acknowledge the uniqueness of Israel over all other nations.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ הַלְ֒לוּ אֶת־יְהֹוָה מִן הַשָּׁמַֽיִם הַלְ֒לֽוּהוּ בַּמְּ֒רוֹמִים: הַלְ֒לֽוּהוּ כָּל־מַלְאָכָיו הַלְ֒לֽוּהוּ כָּל־צְבָאָיו: הַלְ֒לֽוּהוּ שֶֽׁמֶשׁ וְיָרֵֽחַ הַלְ֒לֽוּהוּ כָּל־כּֽוֹכְ֒בֵי אוֹר: הַלְ֒לֽוּהוּ שְׁמֵי הַשָּׁמָֽיִם וְהַמַּֽיִם אֲשֶׁר מֵעַל הַשָּׁמָֽיִם: יְהַלְ֒לוּ אֶת־שֵׁם יְהֹוָה כִּי הוּא צִוָּה וְנִבְרָֽאוּ: וַיַּעֲמִידֵם לָעַד לְעוֹלָם חָק־נָתַן וְלֹא יַעֲבוֹר: הַלְ֒לוּ אֶת־יְהֹוָה מִן־הָאָֽרֶץ תַּנִּינִים וְכָל־תְּהֹמוֹת: אֵשׁ וּבָרָד שֶֽׁלֶג וְקִיטוֹר רֽוּחַ סְעָרָה עֹשָׂה דְבָרוֹ: הֶהָרִים וְכָל־גְּבָעוֹת עֵץ פְּרִי וְכָל־אֲרָזִים: הַחַיָּה וְכָל־בְּהֵמָה רֶֽמֶשׂ וְצִפּוֹר כָּנָף: מַלְכֵי־אֶֽרֶץ וְכָל־לְאֻמִּים שָׂרִים וְכָל־שֹׁפְטֵי אָֽרֶץ: בַּחוּרִים וְגַם־בְּתוּלוֹת זְקֵנִים עִם־נְעָרִים: יְהַלְ֒לוּ אֶת־שֵׁם יְהֹוָה כִּי־נִשְׂגָּב שְׁמוֹ לְבַדּוֹ הוֹדוֹ עַל־אֶֽרֶץ וְשָׁמָֽיִם: וַיָּֽרֶם קֶֽרֶן לְעַמּוֹ תְּהִלָּה לְכָל־חֲסִידָיו לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל עַם קְרֹבוֹ הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','Praise God. Praise Adonoy from the sky; Praise Him in the heights! Praise Him, all His angels; Praise Him, all His hosts! Praise Him, sun and moon; Praise Him, all the stars of light. Praise Him, skies of skies, and the waters that are above the skies. They will praise the Name of Adonoy, for He commanded it and they were created. He established them for all time, for as long as the world exists; He decreed it and it is unalterable. Praise Adonoy from the earth, sea-monsters and all [that dwell in] the depths. Fire and hail, snow and vapor, stormwind, [all] fulfilling His word. The mountains and all the hills, fruit trees and all cedars. Wild beasts and all animals, creeping things and winged fowl. Earthly kings and all peoples, ministers and all earthly judges. Young men and also maidens, elders together with lads. They will praise the Name of Adonoy, for His Name alone is exalted; His majesty is over the earth and the skies. He will raise the might of His people, [which is] praise for all His pious ones, for the Children of Israel, the people near to Him. Praise God.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:24:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','hah-LE-loo-yahh hah-LE-loo eht ah-doh-NAI meen hah-shah-mah-yeem hah-LE-loo-hoo bah-ME-roh-meem: hah-LE-loo-hoo kohl mahl-ah-khahv hah-LE-loo-hoo kohl tse-vah-ahv: hah-LE-loo-hoo sheh-mehsh ve-yah-reh-ahkh hah-LE-loo-hoo kohl koh-KHE-vey ohr: hah-LE-loo-hoo she-mey hah-shah-mah-yeem ve-hah-mah-yeem ah-shehr meh-ahl hah-shah-mah-yeem: ye-hah-LE-loo eht shehm ah-doh-NAI kee hoo tsee-vah ve-neev-rah-oo: vah-yah-ah-mee-dehm lah-ahd le-oh-lahm khohk nah-tahn ve-loh yah-ah-vohr: hah-LE-loo eht ah-doh-NAI meen hah-ah-rehts tah-nee-neem ve-khohl te-hoh-moht: ehsh oo-vah-rahd sheh-lehg ve-kee-tohr roo-ahkh se-ah-rah oh-sah de-vah-roh: heh-hah-reem ve-khohl ge-vah-oht ehts pe-ree ve-khohl ah-rah-zeem: hah-khah-yah ve-khohl be-heh-mah reh-mehs ve-tsee-pohr kah-nahf: mahl-khey eh-rehts ve-khohl le-oo-meem sah-reem ve-khohl shoh-fe-tey ah-rehts: bah-khoo-reem ve-gahm be-too-loht ze-keh-neem eem ne-ah-reem: ye-hah-LE-loo eht shehm ah-doh-NAI kee nees-gahv she-moh le-vah-doh hoh-doh ahl eh-rehts ve-shah-mah-yeem: vah-yah-rehm keh-rehn le-ah-moh te-hee-lah le-khohl khah-see-dahv leev-ney yees-rah-ehl ahm ke-roh-voh hah-LE-loo-yahh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:25:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','המזמור הזה מדבר לעתיד בביאת משיחנו','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:25:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','This psalm continues the theme of the previous psalm.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:26:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ שִֽׁירוּ לַיהוָֹה שִׁיר חָדָשׁ תְּהִלָּתוֹ בִּקְהַל חֲסִידִים: יִשְׂמַח יִשְׂרָאֵל בְּעֹשָׂיו בְּנֵי־צִיּוֹן יָגִֽילוּ בְמַלְכָּם: יְהַלְ֒לוּ שְׁמוֹ בְמָחוֹל בְּתֹף וְכִנּוֹר יְזַמְּ֒רוּ־לוֹ: כִּי־רוֹצֶה יְהֹוָה בְּעַמּוֹ יְפָאֵר עֲנָוִים בִּישׁוּעָה: יַעְלְזוּ חֲסִידִים בְּכָבוֹד יְרַנְּ֒נוּ עַל־מִשְׁכְּבוֹתָם: רוֹמְ֒מוֹת אֵל בִּגְרוֹנָם וְחֶֽרֶב פִּיפִיּוֹת בְּיָדָם: לַעֲשׂוֹת נְקָמָה בַגּוֹיִם תּוֹכֵחוֹת בַּלְאֻמִּים: לֶאְסֹר מַלְכֵיהֶם בְּזִקִּים וְנִכְבְּדֵיהֶם בְּכַבְלֵי בַרְזֶל: לַעֲשׂוֹת בָּהֶם מִשְׁפָּט כָּתוּב הָדָר הוּא לְכָל־חֲסִידָיו הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:26:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','Praise God. Sing a new song to Adonoy, His praise in the assembly of the pious. Israel will rejoice in its Maker; the children of Zion will exult in their King. They will praise His Name with dance; with drum and harp they will make music to Him. Because Adonoy desires His people; He will adorn the humble with deliverance. The pious will rejoice in honor; they will sing joyously upon their beds. High praises of the Almighty in their throats, and a double-edged sword in their hand. To perform vengeance upon the nations, chastisement upon the peoples. To bind their kings with chains, and their nobles with iron fetters. To execute upon them [the] written judgment; it is the splendor of all His pious ones. Praise God.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:26:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','hah-LE-loo-yahh shee-roo lah-ah-doh-NAI sheer khah-dahsh te-hee-lah-toh beek-hahl khah-see-deem: yees-mahkh yees-rah-ehl be-oh-sahv be-ney tsee-yohn yah-gee-loo ve-mahl-kahm: ye-hah-LE-loo she-moh ve-mah-khohl be-tohf ve-khee-nohr ye-zah-ME-roo LOH: kee roh-tseh ah-doh-NAI be-ah-moh ye-fah-ehr ah-nah-veem bee-shoo-ah: yah-le-zoo khah-see-deem be-khah-vohd ye-rah-NE-noo ahl meesh-ke-voh-tahm: roh-ME-moht ehl beeg-roh-nahm ve-kheh-rehv pee-fee-yoht be-yah-dahm: lah-ah-soht ne-kah-mah vah-goh-yeem toh-kheh-khoht bahl-oo-meem: leh-sohr mahl-khey-hehm be-zee-keem ve-neekh-be-dey-hehm be-khahv-ley vahr-zehl: lah-ah-soht bah-hehm meesh-paht kah-toov hah-dahr hoo le-khohl khah-see-dahv hah-LE-loo-yahh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:27:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','במזמור הזה יש שלשה עשר הלולים. רמז לי"ג מדות.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:27:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','This psalm recapitulates all the previous hymns and tells how God is revealed through His mighty deeds.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:28:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ הַֽלְ֒לוּ־אֵל בְּקָדְשׁוֹ הַלְ֒לֽוּהוּ בִּרְקִֽיעַ עֻזּוֹ: הַלְ֒לֽוּהוּ בִּגְבוּרֹתָיו הַלְ֒לֽוּהוּ כְּרֹב גֻּדְלוֹ: הַלְ֒לֽוּהוּ בְּתֵֽקַע שׁוֹפָר הַלְ֒לֽוּהוּ בְּנֵֽבֶל וְכִנּוֹר: הַלְ֒לֽוּהוּ בְּתֹף וּמָחוֹל הַלְ֒לֽוּהוּ בְּמִנִּים וְעֻגָב: הַלְ֒לֽוּהוּ בְצִלְצְלֵי־שָֽׁמַע הַלְ֒לֽוּהוּ בְּצִלְצְלֵי תְרוּעָה: כֹּל הַנְּ֒שָׁמָה תְּהַלֵּל יָהּ הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ: כֹּל הַנְּ֒שָׁמָה תְּהַלֵּל יָהּ הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:28:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','Praise God. Praise the Almighty in His Sanctuary Praise God in the firmament of His might Praise Him for His mighty deeds; Praise Him according to the abundance of His greatness. Praise Him with the blowing of the shofar; praise Him with lyre and harp. Praise Him with drum and dance. Praise Him with stringed instruments and flute. Praise Him with resounding cymbals. Praise Him with clanging cymbals. Let every soul praise God. Praise God. Let every soul praise God. Praise God.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:28:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','hah-LE-loo-yahh hah-LE-loo EHL be-kohd-shoh hah-LE-loo-hoo beer-kee-ah oo-zoh: hah-LE-loo-hoo beeg-voo-roh-tahv hah-LE-loo-hoo ke-rohv good-loh: hah-LE-loo-hoo be-teh-kah shoh-fahr hah-LE-loo-hoo be-neh-vehl ve-khee-nohr: hah-LE-loo-hoo be-tohf oo-mah-khohl hah-LE-loo-hoo be-mee-neem ve-oo-gahv: hah-LE-loo-hoo ve-tseel-tse-ley shah-mah hah-LE-loo-hoo be-tseel-tse-ley te-roo-ah: kohl hah-NE-shah-mah te-hah-lehl yahh hah-LE-loo-yahh: kohl hah-NE-shah-mah te-hah-lehl yahh hah-LE-loo-yahh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:29:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','קבעו פסוקים אלו אחר כל הנשמה משום שאלו הכתובים מצינו אותם כתובים בסוף ספרי תהלים. לכן תקנו לאמרם בהשלמת פסוקי דזמרה (א"ר סי'' נ"א)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:29:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','The following selected verses from Psalms mark the close of the individual books of Psalms. Eitz Yoseif notes that these verses may constitute a sort of blessing marking the close of the Pesukei Dezimrah.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:30:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','בָּרוּךְ יְהֹוָה לְעוֹלָם אָמֵן וְאָמֵן: בָּרוּךְ יְהֹוָה מִצִּיּוֹן שֹׁכֵן יְרוּשָׁלָֽםִ הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ: בָּרוּךְ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהִים אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל עֹשֵׂה נִפְלָאוֹת לְבַדּוֹ: וּבָרוּךְ שֵׁם כְּבוֹדוֹ לְעוֹלָם וְיִמָּלֵא כְבוֹדוֹ אֶת־כָּל־הָאָֽרֶץ אָמֵן וְאָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:30:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','Blessed is Adonoy forever, Amein and Amein! Blessed is Adonoy from Zion, Who dwells in Jerusalem. Praise God. Blessed is Adonoy, God, God of Israel Who alone performs wonders. And blessed is the Name of His glory forever, and may His glory fill the whole earth. Amein and Amein!','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:30:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','bah-rookh ah-doh-NAI le-oh-lahm ah-mehn ve-ah-mehn: bah-rookh ah-doh-NAI mee-tsee-yohn shoh-khehn ye-roo-shah-lah-mee hah-LE-loo-yahh: bah-rookh ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-heem eh-loh-hey yees-rah-ehl oh-seh neef-lah-oht le-vah-doh: oo-vah-rookh shehm ke-voh-doh le-oh-lahm ve-yee-mah-leh khe-voh-doh eht kohl hah-ah-rehts ah-mehn ve-ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:31:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','הטעם שנהגו לומר ויברך דוד ושירת הים לפי שכל אותם חמשה עשר לשונות של שבח הסדורין בברכת ישתבח דורש במכלתין מתוך שירת הים ומתוך פסוקים של ויברך דוד (אבודרהם). כשמגיע לואתה מושל בכל יתן ג'' פרוטות לצדקה הב׳ בבת אחת ואח״כ השלישית וסודם נשגב (צפורן שמיר)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:31:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','The following selections are additions to the Pesukei Dezimrah. The custom of reciting them is mentioned as early as the Gaonic era, specifically by Rav Amram Gaon. The first four verses (1 Chronicles 29:10-13) relate David''s blessing to God, when he presented the gold, silver, and jewels he amassed for the construction of the Holy Temple. It was a day of great rejoicing as, following David''s example, the leaders and princes also presented generous gifts for the construction of the Temple. These verses were incorporated into our daily prayers because they speak so eloquently of God''s majesty, and of the Divine providence which is the source of the power, riches, might, and honor of all human beings.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:32:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','בויברך דויד יעמוד עד שיאמר אתה הוא ה'' האלהים ועד בכלל','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:32:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','The following until after ישתבח should be said standing.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:33:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','וַיְבָֽרֶךְ דָּוִיד אֶת־יְהֹוָה לְעֵינֵי כָּל־הַקָּהָל וַיֹּֽאמֶר דָּוִיד בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אָבִֽינוּ, מֵעוֹלָם וְעַד־עוֹלָם: לְךָ יְהֹוָה הַגְּ֒דֻלָּה וְהַגְּ֒בוּרָה וְהַתִּפְאֶֽרֶת וְהַנֵּֽצַח וְהַהוֹד כִּי־כֹל בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם וּבָאָֽרֶץ לְךָ יְהֹוָה הַמַּמְלָכָה וְהַמִּתְנַשֵּׂא לְכֹל לְרֹאשׁ: וְהָעֽשֶׁר וְהַכָּבוֹד מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ וְאַתָּה מוֹשֵׁל בַּכֹּל, וּבְיָדְ֒ךָ כֹּֽחַ וּגְבוּרָה, וּבְיָדְ֒ךָ לְגַדֵּל וּלְחַזֵּק לַכֹּל: וְעַתָּה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ מוֹדִים אֲנַֽחְנוּ לָךְ וּמְהַלְ֒לִים לְשֵׁם תִּפְאַרְתֶּֽךָ: וִיבָרְכוּ שֵׁם כְּבוֹדֶךָ, וּמְרוֹמַם עַל כָּל בְּרָכָה וּתְהִלָּה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:33:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','And David blessed Adonoy in the presence of all the assembly; and David said, Blessed are You, Adonoy, God of Israel, our father, forever and ever. Yours, Adonoy, is the greatness, the might, the glory the victory and the beauty, for all that is in heaven and on earth [is Yours]; Yours, Adonoy, is the kingdom and You are uplifted, [supreme] over all rulers. The riches and the honor come from You, and You rule over all; in Your hand are power and might, and [it is] in Your hand to bestow greatness and strength upon all. And now, our God, we give thanks to You and praise Your glorious Name.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:33:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','vah-ye-vah-rehkh dah-veed eht ah-doh-NAI le-ey-ney kohl hah-kah-hahl vah-yoh-mehr dah-veed bah-rookh ah-tah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey yees-rah-ehl ah-vee-noo, meh-oh-lahm ve-ahd oh-lahm: le-khah ah-doh-NAI hah-GE-doo-lah ve-hah-GE-voo-rah ve-hah-teef-eh-reht ve-hah-neh-tsahkh ve-hah-hohd kee khohl bah-shah-mah-yeem oo-vah-ah-rehts le-khah ah-doh-NAI hah-mahm-lah-khah ve-hah-meet-nah-seh le-khohl le-rohsh: ve-hah--shehr ve-hah-kah-vohd mee-LE-fah-ney-khah ve-ah-tah moh-shehl bah-kohl, oo-ve-yah-DE-khah koh-ahkh oo-ge-voo-rah, oo-ve-yah-DE-khah le-gah-dehl oo-le-khah-zehk lah-kohl: ve-ah-tah eh-loh-hey-noo moh-deem ahnah-khe-noo lahkh oo-me-hah-LE-leem le-shehm teef-ahr-teh-khah: vee-vah-re-khoo shehm ke-voh-deh-khah, oo-me-roh-mahm ahl kohl be-rah-khah oo-te-hee-lah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:34:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','אַתָּה־הוּא יְהֹוָה לְבַדֶּֽךָ, אַתָּה עָשִֽׂיתָ אֶת־הַשָּׁמַֽיִם שְׁמֵי הַשָּׁמַֽיִם וְכָל־צְבָאָם, הָאָֽרֶץ וְכָל־אֲשֶׁר עָלֶֽיהָ הַיַּמִּים וְכָל־אֲשֶׁר בָּהֶם, וְאַתָּה מְחַיֶּה אֶת־כֻּלָּם וּצְ֒בָא הַשָּׁמַֽיִם לְךָ מִשְׁתַּחֲוִים: אַתָּה הוּא יְהֹוָה הָאֱלֹהִים אֲשֶׁר בָּחַֽרְתָּ בְּאַבְרָם וְהוֹצֵאתוֹ מֵאוּר כַּשְׂדִּים וְשַֽׂמְתָּ שְׁמוֹ אַבְרָהָם: וּמָצָֽאתָ אֶת־לְבָבוֹ נֶאֱמָן לְפָנֶֽיךָ','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:34:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','You alone are Adonoy; You have made the skies, the skies of skies and all their hosts, the earth and all that is upon it, the seas and all that is in them; and You give life to all of them, and the heavenly hosts bow before You. You are Adonoy, the God Who chose Avrom, and brought him out of Ur Kasdim and established his name (as) Avrohom. And You found his heart faithful before You,','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:34:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','ah-tah hoo ah-doh-NAI le-vah-deh-khah, ah-tah ah-see-tah eht hah-shah-mah-yeem she-mey hah-shah-mah-yeem ve-khohl tse-vah-ahm, hah-ah-rehts ve-khohl ah-shehr ah-ley-hah hah-yah-meem ve-khohl ah-shehr bah-hehm, ve-ah-tah me-khah-yeh eht koo-lahm oo-TSE-vah hah-shah-mah-yeem le-khah meesh-tah-khah-veem: ah-tah hoo ah-doh-NAI hah-eh-loh-heem ah-shehr bah-khah-re-tah be-ahv-rahm ve-hoh-tseh-toh meh-oor kahs-deem ve-sah-me-tah she-moh ahv-rah-hahm: oo-mah-tsah-tah eht le-vah-voh neh-eh-mahn le-fah-ney-khah','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:35:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','וְכָרוֹת עִמּוֹ הַבְּ֒רִית לָתֵת אֶת־אֶֽרֶץ הַכְּ֒נַעֲנִי הַחִתִּי הָאֱמֹרִי וְהַפְּ֒רִזִּי וְהַיְבוּסִי וְהַגִּרְגָּשִׁי לָתֵת לְזַרְעוֹ וַתָּֽקֶם אֶת־דְּבָרֶֽיךָ כִּי צַדִּיק אָֽתָּה: וַתֵּֽרֶא אֶת־עֳנִי אֲבֹתֵֽינוּ בְּמִצְרָֽיִם וְאֶת־זַעֲקָתָם שָׁמַֽעְתָּ עַל־יַם־סוּף: וַתִּתֵּן אֹתֹת וּמֹפְ֒תִים בְּפַרְעֹה וּבְכָל־עֲבָדָיו וּבְכָל־עַם אַרְצוֹ כִּי יָדַֽעְתָּ כִּי הֵזִֽידוּ עֲלֵיהֶם וַתַּֽעַשׂ־לְךָ שֵׁם כְּהַיּוֹם הַזֶּה: וְהַיָּם בָּקַֽעְתָּ לִפְנֵיהֶם וַיַּעַבְרוּ בְתוֹךְ־הַיָּם בַּיַּבָּשָׁה וְאֶת־רֹדְ֒פֵיהֶם הִשְׁלַֽכְתָּ בִמְצוֹלֹת כְּמוֹ־אֶֽבֶן בְּמַֽיִם עַזִּים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:35:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','and You made the covenant with him to give the land of the Canaanites, the Hittites, the Amorites, the Perizites, the Jebusites, and the Girgashites, to give to his seed; and You kept Your word, for You are righteous. And You saw the affliction of our fathers in Egypt, and their cry You heard at the Sea of Reeds. And You imposed signs and wonders against Pharaoh and all his servants and all the people of his land, for You knew that they acted malevolently against them; and (thus) You have made a name for Yourself, like this day. And the sea, You split before them, and they went through the midst of the sea on the dry land; and their pursuers You hurled into the depths, like a stone into mighty waters.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:35:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','ve-khah-roht ee-moh hah-BE-reet lah-teht eht eh-rehts hah-KE-nah-ah-nee hah-khee-tee hah-eh-moh-ree ve-hah-PE-ree-zee ve-hah-ye-voo-see ve-hah-geer-gah-shee lah-teht le-zahr-oh vah-tah-kehm eht de-vah-rey-khah kee tsah-deek ah-tah: vah-teh-reh eht oh-nee ah-voh-tey-noo be-meets-rah-yeem ve-eht zah-ah-kah-tahm shah-mah-e-tah ahl yahm soof: vah-tee-tehn oh-toht oo-moh-FE-teem be-fahr-ohh oo-ve-khohl ah-vah-dahv oo-ve-khohl ahm ahr-tsoh kee yah-dah-e-tah kee heh-zee-doo ah-ley-hehm vah-tah-ahs le-khah shehm ke-hah-yohm hah-zeh: ve-hah-yahm bah-kah-e-tah leef-ney-hehm vah-yah-ahv-roo ve-tohkh hah-yahm bah-yah-bah-shah ve-eht roh-DE-fey-hehm heesh-lah-khe-tah veem-tsoh-loht ke-moh eh-vehn be-mah-yeem ah-zeem:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:36:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','תקנו לומר וישע ה'' ביום ההוא ושירת הים והוא זכר ליציאת מצרים. וכופלין פסוק ה'' ימלוך לעולם ועד מפני שהוא סוף השירה (אבודרהם). כל האומר שירת הים בשמחה ובעצמו שיער כאלו הוא ניצול מהים ופרעה וחילו הם נטבעו ואמר שירה מכפרים לו עונותיו (צפורן שמיר)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:36:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','In Temple times Shiras Hayam, the Song of the Sea, was sung by the Levites when the daily afternoon sacrifice was offered. After the destruction, the Jews of the Holy Land continued the tradition, reciting the Shira at the end of the Pesukei Dezimrah. The custom spread to Italy and from there to other Jewish communities. This daily recital is mentioned by Rav Saadya Gaon but not as an obligatory part of the service. Rambam calls it a "custom." Subsequently adopted by all communities, reciting the Shira became an integral part of our daily prayers. Some hold that the Shira should be chanted aloud while standing. It should be sung with joy as at the time of the Exodus. "Sheloh" writes that reciting the Shira atones for sin, so that if one wishes to repent a serious sin, he should recite the Shira every day with great fervor. The Zohar says, "If one recites this song with elation and joy, he will be worthy to sing it in the next world. He will also be worthy to sing it when he greets the Messiah."','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:37:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','וַיּֽוֹשַׁע יְהֹוָה בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא אֶת־יִשְׂרָאֵל מִיַּד מִצְרָֽיִם וַיַּרְא יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת־מִצְרַֽיִם מֵת עַל־שְׂפַת הַיָּם: וַיַּרְא יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת־הַיָּד הַגְּ֒דֹלָה אֲשֶׁר עָשָׂה יְהֹוָה בְּמִצְרַֽיִם וַיִּירְ֒אוּ הָעָם אֶת יְהֹוָה וַיַּאֲמִֽינוּ בַּיהוָֹה וּבְמשֶׁה עַבְדּוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:37:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','On that day, Adonoy delivered Israel from the hand of Egypt, and Israel saw the Egyptians dead on the seashore. And Israel saw the great hand which Adonoy wielded against Egypt, and the people feared Adonoy, and they believed in Adonoy, and that Moses was His servant.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:37:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','vah-yoh-shah ah-doh-NAI bah-yohm hah-hoo eht yees-rah-ehl mee-yahd meets-rah-yeem vah-yahr yees-rah-ehl eht meets-rah-yeem meht ahl se-faht hah-yahm: vah-yahr yees-rah-ehl eht hah-yahd hah-GE-doh-lah ah-shehr ah-sah ah-doh-NAI be-meets-rah-yeem vah-yee-RE-oo hah-ahm eht ah-doh-NAI vah-yah-ah-mee-noo bah-ah-doh-NAI oo-ve-m-sheh ahv-doh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:38:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','he','אָז יָשִׁיר משֶׁה וּבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת־הַשִּׁירָה הַזֹּאת לַיהוָֹה וַיֹּאמְרוּ לֵאמֹר אָשִֽׁירָה לַיהוָֹה כִּי־גָאֹה גָּאָה סוּס וְרֹכְ֒בוֹ רָמָה בַיָּם: עָזִּי וְזִמְרָת יָהּ וַיְ֒הִי־לִי לִישׁוּעָה זֶה אֵלִי וְאַנְוֵֽהוּ אֱלֹהֵי אָבִי וַאֲרֹמְ֒מֶֽנְהוּ: יְהֹוָה אִישׁ מִלְחָמָה יְהֹוָה שְׁמוֹ: מַרְכְּבֹת פַּרְעֹה וְחֵילוֹ יָרָה בַיָּם וּמִבְחַר שָׁלִשָׁיו טֻבְּ֒עוּ בְיַם־סוּף: תְּהֹמֹת יְכַסְיֻֽמוּ יָרְ֒דוּ בִמְצוֹלֹת כְּמוֹ־אָֽבֶן: יְמִינְ֒ךָ יְהֹוָה נֶאְדָּרִי בַּכֹּֽחַ יְמִֽינְ֒ךָ יְהֹוָה תִּרְעַץ אוֹיֵב: וּבְרֹב גְּאוֹנְ֒ךָ תַּהֲרֹס קָמֶֽיךָ תְּשַׁלַּח חֲרֹנְ֒ךָ יֹֽאכְ֒לֵמוֹ כַּקַּשׁ: וּבְרֽוּחַ אַפֶּֽיךָ נֶֽעֶרְמוּ מַֽיִם נִצְּ֒בוּ כְמוֹ־נֵד נֹזְ֒לִים קָפְ֒אוּ תְהֹמֹת בְּלֶב־יָם: אָמַר אוֹיֵב אֶרְדֹּף אַשִּׂיג אֲחַלֵּק שָׁלָל תִּמְלָאֵֽמוֹ נַפְשִׁי אָרִיק חַרְבִּי תּוֹרִישֵֽׁמוֹ יָדִי: נָשַֽׁפְתָּ בְרוּחֲךָ כִּסָּֽמוֹ יָם צָלֲלוּ כַּעוֹפֶֽרֶת בְּמַֽיִם אַדִּירִים: מִי־כָמֹֽכָה בָּאֵלִם יְהֹוָה מִי כָּמֹֽכָה נֶאְדָּר בַּקֹּֽדֶשׁ נוֹרָא תְהִלֹּת עֹֽשֵׂה־פֶֽלֶא: נָטִֽיתָ יְמִינְ֒ךָ תִּבְלָעֵֽמוֹ אָֽרֶץ: נָחִֽיתָ בְחַסְדְּ֒ךָ עַם־זוּ גָּאָֽלְתָּ נֵהַֽלְתָּ בְעָזְּ֒ךָ אֶל־נְוֵה קָדְשֶֽׁךָ: שָֽׁמְ֒עוּ עַמִּים יִרְגָּזוּן חִיל אָחַז ישְׁ֒בֵי פְּלָֽשֶׁת: אָז נִבְהֲלוּ אַלּוּפֵי אֱדוֹם אֵילֵי מוֹאָב יֹֽאחֲזֵֽמוֹ רָֽעַד נָמֹֽגוּ כֹּל ישְׁ֒בֵי כְנָֽעַן: תִּפֹּל עֲלֵיהֶם אֵימָֽתָה וָפַֽחַד בִּגְדֹל זְרוֹעֲךָ יִדְּ֒מוּ כָּאָֽבֶן עַד־יַֽעֲבֹר עַמְּ֒ךָ יְהֹוָה עַד־יַֽעֲבֹר עַם־זוּ קָנִֽיתָ: תְּבִאֵֽמוֹ וְתִטָּעֵֽמוֹ בְּהַר נַחֲלָתְ֒ךָ מָכוֹן לְשִׁבְתְּ֒ךָ פָּעַֽלְתָּ יְהֹוָה מִקְּ֒דָשׁ אֲדֹנָי כּוֹנְ֒נוּ יָדֶֽיךָ: יְהֹוָה יִמְלֹךְ לְעֹלָם וָעֶד: יְהֹוָה יִמְלֹךְ לְעֹלָם וָעֶד: יְהֹוָה מַלְכוּתֵהּ קָאֵים לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא: כִּי בָא סוּס פַּרְעֹה בְּרִכְבּוֹ וּבְפָרָשָׁיו בַּיָּם וַיָּֽשֶׁב יְהֹוָה עֲלֵהֶם אֶת־מֵי הַיָּם וּבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל הָלְ֒כוּ בַיַּבָּשָׁה בְּתוֹךְ הַיָּֽם: כִּי לַיהוָֹה הַמְּ֒לוּכָה וּמשֵׁל בַּגּוֹיִם: וְעָלוּ מוֹשִׁעִים בְּהַר צִיּוֹן לִשְׁפֹּט אֶת־הַר עֵשָׂו, וְהָיְ֒תָה לַיהוָֹה הַמְּ֒לוּכָה: וְהָיָה יְהֹוָה לְמֶֽלֶךְ עַל־כָּל הָאָֽרֶץ בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא יִהְיֶה יְהֹוָה אֶחָד וּשְׁמוֹ אֶחָד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:38:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','en','Then Moses and the Children of Israel sang this song to Adonoy, and they said: I will sing to Adonoy for He is most high; the horse with its rider, He threw into the sea. The strength and retribution of God was the cause of my deliverance; this is my Almighty and I will glorify Him, God of my father and I will exalt Him. Adonoy is master of war Adonoy is His Name. Pharaoh''s chariots and army, He hurled into the sea; and his elite officers were drowned in the Sea of Reeds. The deep waters covered them; they descended into the depths like stone. Your right hand Adonoy is adorned with power, Your right hand Adonoy crushes the enemy. And in Your great majesty, You destroyed Your opponents; You sent forth Your fury, it consumed them like straw. And with the wind from Your nostrils the waters were heaped up, flowing water stood erect like a wall; the deep waters congealed in the heart of the sea. The enemy (Pharaoh) said: I will pursue [them], I will overtake [them], I will divide the spoils; I will satisfy myself; I will unsheathe my sword, my hand will destroy them. You blew with Your wind, the sea covered them; they sank like lead in the mighty waters. Who is like You among the mighty, Adonoy! who is like You? [You are] adorned in holiness, awesome in praise, performing wonders. You stretched out Your right hand, the earth swallowed them. You led in Your kindliness, the people whom You redeemed; You guided them with Your might to Your holy dwelling place. The peoples heard and trembled, pangs of fear gripped the inhabitants of Philistia. Then the chieftains of Edom panicked, the mighty men of Moab were seized with trembling, all the inhabitants of Canaan melted away. Terror and dread fall upon them; at the greatness of Your arm they were still as stone; until Your people cross over, Adonoy, until [they] cross over, —the people You have acquired. You will bring them and plant them on the mountain of Your inheritance, the place for Your habitation which You, Adonoy, have made; the Sanctuary, my Master, [which] Your hands established. Adonoy will reign forever and ever. Adonoy will reign forever and ever. Adonoy! His sovereignty is established forever and to all eternity. When Pharaoh''s horses, with his chariots, and his horsemen, went into the sea, Adonoy turned back on them the waters of the sea; and the Children of Israel walked on dry land in the midst of the sea. For the kingship is Adonoy''s and He rules over nations. And deliverers will go up to Mount Zion to judge Mount Esau, and the kingdom will be Adonoy''s. And Adonoy will be King over the whole earth; on that day Adonoy will be One and His Name One.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu:38:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-hodu','transliteration','ahz yah-sheer m-sheh oo-ve-ney yees-rah-ehl eht hah-shee-rah hah-zoht lah-ah-doh-NAI vah-yoh-me-roo leh-mohr ah-shee-rah lah-ah-doh-NAI kee gah-ohh gah-ah soos ve-roh-KHE-voh rah-mah vah-yahm: oh-zee ve-zeem-raht yahh vah-YE-hee LEE lee-shoo-ah zeh eh-lee ve-ahn-veh-hoo eh-loh-hey ah-vee vah-ah-roh-ME-meh-ne-hoo: ah-doh-NAI eesh meel-khah-mah ah-doh-NAI she-moh: mahr-ke-voht pahr-ohh ve-khey-loh yah-rah vah-yahm oo-meev-khahr shah-lee-shahv too-BE-oo ve-yahm soof: te-hoh-moht ye-khahs-yoo-moo yah-RE-doo veem-tsoh-loht ke-moh ah-vehn: ye-mee-NE-khah ah-doh-NAI neh-dah-ree bah-koh-ahkh ye-mee-NE-khah ah-doh-NAI teer-ahts oh-yehv: oo-ve-rohv ge-oh-NE-khah tah-hah-rohs kah-mey-khah te-shah-lahkh khah-roh-NE-khah yoh-KHE-leh-moh kah-kahsh: oo-ve-roo-ahkh ah-pey-khah neh-ehr-moo mah-yeem nee-TSE-voo khe-moh nehd noh-ZE-leem kah-FE-oo te-hoh-moht be-lehv yahm: ah-mahr oh-yehv ehr-dohf ah-seeg ah-khah-lehk shah-lahl teem-lah-eh-moh nahf-shee ah-reek khahr-bee toh-ree-sheh-moh yah-dee: nah-shah-fe-tah ve-roo-khah-khah kee-sah-moh yahm tsah-lah-loo kah-oh-feh-reht be-mah-yeem ah-dee-reem: mee khah-moh-khah bah-eh-leem ah-doh-NAI mee kah-moh-khah neh-dahr bah-koh-dehsh noh-rah te-hee-loht oh-seh feh-leh: nah-tee-tah ye-mee-NE-khah teev-lah-eh-moh ah-rehts: nah-khee-tah ve-khahs-DE-khah ahm zoo gah-ah-le-tah neh-hah-le-tah ve-oh-ZE-khah ehl ne-veh kohd-sheh-khah: shah-ME-oo ah-meem yeer-gah-zoon kheel ah-khahz YSHE-vey pe-lah-sheht: ahz neev-hah-loo ah-loo-fey eh-dohm ey-ley moh-ahv yoh-khah-zeh-moh rah-ahd nah-moh-goo kohl YSHE-vey khe-nah-ahn: tee-pohl ah-ley-hehm ey-mah-tah vah-fah-khahd beeg-dohl ze-roh-ah-khah yee-DE-moo kah-ah-vehn ahd yah-ah-vohr ah-ME-khah ah-doh-NAI ahd yah-ah-vohr ahm zoo kah-nee-tah: te-vee-eh-moh ve-tee-tah-eh-moh be-hahr nah-khah-lah-TE-khah mah-khohn le-sheev-TE-khah pah-ah-le-tah ah-doh-NAI mee-KE-dahsh ah-doh-nahy koh-NE-noo yah-dey-khah: ah-doh-NAI yeem-lohkh le-oh-lahm vah-ehd: ah-doh-NAI yeem-lohkh le-oh-lahm vah-ehd: ah-doh-NAI mahl-khoo-teh kah-eym le-ah-lahm oo-le-ah-LE-mey ah-LE-mah-yah: kee vah soos pahr-ohh be-reekh-boh oo-ve-fah-rah-shahv bah-yahm vah-yah-shehv ah-doh-NAI ah-leh-hehm eht mey hah-yahm oo-ve-ney yees-rah-ehl hah-LE-khoo vah-yah-bah-shah be-tohkh hah-yahm: kee lah-ah-doh-NAI hah-ME-loo-khah oo-m-shehl bah-goh-yeem: ve-ah-loo moh-shee-eem be-hahr tsee-yohn leesh-poht eht hahr eh-sahv, ve-hah-YE-tah lah-ah-doh-NAI hah-ME-loo-khah: ve-hah-yah ah-doh-NAI le-meh-lehkh ahl kohl hah-ah-rehts bah-yohm hah-hoo yeeh-yeh ah-doh-NAI eh-khahd oo-she-moh eh-khahd:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Hodu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','he','ברכה זו אינה פותחת בברוך מפני שסמוכה היא לברוך שאמר. ופסוקים שבנתים לא הוו הפסק. (אבודרהם)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','en','Rabbeinu Alfasi (Maseches Berachos 32) refers to Baruch She''amar as the opening blessing of the Pesukei Dezimrah, and Yishtabach as the concluding blessing.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','he','יִשְׁתַּבַּח שִׁמְךָ לָעַד מַלְכֵּֽנוּ הָאֵל הַמֶּֽלֶךְ הַגָּדוֹל וְהַקָּדוֹשׁ בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם וּבָאָֽרֶץ, כִּי לְךָ נָאֶה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ (לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד) שִׁיר וּשְׁבָחָה הַלֵּל וְזִמְרָה עֹז וּמֶמְשָׁלָה נֶֽצַח גְּדֻלָּה וּגְבוּרָה תְּהִלָּה וְתִפְאֶֽרֶת קְדֻשָּׁה וּמַלְכוּת, בְּרָכוֹת וְהוֹדָאוֹת לְשִׁמְךָ הַגָּדוֹל וְהַקָּדוֹשׁ וּמֵעוֹלָם וְעַד עוֹלָם אַתָּה אֵל: בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֵל מֶֽלֶךְ גָּדוֹל וּמְהֻלָּל בַּתִּשְׁבָּחוֹת אֵל הַהוֹדָאוֹת אֲדוֹן הַנִּפְלָאוֹת בּוֹרֵא כָּל הַנְּ֒שָׁמוֹת רִבּוֹן כָּל הַמַעֲשִׂים הַבּוֹחֵר בְּשִׁירֵי זִמְרָה מֶֽלֶךְ יָחִיד אֵל חֵי הָעוֹלָמִים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','en','Praised be Your Name forever, our King, Almighty the great and holy King in heaven and on earth. For to You it is fitting [to offer] Adonoy, our God, and God of our fathers, (forever,) song and praise, glorification and hymns, [to proclaim your] strength and dominion, victory, grandeur, and might, praise and glory, holiness and sovereignty, blessings and thanksgivings, to your great and holy name; and from the highest world to the lowest you are Almighty. Blessed are You, Adonoy, Almighty, King [Who is] great in [our] praise Almighty, of [to Whom we offer our] thanksgiving, Master of [Whom we praise for His] wonders, creator of all souls master of all creatures the Selector of song-hymns, You are the only King, Almighty, Life of [all] the worlds.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','transliteration','yeesh-tah-bahkh sheem-khah lah-ahd mahl-keh-noo hah-ehl hah-meh-lehkh hah-gah-dohl ve-hah-kah-dohsh bah-shah-mah-yeem oo-vah-ah-rehts, kee le-khah nah-eh ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo veh-loh-hey ah-voh-tey-noo (le-oh-lahm vah-ehd) sheer oo-she-vah-khah hah-lehl ve-zeem-rah ohz oo-mehm-shah-lah neh-tsahkh ge-doo-lah oo-ge-voo-rah te-hee-lah ve-teef-eh-reht ke-doo-shah oo-mahl-khoot, be-rah-khoht ve-hoh-dah-oht le-sheem-khah hah-gah-dohl ve-hah-kah-dohsh oo-meh-oh-lahm ve-ahd oh-lahm ah-tah ehl: bah-rookh ah-tah ah-doh-NAI ehl meh-lehkh gah-dohl oo-me-hoo-lahl bah-teesh-bah-khoht ehl hah-hoh-dah-oht ah-dohn hah-neef-lah-oht boh-reh kohl hah-NE-shah-moht ree-bohn kohl hah-mah-ah-seem hah-boh-khehr be-shee-rey zeem-rah meh-lehkh yah-kheed ehl khey hah-oh-lah-meem:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','he','בעשרת ימי תשובה מוסיפין:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','en','During the Ten Days of Penitence add: In this Psalm, said during the Ten Days of Penitence, the Jewish soul sings of the Jewish spirit ascending from the depths of the deepest misery of all, the burden of sin and guilt.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','he','שִׁיר הַמַּעֲלוֹת מִמַּעֲמַקִּים קְרָאתִֽיךָ יְהֹוָה: אֲדֹנָי שִׁמְעָה בְקוֹלִי תִּהְיֶֽינָה אָזְנֶֽיךָ קַשֻּׁבוֹת לְקוֹל תַּחֲנוּנָי: אִם־עֲוֹנוֹת תִּשְׁמָר־יָהּ אֲדֹנָי מִי יַעֲמֹד: כִּי־עִמְּ֒ךָ הַסְּ֒לִיחָה לְמַֽעַן תִּוָּרֵא: קִוִּיתִי יְהֹוָה קִוְּתָה נַפְשִׁי וְלִדְ֒בָרוֹ הוֹחָֽלְתִּי: נַפְשִׁי לַאדֹנָי מִשֹּׁמְ֒רִים לַבֹּֽקֶר שֹׁמְ֒רִים לַבֹּֽקֶר: יַחֵל יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶל־יְהֹוָה כִּי־עִם־יְהֹוָה הַחֶֽסֶד וְהַרְבֵּה עִמּוֹ פְדוּת: וְהוּא יִפְדֶּה אֶת־יִשְׂרָאֵל מִכֹּל עֲוֹנוֹתָיו:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','en','A Song of Ascents. Out of the depths I have called to You, Adonoy. My Master, hear my voice; let Your ears be attentive to the voice of my supplications. If You God should take account of iniquities, my Master, who could survive? For with You is forgiveness, in order that You be feared. I hope for Adonoy, my soul hopes; and for His word, I wait. My soul [waits] for my Master more than the watchman [waits] for the morning, [more than] the watchman [waits] for the morning. Wait, Israel, upon Adonoy, for with Adonoy there is loving-kindness, and with Him there is much redemption. And He will redeem Israel from all its iniquities.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','transliteration','sheer hah-mah-ah-loht mee-mah-ah-mah-keem ke-rah-tee-khah ah-doh-NAI: ah-doh-nahy sheem-ah ve-koh-lee teeh-yey-nah ohz-ney-khah kah-shoo-voht le-kohl tah-khah-noo-nahy: eem ah-voh-noht teesh-mohr yahh ah-doh-nahy mee yah-ah-mohd: kee ee-ME-khah hah-SE-lee-khah le-mah-ahn tee-vah-reh: kee-vee-tee ah-doh-NAI kee-ve-tah nahf-shee ve-LEED-vah-roh hoh-khah-le-tee: nahf-shee lah-doh-nahy mee-shoh-ME-reem lah-boh-kehr shoh-ME-reem lah-boh-kehr: yah-khehl yees-rah-ehl ehl ah-doh-NAI kee eem ah-doh-NAI hah-kheh-sehd ve-hahr-beh ee-moh fe-doot: ve-hoo yeef-deh eht yees-rah-ehl mee-kohl ah-voh-noh-tahv:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','he','ואומר החזן חצי קדיש:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','en','The Half-Kaddish is recited by the Chazzan Here, as elsewhere in the Liturgy, the Half-Kaddish marks the end of a distinct section of the prayers, in this case, the Pesukei Dezimrah. It is called the Half-Kaddish, the final three verses of the complete Kaddish having been omitted.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְ֒מָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְקָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming if His Messiah in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','transliteration','yeet-gah-dahl ve-yeet-kah-dahsh she-meh rah-bah be-ah-LE-mah dee ve-rah kheer-oo-teh ve-yahm-leekh mahl-khoo-teh ve-yahts-mahkh poo-re-kah-neh vee-kah-rehv (kehts) me-shee-kheh be-khah-yey-khohn oo-ve-yoh-mey-khohn oo-ve-khah-yey de-khahl beyt yees-rah-ehl, bah-ah-gah-lah oo-veez-mahn kah-reev ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','transliteration','ye-heh she-meh rah-bah me-vah-rahkh le-ah-lahm oo-le-ah-LE-mey ah-LE-mah-yah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He;','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','transliteration','yeet-bah-rahkh ve-yeesh-tah-bahkh ve-yeet-pah-ahr ve-yeet-roh-mahm ve-yeet-nah-seh ve-yeet-hah-dahr ve-yeet-ah-leh ve-yeet-hah-lahl she-meh de-koo-de-shah, be-reekh hoo','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','he','לְעֵֽלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְ֒עֵֽלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְ֒מָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן,','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','en','above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-yishtabach','transliteration','le-eh-lah (vshyt" oo-LE-eh-lah mee-kahl) meen kohl beer-khah-tah ve-shee-rah-tah, toosh-be-khah-tah ve-neh-kheh-mah-tah, dah-ah-mee-rahn be-ah-LE-mah, ve-eem-roo ah-mehn,','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','he','בר"ח וחולו של מועד וחנוכה אומרים כאן הלל לאחר חזרת הש"ץ. בת"צ אומרים סליחות. בימים שאין אומרים בהם תחנון יאמר הש"ץ חצי קדיש.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','en','On Rosh Chodesh, Chol HaMoed, and Chanukah, Hallel is recited. On Fast Days (Monday—Thursday—Monday, Tenth of Teves, Fast of Esther, Seventeenth of Tamuz) Selichos are recited. On days when Tachanun is omitted (see below) the chazzan continues with Half Kaddish. (14 and 15 Adar Rishon in a leap year); the entire month of Nissan; Pesach Sheini (14 Iyar); Lag BaOmer; 1-8 Sivan; 9 and 15 Av; and 29 Elul. When Tachanun is omitted on these days, it is also omitted at the preceding Mincha (afternoon service). Tachanun is also omitted in the presence of a bridegroom, in the house of a mourner during the week of mourning, and on the occasion of a circumcision if the father, the sandak or the mohel is present.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','he','טעם נכון למה נתקן הוידוי בלשון רבים כי היה צריך לומר אשמתי בגדתי וכו''. אך העניין הוא שמלבד מה שנענש האדם על חטאיו גם הוא נענש על חברו מטעם הערבות כי כל ישראל הם גוף אחד כלול מאיברים רבים. אם כן לזה ראוי לאדם שיתוודה בלשון רבים כדי שיתוודה גם על חברו. (שער הכונות)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','en','The worshipper recites the Tachanun in a sitting position, while resting his brow on his arm. During the morning service, when the hand-tefillin is on the left arm, he leans his brow on his right arm, but at the Mincha service he leans his brow on his left arm. This "falling on one''s face" symbolizes complete submission to God and the committing of our destinies into His hands. It is mentioned in the Talmud (Maseches Megillah 22b), and originates with Moses, who "Fell down before God" (Deuteronomy 9:18) and was followed by Joshua, who "Fell on the earth upon his face before the Ark of God" (Joshua 7:6)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','he','אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֺהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ תָּבֹא לְפָנֶֽיךָ תְּפִלָּֽתֵֽנוּ, וְאַל־תִּתְעַלַּם מִתְּ֒חִנָּתֵֽנוּ שֶׁאֵין אָֽנוּ עַזֵּי פָנִים וּקְשֵׁי עֹֽרֶף לוֹמַר לְפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֺהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ צַדִּיקִים אֲנַֽחְנוּ וְלֺא חָטָֽאנוּ אֲבָל אֲנַֽחְנוּ וַאֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ חָטָֽאנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','en','Our God and God of our fathers, let our prayer come before you and do not ignore our supplication. For we are not so brazen-faced and stiff-necked to say to you, Adonoy, our God, and God of our fathers, We are righteous and have not sinned. But, indeed, we and our fathers have sinned.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','transliteration','eh-loh-hey-noo veh-loh-hey ah-voh-tey-noo tah-voh le-fah-ney-khah te-fee-lah-teh-noo, ve-ahl teet-ah-lahm mee-TE-khee-nah-teh-noo sheh-eyn ah-noo ah-zey fah-neem oo-ke-shey oh-rehf loh-mahr le-fah-ney-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo veh-loh-hey ah-voh-tey-noo tsah-dee-keem ahnah-khe-noo ve-loh khah-tah-noo ah-vahl ahnah-khe-noo vah-ah-voh-tey-noo khah-tah-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','he','אָשַֽׁמְנוּ. בָּגַֽדְנוּ. גָּזַֽלְנוּ. דִּבַּֽרְנוּ דֹּֽפִי. הֶעֱוִֽינוּ. וְהִרְשַֽׁעְנוּ. זַֽדְנוּ. חָמַֽסְנוּ. טָפַֽלְנוּ שֶֽׁקֶר. יָעַֽצְנוּ רָע. כִּזַּֽבְנוּ. לַֽצְנוּ. מָרַֽדְנוּ. נִאַֽצְנוּ. סָרַֽרְנוּ. עָוִֽינוּ. פָּשַֽׁעְנוּ. צָרַֽרְנוּ. קִשִּֽׁינוּ עֹֽרֶף. רָשַֽׁעְנוּ. שִׁחַֽתְנוּ. תִּעַֽבְנוּ. תָּעִֽינוּ. תִּעְתָּֽעְנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','en','We have trespassed [against God and man, and we are devastated by our guilt]; We have betrayed [God and man, we have been ungrateful for the good done to us]; We have stolen; We have slandered. We have caused others to sin; We have caused others to commit sins for which they are called רְשָׁעִים, wicked; We have sinned with malicious intent; We have forcibly taken other''s possessions even though we paid for them; We have added falsehood upon falsehood; we have joined with evil individuals or groups. We have given harmful advice; We have deceived; We have mocked; We have rebelled against God and His Torah; We have caused God to be angry with us; We have turned away from God''s Torah; We have sinned deliberately; We have been negligent in our performance of the commandments; We have caused our friends grief; We have been stiff-necked, refusing to admit that the cause of our suffering is our own sins. We have committed sins for which we are called רָשָׁע [raising a hand to hit someone]. We have committed sins which are the result of moral corruption; We have committed sins which the Torah refers to as abominations; We have gone astray; We have led others astray.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','transliteration','ah-shah-me-noo. bah-gah-de-noo. gah-zah-le-noo. dee-bah-re-noo doh-fee. heh-eh-vee-noo. ve-heer-shah-e-noo. zah-de-noo. khah-mah-se-noo. tah-fah-le-noo sheh-kehr. yah-ah-tse-noo rah. kee-zah-ve-noo. lah-tse-noo. mah-rah-de-noo. neeah-tse-noo. sah-rah-re-noo. ah-vee-noo. pah-shah-e-noo. tsah-rah-re-noo. kee-shee-noo oh-rehf. rah-shah-e-noo. sheekhah-te-noo. teeah-ve-noo. tah-ee-noo. tee-tah-e-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','he','סַֽרְנוּ מִמִּצְוֹתֶֽיךָ וּמִמִּשְׁפָּטֶֽיךָ הַטּוֹבִים וְלֺא שָֽׁוָה לָֽנוּ. וְאַתָּה צַדִּיק עַל כָּל הַבָּא עָלֵֽינוּ. כִּי אֱמֶת עָשִֽׂיתָ וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ הִרְשָֽׁעְנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','en','We have turned away from Your commandments and from Your good laws, and we have gained nothing from it. And You are the Righteous One in all [punishment] that has come upon us; for You have acted truthfully and we have acted wickedly.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','transliteration','sah-re-noo mee-meets-voh-tey-khah oo-mee-meesh-pah-tey-khah hah-toh-veem ve-loh shah-vah lah-noo. ve-ah-tah tsah-deek ahl kohl hah-bah ah-ley-noo. kee eh-meht ah-see-tah vah-ahnah-khe-noo heer-shah-e-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','he','אֵל אֶֽרֶךְ־אַפַּֽיִם אַתָּה. וּבַֽעַל הָרַחֲמִים נִקְרֵֽאתָ. וְדֶֽרֶךְ תְּשׁוּבָה הוֹרֵֽיתָ: גְּדֻלַּת רַחֲמֶֽיךָ וַחֲסָדֶֽיךָ. תִּזְכֺּר הַיּוֹם וּבְכָל־יוֹם לְזֶֽרַע יְדִידֶֽיךָ: תֵּֽפֶן אֵלֵֽינוּ בְּרַחֲמִים. כִּי אַתָּה הוּא בַּֽעַל הָרַחֲמִים: בְּתַחֲנוּן וּבִתְ֒פִלָּה פָּנֶֽיךָ נְקַדֵּם. כְּהוֹדַֽעְתָּ לֶעָנָיו מִקֶּֽדֶם: מֵחֲרוֹן אַפְּ֒ךָ שׁוּב. כְּמוֹ בְּתוֹרָתְ֒ךָ כָּתוּב: וּבְ֒צֵל כְּנָפֶֽיךָ נֶחֱסֶה וְנִתְלוֹנָן. כְּיוֹם וַיֵֽרֶד יְהֺוָה בֶּעָנָן: תַּעֲבֺר עַל־פֶּֽשַׁע וְתִמְחֶה אָשָׁם. כְּיוֹם וַַיִּתְיַצֵּב עִמּוֹ שָׁם: תַּאֲזִין שַׁוְעָתֵֽנוּ וְתַקְשִׁיב מֶֽנוּ מַאֲמַר. כְּיוֹם וַיִּקְרָא בְשֵׁם יְהֹוָה, וְשָׁם נֶאֱמַר:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','en','You are Almighty, Slow to anger, Lord of Mercy, You are called, and the way of repentance, You have taught us. The greatness of Your mercy and kindness, remember this day and every day for the descendants of Your loved ones. Turn to us with compassion for You are the Lord of Mercy. With supplication and prayer we approach Your Presence, as You made know to [Moses,] the modest one of old. From Your fierce anger turn, as it is written in Your Torah: In the shadow of Your wings, may we be sheltered and lodged, as on the day [of which it is said:] When Adonoy descended in the cloud. Remove [our] transgression, and blot out [our] iniquity, as on the day [of which it is said:] And He stood with him there. Give ear to our cry and listen to our speech, as on the day [of which it is said:] And He proclaimed in the Name, Adonoy And there it is said:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','transliteration','ehl eh-rehkh ah-pah-yeem ah-tah. oo-vah-ahl hah-rah-khah-meem neek-reh-tah. ve-deh-rehkh te-shoo-vah hoh-rey-tah: ge-doo-laht rah-khah-mey-khah vah-khah-sah-dey-khah. teez-kohr hah-yohm oo-ve-khohl yohm le-zeh-rah ye-dee-dey-khah: teh-fehn eh-ley-noo be-rah-khah-meem. kee ah-tah hoo bah-ahl hah-rah-khah-meem: be-tah-khah-noon oo-VEET-fee-lah pah-ney-khah ne-kah-dehm. ke-hoh-dah-e-tah leh-ah-nahv mee-keh-dehm: meh-khah-rohn ah-PE-khah shoov. ke-moh be-toh-rah-TE-khah kah-toov: oo-VE-tsehl ke-nah-fey-khah neh-kheh-seh ve-neet-loh-nahn. ke-yohm vah-yeh-rehd ah-doh-NAI beh-ah-nahn: tah-ah-vohr ahl peh-shah ve-teem-kheh ah-shahm. ke-yohm vahah-yeet-yah-tsehv ee-moh shahm: tah-ah-zeen shahv-ah-teh-noo ve-tahk-sheev meh-noo mah-ah-mahr. ke-yohm vah-yeek-rah ve-shehm ah-doh-NAI, ve-shahm neh-eh-mahr:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','he','קהל וש"ץ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','en','Congregation and Chazzan:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','he','וַיַּעֲבֹר יְהֺוָה עַל פָּנָיו וַיִּקְרָא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','en','And Adonoy passed before him [Moses] and proclaimed:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','transliteration','vah-yah-ah-vohr ah-doh-NAI ahl pah-nahv vah-yeek-rah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','he','יְהֺוָה יְהֺוָה אֵל רַחוּם וְחַנּוּן אֶֽרֶךְ אַפַּֽיִם וְרַב־חֶֽסֶד וֶאֱמֶת: נֹצֵר חֶֽסֶד לָאֲלָפִים נֹשֵׂא עָוֹן וָפֶֽשַׁע וְחַטָּאָה וְנַקֵּה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','en','Adonoy, Adonoy, Almighty, Merciful, Gracious, Slow to Anger, and Abundant in Kindness and Truth. Keeper of kindness for thousands of generations, Endurer of iniquity and transgression, and sin, and Acquitter of those who repent.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','transliteration','ah-doh-NAI ah-doh-NAI ehl rah-khoom ve-khah-noon eh-rehkh ah-pah-yeem ve-rahv kheh-sehd veh-eh-meht: noh-tsehr kheh-sehd lah-ah-lah-feem noh-seh ah-vohn vah-feh-shah ve-khah-tah-ah ve-nah-keh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','he','וְסָלַחְתָּ לַעֲוֺנֵֽנוּ וּלְ֒חַטָּאתֵֽנוּ וּנְ֒חַלְתָּֽנוּ: סְלַח־לָֽנוּ אָבִֽינוּ כִּי־חָטָֽאנוּ. מְחַל־לָֽנוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ כִּי־פָשָֽׁעְנוּ: כִּי־אַתָּה אֲדֺנָי טוֹב וְסַלָּח וְרַב־חֶֽסֶד לְכָל־קוֹרְ֒אֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','en','And pardon our iniquity and our sin, and take us for Your inheritance. Pardon us, our Father, for we have sinned, forgive us, our King, for we have transgressed. For You, my Master, are good and forgiving, and abounding in kindness to all who call upon You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','transliteration','ve-sah-lahkh-tah lah-ah-voh-neh-noo oo-LE-khah-tah-teh-noo oo-NE-khahl-tah-noo: se-lahkh lah-noo ah-vee-noo kee khah-tah-noo. me-khahl lah-noo mahl-keh-noo kee fah-shah-e-noo: kee ah-tah ah-doh-nahy tohv ve-sah-lahkh ve-rahv kheh-sehd le-khohl koh-RE-ey-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','he','כשנופל על פניו יש נוהגים להטות על צד ימין משום דכתיב שויתי ה'' לנגדי תמיד. ויש נוהגים להטות על צד שמאל משום דהסבת שמאל שמה הסבה הלכך באותו צד שהוא נראה כבן מלך צריך ליכנע לפני המקום. וכבר נהגו ליפול בשחרית על צד ימין ובמנחה על צד שמאל.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','en','The following supplication is recited while resting your brow on your arm.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','he','וַיֹּֽאמֶר דָּוִד אֶל־גָּד צַר־לִי מְאֹד נִפְּ֒לָה־נָּא בְיַד־יְהֹוָה כִּי־רַבִּים רַחֲמָיו וּבְ֒יַד־אָדָם אַל־אֶפֹּֽלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','en','And David said to Gad (II Samuel 24:14), I am greatly distressed; let us fall into the hand of Adonoy for His mercies are great, but into the hand of man let me not fall."','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','transliteration','vah-yoh-mehr dah-veed ehl gahd tsahr lee me-ohd nee-PE-lah NAH ve-yahd ah-doh-NAI kee rah-beem rah-khah-mahv oo-VE-yahd ah-DAHM ahl eh-poh-lah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','he','רַחוּם וְחַנּוּן חָטָֽאתִי לְפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה מָלֵא רַחֲמִים רַחֵם עָלַי וְקַבֵּל תַּחֲנוּנָי:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','en','Merciful and gracious One, I have sinned before You; Adonoy, full of mercy, have compassion upon me and accept my supplications.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','transliteration','rah-khoom ve-khah-noon khah-tah-tee le-fah-ney-khah ah-doh-NAI mah-leh rah-khah-meem rah-khehm ah-lahy ve-kah-behl tah-khah-noo-nahy:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','he','יְהֹוָה אַל־בְּאַפְּ֒ךָ תוֹכִיחֵֽנִי וְאַל־בַּחֲמָתְ֒ךָ תְיַסְּ֒רֵֽנִי: חָנֵּֽנִי יְהֹוָה כִּי אֻמְלַל אָֽנִי רְפָאֵֽנִי יְהֹוָה כִּי נִבְהֲלוּ עֲצָמָי: וְנַפְשִׁי נִבְהֲלָה מְאֹד וְאַתָּה יְהֹוָה עַד־מָתָי: שׁוּבָה יְהֹוָה חַלְּ֒צָה נַפְשִׁי הוֹשִׁיעֵֽנִי לְמַֽעַן חַסְדֶּֽךָ: כִּי אֵין בַּמָּֽוֶת זִכְרֶךָ בִּשְׁ֒אוֹל מִי־יוֹדֶה לָּךְ: יָגַֽעְתִּי־בְּאַנְחָתִי אַשְׂחֶה בְכָל־לַֽיְלָה מִטָּתִי בְּדִמְעָתִי עַרְשִׂי אַמְסֶה: עָשְׁ֒שָׁה מִכַּֽעַס עֵינִי עָתְ֒קָה בְּכָל־צוֹרְ֒רָי: סֽוּרוּ מִמֶּֽנִּי כָּל־פֹּֽעֲלֵי אָוֶן כִּי־שָׁמַע יְהֹוָה קוֹל בִּכְיִי: שָׁמַע יְהֹוָה תְּחִנָּתִי יְהֹוָה תְּפִלָּתִי יִקָּח: יֵבֽשׁוּ וְיִבָּהֲלוּ מְאֹד כָּל־אֹיְ֒בָי יָשֻֽׁבוּ יֵבֽשׁוּ רָֽגַע:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','en','Adonoy, do not rebuke me with Your anger, nor chastise me with Your rage. Be gracious unto me, Adonoy, for I am desolate, heal me Adonoy, for my bones are terrified. My soul, [too,] is utterly terrified, and You Adonoy, how long? Return Adonoy, free my soul, deliver me for the sake of Your lovingkindness. For in death there is no mention of You; in the lower world who will thank You. I am worn out with my sighing, every night I cause my bed to float; with my tears, I melt my couch. My eye is dimmed from anger, it has aged because of my tormentors. Depart from me, all you evildoers, for Adonoy has heard the voice of my weeping. Adonoy has heard my supplication, Adonoy will (also) accept my prayer. Ashamed and utterly terrified will all my foes be, they will return and be instantaneously ashamed.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-tachanun','transliteration','ah-doh-NAI ahl be-ah-PE-khah toh-khee-kheh-nee ve-ahl bah-khah-mah-TE-khah te-yah-SE-reh-nee: khah-neh-nee ah-doh-NAI kee oom-lahl ah-nee re-fah-eh-nee ah-doh-NAI kee neev-hah-loo ah-tsah-mahy: ve-nahf-shee neev-hah-lah me-ohd ve-ah-tah ah-doh-NAI ahd mah-tahy: shoo-vah ah-doh-NAI khah-LE-tsah nahf-shee hoh-shee-eh-nee le-mah-ahn khahs-deh-khah: kee eyn bah-mah-veht zeekh-reh-khah BEESH-ohl mee yoh-deh lahkh: yah-gah-e-tee be-ahn-khah-tee ahs-kheh ve-khohl lah-ye-lah mee-tah-tee be-deem-ah-tee ahr-see ahm-seh: ah-SHE-shah mee-kah-ahs ey-nee ah-TE-kah be-khohl tsoh-RE-rahy: soo-roo mee-meh-nee kohl poh-ah-ley ah-vehn kee shah-mah ah-doh-NAI kohl beekh-yee: shah-mah ah-doh-NAI te-khee-nah-tee ah-doh-NAI te-fee-lah-tee yee-kahkh: yeh-v-shoo ve-yee-bah-hah-loo me-ohd kohl oh-YE-vahy yah-shoo-voo yeh-v-shoo rah-gah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','בתענית ציבור ובעשי"ת אומרים כאן אבינו מלכנו. גודל מעלת אבינו מלכנו הובא בספרים. ויסדה רבי עקיבא. ונתקן כנגד ברכות אמצעיות דתפלת י"ח דחול. ולפי שיש בו מעין י"ח אין אומרים בשבת.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','During the Ten Days of Penitence, Avinu Malkeinu is recited here during Shacharis—the morning service, and Mincha—the afternoon service. It is also said by some congregations on public Fast Days. The number of petitions in this prayer varies with custom, but in our rite, Avinu Malkeinu consists of 44 petitions. Since many of them are similar to the petitions of Shemoneh Esrei, Avinu Malkeinu is never recited on Shabbos, when the petitions of Shemoneh Esrei are also omitted. This unique and moving prayer is recorded as having been recited by Rabbi Akiva. The Talmud (Maseches Taanis 25b) relates that Rabbi Eliezer once stepped down before the Ark and recited the 24 benedictions for fast days and his prayers were not answered. Rabbi Akiva stepped down after him and exclaimed, "Our Father, our King, we have no king except You. Our Father, our King, for Your sake have mercy on us," and rain fell.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ חָטָֽאנוּ לְפָנֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, our King! we have sinned before You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo khah-tah-noo le-fah-ney-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ אֵין לָֽנוּ מֶֽלֶךְ אֶלָּא אָֽתָּה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father our King! we have no King except You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo eyn lah-noo meh-lehkh eh-lah ah-tah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה עִמָּֽנוּ לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, our King! deal with us [kindly] for the sake of Your Name.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo ah-seh ee-mah-noo le-mah-ahn she-meh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','בעשי"ת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','During the Ten Days of Penitence, say:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ חַדֵּשׁ עָלֵֽינוּ שָׁנָה טוֹבָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, our King! renew for us a good year.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo khah-dehsh ah-ley-noo shah-nah toh-vah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','בתענית ציבור:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','On public fast-days, say:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ בָּרֵךְ עָלֵֽינוּ שָׁנָה טוֹבָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, our King! bless us with a good year.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo bah-rehkh ah-ley-noo shah-nah toh-vah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ בַּטֵּל מֵעָלֵֽינוּ כָּל גְּזֵרוֹת קָשׁוֹת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, our King! annul all harsh decrees concerning us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo bah-tehl meh-ah-ley-noo kohl ge-zeh-roht kah-shoht:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ בַּטֵּל מַחְשְׁ֒בוֹת שׂוֹנְ֒אֵֽינוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, our King! annul the designs of those who hate us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo bah-tehl mahkh-SHE-voht soh-NE-ey-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ הָפֵר עֲצַת אוֹיְ֒בֵֽינוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, our King! thwart the plans of our enemies.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo hah-fehr ah-tsaht oh-YE-vey-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ כַּלֵּה כָּל צַר וּמַשְׂטִין מֵעָלֵֽינוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! rid us of every oppressor and adversary.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo kah-leh kohl tsahr oo-mahs-teen meh-ah-ley-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ סְתוֹם פִּיּוֹת מַשְׂטִינֵֽנוּ וּמְ֒קַטְרִיגֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! seal the mouths of our adversaries and accusers.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo se-tohm pee-yoht mahs-tee-neh-noo oo-ME-kaht-ree-geh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ כַּלֵּה דֶּֽבֶר וְחֶֽרֶב וְרָעָב וּשְׁ֒בִי וּמַשְׁחִית וְעָוֹן וּשְׁ֒מַד מִבְּ֒נֵי בְרִיתֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! remove pestilence, sword, famine, captivity, destruction, [the burden of] iniquity and religious persecution from the members of Your covenant.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo kah-leh deh-vehr ve-kheh-rehv ve-rah-ahv oo-SHE-vee oo-mahsh-kheet ve-ah-vohn oo-SHE-mahd mee-BE-ney ve-ree-teh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ מְנַע מַגֵּפָה מִנַּחֲלָתֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! withhold the plague from Your inheritance.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo me-nah mah-geh-fah mee-nah-khah-lah-teh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ סְלַח וּמְ֒חַל לְכָל עֲוֹנוֹתֵֽינוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! forgive and pardon all our iniquities.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo se-lahkh oo-ME-khahl le-khohl ah-voh-noh-tey-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ מְחֵה וְהַעֲבֵר פְּשָׁעֵֽינוּ וְחַטֹּאתֵֽינוּ מִנֶּֽגֶד עֵינֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! blot out and remove our transgressions and sins from before Your eyes.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:16:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo me-kheh ve-hah-ah-vehr pe-shah-ey-noo ve-khah-toh-tey-noo mee-neh-gehd ey-ney-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ מְחוֹק בְּרַחֲמֶֽיךָ הָרַבִּים כָּל שִׁטְ֒רֵי חוֹבוֹתֵֽינוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! erase in Your abundant mercy all records of our liabilities.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:17:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo me-khohk be-rah-khah-mey-khah hah-rah-beem kohl SHEET-rey khoh-voh-tey-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ הַחֲזִירֵֽנוּ בִּתְ֒שׁוּבָה שְׁלֵמָה לְפָנֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! bring us back in wholehearted repentance before You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:18:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo hah-khah-zee-reh-noo BEET-shoo-vah she-leh-mah le-fah-ney-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ שְׁלַח רְפוּאָה שְׁלֵמָה לְחוֹלֵי עַמֶּֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! send complete healing to the sick among Your people.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo she-lahkh re-foo-ah she-leh-mah le-khoh-ley ah-meh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ קְרַע רֹֽעַ גְּזַר דִּינֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! tear up the evil [parts] of our sentence.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:20:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo ke-rah roh-ah ge-zahr dee-neh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ זָכְ֒רֵֽנוּ בְּזִכָּרוֹן טוֹב לְפָנֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! remember us favorably before You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:21:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo zah-KHE-reh-noo be-zee-kah-rohn tohv le-fah-ney-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','בעשרת ימי תשובה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','The following five prayers are said during the Ten Days of Penitence.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ כָּתְ֒בֵֽנוּ בְּסֵֽפֶר חַיִּים טוֹבִים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! inscribe us in the Book of the Good Life.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:23:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo kah-TE-veh-noo be-seh-fehr khah-yeem toh-veem:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ כָּתְ֒בֵֽנוּ בְּסֵֽפֶר גְּאֻלָּה וִישׁוּעָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! inscribe us in the Book of Redemption and Deliverance.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:24:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo kah-TE-veh-noo be-seh-fehr ge-oo-lah vee-shoo-ah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:25:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ כָּתְ֒בֵֽנוּ בְּסֵֽפֶר פַּרְנָסָה וְכַלְכָּלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:25:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! inscribe us in the Book of Maintenance and Sustenance.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:25:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo kah-TE-veh-noo be-seh-fehr pahr-nah-sah ve-khahl-kah-lah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:26:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ כָּתְ֒בֵֽנוּ בְּסֵֽפֶר זְכֻיּוֹת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:26:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! inscribe us in the Book of Merits.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:26:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo kah-TE-veh-noo be-seh-fehr ze-khoo-yoht:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:27:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ כָּתְ֒בֵֽנוּ בְּסֵֽפֶר סְלִיחָה וּמְ֒חִילָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:27:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! inscribe us in the Book of Pardon and Forgiveness.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:27:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo kah-TE-veh-noo be-seh-fehr se-lee-khah oo-ME-khee-lah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:28:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','בתענית ציבור','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:28:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','The following five prayers are said on public fast-days.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:29:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ זָכְ֒רֵֽנוּ לְחַיִּים טוֹבִים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:29:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! remember us for a good life.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:29:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo zah-KHE-reh-noo le-khah-yeem toh-veem:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:30:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ זָכְ֒רֵֽנוּ לִגְ֒אֻלָּה וִישׁוּעָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:30:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! remember us for redemption and deliverance.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:30:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo zah-KHE-reh-noo LEEG-oo-lah vee-shoo-ah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:31:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ זָכְ֒רֵֽנוּ לְפַרְנָסָה וְכַלְכָּלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:31:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! remember us for maintenance and sustenance.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:31:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo zah-KHE-reh-noo le-fahr-nah-sah ve-khahl-kah-lah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:32:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ זָכְ֒רֵֽנוּ לִזְ֒כֻיּוֹת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:32:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! remember us for merit.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:32:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo zah-KHE-reh-noo LEEZ-khoo-yoht:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:33:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ זָכְ֒רֵֽנוּ לִסְ֒לִיחָה וּמְ֒חִילָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:33:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! remember us for pardon and forgiveness.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:33:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo zah-KHE-reh-noo LEES-lee-khah oo-ME-khee-lah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:34:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ הַצְמַח לָֽנוּ יְשׁוּעָה בְּקָרוֹב:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:34:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! cause deliverance to spring forth for us soon.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:34:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo hahts-mahkh lah-noo ye-shoo-ah be-kah-rohv:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:35:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ הָרֵם קֶֽרֶן יִשְׂרָאֵל עַמֶּֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:35:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! raise up the might of Your people Israel.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:35:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo hah-rehm keh-rehn yees-rah-ehl ah-meh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:36:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ הָרֵם קֶֽרֶן מְשִׁיחֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:36:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! raise up the might of Your anointed.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:36:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo hah-rehm keh-rehn me-shee-kheh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:37:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ מַלֵּא יָדֵֽינוּ מִבִּרְ֒כוֹתֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:37:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! fill our hands with Your blessings.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:37:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo mah-leh yah-dey-noo mee-BEER-khoh-tey-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:38:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ מַלֵּא אֲסָמֵֽינוּ שָׂבָע:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:38:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! fill our storehouses with abundance.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:38:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo mah-leh ah-sah-mey-noo sah-vah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:39:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ שְׁמַע קוֹלֵֽנוּ חוּס וְרַחֵם עָלֵֽינוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:39:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! hear our voice, spare us and have compassion upon us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:39:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo she-mah koh-leh-noo khoos ve-rah-khehm ah-ley-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:40:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ קַבֵּל בְּרַחֲמִים וּבְ֒רָצוֹן אֶת תְּפִלָּתֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:40:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! accept our prayer with compassion and favor.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:40:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo kah-behl be-rah-khah-meem oo-VE-rah-tsohn eht te-fee-lah-teh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:41:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ פְּתַח שַׁעֲרֵי שָׁמַֽיִם לִתְ֒פִלָּתֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:41:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! open the gates of heaven to our prayer.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:41:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo pe-tahkh shah-ah-rey shah-mah-yeem LEET-fee-lah-teh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:42:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ זָכוֹר כִּי עָפָר אֲנָֽחְנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:42:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! remember, that we are dust.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:42:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo zah-khohr kee ah-fahr ah-nah-khe-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:43:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ נָא אַל תְּשִׁיבֵֽנוּ רֵיקָם מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:43:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! Please do not turn us away empty-handed from You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:43:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo nah ahl te-shee-veh-noo rey-kahm mee-LE-fah-ney-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:44:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ תְּהֵא הַשָּׁעָה הַזֹּאת שְׁעַת רַחֲמִים וְעֵת רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:44:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! let this hour be an hour of compassion and a time of favor before You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:44:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo te-heh hah-shah-ah hah-zoht she-aht rah-khah-meem ve-eht rah-tsohn mee-LE-fah-ney-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:45:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ חֲמוֹל עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל עוֹלָלֵֽינוּ וְטַפֵּֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:45:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! have compassion upon us, and upon our children and infants.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:45:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo khah-mohl ah-ley-noo ve-ahl oh-lah-ley-noo ve-tah-peh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:46:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן הֲרוּגִים עַל שֵׁם קָדְשֶֽׁךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:46:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of those who were slain for Your holy Name.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:46:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo ah-seh le-mah-ahn hah-roo-geem ahl shehm kohd-sheh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:47:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן טְבוּחִים עַל יִחוּדֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:47:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of those who were slaughtered for [proclaiming] Your Unity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:47:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo ah-seh le-mah-ahn te-voo-kheem ahl yee-khoo-deh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:48:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן בָּאֵי בָאֵשׁ וּבַמַּֽיִם עַל קִדּוּשׁ שְׁמֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:48:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of those who went through fire and water for the sanctification of Your Name.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:48:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo ah-seh le-mah-ahn bah-ey vah-ehsh oo-vah-mah-yeem ahl kee-doosh she-meh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:49:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ נְקוֹם לְעֵינֵֽינוּ נִקְ֒מַת דַּם עֲבָדֶֽיךָ הַשָּׁפוּךְ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:49:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! avenge before our eyes the spilled blood of Your servants.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:49:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo ne-kohm le-ey-ney-noo NEEK-maht dahm ah-vah-dey-khah hah-shah-fookh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:50:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַעַנְ֒ךָ אִם לֺא לְמַעֲנֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:50:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for Your sake if not for ours.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:50:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo ah-seh le-mah-AHN-khah eem loh le-mah-ah-neh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:51:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַעַנְ֒ךָ וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:51:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for Your sake and deliver us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:51:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo ah-seh le-mah-AHN-khah ve-hoh-shee-eh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:52:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן רַחֲמֶֽיךָ הָרַבִּים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:52:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of Your great mercy.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:52:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo ah-seh le-mah-ahn rah-khah-mey-khah hah-rah-beem:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:53:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן שִׁמְךָ הַגָּדוֹל הַגִּבּוֹר וְהַנּוֹרָא שֶׁנִּקְרָא עָלֵֽינוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:53:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of Your great, mighty, and awesome Name which is proclaimed upon us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:53:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo ah-seh le-mah-ahn sheem-khah hah-gah-dohl hah-gee-bohr ve-hah-noh-rah sheh-neek-rah ah-ley-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:54:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ חָנֵּֽנוּ וַעֲנֵֽנוּ כִּי אֵין בָּֽנוּ מַעֲשִׂים עֲשֵׂה עִמָּֽנוּ צְדָקָה וָחֶֽסֶד וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:54:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! favor us and answer us for we have no accomplishments; deal with us charitably and kindly with us and deliver us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:54:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo khah-neh-noo vah-ah-neh-noo kee eyn bah-noo mah-ah-seem ah-seh ee-mah-noo tse-dah-kah vah-kheh-sehd ve-hoh-shee-eh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','בשני וחמישי יאמר והוא רחום. בשאר ימים שאומרים בהם תחנון יאמר שומר ישראל.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','The following prayers are added on Mondays and Thursday. On other days, continue "Guardian of Israel. . .":','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','נוהגים להרבות בתחנונים בשני וחמישי משום דאמרינן במדרש דמרע"ה עלה בחמישי לקבל לוחות אחרונות וירד בשני. ואומרים והוא רחום. ויש במדרש דג'' זקנים תקנוהו. שתפשם מלך אחד ונתנם בג'' ספינות בלא מנהיג. ושלחם לים ונתפזרו למרחקים. ולמקום שבאו הציר להם מאד ועמדו בתפלה וכל אחד יסד מקצת. ובכל חלק י"ח שמות כנגד תפלת י"ח. וימת אותו מלך שהציר להם בתחלואים רעים. ושלחו תפלתם בכל תפוצות ישראל לאמרה בשני וחמישי (ע"פ מחזור מכל השנה)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','This group of somber plaints, known as the "long Vehu Rachum" is recited in the morning service on Mondays and Thursdays, except on days when Tachanun is omitted. The origin of these seven prayers is shrouded in legend. It has been suggested that they were composed during the terrible persecutions at the hands of the Goths in seventh-century Spain. It has been said, "Whoever can read this ‘long Vehu Rachum'' prayer without emotion has lost all feeling for what is great and noble." Despite all the repetition in these cries for forgiveness, mercy, help, and protection, the effect is not tiring; because here it is not merely an individual soul, but the soul of an entire people that utters these laments and supplications, that gives voice to this woe of nearly two thousand years. Moses ascended Mount Sinai to receive the Second Tablets on the fifth day of the week, and he returned to the people on the second day of the week, bringing them the new tablets as a security for the Divine covenant and as confirmation of God''s atonement for their transgression. Ever since, the second and fifth day of each week, Monday and Thursday, have been days of summons to the Jewish people to assemble anew before God and to reaffirm their sincere "return" to the Law of God. Our regular service is therefore augmented on these days by these additional supplications.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','וְהוּא רַחוּם יְכַפֵּר עָוֺן וְלֹא־יַשְׁחִית וְהִרְבָּה לְהָשִׁיב אַפּוֹ וְלֹא־יָעִיר כָּל־חֲמָתוֹ: אַתָּה יְהֹוָה לֺא תִכְלָא רַחֲמֶֽיךָ מִמֶּֽנּוּ חַסְדְּ֒ךָ וַאֲמִתְּ֒ךָ תָּמִיד יִצְ֒רֽוּנוּ: הוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ וְקַבְּ֒צֵֽנוּ מִן־הַגּוֹיִם לְהוֹדוֹת לְשֵׁם קָדְשֶֽׁךָ לְהִשְׁתַּבֵּֽחַ בִּתְ֒הִלָּתֶֽךָ: אִם־עֲוֺנוֹת תִּשְׁמָר־יָהּ אֲדֹנָי מִי יַעֲמֹד: כִּי־עִמְּ֒ךָ הַסְּ֒לִיחָה לְמַֽעַן תִּוָּרֵא: לֺא כַחֲטָאֵֽינוּ תַּעֲשֶׂה־לָּֽנוּ וְלֹא כַעֲוֺנֹתֵֽינוּ תִּגְמֹל עָלֵֽינוּ: אִם־עֲוֺנֵֽינוּ עָֽנוּ בָֽנוּ יְהֹוָה עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ: זְכָר־רַחֲמֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה וַחֲסָדֶֽיךָ כִּי מֵעוֹלָם הֵֽמָּה: יַעֲנֵֽנוּ יְהֹוָה בְּיוֹם צָרָה יְשַׂגְּ֒בֵֽנוּ שֵׁם אֱלֺהֵי יַעֲקֹב: יְהֹוָה הוֹשִֽׁיעָה הַמֶּֽלֶךְ יַעֲנֵֽנוּ בְיוֹם־קָרְאֵֽנוּ: אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ חָנֵּֽנוּ וַעֲנֵֽנוּ כִּי אֵין בָּֽנוּ מַעֲשִׂים עֲשֵׂה עִמָּֽנוּ צְדָקָה כְּרוֹב רַחֲמֶֽיךָ וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ: אֲדוֹנֵֽינוּ אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ שְׁמַע קוֹל תַּחֲנוּנֵֽינוּ וּזְ֒כָר־לָֽנוּ אֶת־בְּרִית אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','And He, the merciful One, will atone iniquity, and will not destroy, He frequently withdraws His anger, and does not arouse all His rage. You, Adonoy, do not withhold Your mercy from us; may Your kindness and truth always protect us. Deliver us, Adonoy, our God, and gather us from among the nations to give thanks to Your holy Name to be extolled in Your praise. If You, God, should preserve iniquities, my Master, who could survive? But with You there is forgiveness, [in order] that You may be feared. Do not deal with us according to our sins nor repay us according to our iniquities. If our iniquities testify against us, Adonoy, act [mercifully] for Your Name''s sake. Remember Your mercies Adonoy, and Your kindnesses, for they are from the beginning of the world. Adonoy will answer us on the day of distress, the Name of the God of Jacob will fortify us. Adonoy, deliver [us]; the King will answer us on the day we call. Our Father, our King, favor us and answer us, for we have no [good] deeds; deal charitably with us according to Your abundant mercy and deliver us for the sake of Your Name. Our Master, our God, heed our supplications; and remember unto us the covenant of our fathers, and deliver us for Your Name''s sake.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','ve-hoo rah-khoom ye-khah-pehr ah-vohn ve-loh yahsh-kheet ve-heer-bah le-hah-sheev ah-poh ve-loh yah-eer kohl khah-mah-toh: ah-tah ah-doh-NAI loh teekh-lah rah-khah-mey-khah mee-meh-noo khahs-DE-khah vah-ah-mee-TE-khah tah-meed YEETS-roo-noo: hoh-shee-eh-noo ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo ve-kah-BE-tseh-noo meen hah-goh-yeem le-hoh-doht le-shehm kohd-sheh-khah le-heesh-tah-beh-ahkh BEET-hee-lah-teh-khah: eem ah-voh-noht teesh-mohr yahh ah-doh-nahy mee yah-ah-mohd: kee ee-ME-khah hah-SE-lee-khah le-mah-ahn tee-vah-reh: loh khah-khah-tah-ey-noo tah-ah-seh lah-noo ve-loh khah-ah-voh-noh-tey-noo teeg-mohl ah-ley-noo: eem ah-voh-ney-noo ah-noo vah-noo ah-doh-NAI ah-seh le-mah-ahn she-meh-khah: ze-khahr rah-khah-mey-khah ah-doh-NAI vah-khah-sah-dey-khah kee meh-oh-lahm heh-mah: yah-ah-neh-noo ah-doh-NAI be-yohm tsah-rah ye-sah-GE-veh-noo shehm eh-loh-hey yah-ah-kohv: ah-doh-NAI hoh-shee-ah hah-meh-lehkh yah-ah-neh-noo ve-yohm kah-re-eh-noo: ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo khah-neh-noo vah-ah-neh-noo kee eyn bah-noo mah-ah-seem ah-seh ee-mah-noo tse-dah-kah ke-rohv rah-khah-mey-khah ve-hoh-shee-eh-noo le-mah-ahn she-meh-khah: ah-doh-ney-noo eh-loh-hey-noo she-mah kohl tah-khah-noo-ney-noo oo-ZE-khahr lah-NOO eht be-reet ah-voh-tey-noo ve-hoh-shee-eh-noo le-mah-ahn she-meh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','וְעַתָּה אֲדֹנָי אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ אֲשֶׁר הוֹצֵֽאתָ אֶת־עַמְּ֒ךָ מֵאֶֽרֶץ מִצְרַֽיִם בְּיָד חֲזָקָה וַתַּֽעַשׂ־לְךָ שֵׁם כַּיּוֹם הַזֶּה חָטָֽאנוּ רָשָֽׁעְנוּ: אֲדֹנָי כְּכָל־צִדְ֒קֹתֶֽיךָ יָֽשָׁב־נָא אַפְּ֒ךָ וַחֲמָתְ֒ךָ מֵעִירְ֒ךָ יְרוּשָׁלַֽםִ הַר־קָדְשֶֽׁךָ כִּי בַחֲטָאֵֽינוּ וּבַעֲוֺנוֹת אֲבֹתֵֽינוּ יְרוּשָׁלַֽםִ וְעַמְּ֒ךָ לְחֶרְפָּה לְכָל־סְבִיבֹתֵֽינוּ: וְעַתָּה שְׁמַע אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ אֶל־תְּפִלַּת עַבְדְּךָ וְאֶל־תַּחֲנוּנָיו וְהָאֵר פָּנֶֽיךָ עַל־מִקְדָּשְׁ֒ךָ הַשָּׁמֵם לְמַֽעַן אֲדֹנָי:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','And now, my Master, our God, who brought out Your people, from the land of Egypt with a mighty hand, and made for Yourself a name to this day;'' we have sinned, we have acted wickedly. My Master, with all Your righteousness turn away Your anger and Your rage from Your city, Jerusalem, Your holy mountain; for because of our sins and the iniquities of our fathers, Jerusalem and Your people are [held] in contempt by all who surround us. And now, listen our God, to the prayers of Your servant and to his supplications; and let Your radiant countenance shine upon Your desolate Sanctuary for Your sake, my Master.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','ve-ah-tah ah-doh-nahy eh-loh-hey-noo ah-shehr hoh-tseh-tah eht ah-ME-khah meh-eh-rehts meets-rah-yeem be-yahd khah-zah-kah vah-tah-ahs le-khah shehm kah-yohm hah-zeh khah-tah-noo rah-shah-e-noo: ah-doh-nahy ke-khohl TSEED-koh-tey-khah yah-shahv nah ah-PE-khah vah-khah-mah-TE-khah meh-ee-RE-khah ye-roo-shah-lah-mee hahr kohd-sheh-khah kee vah-khah-tah-ey-noo oo-vah-ah-voh-noht ah-voh-tey-noo ye-roo-shah-lah-mee ve-ah-ME-khah le-khehr-pah le-khohl se-vee-voh-tey-noo: ve-ah-tah she-mah eh-loh-hey-noo ehl te-fee-laht ahv-de-khah ve-ehl tah-khah-noo-nahv ve-hah-ehr pah-ney-khah ahl meek-dah-SHE-khah hah-shah-mehm le-mah-ahn ah-doh-nahy:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','הַטֵּה אֱלֺהַי אָזְנְךָ וּשְׁ֒מָע פְּקַח עֵינֶֽיךָ וּרְ֒אֵה שֹׁמְ֒מוֹתֵֽינוּ וְהָעִיר אֲשֶׁר־נִקְרָא שִׁמְךָ עָלֶֽיהָ כִּי לֺא עַל־צִדְ֒קֹתֵֽינוּ אֲנַֽחְנוּ מַפִּילִים תַּחֲנוּנֵֽינוּ לְפָנֶֽיךָ כִּי עַל־רַחֲמֶֽיךָ הָרַבִּים: אֲדֹנָי שְׁמָֽעָה אֲדֹנָי סְלָֽחָה אֲדֹנָי הַקְשִֽׁיבָה וַעֲשֵׂה אַל־תְּאַחַר: לְמַעַנְ֒ךָ אֱלֺהַי כִּי־שִׁמְךָ נִקְרָא עַל־עִירְ֒ךָ וְעַל־עַמֶּֽךָ: אָבִֽינוּ אָב הָרַחֲמָן הַרְאֵֽנוּ אוֹת לְטוֹבָה וְקַבֵּץ נְפוּצוֹתֵֽינוּ מֵאַרְבַּע כַּנְ֒פוֹת הָאָֽרֶץ: יַכִּֽירוּ וְיֵדְ֒עוּ כָּל־הַגּוֹיִם כִּי אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ: וְעַתָּה יְהֹוָה אָבִֽינוּ אָֽתָּה אֲנַֽחְנוּ הַחֹֽמֶר וְאַתָּה יֹצְ֒רֵֽנוּ וּמַעֲשֵׂה יָדְ֒ךָ כֻּלָּֽנוּ: הוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ צוּרֵֽנוּ וְגוֹאֲלֵֽנוּ: חֽוּסָה יְהֹוָה עַל־עַמֶּֽךָ וְאַל־תִּתֵּן נַחֲלָתְ֒ךָ לְחֶרְפָּה לִמְשָׁל־בָּם גּוֹיִם: לָֽמָּה יֹאמְ֒רוּ בָעַמִּים אַיֵּה (נָא) אֱלֺהֵיהֶם: יָדַֽעְנוּ יְהֺוָה כִּי חָטָֽאנוּ וְאֵין מִי יַעֲמֹד בַּעֲדֵֽנוּ אֶלָּא שִׁמְךָ הַגָּדוֹל יַעֲמָד־לָֽנוּ בְּעֵת צָרָה: יָדַֽעְנוּ כִּי אֵין בָּֽנוּ מַעֲשִׂים צְדָקָה עֲשֵׂה עִמָּֽנוּ לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ: כְּרַחֵם אָב עַל־בָּנִים כֵּן תְּרַחֵם יְהֹוָה עָלֵֽינוּ וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ: חֲמוֹל עַל עַמֶּֽךָ רַחֵם עַל נַחֲלָתֶֽךָ חֽוּסָה־נָּא כְּרוֹב רַחֲמֶֽיךָ חָנֵּֽנוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ וַעֲנֵֽנוּ כִּי לְךָ יְהֹוָה הַצְּ֒דָקָה עֹשֵׂה נִפְלָאוֹת בְּכָל עֵת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Incline Your ear, my God, and hear; open Your eyes and behold our desolate places and the city which is called by Your Name, for it is not on account of our righteousness that we let fall our supplications before You, but because of Your great mercy. My Master, hear! my Master, forgive! my Master, listen and take action, do not delay! For Your sake, my God, for Your Name is proclaimed over Your city and Your people. Our Father, merciful Father, show us a sign for good and gather our dispersed [people] from the four corners of the earth, [so that] all nations will recognize and know that You, Adonoy, are our God. And now, Adonoy, You are our Father; we are the clay and You are our Former; and we are all the work of Your hand. Deliver us, for Your Name''s sake our Father, our King, our Rock and our Redeemer. Adonoy, spare Your people, and let not Your heritage be [an object] of contempt for nations to rule over. Why should they say among the peoples, Where is their God? Adonoy, we know that we have sinned, and there is none to stand up in our behalf; let Your great Name, then, stand up for us at the time of distress. We know that we have no [good] deeds, [therefore] deal charitably with us for Your Name''s sake. As a father has compassion on his children, so do You have compassion on us, Adonoy, and [therefore] deliver us for Your Name''s sake. Have pity on Your people, have compassion on Your heritage, spare us with Your great mercy; favor us. our King, and answer us, for righteousness is Yours, Adonoy, Who performs wonders at all times.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','hah-teh eh-loh-hahy ohz-ne-khah oo-SHE-mah pe-kahkh ey-ney-khah oo-RE-eh shoh-ME-moh-tey-noo ve-hah-eer ah-shehr neek-rah sheem-khah ah-ley-hah kee loh ahl TSEED-koh-tey-noo ahnah-khe-noo mah-pee-leem tah-khah-noo-ney-noo le-fah-ney-khah kee ahl rah-khah-mey-khah hah-rah-beem: ah-doh-nahy she-mah-ah ah-doh-nahy se-lah-khah ah-doh-nahy hahk-shee-vah vah-ah-seh ahl te-ah-khahr: le-mah-AHN-khah eh-loh-hahy kee sheem-khah neek-rah ahl ee-RE-khah ve-ahl ah-meh-khah: ah-vee-noo ahv hah-rah-khah-mahn hahr-eh-noo oht le-toh-vah ve-kah-behts ne-foo-tsoh-tey-noo meh-ahr-bah KAHN-foht hah-ah-rehts: yah-kee-roo ve-yeh-DE-oo kohl hah-goh-yeem kee ah-tah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo: ve-ah-tah ah-doh-NAI ah-vee-noo ah-tah ahnah-khe-noo hah-khoh-mehr ve-ah-tah yoh-TSE-reh-noo oo-mah-ah-seh yah-DE-khah koo-lah-noo: hoh-shee-eh-noo le-mah-ahn she-meh-khah ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo tsoo-reh-noo ve-goh-ah-leh-noo: khoo-sah ah-doh-NAI ahl ah-meh-khah ve-ahl tee-tehn nah-khah-lah-TE-khah le-khehr-pah leem-shahl bahm goh-yeem: lah-mah yoh-ME-roo vah-ah-meem ah-yeh (nah) eh-loh-hey-hehm: yah-dah-e-noo ah-doh-NAI kee khah-tah-noo ve-eyn mee yah-ah-mohd bah-ah-deh-noo eh-lah sheem-khah hah-gah-dohl yah-ah-mahd lah-noo be-eht tsah-rah: yah-dah-e-noo kee eyn bah-noo mah-ah-seem tse-dah-kah ah-seh ee-mah-noo le-mah-ahn she-meh-khah: ke-rah-khehm ahv ahl bah-neem kehn te-rah-khehm ah-doh-NAI ah-ley-noo ve-hoh-shee-eh-noo le-mah-ahn she-meh-khah: khah-mohl ahl ah-meh-khah rah-khehm ahl nah-khah-lah-teh-khah khoo-sah nah ke-rohv rah-khah-mey-khah khah-neh-noo mahl-keh-noo vah-ah-neh-noo kee le-khah ah-doh-NAI hah-TSE-dah-kah oh-seh neef-lah-oht be-khohl eht:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','הַבֶּט־נָא רַחֶם־נָא וְהוֹשִֽׁיעָה־נָא צֹאן מַרְעִיתֶֽךָ וְאַל יִמְשָׁל־בָּֽנוּ קֶֽצֶף כִּי לְךָ יְהֹוָה הַיְ֒שׁוּעָה: בְּךָ תוֹחַלְתֵּֽנוּ אֱלֽוֹהַּ סְלִיחוֹת אָנָּא סְלַח־נָא כִּי אֵל טוֹב וְסַלָּח אָֽתָּה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Look, we beseech You, speedily have compassion and deliver the sheep of Your pasture; let wrath not prevail over us, for, Adonoy, deliverance is Yours. Our hope rests with You, God of forgiveness; please forgive [us], for You Almighty, are good, and forgiving.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','hah-beht nah rah-khehm nah ve-hoh-shee-ah nah tsohn mahr-ee-teh-khah ve-ahl yeem-shahl bah-noo keh-tsehf kee le-khah ah-doh-NAI hah-YE-shoo-ah: be-khah toh-khahl-teh-noo eh-loh-ahh se-lee-khoht ah-nah se-lahkh nah kee ehl tohv ve-sah-lahkh ah-tah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','אָנָּא מֶֽלֶךְ חַנוּן וְרַחוּם זְכוֹר וְהַבֵּט לִבְ֒רִית בֵּין הַבְּ֒תָרִים וְתֵרָאֶה לְפָנֶֽיךָ עֲקֵדַת יָחִיד וּלְ֒מַֽעַן יִשְׂרָאֵל אָבִֽינוּ: אַל־תַּעַזְ֒בֵֽנוּ אָבִֽינוּ וְאַל־תִּטְּ֒שֵֽׁנוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ וְאַל־תִּשְׁכָּחֵֽנוּ יוֹצְ֒רֵֽנוּ וְאַל־תַּֽעַשׁ עִמָּֽנוּ כָּלָה בְּגָלוּתֵֽנוּ כִּי אֵל מֶֽלֶךְ חַנּוּן וְרַחוּם אָֽתָּה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','We beseech You, gracious and compassionate King, remember and look to the Covenant between the divided pieces, and let appear before You the binding [upon the Altar] of the only son, and for the sake of Israel, our father. Do not abandon us our father, do not cast us off our King, do not forget us our Creator, and do not bring destruction upon us in our exile for You are the Almighty who is King, gracious and merciful.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','ah-nah meh-lehkh khah-noon ve-rah-khoom ze-khohr ve-hah-beht LEEV-reet beyn hah-BE-tah-reem ve-teh-rah-eh le-fah-ney-khah ah-keh-daht yah-kheed oo-LE-mah-ahn yees-rah-ehl ah-vee-noo: ahl tah-AHZ-veh-noo ah-vee-noo ve-ahl tee-TE-sheh-noo mahl-keh-noo ve-ahl teesh-kah-kheh-noo yoh-TSE-reh-noo ve-ahl tah-ahsh ee-mah-noo kah-lah be-gah-loo-teh-noo kee ehl meh-lehkh khah-noon ve-rah-khoom ah-tah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','אֵין כָּמֽוֹךָ חַנּוּן וְרַחוּם יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ אֵין כָּמֽוֹךָ אֵל אֶֽרֶךְ אַפַּֽיִם וְרַב חֶֽסֶד וֶאֱמֶת: הוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ וְרַחֲמֵֽנוּ בְּרַחֲמֶֽיךָ הָרַבִּים מֵרַֽעַשׁ וּמֵרֺֽגֶז הַצִּילֵֽנוּ: זְכֺר לַעֲבָדֶֽיךָ לְאַבְרָהָם לְיִצְחָק וּלְ֒יַעֲקֹב אַל־תֵּֽפֶן אֶל־קְשִׁי הָעָם הַזֶּה וְאֶל־רִשְׁעוֹ וְאֶל־חַטָּאתוֹ: שׁוּב מֵחֲרוֹן אַפֶּֽךָ וְהִנָּחֵם עַל־הָרָעָה לְעַמֶּֽךָ: וְהָסֵר מִמֶּֽנּוּ מַכַּת הַמָּֽוֶת כִּי רַחוּם אָֽתָּה: כִּי כֵן דַּרְכֶּֽךָ עֹשֶׂה חֶֽסֶד חִנָּם בְּכָל־דּוֹר וָדוֹר: חֽוּסָה יְהֹוָה עַל־עַמֶּֽךָ וְהַצִּילֵֽנוּ מִזַּעְמֶֽךָ: וְהָסֵר מִמֶּֽנּוּ מַכַּת הַמַּגֵּפָה וּגְ֒זֵרָה קָשָׁה כִּי אַתָּה שׁוֹמֵר יִשְׂרָאֵל: לְךָ אֲדֹנָי הַצְּ֒דָקָה וְלָֽנוּ בּֽשֶׁת הַפָּנִים: מַה־נִּתְאוֹנֵן וּמַה־נֹּאמַר מַה־נְּדַבֵּר וּמַה־נִּצְטַּדָּק: נַחְפְּשָׂה דְרָכֵֽינוּ וְנַחְקֺֽרָה וְנָשֽׁוּבָה אֵלֶֽיךָ כִּי יְמִינְ֒ךָ פְשׁוּטָה לְקַבֵּל שָׁבִים: אָֽנָּא יְהֹוָה הוֹשִֽׁיעָה נָּא אָֽנָּא יְהֹוָה הַצְלִיחָה נָא: אָֽנָּא יְהֹוָה עֲנֵֽנוּ בְיוֹם קָרְאֵֽנוּ: לְךָ יְהֹוָה חִכִּֽינוּ לְךָ יְהֹוָה קִוִּינוּ לְךָ יְהֹוָה נְיַחֵל אַל תֶּחֱשֶׁה וּתְ֒עַנֵּֽנוּ כִּי נָאֲמוּ גוֹיִם אָבְ֒דָה תִקְוָתָם: כָּל־בֶּֽרֶךְ לְךָ תִכְרַע וְכָל־קוֹמָה לְפָנֶֽיךָ לְבַד תִּשְׁתַּחֲוֶה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','There is none like You, gracious and merciful Adonoy, our God; there is none like You, Almighty, slow to anger, abundant in kindliness and truth. Deliver us, and have mercy on us with Your great mercy, save us from storm and rage. Remember Your servants, Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob; do not consider the stubbornness of this people, their wickedness, and their sinfulness. Turn from Your fierce anger and let Your mind be changed concerning the evil [intended] for Your people. Remove from us the scourge of death, for You are merciful; for such is Your way— to bestow undeserved kindness in every generation. Spare Your people, Adonoy, and save us from Your wrath; remove from us the scourge of plague, and harsh decree, for You are the Guardian of Israel. Righteousness is Yours, my Master, while shame is ours. How can we complain? What can we say? What can we speak? and how can we justify ourselves? Let us search into our ways and examine them, and return to You; for Your right hand is extended to receive those who repent. We beseech You Adonoy!—deliver us. We beseech You Adonoy!—grant us success; We beseech You Adonoy! — answer us on the day we call. For You, Adonoy, we have waited, For You, Adonoy, we have hoped, For You, Adonoy, we yearn. Do not be silent, and do not allow us to be tormented; for the nations have said, "Their hope is lost." Let every knee bend to You and all who stand erect prostrate themselves before You','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','eyn kah-moh-khah khah-noon ve-rah-khoom ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo eyn kah-moh-khah ehl eh-rehkh ah-pah-yeem ve-rahv kheh-sehd veh-eh-meht: hoh-shee-eh-noo ve-rah-khah-meh-noo be-rah-khah-mey-khah hah-rah-beem meh-rah-ahsh oo-meh-roh-gehz hah-tsee-leh-noo: ze-khohr lah-ah-vah-dey-khah le-ahv-rah-hahm le-yeets-khahk oo-LE-yah-ah-kohv ahl teh-fehn ehl ke-shee hah-ahm hah-zeh ve-ehl reesh-oh ve-ehl khah-tah-toh: shoov meh-khah-rohn ah-peh-khah ve-hee-nah-khehm ahl hah-rah-ah le-ah-meh-khah: ve-hah-sehr mee-meh-noo mah-kaht hah-mah-veht kee rah-khoom ah-tah: kee khehn dahr-keh-khah oh-seh kheh-sehd khee-nahm be-khohl dohr vah-dohr: khoo-sah ah-doh-NAI ahl ah-meh-khah ve-hah-tsee-leh-noo mee-zah-meh-khah: ve-hah-sehr mee-meh-noo mah-kaht hah-mah-geh-fah oo-GE-zeh-rah kah-shah kee ah-tah shoh-mehr yees-rah-ehl: le-khah ah-doh-nahy hah-TSE-dah-kah ve-lah-noo b-sheht hah-pah-neem: mahh neet-oh-nehn oo-mahh noh-mahr mahh ne-dah-behr oo-mahh neets-tah-dahk: nahkh-pe-sah de-rah-khey-noo ve-nahkh-koh-rah ve-nah-shoo-vah eh-ley-khah kee ye-mee-NE-khah fe-shoo-tah le-kah-behl shah-veem: ah-nah ah-doh-NAI hoh-shee-ah nah ah-nah ah-doh-NAI hahts-lee-khah nah: ah-nah ah-doh-NAI ah-neh-noo ve-yohm kah-re-eh-noo: le-khah ah-doh-NAI khee-kee-noo le-khah ah-doh-NAI kee-vee-noo le-khah ah-doh-NAI ne-yah-khehl ahl teh-kheh-sheh oo-TE-ah-neh-noo kee nah-ah-moo goh-yeem ah-VE-dah teek-vah-tahm: kohl beh-rehkh le-khah teekh-rah ve-khohl koh-mah le-fah-ney-khah le-vahd teesh-tah-khah-veh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','הַפּוֹתֵֽחַ יָד בִּתְ֒שׁוּבָה לְקַבֵּל פּוֹשְׁ֒עִים וְחַטָּאִים נִבְהֲלָה נַפְשֵֽׁנוּ מֵרוֹב עִצְּ֒בוֹנֵֽנוּ אַל־תִּשְׁכָּחֵֽנוּ נֶֽצַח קֽוּמָה וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ: אַל־תִּשְׁפּוֹךְ חֲרוֹנְ֒ךָ עָלֵֽינוּ כִּי אֲנַֽחְנוּ עַמְּ֒ךָ בְּנֵי בְרִיתֶֽךָ: אֵל הַבִּֽיטָה דַּל כְּבוֹדֵֽנוּ בַּגּוֹיִם וְשִׁקְּ֒צֽוּנוּ כְּטֻמְאַת הַנִּדָּה: עַד־מָתַי עֻזְּ֒ךָ בַּשְּׁ֒בִי וְתִפְאַרְתְּ֒ךָ בְּיַד־צָר: עוֹרְ֒רָה גְבוּרָתְ֒ךָ וְהוֹשִׁעֵֽנוּ לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ: אַל־יִמְעֲטוּ לְפָנֶֽיךָ תְּלָאוֹתֵֽינוּ: מַהֵר יְקַדְּ֒מֽוּנוּ רַחֲמֶֽיךָ בְּעֵת צָרוֹתֵֽינוּ, לֺא לְמַעֲנֵֽנוּ אֶלָּא לְמַעַנְ֒ךָ פְעַל, וְאַל תַּשְׁחִית אֶת־זֵֽכֶר שְׁאֵרִיתֵֽנוּ, כִּי לְךָ מְיַחֲלוֹת עֵינֵֽינוּ כִּי אֵל מֶֽלֶךְ חַנוּן וְרַחוּם אָֽתָּה: וּזְ֒כוֹר עֵדוּתֵֽנוּ בְּכָל־יוֹם תָּמִיד אוֹמְ֒רִים פַּעֲמַֽיִם בְּאַהֲבָה: שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ יְהֹוָה אֶחָד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','You Who opens Your hand to [accept] repentance, to receive transgressors and sinners: our soul is terrified from our great sorrow— forget us not forever; arise and deliver us. Do not pour out Your wrath upon us, for we are Your people, the children of Your covenant. Almighty, look! Our glory has sunk low among the nations, and they abominate us like the impurity of the nidah. How long will Your strength be in captivity, and Your glory, in the hand of the foe? Arouse Your might and deliver us for the sake of Your Name, let our sufferings not seem trivial to You. May Your mercy come swiftly toward us in time of our distress; not for our sake, but do it for Your sake, and do not obliterate the remembrance of our remnant, for our eyes look hopefully to You, for You are the Almighty Who is King, Gracious, and Merciful. Remember our testimony every day we proclaim twice a day with love: Hear Israel, Adonoy is our God, Adonoy is One.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','hah-poh-teh-ahkh yahd BEET-shoo-vah le-kah-behl poh-SHE-eem ve-khah-tah-eem neev-hah-lah nahf-sheh-noo meh-rohv ee-TSE-voh-neh-noo ahl teesh-kah-kheh-noo neh-tsahkh koo-mah ve-hoh-shee-eh-noo: ahl teesh-pohkh khah-roh-NE-khah ah-ley-noo kee ahnah-khe-noo ah-ME-khah be-ney ve-ree-teh-khah: ehl hah-bee-tah dahl ke-voh-deh-noo bah-goh-yeem ve-shee-KE-tsoo-noo ke-toom-aht hah-nee-dah: ahd mah-tahy oo-ZE-khah bah-SHE-vee ve-teef-ahr-TE-khah be-yahd tsahr: oh-RE-rah ge-voo-rah-TE-khah ve-hoh-shee-eh-noo le-mah-ahn she-meh-khah: ahl yeem-ah-too le-fah-ney-khah te-lah-oh-tey-noo: mah-hehr ye-kah-DE-moo-noo rah-khah-mey-khah be-eht tsah-roh-tey-noo, loh le-mah-ah-neh-noo eh-lah le-mah-AHN-khah fe-ahl, ve-ahl tahsh-kheet eht zeh-khehr she-eh-ree-teh-noo, kee le-khah me-yah-khah-loht ey-ney-noo kee ehl meh-lehkh khah-noon ve-rah-khoom ah-tah: oo-ZE-khohr eh-doo-teh-noo be-khohl yohm tah-meed oh-ME-reem pah-ah-mah-yeem be-ah-hah-vah: she-mah yees-rah-ehl ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo ah-doh-NAI eh-khahd:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל שׁוּב מֵחֲרוֹן אַפֶּֽךָ וְהִנָּחֵם עַל־הָרָעָה לְעַמֶּֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Adonoy, God of Israel, turn from Your fierce anger, and let Your mind be changed concerning the evil intended for Your people.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey yees-rah-ehl shoov meh-khah-rohn ah-peh-khah ve-hee-nah-khehm ahl hah-rah-ah le-ah-meh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','הַבֵּט מִשָּׁמַֽיִם וּרְ֒אֵה כִּי הָיִֽינוּ לַֽעַג וָקֶֽלֶס בַּגּוֹיִם: נֶחְשַֽׁבְנוּ כַּצֹּאן לָטֶֽבַח יוּבָל, לַהֲרוֹג וּלְ֒אַבֵּד וּלְ֒מַכָּה וּלְ֒חֶרְפָּה: וּבְכָל־זֹאת שִׁמְךָ לֺא שָׁכָֽחְנוּ נָא אַל־תִּשְׁכָּחֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Look from heaven and behold that we have become [an object] of scorn and derision among the nations; we are considered as the sheep led to the slaughter to be slain and destroyed, tortured and humiliated. And yet despite all this, we have not forgotten Your Name; please, do not forget us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','hah-beht mee-shah-mah-yeem oo-RE-eh kee hah-yee-noo lah-ahg vah-keh-lehs bah-goh-yeem: nehkh-shah-ve-noo kah-tsohn lah-teh-vahkh yoo-vahl, lah-hah-rohg oo-LE-ah-behd oo-LE-mah-kah oo-LE-khehr-pah: oo-ve-khohl zoht sheem-khah loh shah-khah-khe-noo nah ahl teesh-kah-kheh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל שׁוּב מֵחֲרוֹן אַפֶּֽךָ וְהִנָּחֵם עַל־הָרָעָה לְעַמֶּֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Adonoy, God of Israel, turn from Your fierce anger, and let Your mind be changed concerning the evil intended for Your people.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey yees-rah-ehl shoov meh-khah-rohn ah-peh-khah ve-hee-nah-khehm ahl hah-rah-ah le-ah-meh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','זָרִים אוֹמְ֒רִים אֵין תּוֹחֶֽלֶת וְתִקְוָה: חוֹן אוֹם לְשִׁמְךָ מְקַוֶּה: טָהוֹר, יְשׁוּעָתֵֽנוּ קָרְ֒בָה, יָגַֽעְנוּ וְלֺא הֽוּנַח־לָֽנוּ: רַחֲמֶֽיךָ יִכְבְּ֒שׁוּ אֶת־כַּעַסְ֒ךָ מֵעָלֵֽינוּ: אָנָּא שׁוּב מֵחֲרוֹנְ֒ךָ וְרַחֵם סְגֻלָּה אֲשֶׁר בָּחָֽרְתָּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Strangers say: there is no hope or expectation [for us.] Be gracious to the people who place their hope in Your Name. Pure One, bring our deliverance near; we are weary and no relief is granted us. May Your mercy suppress Your anger from us. We beseech You, turn from Your anger, and have compassion on the treasured people whom You have chosen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','zah-reem oh-ME-reem eyn toh-kheh-leht ve-teek-vah: khohn ohm le-sheem-khah me-kah-veh: tah-hohr, ye-shoo-ah-teh-noo kah-RE-vah, yah-gah-e-noo ve-loh hoo-nahkh lah-noo: rah-khah-mey-khah yeekh-BE-shoo eht kah-AHS-khah meh-ah-ley-noo: ah-nah shoov meh-khah-roh-NE-khah ve-rah-khehm se-goo-lah ah-shehr bah-khah-re-tah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל שׁוּב מֵחֲרוֹן אַפֶּֽךָ וְהִנָּחֵם עַל־הָרָעָה לְעַמֶּֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Adonoy, God of Israel, turn from Your fierce anger, and let Your mind be changed concerning the evil intended for Your people.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey yees-rah-ehl shoov meh-khah-rohn ah-peh-khah ve-hee-nah-khehm ahl hah-rah-ah le-ah-meh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','חֽוּסָה יְהֹוָה עָלֵֽינוּ בְּרַחֲמֶֽיךָ, וְאַל תִּתְּ֒נֵֽנוּ בִּידֵי אַכְזָרִים: לָֽמָּה יֹאמְ֒רוּ הַגּוֹיִם אַיֵּה־נָא אֱלֺהֵיהֶם לְמַעַנְ֒ךָ עֲשֵׂה עִמָּֽנוּ חֶֽסֶד וְאַל תְּאַחַר: אָנָּא שׁוּב מֵחֲרוֹנְ֒ךָ וְרַחֵם סְגֻלָּה אֲשֶׁר בָּחָֽרְתָּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Adonoy, in Your mercy, spare us, do not discard us in the hands of cruel foes. Why should the nations say: Where now is their God? For Your sake, deal kindly with us and do not delay. We beseech You, turn from Your anger, and have compassion on the treasured people whom You have chosen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','khoo-sah ah-doh-NAI ah-ley-noo be-rah-khah-mey-khah, ve-ahl tee-TE-neh-noo bee-dey ahkh-zah-reem: lah-mah yoh-ME-roo hah-goh-yeem ah-yeh nah eh-loh-hey-hehm le-mah-AHN-khah ah-seh ee-mah-noo kheh-sehd ve-ahl te-ah-khahr: ah-nah shoov meh-khah-roh-NE-khah ve-rah-khehm se-goo-lah ah-shehr bah-khah-re-tah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל שׁוּב מֵחֲרוֹן אַפֶּֽךָ וְהִנָּחֵם עַל־הָרָעָה לְעַמֶּֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Adonoy, God of Israel, turn from Your fierce anger, and let Your mind be changed concerning the evil intended for Your people.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey yees-rah-ehl shoov meh-khah-rohn ah-peh-khah ve-hee-nah-khehm ahl hah-rah-ah le-ah-meh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','קוֹלֵֽנוּ תִשְׁמַע וְתָחוֹן וְאַל־תִּטְּ֒שֵֽׁנוּ בְּיַד אֹיְ֒בֵֽינוּ לִמְחוֹת אֶת־שְׁמֵֽנוּ: זְכוֹר אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּֽעְתָּ לַאֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ, כְּכוֹכְ֒בֵי הַשָּׁמַֽיִם אַרְבֶּה אֶת־זַרְעֲכֶם וְעַתָּה נִשְׁאַֽרְנוּ מְעַט מֵהַרְבֵּה: וּבְכָל־זֹאת שִׁמְךָ לֺא שָׁכָֽחְנוּ נָא אַל תִּשְׁכָּחֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Hear our voice and be gracious, do not cast us off into the hands of our enemies to obliterate our name. Remember what You have sworn to our fathers: Like the stars of the heavens will I multiply your descendants, and now, we are left only a few out of many. And yet despite all this, we have not forgotten Your Name; please, do not forget us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:16:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','koh-leh-noo teesh-mah ve-tah-khohn ve-ahl tee-TE-sheh-noo be-yahd oh-YE-vey-noo leem-khoht eht she-meh-noo: ze-khohr ah-shehr neesh-bah-e-tah lah-ah-voh-tey-noo, ke-khoh-KHE-vey hah-shah-mah-yeem ahr-beh eht zahr-ah-khehm ve-ah-tah neesh-ah-re-noo me-aht meh-hahr-beh: oo-ve-khohl zoht sheem-khah loh shah-khah-khe-noo nah ahl teesh-kah-kheh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל שׁוּב מֵחֲרוֹן אַפֶּֽךָ וְהִנָּחֵם עַל־הָרָעָה לְעַמֶּֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Adonoy, God of Israel, turn from Your fierce anger, and let Your mind be changed concerning the evil intended for Your people.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:17:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey yees-rah-ehl shoov meh-khah-rohn ah-peh-khah ve-hee-nah-khehm ahl hah-rah-ah le-ah-meh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','עָזְ֒רֵֽנוּ אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׁעֵֽנוּ עַל־דְּבַר כְּבוֹד־שְׁמֶֽךָ וְהַצִּילֵֽנוּ וְכַפֵּר עַל־חַטֹּאתֵֽינוּ לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Help us, God of our deliverance for the sake of the glory of Your Name; save us and atone our sins for the sake of Your Name.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:18:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','ah-ZE-reh-noo eh-loh-hey yeesh-eh-noo ahl de-vahr ke-vohd she-meh-khah ve-hah-tsee-leh-noo ve-khah-pehr ahl khah-toh-tey-noo le-mah-ahn she-meh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל שׁוּב מֵחֲרוֹן אַפֶּֽךָ וְהִנָּחֵם עַל־הָרָעָה לְעַמֶּֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Adonoy, God of Israel, turn from Your fierce anger, and let Your mind be changed concerning the evil intended for Your people.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey yees-rah-ehl shoov meh-khah-rohn ah-peh-khah ve-hee-nah-khehm ahl hah-rah-ah le-ah-meh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','שׁוֹמֵר יִשְׂרָאֵל שְׁמוֹר שְׁאֵרִית יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאַל יֹאבַד יִשְׂרָאֵל הָאֹמְ֒רִים שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Guardian of Israel, guard the remnant of Israel, and let not Israel perish, who say, "Hear Israel."','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:20:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','shoh-mehr yees-rah-ehl she-mohr she-eh-reet yees-rah-ehl ve-ahl yoh-vahd yees-rah-ehl hah-oh-ME-reem she-mah yees-rah-ehl:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','שׁוֹמֵר גּוֹי אֶחָד שְׁמוֹר שְׁאֵרִית עַם אֶחָד וְאַל יֹאבַד גּוֹי אֶחָד הַמְ֒יַחֲדִים שִׁמְךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ יְהֹוָה אֶחָד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Guardian of the unique nation, guard the remnant of the unique people, and let not the unique nation perish, who proclaim the Oneness of Your Name, [saying:] Adonoy is our God, Adonoy is One.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:21:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','shoh-mehr gohy eh-khahd she-mohr she-eh-reet ahm eh-khahd ve-ahl yoh-vahd gohy eh-khahd hah-ME-yah-khah-deem sheem-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo ah-doh-NAI eh-khahd:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','שׁוֹמֵר גּוֹי קָדוֹשׁ שְׁמוֹר שְׁאֵרִית עַם קָדוֹשׁ וְאַל יֹאבַד גּוֹי קָדוֹשׁ הַמְ֒שַׁלְּ֒שִׁים בְּשָׁלשׁ קְדֻשּׁוֹת לְקָדוֹשׁ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Guardian of the holy nation, guard the remnant of the holy people and let not the holy nation perish who repeat the threefold sanctification to the Holy One.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:22:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','shoh-mehr gohy kah-dohsh she-mohr she-eh-reet ahm kah-dohsh ve-ahl yoh-vahd gohy kah-dohsh hah-ME-shah-LE-sheem be-shahlsh ke-doo-shoht le-kah-dohsh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','מִתְרַצֶּה בְּרַחֲמִים וּמִתְפַּיֵּס בְּתַחֲנוּנִים הִתְרַצֶּה וְהִתְפַּיֵּס לְדוֹר עָנִי כִּי אֵין עוֹזֵר: אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ חָנֵּֽנוּ וַעֲנֵֽנוּ כִּי אֵין בָּֽנוּ מַעֲשִׂים עֲשֵׂה עִמָּֽנוּ צְדָקָה וָחֶֽסֶד וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','You Who are appeased by pleas for mercy, and conciliated by supplications, be appeased and conciliated to an afflicted generation, for there is none else to help. Our Father, our King! be gracious to us and answer us for we have no [good] deeds, deal with us charitably and kindly and deliver us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:23:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','meet-rah-tseh be-rah-khah-meem oo-meet-pah-yehs be-tah-khah-noo-neem heet-rah-tseh ve-heet-pah-yehs le-dohr ah-nee kee eyn oh-zehr: ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo khah-neh-noo vah-ah-neh-noo kee eyn bah-noo mah-ah-seem ah-seh ee-mah-noo tse-dah-kah vah-kheh-sehd ve-hoh-shee-eh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ לֺא נֵדַע מַה נַּעֲשֶׂה כִּי עָלֶֽיךָ עֵינֵֽינוּ: זְכֹר רַחֲמֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה וַחֲסָדֶֽיךָ כִּי מֵעוֹלָם הֵֽמָּה: יְהִי חַסְדְּ֒ךָ יְהֹוָה עָלֵֽינוּ כַּאֲשֶׁר יִחַֽלְנוּ לָךְ: אַל תִּזְכָּר לָֽנוּ עֲוֹנוֹת רִאשׁוֹנִים מַהֵר יְקַדְּ֒מֽוּנוּ רַחֲמֶֽיךָ כִּי דַלּֽוֹנוּ מְאֹד: עֶזְרֵֽנוּ בְּשֵׁם יְהֹוָה עֹשֵׂה שָׁמַֽיִם וְאָֽרֶץ: חָנֵּֽנוּ יְהֹוָה חָנֵּֽנוּ כִּי־רַב שָׂבַֽעְנוּ בוּז: בְּרֺֽגֶז רַחֵם תִּזְכּוֹר: בְּרֹֽגֶז עַקֵדָה תִּזְכּוֹר, בְּרֹֽגֶז תְּמִימוֹת תִּזְכּוֹר: יְהֹוָה הוֹשִֽׁיעָה, הַמֶּֽלֶךְ יַעֲנֵֽנוּ בְיוֹם קָרְאֵֽנוּ: כִּי הוּא יָדַע יִצְרֵֽנוּ זָכוּר כִּי עָפָר אֲנָֽחְנוּ: עָזְ֒רֵֽנוּ אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׁעֵֽנוּ עַל־דְּבַר כְּבוֹד־שְׁמֶֽךָ וְהַצִּילֵֽנוּ וְכַפֵּר עַל־חַטֹּאתֵֽינוּ לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','As for us, we know not what to do; but our eyes are upon You. Remember Your mercies, Adonoy, and kindnesses for they are from the beginning of the world. Adonoy! may Your kindness be upon us, as we have waited for You. Remember not the sins of our ancestors; let Your mercy come swiftly toward us, for we have been brought very low. Help us for the Name of Adonoy Creator of Heaven and earth. Be gracious to us, Adonoy, be gracious to us for we are saturated with humiliation. [Even] in anger remember to have compassion. [Even] in anger remember the binding of Isaac. Even in anger remember the uprightness of Jacob Adonoy deliver [us] the King will answer us on the day we call. For He knows of what we are made; He is mindful that we are but dust. Help us, God of our deliverance, for the sake of the glory of Your Name; save us and atone our sins, for the sake of Your Name.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:24:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','vah-ahnah-khe-noo loh neh-dah mahh nah-ah-seh kee ah-ley-khah ey-ney-noo: ze-khohr rah-khah-mey-khah ah-doh-NAI vah-khah-sah-dey-khah kee meh-oh-lahm heh-mah: ye-hee khahs-DE-khah ah-doh-NAI ah-ley-noo kah-ah-shehr yeekhah-le-noo lahkh: ahl teez-kahr lah-noo ah-voh-noht ree-shoh-neem mah-hehr ye-kah-DE-moo-noo rah-khah-mey-khah kee dah-loh-noo me-ohd: ehz-reh-noo be-shehm ah-doh-NAI oh-seh shah-mah-yeem ve-ah-rehts: khah-neh-noo ah-doh-NAI khah-neh-noo kee rahv sah-vah-e-noo vooz: be-roh-gehz rah-khehm teez-kohr: be-roh-gehz ah-keh-dah teez-kohr, be-roh-gehz te-mee-moht teez-kohr: ah-doh-NAI hoh-shee-ah, hah-meh-lehkh yah-ah-neh-noo ve-yohm kah-re-eh-noo: kee hoo yah-dah yeets-reh-noo zah-khoor kee ah-fahr ah-nah-khe-noo: ah-ZE-reh-noo eh-loh-hey yeesh-eh-noo ahl de-vahr ke-vohd she-meh-khah ve-hah-tsee-leh-noo ve-khah-pehr ahl khah-toh-tey-noo le-mah-ahn she-meh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:25:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','ש"ץ אומר חצי קדיש:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:25:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','The Chazzan recites the Half Kaddish','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:26:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְ֒מָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְקָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:26:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming if His Messiah in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:26:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','yeet-gah-dahl ve-yeet-kah-dahsh she-meh rah-bah be-ah-LE-mah dee ve-rah kheer-oo-teh ve-yahm-leekh mahl-khoo-teh ve-yahts-mahkh poo-re-kah-neh vee-kah-rehv (kehts) me-shee-kheh be-khah-yey-khohn oo-ve-yoh-mey-khohn oo-ve-khah-yey de-khahl beyt yees-rah-ehl, bah-ah-gah-lah oo-veez-mahn kah-reev ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:27:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:27:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:27:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','ye-heh she-meh rah-bah me-vah-rahkh le-ah-lahm oo-le-ah-LE-mey ah-LE-mah-yah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:28:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:28:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He;','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:28:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','yeet-bah-rahkh ve-yeesh-tah-bahkh ve-yeet-pah-ahr ve-yeet-roh-mahm ve-yeet-nah-seh ve-yeet-hah-dahr ve-yeet-ah-leh ve-yeet-hah-lahl she-meh de-koo-de-shah, be-reekh hoo','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:29:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','לְעֵֽלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְ֒עֵֽלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְ֒מָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:29:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:29:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','le-eh-lah (vshyt" oo-LE-eh-lah mee-kahl) meen kohl beer-khah-tah ve-shee-rah-tah, toosh-be-khah-tah ve-neh-kheh-mah-tah, dah-ah-mee-rahn be-ah-LE-mah, ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:30:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','אשרי ובא לציון. כשמכריזים דבר יש להכריז קודם שיתחיל החזן אשרי (מגן אברהם סי'' קלב)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:30:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','On days when the Torah is not read continue with Ashrei.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','אַשְׁרֵי יוֹשְׁ֒בֵי בֵיתֶֽךָ עוֹד יְהַלְ֒לֽוּךָ סֶּֽלָה: אַשְׁרֵי הָעָם שֶׁכָּֽכָה לּוֹ אַשְׁרֵי הָעָם שֶׁיְהֹוָה אֱלֺהָיו: תְּהִלָּה לְדָוִד אֲרוֹמִמְךָ אֱלוֹהַי הַמֶּֽלֶךְ וַאֲבָרְ֒כָה שִׁמְךָ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד: בְּכָל־יוֹם אֲבָרְ֒כֶֽךָ וַאֲהַלְ֒לָה שִׁמְךָ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד: גָּדוֹל יְהֹוָה וּמְהֻלָּל מְאֹד וְלִגְ֒דֻלָּתוֹ אֵין חֵֽקֶר: דּוֹר לְדוֹר יְשַׁבַּח מַעֲשֶׂיךָ וּגְ֒בוּרֹתֶֽיךָ יַגִּֽידוּ: הֲדַר כְּבוֹד הוֹדֶֽךָ וְדִבְרֵי נִפְלְ֒אֹתֶֽיךָ אָשִֽׂיחָה: וֶעֱזוּז נוֹרְ֒אוֹתֶֽיךָ יֹאמֵֽרוּ וּגְ֒דֻלָּתְ֒ךָ אֲסַפְּ֒רֶֽנָּה: זֵֽכֶר רַב־טוּבְ֒ךָ יַבִּֽיעוּ וְצִדְ֒קָתְ֒ךָ יְרַנֵּֽנוּ: חַנּוּן וְרַחוּם יְהֹוָה אֶֽרֶךְ אַפַּֽיִם וּגְ֒דָל־חָֽסֶד: טוֹב־יְהֹוָה לַכֹּל וְרַחֲמָיו עַל־כָּל־מַעֲשָׂיו: יוֹדֽוּךָ יְהֹוָה כָּל־מַעֲשֶֽׂיךָ וַחֲסִידֶֽיךָ יְבָרְ֒כֽוּכָה: כְּבוֹד מַלְכוּתְ֒ךָ יֹאמֵֽרוּ וּגְ֒בוּרָתְ֒ךָ יְדַבֵּֽרוּ: לְהוֹדִֽיעַ לִבְנֵי הָאָדָם גְּבוּרֹתָיו וּכְ֒בוֹד הֲדַר מַלְכוּתוֹ: מַלְכוּתְ֒ךָ מַלְכוּת כָּל־עֹלָמִים וּמֶמְשַׁלְתְּ֒ךָ בְּכָל־דּוֹר וָדֹר: סוֹמֵךְ יְהֹוָה לְכָל־הַנֹּפְ֒לִים וְזוֹקֵף לְכָל־הַכְּ֒פוּפִים: עֵינֵי־כֹל אֵלֶֽיךָ יְשַׂבֵּֽרוּ וְאַתָּה נוֹתֵן־לָהֶם אֶת־אָכְלָם בְּעִתּוֹ: פּוֹתֵֽחַ אֶת־יָדֶֽךָ וּמַשְׂבִּֽיעַ לְכָל־חַי רָצוֹן: צַדִּיק יְהֹוָה בְּכָל־דְּרָכָיו וְחָסִיד בְּכָל־מַעֲשָׂיו: קָרוֹב יְהֹוָה לְכָל־קֹרְ֒אָיו לְכֹל אֲשֶׁר יִקְרָאֻֽהוּ בֶאֱמֶת: רְצוֹן־יְרֵאָיו יַעֲשֶׂה וְאֶת־שַׁוְעָתָם יִשְׁמַע וְיוֹשִׁיעֵם: שׁוֹמֵר יְהֹוָה אֶת־כָּל־אֹהֲבָיו וְאֵת כָּל־הָרְ֒שָׁעִים יַשְׁמִיד: תְּהִלַּת יְהֹוָה יְדַבֶּר פִּי וִיבָרֵךְ כָּל־בָּשָׂר שֵׁם קָדְשׁוֹ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד: וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ נְבָרֵךְ יָהּ מֵעַתָּה וְעַד־עוֹלָם הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','Fortunate are those who dwell in Your house; may they continue to praise You, Selah. Fortunate is the people whose lot is thus; Fortunate is the people for whom Adonoy is their God. A praise by David! I will exalt You, my God, the King, and bless Your Name forever and ever. Every day I will bless You and extol Your Name forever and ever. Adonoy is great and highly extolled, and His greatness is unfathomable. One generation to another will praise Your works and Your mighty acts they will declare. The splendor of Your glorious majesty, and the words of Your wonders I will speak. Of Your awesome might, they will speak, and Your greatness I will recount. Mention of Your bountifulness they will express, and in Your righteousness joyfully exult. Adonoy is gracious and compassionate, slow to anger and great in kindliness. Adonoy is good to all, His mercy encompasses all His works. All Your works will thank You, Adonoy, and Your pious ones will bless You. Of the honor of Your kingship, they will speak and Your might they will declare. To reveal to men His mighty acts, and the glorious splendor of His kingship. Your kingship is the kingship for all times, and Your dominion is in every generation. Adonoy supports all the fallen, and straightens all the bent. The eyes of all look expectantly to You, and You give them their food at its proper time. You open Your hand and satisfy the desire of every living being. Adonoy is just in all His ways, and benevolent in all His deeds. Adonoy is near to all who call upon Him, to all who call upon Him in truth. The will of those who fear Him He fulfills; He hears their cry and delivers them. Adonoy watches over all those who love Him, and will destroy all the wicked. Praise of Adonoy, my mouth will declare, and all flesh will bless His holy Name forever and ever. And we will bless God from now on forever. Praise God.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','ahsh-rey yoh-SHE-vey vey-teh-khah ohd ye-hah-LE-loo-khah seh-lah: ahsh-rey hah-ahm sheh-kah-khah loh ahsh-rey hah-ahm shehy-ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hahv: te-hee-lah le-dah-veed ah-roh-meem-khah eh-loh-hahy hah-meh-lehkh vah-ah-vah-RE-khah sheem-khah le-oh-lahm vah-ehd: be-khohl yohm ah-vah-RE-kheh-khah vah-ah-hah-LE-lah sheem-khah le-oh-lahm vah-ehd: gah-dohl ah-doh-NAI oo-me-hoo-lahl me-ohd ve-LEEG-doo-lah-toh eyn kheh-kehr: dohr le-dohr ye-shah-bahkh mah-ah-sey-khah oo-GE-voo-roh-tey-khah yah-gee-doo: hah-dahr ke-vohd hoh-deh-khah ve-deev-rey neef-LE-oh-tey-khah ah-see-khah: veh-eh-zooz noh-RE-oh-tey-khah yoh-meh-roo oo-GE-doo-lah-TE-khah ah-sah-PE-reh-nah: zeh-khehr rahv too-VE-khah yah-bee-oo ve-TSEED-kah-TE-khah ye-rah-neh-noo: khah-noon ve-rah-khoom ah-doh-NAI eh-rehkh ah-pah-yeem oo-GE-dahl khah-SEHD: tohv ah-doh-NAI lah-kohl ve-rah-khah-mahv ahl kohl mah-ah-sahv: yoh-doo-khah ah-doh-NAI kohl mah-ah-sey-khah vah-khah-see-dey-khah ye-vah-RE-khoo-khah: ke-vohd mahl-khoo-TE-khah yoh-meh-roo oo-GE-voo-rah-TE-khah ye-dah-beh-roo: le-hoh-dee-ah leev-ney hah-ah-dahm ge-voo-roh-tahv oo-KHE-vohd hah-dahr mahl-khoo-toh: mahl-khoo-TE-khah mahl-khoot kohl oh-lah-meem oo-mehm-shahl-TE-khah be-khohl dohr vah-dohr: soh-mehkh ah-doh-NAI le-khohl hah-noh-FE-leem ve-zoh-kehf le-khohl hah-KE-foo-feem: ey-ney khohl eh-ley-khah ye-sah-beh-roo ve-ah-tah noh-tehn lah-hehm eht ohkh-lahm be-ee-toh: poh-teh-ahkh eht yah-deh-khah oo-mahs-bee-ah le-khohl khahy rah-tsohn: tsah-deek ah-doh-NAI be-khohl de-rah-khahv ve-khah-seed be-khohl mah-ah-sahv: kah-rohv ah-doh-NAI le-khohl koh-RE-ahv le-khohl ah-shehr yeek-rah-oo-hoo veh-eh-meht: re-tsohn ye-reh-ahv yah-ah-seh ve-eht shahv-ah-tahm yeesh-mah ve-yoh-shee-ehm: shoh-mehr ah-doh-NAI eht kohl oh-hah-vahv ve-eht kohl hah-RE-shah-eem yahsh-meed: te-hee-laht ah-doh-NAI ye-dah-behr pee vee-vah-rehkh kohl bah-sahr shehm kohd-shoh le-oh-lahm vah-ehd: vah-ahnah-khe-noo ne-vah-rehkh yahh meh-ah-tah ve-ahd oh-lahm hah-LE-loo-yahh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','אלו ימים שאין אומרים בהם למנצח ואל ארך אפים. ר"ח חנוכה ופורים ערב פסח וערב יו"כ ותשעה באב. והוא הדין ביום י"ד וט"ו באדר ראשון. גם אין אומרים אותם בבית האבל דכללא הוא דאא"א ולמנצח דינם שוה. (דה"ח)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','Psalm 20 is omitted on the following days: Rosh Chodesh, the day before Yom Kippur, Chanukah, both days of Purim, the day before Passover, the intermediate days of the Festivals (Chol HaMoed), and Tisha b''Av. It is also omitted when prayers are recited in the house of a mourner, the entire month of Nisssan, Pesach Sheni (14th of Iyar) Lag-b''omer, from Rosh Codesh Sivan through the twelfth of the month i.e., 5 days after Shavuoth, the Fifteenth of av, from Erev Yom Kippur until the end of Tishre, the Fifteenth of Shevat, when there is a circumcision in the Synagogue, or when a bride groom during the seven days of his wedding celebration is present.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','מה שתקנו לאומרו בסוף התפלה מפני שאומר במדרש תלים אמר ר'' שמעון בר אבא אתה מוצא י"ח מזמורים מראש הספר ועד פסוק זה ואשרי האיש ולמה רגשו גוים חד הוא כנגד י"ח ברכות שאדם מתפלל בכל יום. אדם אומר לחבירו תתעני צלותך כך דוד המלך לאחר ששר י"ח שירות ותושבחות אמר יענך ה'' ביום צרה והכי איתא בירושלמי. ובשבתות ובימים טובים אין אומרים אותו מפני שהוא מזמור של תחנה וגם הוא מתחיל יענך ה'' ביום צרה ושבתות וימים טובים אינם ימי צרה אלא ימי שמחה. (אבודרהם)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','According to Rabbi S.R. Hirsch, this psalm is addressed to David by the people of Israel. It is a testimonial of trust that the people have in the Divinely-appointed king, who is accustomed to victory and triumph. At the same time, it proclaims the eternal truth that the victories which our king wins for our people are to be attributed not to his bravery, nor to his sword, nor to his soldiers, but solely to his relationship with God, His Sanctuary, and His Law.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','לַמְנַצֵּֽחַ מִזְמוֹר לְדָוִד: יַעַנְ֒ךָ יְהֹוָה בְּיוֹם צָרָה יְשַׂגֶּבְ֒ךָ שֵׁם אֱלֺהֵי יַעֲקֹב: יִשְׁלַח עֶזְרְךָ מִקֹּֽדֶשׁ וּמִצִּיּוֹן יִסְעָדֶֽךָּ: יִזְכֹּר כָּל מִנְחֹתֶֽיךָ וְעוֹלָתְ֒ךָ יְדַשְּׁ֒נֶה סֶּֽלָה: יִתֶּן לְךָ כִלְ֒בָבֶֽךָ וְכָל עֲצָתְ֒ךָ יְמַלֵּא: נְרַנְּ֒נָה בִּישׁוּעָתֶֽךָ וּבְ֒שֵׁם אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ נִדְגֹּל יְמַלֵּא יְהֹוָה כָּל מִשְׁאֲלוֹתֶֽיךָ: עַתָּה יָדַֽעְתִּי כִּי הוֹשִֽׁיעַ יְהֹוָה מְשִׁיחוֹ יַעֲנֵֽהוּ מִשְּׁ֒מֵי קָדְשׁוֹ בִּגְ֒בוּרוֹת יֵֽשַׁע יְמִינוֹ: אֵֽלֶּה בָרֶֽכֶב וְאֵֽלֶּה בַסּוּסִים וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ בְּשֵׁם יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ נַזְכִּיר: הֵֽמָּה כָּרְ֒עוּ וְנָפָֽלוּ וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ קַֽמְנוּ וַנִּתְעוֹדָד: יְהֹוָה הוֹשִׁיעָה הַמֶּֽלֶךְ יַעֲנֵֽנוּ בְיוֹם קָרְאֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','To Him Who grants victory, a Psalm of David May Adonoy answer you on the day of distress; May the Name of Jacob''s God fortify you. May He send your help from the Sanctuary, and support you from Zion. May He remember all your meal-offerings, and accept your burnt sacrifices, Selah. May He grant you what your heart desires, and fulfill all your plans. We will sing at Your deliverance, and in the Name of our God, raise our banners; May Adonoy fulfill all your wishes. Now I know that Adonoy has delivered His anointed one, He will answer him from His holy heavens with the mighty deliverance of His right hand. Some [rely] upon chariots and some upon horses, but as for us, upon the Name of Adonoy, our God, we call. They have bowed down and fallen, but we have risen and stand firm. Adonoy, deliver [us], the King will answer us on the day we call.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','lahm-nah-tseh-ahkh meez-mohr le-dah-veed: yah-AHN-khah ah-doh-NAI be-yohm tsah-rah ye-sah-GEHV-khah shehm eh-loh-hey yah-ah-kohv: yeesh-lahkh ehz-re-khah mee-koh-dehsh oo-mee-tsee-yohn yees-ah-deh-kah: yeez-kohr kohl meen-khoh-tey-khah ve-oh-lah-TE-khah ye-dah-SHE-neh seh-lah: yee-tehn le-khah KHEEL-vah-veh-khah ve-khohl ah-tsah-TE-khah ye-mah-leh: ne-rah-NE-nah bee-shoo-ah-teh-khah oo-VE-shehm eh-loh-hey-noo need-gohl ye-mah-leh ah-doh-NAI kohl meesh-ah-loh-tey-khah: ah-tah yah-dah-e-tee kee hoh-shee-ah ah-doh-NAI me-shee-khoh yah-ah-neh-hoo mee-SHE-mey kohd-shoh BEEG-voo-roht yeh-shah ye-mee-noh: eh-leh vah-reh-khehv ve-eh-leh vah-soo-seem vah-ahnah-khe-noo be-shehm ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo nahz-keer: heh-mah kah-RE-oo ve-nah-fah-loo vah-ahnah-khe-noo kah-me-noo vah-neet-oh-dahd: ah-doh-NAI hoh-shee-ah hah-meh-lehkh yah-ah-neh-noo ve-yohm kah-re-eh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','מה שתקנו סדר קדושה בסוף התפלה בעבור עמי הארץ המאחרים לבא לתפלה שלא יפסידו שמיעת הקדושה. דאמרינן בשלהי סוטה אמאי קאי עלמא אסדרא דקדושה ואיהא שמיה רבה דאגדתא. ולכך תקנו לתרגם סדר קדושה זה כדי שיבינו עמי הארץ שאין מכירים לדבר בלשון הקדש אלא בלשון תרגום שהיו רגילין לדבר בו באותו זמן. (אבודרהם)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','This portion, known as Kedushas d''Sidra, was introduced at the conclusion of the morning service to accomodate those who came to the synagogue too late to hear the Kedushah in Shemoneh Esrei. The Talmud (Maseches Sotah 49a) declares that the world is preserved solely by virtue of this Kedushah, and by the virtue of our answering, "May His great Name," which is part of the Kaddish recited following the study of the Aggadah. Because of its importance, a vernacular translation in Aramaic was added, so that even those ignorant of Hebrew would understand the sacred words.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','וּבָא לְצִיּוֹן גּוֹאֵל וּלְ֒שָׁבֵי פֶֽשַׁע בְּיַעֲקֹב נְאֻם יְהֹוָה: וַאֲנִי זֹאת בְּרִיתִי אֹתָם אָמַר יְהֹוָה רוּחִי אֲשֶׁר עָלֶֽיךָ וּדְ֒בָרַי אֲשֶׁר שַֽׂמְתִּי בְּפִֽיךָ לֺא יָמֽוּשׁוּ מִפִּֽיךָ וּמִפִּי זַרְעֲךָ וּמִפִּי זֶֽרַע זַרְעֲךָ אָמַר יְהֹוָה מֵעַתָּה וְעַד עוֹלָם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','The Redeemer shall come to Zion and to those of Jacob who repent from sin, says Adonoy. As for Me, this is My covenant with them, said Adonoy: My spirit which is upon you, and My words which I have put in your mouth shall not depart from your mouth, nor from the mouth of your children, nor from the mouth of your children''s children, said Adonoy— from now to eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','oo-vah le-tsee-yohn goh-ehl oo-LE-shah-vey feh-shah be-yah-ah-kohv ne-oom ah-doh-NAI: vah-ah-nee zoht be-ree-tee oh-tahm ah-mahr ah-doh-NAI roo-khee ah-shehr ah-ley-khah oo-DE-vah-rahy ah-shehr sah-me-tee be-fee-khah loh yah-moo-shoo mee-pee-khah oo-mee-pee zahr-ah-khah oo-mee-pee zeh-rah zahr-ah-khah ah-mahr ah-doh-NAI meh-ah-tah ve-ahd oh-lahm:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','וְאַתָּה קָדוֹשׁ יוֹשֵׁב תְּהִלּוֹת יִשְׂרָאֵל: וְקָרָא זֶה אֶל זֶה וְאָמַר קָדוֹשׁ קָדוֹשׁ קָדוֹשׁ יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת מְלֺא כָל הָאָֽרֶץ כְּבוֹדוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','(This next section is the actual Kedushah d''Sidra) And You, Holy One, are enthroned upon the praises of Israel. And [the angels] call one to another and say: Holy, holy, holy is Adonoy of Hosts: the fullness of all the earth is His glory."','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','ve-ah-tah kah-dohsh yoh-shehv te-hee-loht yees-rah-ehl: ve-kah-rah zeh ehl zeh ve-ah-mahr kah-dohsh kah-dohsh kah-dohsh ah-doh-NAI tse-vah-oht me-loh khohl hah-ah-rehts ke-voh-doh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','וּמְ֒קַבְּ֒לִין דֵּין מִן דֵּין וְאָמְ֒רִין קַדִּישׁ בִּשְׁ֒מֵי מְרוֹמָא עִלָּאָה בֵּית שְׁכִינְתֵּהּ קַדִּישׁ עַל אַרְעָא עוֹבַד גְּבוּרְתֵּהּ קַדִּישׁ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת, מַלְיָא כָל אַרְעָא זִיו יְקָרֵהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','And they receive [sanction] one from another, and say, Holy in the highest heights of heaven, the abode of His Divine Presence; holy upon earth, the work of His mighty power; holy forever and to all eternity— is Adonoy of hosts; the whole earth is filled with the radiance of His glory.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','oo-ME-kah-BE-leen deyn meen deyn ve-ah-ME-reen kah-deesh BEESH-mey me-roh-mah ee-lah-ah beyt she-khee-ne-teh kah-deesh ahl ahr-ah oh-vahd ge-voo-re-teh kah-deesh le-ah-lahm oo-le-ah-LE-mey ah-LE-mah-yah ah-doh-NAI tse-vah-oht, mahl-yah khohl ahr-ah zeev ye-kah-reh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','וַתִּשָּׂאֵֽנִי רֽוּחַ וָאֶשְׁמַע אַחֲרַי קוֹל רַֽעַשׁ גָּדוֹל בָּרוּךְ כְּבוֹד יְהֹוָה מִמְּ֒קוֹמוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','And a wind lifted me; and I heard behind me the sound of a great rushing; Blessed is the glory of Adonoy from His place.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','vah-tee-sah-eh-nee roo-ahkh vah-ehsh-mah ah-khah-rahy kohl rah-ahsh gah-dohl bah-rookh ke-vohd ah-doh-NAI mee-ME-koh-moh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','וּנְ֒טָלַתְנִי רוּחָא וּשְׁמָעִית בַּתְרַי קָל זִֽיעַ סַגִּיא דִּמְ֒שַׁבְּ֒חִין וְאָמְ֒רִין בְּרִיךְ יְקָרָא דַיהוָֹה מֵאֲתַר בֵּית שְׁכִינְתֵּהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','And a wind lifted me and I heard behind me a sound of a great rushing of those who uttered praises and said, ‘Blessed is the glory of Adonoy from the place, the abode of His Divine Presence.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','oo-NE-tah-laht-nee roo-khah oo-she-mah-eet baht-rahy kahl zee-ah sah-gee DEEM-shah-BE-kheen ve-ah-ME-reen be-reekh ye-kah-rah dah-ah-doh-NAI meh-ah-tahr beyt she-khee-ne-teh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','יְהֹוָה יִמְלֺךְ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','Adonoy will reign forever and ever.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','ah-doh-NAI yeem-lohkh le-oh-lahm vah-ehd:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','יְהֹוָה מַלְכוּתֵהּ קָאֵים לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','Adonoy, His kingdom is established forever and to all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','ah-doh-NAI mahl-khoo-teh kah-eym le-ah-lahm oo-le-ah-LE-mey ah-LE-mah-yah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵי אַבְרָהָם יִצְחָק וְיִשְׂרָאֵל אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ שָׁמְ֒רָה זֹאת לְעֹלָם לְיֵֽצֶר מַחְשְׁ֒בוֹת לְבַב עַמֶּֽךָ וְהָכֵן לְבָבָם אֵלֶֽיךָ: וְהוּא רַחוּם יְכַפֵּר עָוֹן וְלֺא יַשְׁחִית וְהִרְבָּה לְהָשִׁיב אַפּוֹ וְלֺא יָעִיר כָּל חֲמָתוֹ: כִּי אַתָּה אֲדֹנָי טוֹב וְסַלָּח וְרַב חֶֽסֶד לְכָל קֹרְ֒אֶֽיךָ: צִדְ֒קָתְ֒ךָ צֶֽדֶק לְעוֹלָם וְתוֹרָתְ֒ךָ אֱמֶת: תִּתֵּן אֱמֶת לְיַעֲקֹב חֶֽסֶד לְאַבְרָהָם אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּֽעְתָּ לַאֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ מִֽימֵי קֶֽדֶם: בָּרוּךְ אֲדֹנָי יוֹם יוֹם יַעֲמָס לָֽנוּ הָאֵל יְשׁוּעָתֵֽנוּ סֶֽלָה: יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת עִמָּֽנוּ מִשְׂגָּב לָֽנוּ אֱלֺהֵי יַעֲקֹב סֶֽלָה: יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת אַשְׁרֵי אָדָם בֹּטֵֽחַ בָּךְ: יְהֹוָה הוֹשִֽׁיעָה הַמֶּֽלֶךְ יַעֲנֵֽנוּ בְיוֹם קָרְאֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','Adonoy, God of Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, our fathers, keep this forever as the intention of the hearts of Your people, and direct their hearts to You. And He, the merciful One, atones iniquity and does not destroy; He frequently withdraws His anger and does not arouse all His rage. For You, my Master, are good and forgiving, and abounding in kindness to all who call upon You. Your righteousness is everlasting and Your Torah is truth. You will grant truth to Jacob, kindliness to Abraham, as You have sworn to our fathers from the days of old. Blessed is my Master day by day; He loads us [with blessings], the Almighty Who is our deliverance, forever. Adonoy of Hosts is with us a stronghold for us is the God of Jacob, Selah. Adonoy of Hosts, fortunate is the man who trusts in You. Adonoy, deliver [us]; the King will answer us on the day we call.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey ahv-rah-hahm yeets-khahk ve-yees-rah-ehl ah-voh-tey-noo shah-ME-rah zoht le-oh-lahm le-yeh-tsehr mahkh-SHE-voht le-vahv ah-meh-khah ve-hah-khehn le-vah-vahm eh-ley-khah: ve-hoo rah-khoom ye-khah-pehr ah-vohn ve-loh yahsh-kheet ve-heer-bah le-hah-sheev ah-poh ve-loh yah-eer kohl khah-mah-toh: kee ah-tah ah-doh-nahy tohv ve-sah-lahkh ve-rahv kheh-sehd le-khohl koh-RE-ey-khah: TSEED-kah-TE-khah tseh-dehk le-oh-lahm ve-toh-rah-TE-khah eh-meht: tee-tehn eh-meht le-yah-ah-kohv kheh-sehd le-ahv-rah-hahm ah-shehr neesh-bah-e-tah lah-ah-voh-tey-noo mee-mey keh-dehm: bah-rookh ah-doh-nahy yohm yohm yah-ah-mahs lah-noo hah-ehl ye-shoo-ah-teh-noo seh-lah: ah-doh-NAI tse-vah-oht ee-mah-noo mees-gahv lah-noo eh-loh-hey yah-ah-kohv seh-lah: ah-doh-NAI tse-vah-oht ahsh-rey ah-dahm boh-teh-ahkh bahkh: ah-doh-NAI hoh-shee-ah hah-meh-lehkh yah-ah-neh-noo ve-yohm kah-re-eh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','בָּרוּךְ הוּא אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ שֶׁבְּ֒רָאָֽנוּ לִכְ֒בוֹדוֹ וְהִבְדִּילָֽנוּ מִן הַתּוֹעִים וְנָֽתַן לָֽנוּ תּוֹרַת אֱמֶת וְחַיֵּי עוֹלָם נָטַע בְּתוֹכֵֽנוּ הוּא יִפְתַּח לִבֵּֽנוּ בְּתוֹרָתוֹ וְיָשֵׂם בְּלִבֵּֽנוּ אַהֲבָתוֹ וְיִרְאָתוֹ וְלַעֲשׂוֹת רְצוֹנוֹ וּלְ֒עָבְ֒דוֹ בְּלֵבָב שָׁלֵם לְמַֽעַן לֺא נִיגַע לָרִיק וְלֺא נֵלֵד לַבֶּהָלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','Blessed is He, our God, Who created us for His glory, and set us apart from those who go astray; and gave us the Torah of truth, and eternal life He implanted within us. May He open our heart to His Torah, and instill in our heart love and awe of Him, to do His will and serve Him with a perfect heart, so that we shall not labor in vain nor bring forth that which causes dismay.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','bah-rookh hoo eh-loh-hey-noo sheh-BE-rah-ah-noo LEEKH-voh-doh ve-heev-dee-lah-noo meen hah-toh-eem ve-nah-tahn lah-noo toh-raht eh-meht ve-khah-yey oh-lahm nah-tah be-toh-kheh-noo hoo yeef-tahkh lee-beh-noo be-toh-rah-toh ve-yah-sehm be-lee-beh-noo ah-hah-vah-toh ve-yeer-ah-toh ve-lah-ah-soht re-tsoh-noh oo-LE-ah-VE-doh be-leh-vahv shah-lehm le-mah-ahn loh nee-gah lah-reek ve-loh neh-lehd lah-beh-hah-lah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','יְהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֺהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ שֶׁנִּשְׁמֹר חֻקֶּֽיךָ בָּעוֹלָם הַזֶּה וְנִזְכֶּה וְנִחְיֶה וְנִרְאֶה וְנִירַשׁ טוֹבָה וּבְ֒רָכָה לִשְׁ֒נֵי יְמוֹת הַמָּשִֽׁיחַ וּלְ֒חַיֵּי הָעוֹלָם הַבָּא: לְמַֽעַן יְזַמֶּרְ֒ךָ כָבוֹד וְלֺא יִדֹּם יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהַי לְעוֹלָם אוֹדֶֽךָּ: בָּרוּךְ הַגֶּֽבֶר אֲשֶׁר יִבְטַח בַּיהוָֹה וְהָיָה יְהֹוָה מִבְטַחוֹ: בִּטְ֒חוּ בַיהוָֹה עֲדֵי עַד כִּי בְּיָהּ יְהֹוָה צוּר עוֹלָמִים: וְיִבְטְחוּ בְךָ יוֹדְ֒עֵי שְׁמֶֽךָ כִּי לֺא עָזַֽבְתָּ דֹרְ֒שֶֽׁיךָ יְהֹוָה: יְהֹוָה חָפֵץ לְמַֽעַן צִדְקוֹ יַגְדִּיל תּוֹרָה וְיַאְדִּיר:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','May it be Your will, Adonoy, our God, and God of our fathers, that we keep Your statutes in this world, and [thus] be privileged to live and behold, and to inherit the goodness and blessing of the Messianic days, and in the life of the World to Come. In order that my soul sing to You and not be stilled; Adonoy, my God, forever will I thank You. Blessed is the man who trusts in Adonoy, so that Adonoy is his security. Trust in Adonoy until the end of days, for in God, Adonoy, is the strength of the worlds. And they will trust in You— those who know your Name, for You have never forsaken those who seek You, Adonoy. Adonoy desired, for the sake of His righteousness, to make the Torah great and to glorify it.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','ye-hee rah-tsohn mee-LE-fah-ney-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo veh-loh-hey ah-voh-tey-noo sheh-neesh-mohr khoo-key-khah bah-oh-lahm hah-zeh ve-neez-keh ve-neekh-yeh ve-neer-eh ve-nee-rahsh toh-vah oo-VE-rah-khah LEESH-ney ye-moht hah-mah-shee-ahkh oo-LE-khah-yey hah-oh-lahm hah-bah: le-mah-ahn ye-zah-MEHR-khah khah-vohd ve-loh yee-dohm ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hahy le-oh-lahm oh-deh-kah: bah-rookh hah-geh-vehr ah-shehr yeev-tahkh bah-ah-doh-NAI ve-hah-yah ah-doh-NAI meev-tah-khoh: BEET-khoo vah-ah-doh-NAI ah-dey ahd kee be-yahh ah-doh-NAI tsoor oh-lah-meem: ve-yeev-te-khoo ve-khah yoh-DE-ey she-meh-khah kee loh ah-zah-ve-tah doh-RE-shey-khah ah-doh-NAI: ah-doh-NAI khah-fehts le-mah-ahn tseed-koh yahg-deel toh-rah ve-yah-deer:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','(יְהֺוָה אֲדוֹנֵֽינוּ, מָה אַדִּיר שִׁמְךָ בְּכָל הָאָֽרֶץ: חִזְ֒קוּ וְיַאֲמֵץ לְבַבְ֒כֶם כָּל הַמְ֒יַחֲלִים לַיהֹוָה:)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','(Adonoy, our Master, how mighty is Your Name over all the earth. Be strong and take courage, all who wait for Adonoy.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','(ah-doh-NAI ah-doh-ney-noo, mah ah-deer sheem-khah be-khohl hah-ah-rehts: KHEEZ-koo ve-yah-ah-mehts le-VAHV-khehm kohl hah-ME-yah-khah-leem lah-ah-doh-NAI)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','כל ימות השנה כשאין מוסף אומר הש"ץ קדיש תתקבל אחר ובא לציון. אבל כשיש מוסף אומר הש"ץ רק חצי קדיש על סדר קדושה ומתפללין מוסף. ובר"ח חולצין התפילין קודם תפלת מוסף.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','On Rosh Chodesh the Chazzan recites the half-Kaddish, the Tefillin are then removed and the congregation says the Musaf Amidah; and on Chol Hamoed the Chazzan recites the half-Kaddish, and the congregation says the Mussaf Amidah. On regular weekdays the Chazzan recites the following Kaddish:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְ֒מָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְ֒קָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming if His Messiah in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:17:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','yeet-gah-dahl ve-yeet-kah-dahsh she-meh rah-bah be-ah-LE-mah dee ve-rah kheer-oo-teh ve-yahm-leekh mahl-khoo-teh ve-yahts-mahkh poo-RE-kah-neh vee-kah-rehv (kehts) me-shee-kheh be-khah-yey-khohn oo-ve-yoh-mey-khohn oo-ve-khah-yey de-khahl beyt yees-rah-ehl, bah-ah-gah-lah oo-veez-mahn kah-reev ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:18:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','ye-heh she-meh rah-bah me-vah-rahkh le-ah-lahm oo-le-ah-LE-mey ah-LE-mah-yah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְ֒עֵֽלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְ֒מָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן,','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','yeet-bah-rahkh ve-yeesh-tah-bahkh ve-yeet-pah-ahr ve-yeet-roh-mahm ve-yeet-nah-seh ve-yeet-hah-dahr ve-yeet-ah-leh ve-yeet-hah-lahl she-meh de-koo-de-shah, be-reekh hoo le-eh-lah (vshyt" oo-LE-eh-lah mee-kahl) meen kohl beer-khah-tah ve-shee-rah-tah, toosh-be-khah-tah ve-neh-kheh-mah-tah, dah-ah-mee-rahn be-ah-LE-mah, ve-eem-roo ah-mehn,','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','תִּתְקַבֵּל צְלוֹתְ֒הוֹן וּבָעוּתְ֒הוֹן דְּכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל קֳדָם אֲבוּהוֹן דִּי בִשְׁ֒מַיָּא וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','May there be acceptance of the prayers and supplications of the entire House of Israel before their Father in heaven. And say, Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:20:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','teet-kah-behl tse-loh-TE-hohn oo-vah-oo-TE-hohn de-khahl beyt yees-rah-ehl koh-dahm ah-voo-hohn dee VEESH-mah-yah ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','May there be abundant peace from heaven and life for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:21:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','ye-heh she-lah-mah rah-bah meen she-mah-yah ve-khah-yeem ah-ley-noo ve-ahl kohl yees-rah-ehl ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','עוֹשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם (בעשי"ת הַשָּׁלוֹם) בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא יַעֲשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם עָלֵינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','He Who makes peace (Ten Days of Penitence: the peace) in His high heavens may He, make peace for us and for all Israel, and say, Amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:22:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','oh-seh shah-lohm (vshyt" hah-shah-lohm) beem-roh-mahv hoo yah-ah-seh shah-lohm ah-ley-noo ve-ahl kohl yees-rah-ehl ve-eem-roo ah-mehn','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','בשני ובחמישי ושאר ימים שמוציאין ספר תורה אומרים יהללו כשמחזירים הס"ת למקומו. ואומר החזן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','On Mondays, Thursdays and other days when the Torah is read, as the Sefer Torah is returned to the Ark the Chazzan takes the Torah and says:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','יְהַלְ֒לוּ אֶת־שֵׁם יְהֹוָה כִּי־נִשְׂגָּב שְׁמוֹ לְבַדּוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','They will praise the Name of Adonoy for His Name alone is exalted.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:24:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','ye-hah-LE-loo eht shehm ah-doh-NAI kee nees-gahv she-moh le-vah-doh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:25:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','קהל:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:25:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','Chazzan and congregation:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:26:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','הוֹדוֹ עַל־אֶֽרֶץ וְשָׁמָֽיִם: וַיָּֽרֶם קֶֽרֶן לְעַמּוֹ תְּהִלָּה לְכָל־חֲסִידָיו לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל עַם קְרֹבוֹ הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:26:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','His majesty is over the earth and the skies. He will raise the might of His people, [which is] praise for all His pious ones, for the children of Israel, the people near to Him. Praise God.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:26:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','hoh-doh ahl eh-rehts ve-shah-mah-yeem: vah-yah-rehm keh-rehn le-ah-moh te-hee-lah le-khohl khah-see-dahv leev-ney yees-rah-ehl ahm ke-roh-voh hah-LE-loo-yahh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:27:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','לְדָוִד מִזְמוֹר לַיהוָֹה הָאָֽרֶץ וּמְ֒לוֹאָהּ תֵּבֵל וְיֽשְׁ֒בֵי בָהּ: כִּי־הוּא עַל־יַמִּים יְסָדָהּ וְעַל־נְהָרוֹת יְכוֹנְ֒נֶֽהָ: מִי־יַעֲלֶה בְהַר־יְהֹוָה וּמִי יָקוּם בִּמְ֒קוֹם קָדְשׁוֹ: נְקִי כַפַּֽיִם וּבַר־לֵבָב אֲשֶׁר לֺא־נָשָׂא לַשָּׁוְא נַפְשִׁי וְלֺא נִשְׁבַּע לְמִרְמָה: יִשָּׂא בְרָכָה מֵאֵת יְהֹוָה וּצְ֒דָקָה מֵאֱלֺהֵי יִשְׁעוֹ: זֶה דּוֹר דּוֹרְ֒שָׁיו מְבַקְ֒שֵׁי פָנֶֽיךָ יַעֲקֹב סֶֽלָה: שְׂאוּ שְׁעָרִים רָאשֵׁיכֶם וְהִנָּשְׂ֒אוּ פִּתְ֒חֵי עוֹלָם וְיָבוֹא מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד: מִי זֶה מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד יְהֹוָה עִזּוּז וְגִבּוֹר יְהֹוָה גִּבּוֹר מִלְחָמָה: שְׂאוּ שְׁעָרִים רָאשֵׁיכֶם וּשְׂ֒אוּ פִּתְ֒חֵי עוֹלָם וְיָבוֹא מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד: מִי הוּא זֶה מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת הוּא מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד סֶֽלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:27:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','A psalm of David: the earth is Adonoy''s and the fullness thereof, the inhabited world and those who dwell in it. For He founded it upon the seas, and established it upon rivers. Who may ascend the mountain of Adonoy, and who may stand in the place of His holiness? The clean of hands and the pure of heart, who has not borne My soul in vain, and has not sworn deceitfully. He will bear Adonoy''s blessing and righteousness from the God of his deliverance. This is the generation of those who seek Him, and seekers of Your Presence, [God of] Jacob, selah. Lift up your heads, gates, and be uplifted [you] entranceways to eternity, so that the King of Glory may enter. Who is this King of Glory? Adonoy, strong and mighty; Adonoy, the Mighty One in battle. Lift up your heads, gates, and lift, entranceways to eternity, so that the King of Glory may enter. Who is He, this King of Glory? Adonoy of hosts, He is the King of Glory, selah.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:27:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','le-dah-veed meez-mohr lah-ah-doh-NAI hah-ah-rehts oo-ME-loh-ahh teh-vehl ve-YSHE-vey vahh: kee hoo ahl yah-meem ye-sah-dahh ve-ahl ne-hah-roht ye-khoh-NE-neh-hah: mee yah-ah-leh ve-hahr ah-doh-NAI oo-mee yah-koom BEEM-kohm kohd-shoh: ne-kee khah-pah-yeem oo-vahr leh-vahv ah-shehr loh nah-sah lah-shahv nahf-shee ve-loh neesh-bah le-meer-mah: yee-sah ve-rah-khah meh-eht ah-doh-NAI oo-TSE-dah-kah meh-eh-loh-hey yeesh-oh: zeh dohr doh-RE-shahv me-VAHK-shey fah-ney-khah yah-ah-kohv seh-lah: se-oo she-ah-reem rah-shey-khehm ve-hee-nah-SE-oo PEET-khey oh-lahm ve-yah-voh meh-lehkh hah-kah-vohd: mee zeh meh-lehkh hah-kah-vohd ah-doh-NAI ee-zooz ve-gee-bohr ah-doh-NAI gee-bohr meel-khah-mah: se-oo she-ah-reem rah-shey-khehm oo-SE-oo PEET-khey oh-lahm ve-yah-voh meh-lehkh hah-kah-vohd: mee hoo zeh meh-lehkh hah-kah-vohd ah-doh-NAI tse-vah-oht hoo meh-lehkh hah-kah-vohd seh-lah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:28:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','בשעת הכנסת ס"ת להיכל אומרים זה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:28:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','As the Torah is returned to the Ark the following is said:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:29:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','וּבְ֒נֻחֹה יֹאמַר שׁוּבָה יְהֹוָה רִבְ֒בוֹת אַלְ֒פֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל: קוּמָה יְהֹוָה לִמְ֒נוּחָתֶֽךָ אַתָּה וַאֲרוֹן עֻזֶּֽךָ: כֹּהֲנֶֽיךָ יִלְבְּ֒שׁוּ צֶֽדֶק וַחֲסִידֶֽיךָ יְרַנֵּֽנוּ: בַּעֲבוּר דָּוִד עַבְדֶּֽךָ אַל תָּשֵׁב פְּנֵי מְשִׁיחֶֽךָ: כִּי לֶֽקַח טוֹב נָתַֽתִּי לָכֶם תּוֹרָתִי אַל תַּעֲזֹֽבוּ: עֵץ חַיִּים הִיא לַמַּחֲזִיקִים בָּהּ וְתוֹמְ֒כֶֽיהָ מְאֻשָּׁר: דְּרָכֶֽיהָ דַּרְ֒כֵי נֹֽעַם וְכָל נְתִיבוֹתֶֽיהָ שָׁלוֹם: הֲשִׁיבֵֽנוּ יְהֹוָה אֵלֶֽיךָ וְנָשׁוּבָה חַדֵּשׁ יָמֵֽינוּ כְּקֶֽדֶם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:29:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','And when it rested, he would say: Return, Adonoy, to the myriads and thousands of Israel. Arise, Adonoy unto Your resting place, You and the Ark of Your strength. Let Your priests clothe themselves in righteousness, and let Your devoted ones sing in joy. For the sake of David, Your servant, do not reject Your anointed. For I have given you good instruction, do not forsake My Torah. It is a tree of life to those who grasp it, and those who support it are fortunate. Its ways are ways of pleasantness and all its paths are peace. Cause us to return to you, Adonoy, and we shall return; renew our days as of old.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:29:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','oo-VE-noo-khohh yoh-mahr shoo-vah ah-doh-NAI REEV-voht AHL-fey yees-rah-ehl: koo-mah ah-doh-NAI LEEM-noo-khah-teh-khah ah-tah vah-ah-rohn oo-zeh-khah: koh-hah-ney-khah yeel-BE-shoo tseh-dehk vah-khah-see-dey-khah ye-rah-neh-noo: bah-ah-voor dah-veed ahv-deh-khah ahl tah-shehv pe-ney me-shee-kheh-khah: kee leh-kahkh tohv nah-tah-tee lah-khehm toh-rah-tee ahl tah-ah-zoh-voo: ehts khah-yeem hee lah-mah-khah-zee-keem bahh ve-toh-ME-khey-hah me-oo-shahr: de-rah-khey-hah DAHR-khey noh-ahm ve-khohl ne-tee-voh-tey-hah shah-lohm: hah-shee-veh-noo ah-doh-NAI eh-ley-khah ve-nah-shoo-vah khah-dehsh yah-mey-noo ke-keh-dehm:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','נהגו לומר בכל ימי השבוע השיר שהיו הלוים אומרים במקדש. ומקורו במס'' סופרים (מס'' סופרים י"ח, א) לפיכך נהגו העם לומר מזמורים בעונתן. דתנינן תמן (תמיד פ"ז מ"ד) השיר שהיו הלוים אומרים בביהמ"ק וכו''. שכל המזכיר פסוק בעונתו מעלה עליו כאילו בונה מזבח חדש ומקריב עליו קרבן. ע"כ. (עץ יוסף)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','The custom of reciting a different psalm each day of the week originated in the Temple. The Mishnah (Maseches Tamid 7:4) describes the psalms which were chanted by the Levites each day during the service.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','בראשון בשבת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','On Sunday:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','הַיּוֹם יוֹם רִאשׁוֹן בַּשַּׁבָּת שֶׁבּוֹ הָיוּ הַלְ֒וִיִּם אוֹמְ֒רִים בְּבֵית הַמִּקְדָּשׁ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','Today is the first day of the week, on which the Levites used to recite in the Holy Temple:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','hah-yohm yohm ree-shohn bah-shah-baht sheh-boh hah-yoo hah-LE-vee-yeem oh-ME-reem be-veyt hah-meek-dahsh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','לְדָוִד מִזְמוֹר לַיהוָֹה הָאָֽרֶץ וּמְ֒לוֹאָהּ תֵּבֵל וְיֽשְׁ֒בֵי בָהּ: כִּי הוּא עַל יַמִּים יְסָדָהּ וְעַל נְהָרוֹת יְכוֹנְ֒נֶֽהָ: מִי יַעֲלֶה בְהַר יְהֹוָה וּמִי יָקוּם בִּמְ֒קוֹם קָדְשׁוֹ: נְקִי כַפַּֽיִם וּבַר לֵבָב אֲשֶׁר לֺא נָשָׂא לַשָּׁוְא נַפְשִׁי וְלֺא נִשְׁבַּע לְמִרְמָה: יִשָּׂא בְרָכָה מֵאֵת יְהֹוָה וּצְ֒דָקָה מֵאֱלֺהֵי יִשְׁעוֹ: זֶה דּוֹר דּוֹרְ֒שָׁיו מְבַקְ֒שֵׁי פָנֶֽיךָ יַעֲקֹב סֶֽלָה: שְׂאוּ שְׁעָרִים רָאשֵׁיכֶם וְהִנָּשְׂ֒אוּ פִּתְ֒חֵי עוֹלָם וְיָבוֹא מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד: מִי זֶה מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד יְהֹוָה עִזּוּז וְגִבּוֹר יְהֹוָה גִּבּוֹר מִלְחָמָה: שְׂאוּ שְׁעָרִים רָאשֵׁיכֶם וּשְׂ֒אוּ פִּתְ֒חֵי עוֹלָם וְיָבוֹא מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד: מִי הוּא זֶה מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת הוּא מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד סֶֽלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','A psalm of David: the earth is Adonoy''s and the fullness thereof, the inhabited world and those who dwell in it. For He founded it upon the seas, and established it upon rivers. Who may ascend the mountain of Adonoy, and who may stand in the place of His holiness? The clean of hands and the pure of heart, who has not borne My soul in vain, and has not sworn deceitfully. He will bear Adonoy''s blessing and righteousness from the God of his deliverance. This is the generation of those who seek Him, the seekers of Your Presence, [God of] Jacob, Selah. Lift up your heads, gates, and be uplifted [you] entranceways to eternity, so that the King of Glory may enter. Who is this King of Glory? Adonoy, strong and mighty; Adonoy, the Mighty One in battle. Lift up your heads, gates, and lift, entranceways to eternity, so that the King of Glory may enter. Who is He, this King of Glory? Adonoy of hosts, He is the King of Glory, Selah.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','le-dah-veed meez-mohr lah-ah-doh-NAI hah-ah-rehts oo-ME-loh-ahh teh-vehl ve-YSHE-vey vahh: kee hoo ahl yah-meem ye-sah-dahh ve-ahl ne-hah-roht ye-khoh-NE-neh-hah: mee yah-ah-leh ve-hahr ah-doh-NAI oo-mee yah-koom BEEM-kohm kohd-shoh: ne-kee khah-pah-yeem oo-vahr leh-vahv ah-shehr loh nah-sah lah-shahv nahf-shee ve-loh neesh-bah le-meer-mah: yee-sah ve-rah-khah meh-eht ah-doh-NAI oo-TSE-dah-kah meh-eh-loh-hey yeesh-oh: zeh dohr doh-RE-shahv me-VAHK-shey fah-ney-khah yah-ah-kohv seh-lah: se-oo she-ah-reem rah-shey-khehm ve-hee-nah-SE-oo PEET-khey oh-lahm ve-yah-voh meh-lehkh hah-kah-vohd: mee zeh meh-lehkh hah-kah-vohd ah-doh-NAI ee-zooz ve-gee-bohr ah-doh-NAI gee-bohr meel-khah-mah: se-oo she-ah-reem rah-shey-khehm oo-SE-oo PEET-khey oh-lahm ve-yah-voh meh-lehkh hah-kah-vohd: mee hoo zeh meh-lehkh hah-kah-vohd ah-doh-NAI tse-vah-oht hoo meh-lehkh hah-kah-vohd seh-lah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','(הושיענו וכו''. קדיש יתום.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','(Deliver us...; Mourner''s Kaddish.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','בשני בשבת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','On Monday:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','הַיּוֹם יוֹם שֵׁנִי בַּשַּׁבָּת שֶׁבּוֹ הָיוּ הַלְ֒וִיִּם אוֹמְ֒רִים בְּבֵית הַמִּקְדָּשׁ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','Today is the second day of the week, on which the Levites used to recite in the Holy Temple:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','hah-yohm yohm sheh-nee bah-shah-baht sheh-boh hah-yoo hah-LE-vee-yeem oh-ME-reem be-veyt hah-meek-dahsh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','שִׁיר מִזְמוֹר לִבְנֵי קֹֽרַח: גָּדוֹל יְהֹוָה וּמְהֻלָּל מְאֹד בְּעִיר אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ הַר קָדְשׁוֹ: יְפֵה נוֹף מְשׂוֹשׂ כָּל הָאָֽרֶץ הַר צִיּוֹן יַרְכְּתֵי צָפוֹן קִרְיַת מֶֽלֶךְ רָב: אֱלֺהִים בְּאַרְמְנוֹתֶֽיהָ נוֹדַע לְמִשְׂגָּב: כִּי הִנֵּה הַמְּ֒לָכִים נוֹעֲדוּ עָבְ֒רוּ יַחְדָּו: הֵֽמָּה רָאוּ כֵּן תָּמָֽהוּ נִבְהֲלוּ נֶחְפָּֽזוּ: רְעָדָה אֲחָזָֽתַם שָׁם חִיל כַּיּוֹלֵדָה: בְּרֽוּחַ קָדִים תְּשַׁבֵּר אֳנִיּוֹת תַּרְשִׁישׁ: כַּאֲשֶׁר שָׁמַֽעְנוּ כֵּן רָאִֽינוּ בְּעִיר יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת בְּעִיר אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ אֱלֺהִים יְכוֹנְ֒נֶֽהָ עַד עוֹלָם סֶֽלָה: דִּמִּֽינוּ אֱלֺהִים חַסְדֶּֽךָ בְּקֶֽרֶב הֵיכָלֶֽךָ: כְּשִׁמְךָ אֱלֺהִים כֵּן תְּהִלָּתְ֒ךָ עַל קַצְוֵי אֶֽרֶץ צֶֽדֶק מָלְ֒אָה יְמִינֶֽךָ: יִשְׂמַח הַר צִיּוֹן תָּגֵֽלְנָה בְּנוֹת יְהוּדָה לְמַֽעַן מִשְׁפָּטֶֽיךָ: סֹֽבּוּ צִיּוֹן וְהַקִּיפֽוּהָ סִפְ֒רוּ מִגְדָּלֶֽיהָ: שִֽׁיתוּ לִבְּ֒כֶם לְחֵילָה פַּסְּ֒גוּ אַרְמְ֒נוֹתֶֽיהָ לְמַֽעַן תְּסַפְּ֒רוּ לְדוֹר אַחֲרוֹן: כִּי זֶה אֱלֺהִים אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ עוֹלָם וָעֶד הוּא יְנַהֲגֵֽנוּ עַל מוּת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','A song, a psalm by the sons of Korach. Adonoy is great and highly extolled in the city of our God, the mountain of His Sanctuary. Beautiful in its panoramic vista, the joy of all the earth is Mount Zion, on the northern extremities (of Jerusalem); the city of the great King. God, in its palaces, has become known as a Stronghold. For behold, the kings assembled, they passed by together. They saw and were astounded, they panicked and fled in haste. Trembling siezed them there, like the pangs of a woman in labor. With an east wind You smashed the ships of Tarshish. As we heard, so we saw in the city of Adonoy of hosts, in the city of our God; may God establish it for eternity, Selah. We hoped, God, for Your lovingkindness in the midst of Your Sanctuary. As Your Name, God, so is Your praise— to the ends of the earth; Your right hand is full of righteousness. Let Mount Zion rejoice, let the daughters of Judah exult, because of Your judgments. Rally around Zion and encircle her, count her towers. Consider well her ramparts, raise high her citadels, that you may recount it to future generations. That this is God, our God forever and ever, He will lead us like children.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','sheer meez-mohr leev-ney koh-rahkh: gah-dohl ah-doh-NAI oo-me-hoo-lahl me-ohd be-eer eh-loh-hey-noo hahr kohd-shoh: ye-feh nohf me-sohs kohl hah-ah-rehts hahr tsee-yohn yahr-ke-tey tsah-fohn keer-yaht meh-lehkh rahv: eh-loh-heem be-ahr-me-noh-tey-hah noh-dah le-mees-gahv: kee hee-neh hah-ME-lah-kheem noh-ah-doo ah-VE-roo yahkh-dahv: heh-mah rah-oo kehn tah-mah-hoo neev-hah-loo nehkh-pah-zoo: re-ah-dah ah-khah-zah-tahm shahm kheel kah-yoh-leh-dah: be-roo-ahkh kah-deem te-shah-behr oh-nee-yoht tahr-sheesh: kah-ah-shehr shah-mah-e-noo kehn rah-ee-noo be-eer ah-doh-NAI tse-vah-oht be-eer eh-loh-hey-noo eh-loh-heem ye-khoh-NE-neh-hah ahd oh-lahm seh-lah: dee-mee-noo eh-loh-heem khahs-deh-khah be-keh-rehv hey-khah-leh-khah: ke-sheem-khah eh-loh-heem kehn te-hee-lah-TE-khah ahl kahts-vey eh-rehts tseh-dehk mah-LE-ah ye-mee-neh-khah: yees-mahkh hahr tsee-yohn tah-geh-le-nah be-noht ye-hoo-dah le-mah-ahn meesh-pah-tey-khah: soh-boo tsee-yohn ve-hah-kee-foo-hah SEEF-roo meeg-dah-ley-hah: shee-too lee-BE-khehm le-khey-lah pah-SE-goo ahr-ME-noh-tey-hah le-mah-ahn te-sah-PE-roo le-dohr ah-khah-rohn: kee zeh eh-loh-heem eh-loh-hey-noo oh-lahm vah-ehd hoo ye-nah-hah-geh-noo ahl moot:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','(הושיענו וכו''. קדיש יתום.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','(Deliver us...; Mourner''s Kaddish.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','בשלישי בשבת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','On Tuesday:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','הַיּוֹם יוֹם שְׁלִישִׁי בַּשַּׁבָּת שֶׁבּוֹ הָיוּ הַלְ֒וִיִּם אוֹמְ֒רִים בְּבֵית הַמִּקְדָּשׁ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','Today is the third day of the week, on which the Levites used to recite in the Holy Temple:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','hah-yohm yohm she-lee-shee bah-shah-baht sheh-boh hah-yoo hah-LE-vee-yeem oh-ME-reem be-veyt hah-meek-dahsh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','מִזְמוֹר לְאָסָף אֱלֺהִים נִצָּב בַּעֲדַת אֵל בְּקֶֽרֶב אֱלֺהִים יִשְׁפֹּט: עַד מָתַי תִּשְׁפְּטוּ עָֽוֶל וּפְ֒נֵי רְשָׁעִים תִּשְׂ֒אוּ סֶֽלָה: שִׁפְ֒טוּ דָל וְיָתוֹם עָנִי וָרָשׁ הַצְדִּֽיקוּ: פַּלְּ֒טוּ דַל וְאֶבְיוֹן מִיַּד רְשָׁעִים הַצִּֽילוּ: לֺא יָדְ֒עוּ וְלֺא יָבִֽינוּ בַּחֲשֵׁכָה יִתְהַלָּֽכוּ יִמּֽוֹטוּ כָּל מֽוֹסְ֒דֵי אָֽרֶץ: אֲנִי אָמַֽרְתִּי אֱלֺהִים אַתֶּם וּבְ֒נֵי עֶלְיוֹן כֻּלְּ֒כֶם: אָכֵן כְּאָדָם תְּמוּתוּן וּכְ֒אַחַד הַשָּׂרִים תִּפֹּֽלוּ: קוּמָה אֱלֺהִים שָׁפְ֒טָה הָאָרֶץ כִּי אַתָּה תִנְחַל בְּכָל הַגּוֹיִם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','A psalm of Assaf God stands in the congregation of the Almighty, in the midst of the judges He gives judgement. How long will you judge lawlessly and show partiality to the wicked forever? Render justice to the lowly and the orphan, deal righteously with the poor and destitute. Rescue the lowly and the needy, save them from the hand of the wicked. They neither know nor understand, they walk along in darkness, all the foundations of the earth are shaken. I had said "You are godlike beings, all of you, sons of the Most High." Nevertheless, you shall die like men, and fall like one of the princes. Arise, God, judge the earth, for You will inherit all the nations.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','meez-mohr le-ah-sahf eh-loh-heem nee-tsahv bah-ah-daht ehl be-keh-rehv eh-loh-heem yeesh-poht: ahd mah-tahy teesh-pe-too ah-vehl oo-FE-ney re-shah-eem TEES-oo seh-lah: SHEEF-too dahl ve-yah-tohm ah-nee vah-rahsh hahts-dee-koo: pah-LE-too dahl ve-ehv-yohn mee-yahd re-shah-eem hah-tsee-loo: loh yah-DE-oo ve-loh yah-vee-noo bah-khah-sheh-khah yeet-hah-lah-khoo yee-moh-too kohl moh-SE-dey ah-rehts: ah-nee ah-mah-re-tee eh-loh-heem ah-tehm oo-VE-ney ehl-yohn koo-LE-khehm: ah-khehn ke-ah-dahm te-moo-toon oo-KHE-ah-khahd hah-sah-reem tee-poh-loo: koo-mah eh-loh-heem shah-FE-tah hah-ah-rehts kee ah-tah teen-khahl be-khohl hah-goh-yeem:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','(הושיענו וכו''. קדיש יתום.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','(Deliver us...; Mourner''s Kaddish.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','ברביעי בשבת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','On Wednesday:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','הַיּוֹם יוֹם רְבִיעִי בַּשַּׁבָּת שֶׁבּוֹ הָיוּ הַלְ֒וִיִּם אוֹמְ֒רִים בְּבֵית הַמִּקְדָּשׁ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','Today is the fourth day of the week, on which the Levites used to recite in the Holy Temple:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','hah-yohm yohm re-vee-ee bah-shah-baht sheh-boh hah-yoo hah-LE-vee-yeem oh-ME-reem be-veyt hah-meek-dahsh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','אֵל נְקָמוֹת יְהֹוָה אֵל נְקָמוֹת הוֹפִֽיעַ: הִנָּשֵׂא שֹׁפֵט הָאָֽרֶץ הָשֵׁב גְּמוּל עַל גֵּאִים: עַד מָתַי רְשָׁעִים יְהֹוָה עַד מָתַי רְשָׁעִים יַעֲלֺֽזוּ: יַבִּֽיעוּ יְדַבְּ֒רוּ עָתָק יִתְאַמְּ֒רוּ כָּל פֹּֽעֲלֵי אָֽוֶן: עַמְּ֒ךָ יְהֹוָה יְדַכְּ֒אוּ וְנַחֲלָתְ֒ךָ יְעַנּוּ: אַלְמָנָה וְגֵר יַהֲרֹֽגוּ וִיתוֹמִים יְרַצֵּֽחוּ: וַיֹּאמְ֒רוּ לֺא יִרְאֶה יָהּ וְלֺא יָבִין אֱלֺהֵי יַעֲקֹב: בִּֽינוּ בֹּעֲרִים בָּעָם וּכְ֒סִילִים מָתַי תַּשְׂכִּֽילוּ: הֲנֹֽטַע אֹֽזֶן הֲלֺא יִשְׁמָע אִם יוֹצֵר עַֽיִן הֲלֺא יַבִּיט: הֲיֹסֵר גּוֹיִם הֲלֺא יוֹכִֽיחַ הַמְ֒לַמֵּד אָדָם דָּֽעַת: יְהֹוָה יֹדֵֽעַ מַחְשְׁ֒בוֹת אָדָם כִּי הֵֽמָּה הָֽבֶל: אַשְׁרֵי הַגֶּֽבֶר אֲשֶׁר תְּיַסְּ֒רֶֽנּוּ יָהּ וּמִתּוֹרָתְ֒ךָ תְלַמְּ֒דֶֽנּוּ: לְהַשְׁקִיט לוֹ מִֽימֵי רָע עַד יִכָּרֶה לָרָשָׁע שָֽׁחַת: כִּי לֺא יִטּשׁ יְהֹוָה עַמּוֹ וְנַחֲלָתוֹ לֺא יַעֲזֹב: כִּי עַד צֶֽדֶק יָשׁוּב מִשְׁפָּט וְאַחֲרָיו כָּל יִשְׁ֒רֵי לֵב: מִי יָקוּם לִי עִם מְרֵעִים מִי יִתְיַצֵּב לִי עִם פֹּֽעֲלֵי אָֽוֶן: לוּלֵי יְהֹוָה עֶזְרָֽתָה לִּי כִּמְ֒עַט שָׁכְ֒נָה דוּמָה נַפְשִׁי: אִם אָמַֽרְתִּי מָֽטָה רַגְלִי חַסְדְּ֒ךָ יְהֹוָה יִסְעָדֵֽנִי: בְּרֹב שַׂרְעַפַּי בְּקִרְבִּי תַּנְחוּמֶֽיךָ יְשַׁעַשְׁ֒עוּ נַפְשִׁי: הַיְ֒חָבְרְךָ כִּסֵּא הַוָּוֹת יֹצֵר עָמָל עֲלֵי חֹק: יָגֽוֹדּוּ עַל נֶֽפֶשׁ צַדִּיק וְדָם נָקִי יַרְשִֽׁיעוּ: וַיְ֒הִי יְהֹוָה לִי לְמִשְׂגָּב וֵאלֺהַי לְצוּר מַחְסִי: וַיָּֽשֶׁב עֲלֵיהֶם אֶת אוֹנָם וּבְ֒רָעָתָם יַצְמִיתֵם יַצְמִיתֵם יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ: לְכוּ נְרַנְּ֒נָה לַיהוָֹה נָרִֽיעָה לְצוּר יִשְׁעֵֽנוּ: נְקַדְּ֒מָה פָנָיו בְּתוֹדָה בִּזְמִרוֹת נָרִֽיעַ לוֹ: כִּי אֵל גָּדוֹל יְהֹוָה וּמֶֽלֶךְ גָּדוֹל עַל כָּל אֱלֺהִים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','Almighty of vengeance, Adonoy, Almighty of vengeance, reveal Yourself. Arise Judge of the earth, repay the arrogant their just reward. How long shall the wicked— Adonoy— how long shall the wicked exult? They express, they speak with arrogance; all the evildoers are boastful. Adonoy, they crush Your people and Your heritage they oppress. The widow and stranger they kill, and orphans they murder. And they say, "God does not see, the God of Jacob is not concerned." Consider, [you] stupid [ones] among the people,— and you fools when will you become wise? He Who implanted the ear, does He not hear? He Who formed the eye, does He not see? He Who chastises nations, does He not reprove— He that teaches man knowledge? Adonoy knows the thoughts of men, that they are vanity. Fortunate is the man whom You chastise, God, and whom You instruct from Your Torah. To grant him tranquility from days of evil, until the pit is dug for the wicked. for Adonoy will not abandon His people and His inheritance, He will not forsake. For justice shall return unto righteousness, and all the upright in heart will follow it. Who will rise up for me against the wicked, who will stand up for me against the evildoers? Had Adonoy not been my help, in an instant my soul would have dwelt in the silent grave. If [Whenever] I said, my foot has slipped, Your kindliness, Adonoy upheld me. When (worrisome) thoughts multiply within me, Your consolations soothe my soul. Can a tribunal of evil have accord with You— [a tribunal] that makes iniquity into law? They gang up against the life of the righteous, and blood of the innocent they condemn. Adonoy has been my stronghold, my God the Rock of my refuge. He turns their violence against them, and with their own wickedness destroys them; Adonoy, my God, destroys them. Come let us sing to Adonoy; let us shout for joy to the Rock of our Deliverance. Let us greet Him with thanksgiving; with song let us shout for joy to Him. for a great Almighty is Adonoy; a great King over all godlike beings.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','ehl ne-kah-moht ah-doh-NAI ehl ne-kah-moht hoh-fee-ah: hee-nah-seh shoh-feht hah-ah-rehts hah-shehv ge-mool ahl geh-eem: ahd mah-tahy re-shah-eem ah-doh-NAI ahd mah-tahy re-shah-eem yah-ah-loh-zoo: yah-bee-oo ye-dah-BE-roo ah-tahk yeet-ah-ME-roo kohl poh-ah-ley ah-vehn: ah-ME-khah ah-doh-NAI ye-dah-KE-oo ve-nah-khah-lah-TE-khah ye-ah-noo: ahl-mah-nah ve-gehr yah-hah-roh-goo vee-toh-meem ye-rah-tseh-khoo: vah-yoh-ME-roo loh yeer-eh yahh ve-loh yah-veen eh-loh-hey yah-ah-kohv: bee-noo boh-ah-reem bah-ahm oo-KHE-see-leem mah-tahy tahs-kee-loo: hah-noh-tah oh-zehn hah-loh yeesh-mah eem yoh-tsehr ah-yeen hah-loh yah-beet: hah-yoh-sehr goh-yeem hah-loh yoh-khee-ahkh hah-ME-lah-mehd ah-dahm dah-aht: ah-doh-NAI yoh-deh-ah mahkh-SHE-voht ah-dahm kee heh-mah hah-vehl: ahsh-rey hah-geh-vehr ah-shehr te-yah-SE-reh-noo yahh oo-mee-toh-rah-TE-khah te-lah-ME-deh-noo: le-hahsh-keet loh mee-mey rah ahd yee-kah-reh lah-rah-shah shah-khaht: kee loh yeetsh ah-doh-NAI ah-moh ve-nah-khah-lah-toh loh yah-ah-zohv: kee ahd tseh-dehk yah-shoov meesh-paht ve-ah-khah-rahv kohl YEESH-rey lehv: mee yah-koom lee eem me-reh-eem mee yeet-yah-tsehv lee eem poh-ah-ley ah-vehn: loo-ley ah-doh-NAI ehz-rah-tah lee KEEM-aht shah-KHE-nah doo-mah nahf-shee: eem ah-mah-re-tee mah-tah rahg-lee khahs-DE-khah ah-doh-NAI yees-ah-deh-nee: be-rohv sahr-ah-pahy be-keer-bee tahn-khoo-mey-khah ye-shah-AHSH-oo nahf-shee: hah-YE-khah-ve-re-khah kee-seh hah-vah-voht yoh-tsehr ah-mahl ah-ley khohk: yah-goh-doo ahl neh-fehsh tsah-deek ve-dahm nah-kee yahr-shee-oo: vah-YE-hee ah-doh-NAI lee le-mees-gahv veh-loh-hahy le-tsoor mahkh-see: vah-yah-shehv ah-ley-hehm eht oh-nahm oo-VE-rah-ah-tahm yahts-mee-tehm yahts-mee-tehm ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo: le-khoo ne-rah-NE-nah lah-ah-doh-NAI nah-ree-ah le-tsoor yeesh-eh-noo: ne-kah-DE-mah fah-nahv be-toh-dah beez-mee-roht nah-ree-ah loh: kee ehl gah-dohl ah-doh-NAI oo-meh-lehkh gah-dohl ahl kohl eh-loh-heem:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','(הושיענו וכו''. קדיש יתום.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
