('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','הַיּוֹם יוֹם חֲמִישִׁי בַּשַּׁבָּת שֶׁבּוֹ הָיוּ הַלְ֒וִיִּם אוֹמְ֒רִים בְּבֵית הַמִּקְדָּשׁ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','Today is the fifth day of the week, on which the Levites used to recite in the Holy Temple:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:18:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','hah-yohm yohm khah-mee-shee bah-shah-baht sheh-boh hah-yoo hah-LE-vee-yeem oh-ME-reem be-veyt hah-meek-dahsh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','לַמְנַצֵּֽחַ עַל הַגִּתִּית לְאָסָף: הַרְנִֽינוּ לֵאלֺהִים עֻזֵּנוּ הָרִֽיעוּ לֵאלֺהֵי יַעֲקֹב: שְׂאוּ זִמְרָה וּתְ֒נוּ תֹף כִּנּוֹר נָעִים עִם נָֽבֶל: תִּקְ֒עוּ בַחֹֽדֶשׁ שׁוֹפָר בַּכֶּֽסֶה לְיוֹם חַגֵּֽנוּ: כִּי חֹק לְיִשְׂרָאֵל הוּא מִשְׁפָּט לֵאלֺהֵי יַעֲקֹב: עֵדוּת בִּיהוֹסֵף שָׂמוֹ בְּצֵאתוֹ עַל אֶֽרֶץ מִצְרָֽיִם שְׂפַת לֺא יָדַֽעְתִּי אֶשְׁמָע: הֲסִירֽוֹתִי מִסֵּֽבֶל שִׁכְמוֹ כַּפָּיו מִדּוּד תַּעֲבֹֽרְ֒נָה: בַּצָּרָה קָרָֽאתָ וָאֲחַלְּ֒צֶֽךָ אֶעֶנְךָ בְּסֵֽתֶר רַֽעַם אֶבְחָנְ֒ךָ עַל מֵי מְרִיבָה סֶֽלָה: שְׁמַע עַמִּי וְאָעִֽידָה בָּךְ יִשְׂרָאֵל אִם תִּשְׁמַע לִי: לֺא יִהְיֶה בְךָ אֵל זָר וְלֺא תִשְׁתַּחֲוֶה לְאֵל נֵכָר: אָנֹכִי יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֶֽיךָ הַמַּעַלְ֒ךָ מֵאֶֽרֶץ מִצְרָֽיִם הַרְחֶב פִּֽיךָ וַאֲמַלְ֒אֵֽהוּ: וְלֺא שָׁמַע עַמִּי לְקוֹלִי וְיִשְׂרָאֵל לֺא אָֽבָה לִי: וָאֲשַׁלְּ֒חֵֽהוּ בִּשְׁרִירוּת לִבָּם יֵלְ֒כוּ בְּמוֹעֲצוֹתֵיהֶם: לוּ עַמִּי שֹׁמֵֽעַ לִי יִשְׂרָאֵל בִּדְ֒רָכַי יְהַלֵּֽכוּ: כִּמְ֒עַט אוֹיְ֒בֵיהֶם אַכְנִֽיעַ וְעַל צָרֵיהֶם אָשִׁיב יָדִי: מְשַׂנְ֒אֵי יְהֹוָה יְכַחֲשׁוּ לוֹ וִיהִי עִתָּם לְעוֹלָם: וַיַּאֲכִילֵֽהוּ מֵחֵֽלֶב חִטָּה וּמִצּוּר דְּבַשׁ אַשְׂבִּיעֶֽךָּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','To Him Who grants victory— upon the Gittis, a psalm of Assaf: Sing joyously to God, our strength, shout for joy to the God of Jacob. Take up the hymn, sound the drum, the pleasant harp and the lute. Blow the shofar on the Rosh Chodesh, at the appointed time for our festive day. For it is a statute for Israel, a [day of] judgement of the God of Jacob. As a testimony for Yehosef, He ordained it when he went out over the land of Egypt, [where] an unfamiliar language I heard. From the burden, I removed his shoulder, his hands were removed from the cauldron. In distress you called out, and I released you, I answered you [though you called] in secret [I answered you] thunderously; I tested you at the waters of Merivah. Selah. Hear, My people, I will testify about you, Israel, if you would just listen to Me. Let no strange god be within you, nor bow before a foreign god. I am Adonoy, your God, Who brought you up from the land of Egypt, open your mouth wide, and I will fill it. But My people did not heed My voice, and Israel did not want Me. So I sent them to follow their heart''s desires, let them follow their own devices. If only My people would heed Me, if Israel would walk in My ways. I would immediately subdue their enemies, and turn My hand against their tormentors. Those who cause hate of Adonoy deceive [pretend obedience to] Him, but their time (of punishment) will be forever. But He would feed him (Israel) from the cream of the wheat, and from the rock, I would sate you with honey.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','lahm-nah-tseh-ahkh ahl hah-gee-teet le-ah-sahf: hahr-nee-noo leh-loh-heem oo-zeh-noo hah-ree-oo leh-loh-hey yah-ah-kohv: se-oo zeem-rah oo-TE-noo tohf kee-nohr nah-eem eem nah-vehl: TEEK-oo vah-khoh-dehsh shoh-fahr bah-keh-seh le-yohm khah-geh-noo: kee khohk le-yees-rah-ehl hoo meesh-paht leh-loh-hey yah-ah-kohv: eh-doot bee-hoh-sehf sah-moh be-tseh-toh ahl eh-rehts meets-rah-yeem se-faht loh yah-dah-e-tee ehsh-mah: hah-see-roh-tee mee-seh-vehl sheekh-moh kah-pahv mee-dood tah-ah-voh-RE-nah: bah-tsah-rah kah-rah-tah vah-ah-khah-LE-tseh-khah eh-ehn-khah be-seh-tehr rah-ahm ehv-khah-NE-khah ahl mey me-ree-vah seh-lah: she-mah ah-mee ve-ah-ee-dah bahkh yees-rah-ehl eem teesh-mah lee: loh yeeh-yeh ve-khah ehl zahr ve-loh teesh-tah-khah-veh le-ehl neh-khahr: ah-noh-khee ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-khah hah-mah-AHL-khah meh-eh-rehts meets-rah-yeem hahr-khehv pee-khah vah-ah-MAHL-eh-hoo: ve-loh shah-mah ah-mee le-koh-lee ve-yees-rah-ehl loh ah-vah lee: vah-ah-shah-LE-kheh-hoo beesh-ree-root lee-bahm yeh-LE-khoo be-moh-ah-tsoh-tey-hehm: loo ah-mee shoh-meh-ah lee yees-rah-ehl BEED-rah-khahy ye-hah-leh-khoo: KEEM-aht oh-YE-vey-hehm ahkh-nee-ah ve-ahl tsah-rey-hehm ah-sheev yah-dee: me-SAHN-ey ah-doh-NAI ye-khah-khah-shoo loh vee-hee ee-tahm le-oh-lahm: vah-yah-ah-khee-leh-hoo meh-kheh-lehv khee-tah oo-mee-tsoor de-vahsh ahs-bee-eh-kah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','(הושיענו וכו''. קדיש יתום.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','(Deliver us...; Mourner''s Kaddish.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','בשישי בשבת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','On Friday:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','הַיּוֹם יוֹם שִׁשִּׁי בַּשַּׁבָּת שֶׁבּוֹ הָיוּ הַלְ֒וִיִּם אוֹמְ֒רִים בְּבֵית הַמִּקְדָּשׁ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','Today is the sixth day of the week, on which the Levites used to recite in the Holy Temple:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:22:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','hah-yohm yohm shee-shee bah-shah-baht sheh-boh hah-yoo hah-LE-vee-yeem oh-ME-reem be-veyt hah-meek-dahsh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','יְהֹוָה מָלָךְ גֵּאוּת לָבֵשׁ לָבֵשׁ יְהֹוָה עֹז הִתְאַזָּר אַף תִּכּוֹן תֵּבֵל בַּל תִּמּוֹט: נָכוֹן כִּסְאֲךָ מֵאָז מֵעוֹלָם אָֽתָּה: נָשְׂ֒אוּ נְהָרוֹת יְהֹוָה נָשְׂ֒אוּ נְהָרוֹת קוֹלָם יִשְׂ֒אוּ נְהָרוֹת דָּכְיָם: מִקֹּלוֹת מַֽיִם רַבִּים אַדִּירִים מִשְׁבְּ֒רֵי יָם אַדִּיר בַּמָּרוֹם יְהֹוָה: עֵדֹתֶֽיךָ נֶאֶמְ֒נוּ מְאֹד לְבֵיתְ֒ךָ נָאֲוָה קֹֽדֶשׁ יְהֹוָה לְאֹֽרֶךְ יָמִים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','Adonoy has begun His reign, with majesty He has clothed Himself; Adonoy clothed Himself, with strength He has girded Himself; He has firmly established the world, so that it cannot be moved. Your throne stands firm from of old, You are from eternity. The rivers have raised—Adonoy— the rivers have raised their voice, the rivers raise their raging waves. More than the roar of many waters, mightier than the breakers of the sea, mighty on high are You "Adonoy." Your testimonies are extremely faithful; holiness is becoming to Your House, Adonoy,—for the length of days.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:23:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','ah-doh-NAI mah-lahkh geh-oot lah-vehsh lah-vehsh ah-doh-NAI ohz heet-ah-zahr ahf tee-kohn teh-vehl bahl tee-moht: nah-khohn kees-ah-khah meh-ahz meh-oh-lahm ah-tah: nah-SE-oo ne-hah-roht ah-doh-NAI nah-SE-oo ne-hah-roht koh-lahm YEES-oo ne-hah-roht dohkh-yahm: mee-koh-loht mah-yeem rah-beem ah-dee-reem meesh-BE-rey yahm ah-deer bah-mah-rohm ah-doh-NAI: eh-doh-tey-khah neh-EHM-noo me-ohd le-vey-TE-khah nah-ah-vah koh-dehsh ah-doh-NAI le-oh-rehkh yah-meem:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','הוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׁעֵֽנוּ וְקַבְּ֒צֵֽנוּ וְהַצִּילֵֽנוּ מִן־הַגּוֹיִם לְהוֹדוֹת לְשֵׁם קָדְשֶֽׁךָ לְהִשְׁתַּבֵּֽחַ בִּתְהִלָּתֶֽךָ: בָּרוּךְ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל מִן־הָעוֹלָם וְעַד הָעֹלָם וְאָמַר כָל־הָעָם אָמֵן הַלְ֒לוּיָה. בָּרוּךְ יְהֹוָה מִצִּיּוֹן שֹׁכֵן יְרוּשָׁלָֽיִם הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ: בְּרוּךְ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהִים אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל עֹשֵׂה נִפְלָאוֹת לְבַדּוֹ: וּבָרוּךְ שֵׁם כְּבוֹדוֹ לְעוֹלָם וְיִמָּלֵא כְבוֹדוֹ אֶת־כָּל־הָאָרֶץ אָמֵן וְאָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','Deliver us, God of our deliverance; gather us and save us from the nations to give thanks to Your holy Name, to be extolled in Your praise. Blessed is Adonoy, the God of Israel for all eternity, and all the people said: "Amen" Praise God. Blessed is Adonoy from Zion, Who dwells in Jerusalem. Praise God. Blessed is Adonoy, God, God of Israel Who alone performs wonders. And blessed is the Name of His glory forever, and may His glory fill the whole earth. Amen and Amen!','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:24:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','hoh-shee-eh-noo eh-loh-hey yeesh-eh-noo ve-kah-BE-tseh-noo ve-hah-tsee-leh-noo meen hah-goh-yeem le-hoh-doht le-shehm kohd-sheh-khah le-heesh-tah-beh-ahkh beet-hee-lah-teh-khah: bah-rookh ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey yees-rah-ehl meen hah-oh-lahm ve-ahd hah-oh-lahm ve-ah-mahr khohl hah-ahm ah-mehn hah-LE-loo-yah. bah-rookh ah-doh-NAI mee-tsee-yohn shoh-khehn ye-roo-shah-lah-yeem hah-LE-loo-yahh: be-rookh ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-heem eh-loh-hey yees-rah-ehl oh-seh neef-lah-oht le-vah-doh: oo-vah-rookh shehm ke-voh-doh le-oh-lahm ve-yee-mah-leh khe-voh-doh eht kohl hah-ah-rehts ah-mehn ve-ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','he','נוהגין בספרד לומר מזמור ברכי נפשי בראש חדש לפי שיש בו עשה ירח למועדים (טור אורח חיים תכג)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','en','The following psalm (104) is recited in many synagogues on Rosh Chodesh days, following the daily psalm.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','he','בָּרְ֒כִי נַפְשִׁי אֶת־יְהֹוָה יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהַי גָּדַֽלְתָּ מְאֹד, הוֹד וְהָדָר לָבָֽשְׁתָּ: עֹֽטֶה אוֹר כַּשַּׂלְמָה, נוֹטֶה שָׁמַֽיִם כַּיְ֒רִיעָה: הַמְ֒קָרֶה בַמַּֽיִם עֲלִיּוֹתָיו הַשָּׂם־עָבִים רְכוּבוֹ, הַמְ֒הַלֵּךְ עַל־כַּנְ֒פֵי־רֽוּחַ: עֹשֶׂה מַלְאָכָיו רוּחוֹת, מְשָׁרְ֒תָיו אֵשׁ לֺהֵט: יָסַד אֶֽרֶץ עַל־מְכוֹנֶֽיהָ, בַּל־תִּמּוֹט עוֹלָם וָעֶד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','en','My soul, bless Adonoy; Adonoy, my God, You are greatly exalted; with beauty and splendor are You clothed. Enwrapped in light, garment-like, He spreads out the heavens like a curtain. He Who covers His upper chambers with water, He Who makes clouds His chariot, He Who walks upon wings of wind. He Who makes winds His messengers, flaming fires His servants. He Who established the earth upon its foundations, [so] that it shall never be moved.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','transliteration','bah-RE-khee nahf-shee eht ah-doh-NAI ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hahy gah-dah-le-tah me-ohd, hohd ve-hah-dahr lah-vah-she-tah: oh-teh ohr kah-sahl-mah, noh-teh shah-mah-yeem KAHY-ree-ah: hah-ME-kah-reh vah-mah-yeem ah-lee-yoh-tahv hah-sahm ah-veem re-khoo-voh, hah-ME-hah-lehkh ahl KAHN-fey roo-AHKH: oh-seh mahl-ah-khahv roo-khoht, me-shah-RE-tahv ehsh loh-heht: yah-sahd eh-rehts ahl me-khoh-ney-hah, bahl tee-moht oh-lahm vah-ehd:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','he','תְּהוֹם כַּלְּ֒בוּשׁ כִּסִּיתוֹ, עַל־הָרִים יַֽעַמְ֒דוּ מָֽיִם: מִן־גַּעֲרָתְ֒ךָ יְנוּסוּן, מִן־קוֹל רַעַמְ֒ךָ יֵחָפֵזוּן: יַעֲלוּ הָרִים יֵרְ֒דוּ בְקָעוֹת, אֶל־מְקוֹם זֶה יָסַֽדְתָּ לָהֶם: גְּבוּל־שַֽׂמְתָּ בַּל־יַעֲבֹרוּן, בַּל־יְשֻׁבוּן לְכַסּוֹת הָאָֽרֶץ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','en','The deep, He covered as with a garment; the waters remain on mountains. At Your shout they retreated, at Your thunderous voice they hastened away. They go up mountains, down into valleys, to the specific place You founded for them. You set a boundary [which] they may not cross, lest they return to cover the earth.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','transliteration','te-hohm kah-LE-voosh kee-see-toh, ahl hah-reem yah-AHM-doo mah-yeem: meen gah-ah-rah-TE-khah ye-noo-soon, meen kohl rah-AHM-khah yeh-khah-feh-zoon: yah-ah-loo hah-reem yeh-RE-doo ve-kah-oht, ehl me-kohm zeh yah-sah-de-tah lah-hehm: ge-vool sah-me-tah bahl yah-ah-voh-roon, bahl ye-shoo-voon le-khah-soht hah-ah-rehts:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','he','הַמְ֒שַׁלֵּֽחַ מַעְיָנִים בַּנְּ֒חָלִים, בֵּין הָרִים יְהַלֵּכוּן: יַשְׁקוּ כָּל־חַיְ֒תוֹ שָׂדָי, יִשְׁבְּרוּ פְרָאִים צְמָאָם: עֲלֵיהֶם עוֹף־הַשָּׁמַֽיִם יִשְׁכּוֹן, מִבֵּין עֳפָאִים יִתְּ֒נוּ־קוֹל: מַשְׁקֶה הָרִים מֵעֲלִיּוֹתָיו, מִפְּ֒רִי מַעֲשֶֽׂיךָ תִּשְׂבַּע הָאָֽרֶץ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','en','He Who sends springs into streams to flow between the mountains; to water all the beasts of the fields; the wild ones quench their thirst. Over them dwell the birds of the sky, from among the branches, they give voice. [You] Who waters the mountains from His upper chambers, from the fruit of Your works the earth is sated.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','transliteration','hah-ME-shah-leh-ahkh mah-yah-neem bah-NE-khah-leem, beyn hah-reem ye-hah-leh-khoon: yahsh-koo kohl KHAHY-toh sah-dahy, yeesh-be-roo fe-rah-eem tse-mah-ahm: ah-ley-hehm ohf hah-shah-mah-yeem yeesh-kohn, mee-beyn oh-fah-eem yee-TE-noo KOHL: mahsh-keh hah-reem meh-ah-lee-yoh-tahv, mee-PE-ree mah-ah-sey-khah tees-bah hah-ah-rehts:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','he','מַצְמִֽיחַ חָצִיר לַבְּ֒הֵמָה וְעֵֽשֶׂב לַעֲבֹדַת הָאָדָם, לְהוֹצִיא לֶֽחֶם מִן־הָאָֽרֶץ: וְיַֽיִן יְשַׂמַּח לְבַב־אֱנוֹשׁ לְהַצְהִיל פָּנִים מִשָּֽׁמֶן, וְלֶֽחֶם לְבַב־אֱנוֹשׁ יִסְעָד: יִשְׂבְּ֒עוּ עֲצֵי יְהֹוָה אַרְ֒זֵי לְבָנוֹן אֲשֶׁר נָטָע: אֲשֶׁר־שָׁם צִפֳּרִים יְקַנֵּֽנוּ, חֲסִידָה בְּרוֹשִׁים בֵּיתָהּ: הָרִים הַגְּ֒בֹהִים לַיְּ֒עֵלִים, סְלָעִים מַחְסֶה לַשְּׁ֒פַנִּים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','en','[You] Who causes grass to sprout for cattle, and vegetation for the labor of man, to bring forth bread from the earth; wine to cheer the heart of man, to make [his] face shine from oil, and bread to sustain the heart of man. Adonoy''s trees are sated, the cedars of Lebanon that He planted; where birds make their nests, the stork—the firs are her home. The high mountains [are] for the wild goats, the rocks a refuge for the rabbits.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','transliteration','mahts-mee-ahkh khah-tseer lah-BE-heh-mah ve-eh-sehv lah-ah-voh-daht hah-ah-dahm, le-hoh-tsee leh-khehm meen hah-ah-rehts: ve-yah-yeen ye-sah-mahkh le-vahv eh-nohsh le-hahts-heel pah-neem mee-shah-mehn, ve-leh-khehm le-vahv eh-nohsh yees-ahd: yees-BE-oo ah-tsey ah-doh-NAI AHR-zey le-vah-nohn ah-shehr nah-tah: ah-shehr shahm tsee-poh-reem ye-kah-neh-noo, khah-see-dah be-roh-sheem bey-tahh: hah-reem hah-GE-voh-heem lah-YE-eh-leem, se-lah-eem mahkh-seh lah-SHE-fah-neem:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','he','עָשָׂה יָרֵֽחַ לְמוֹעֲדִים שֶֽׁמֶשׁ יָדַע מְבוֹאוֹ: תָּֽשֶׁת חֽשֶׁךְ וִיהִי לָֽיְלָה, בּוֹ־תִרְמֹשׂ כָּל־חַֽיְ֒תוֹ־יָֽעַר: הַכְּ֒פִירִים שֹׁאֲגִים לַטָּֽרֶף, וּלְ֒בַקֵּשׁ מֵאֵל אָכְלָם: תִּזְרַח הַשֶּֽׁמֶשׁ יֵאָסֵפוּן, וְאֶל־מְעוֹנֹתָם יִרְבָּצוּן: יֵצֵא אָדָם לְפָעֳלוֹ, וְלַעֲבֹדָתוֹ עֲדֵי־עָֽרֶב:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','en','He made the moon to fix seasons the sun knows its place to set. You make darkness and night comes, in which move about all the beasts of the forest. —The young lions roar for prey, and seek their food from the Almighty. [When] the sun rises, they gather and come into their dens to lie. Man goes out to his work, to his labor until evening.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','transliteration','ah-sah yah-reh-ahkh le-moh-ah-deem sheh-mehsh yah-dah me-voh-oh: tah-sheht kh-shehkh vee-hee lah-ye-lah, boh teer-mohs kohl khah-YE-toh yah-AHR: hah-KE-fee-reem shoh-ah-geem lah-tah-rehf, oo-LE-vah-kehsh meh-ehl ohkh-lahm: teez-rahkh hah-sheh-mehsh yeh-ah-seh-foon, ve-ehl me-oh-noh-tahm yeer-bah-tsoon: yeh-tseh ah-dahm le-foh-oh-loh, ve-lah-ah-voh-dah-toh ah-dey ah-rehv:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','he','מָה־רַבּוּ מַעֲשֶֽׂיךָ יְהֹוָה כֻּלָּם בְּחָכְמָה עָשִֽׂיתָ, מָלְ֒אָה הָאָֽרֶץ קִנְיָנֶֽךָ: זֶה הַיָּם גָּדוֹל וּרְ֒חַב יָדָֽיִם שָׁם־רֶֽמֶשׂ וְאֵין מִסְפָּר, חַיּוֹת קְטַנּוֹת עִם־גְּדֹלוֹת: שָׁם אֳנִיּוֹת יְהַלֵּכוּן, לִוְיָתָן זֶה יָצַֽרְתָּ לְשַֽׂחֶק־בּוֹ: כֻּלָּם אֵלֶֽיךָ יְשַׂבֵּרוּן, לָתֵת אָכְלָם בְּעִתּוֹ: תִּתֵּן לָהֶם יִלְקֹטוּן, תִּפְתַּח יָדְ֒ךָ יִשְׂבְּעוּן טוֹב: תַּסְתִּיר פָּנֶֽיךָ יִבָּהֵלוּן תֹּסֵף רוּחָם יִגְוָעוּן, וְאֶל־עֲפָרָם יְשׁוּבוּן: תְּשַׁלַּח רוּחֲךָ יִבָּרֵאוּן, וּתְ֒חַדֵּשׁ פְּנֵי אֲדָמָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','en','How many are Your works, Adonoy! You made them all with wisdom; the earth is full of Your possessions! This sea, great and wide— therein are innumerable creeping things, animals small and great. There ships travel; this Leviathan You formed to frolic with. They all look to You expectantly, to provide their food in its time. [When] You give it to them, they gather it in; [when] You open Your hand, they are sated with goodness. Whey You hide Your face, they are panic-stricken; When You gather in their breath, they perish, and to their dust they return. When You send Your spirit, they will be created [anew]; and You will renew the face of the earth.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','transliteration','mah rah-boo mah-ah-sey-khah ah-doh-NAI koo-lahm be-khohkh-mah ah-see-tah, mah-LE-ah hah-ah-rehts keen-yah-neh-khah: zeh hah-yahm gah-dohl oo-RE-khahv yah-dah-yeem shahm reh-mehs ve-eyn mees-pahr, khah-yoht ke-tah-noht eem ge-doh-loht: shahm oh-nee-yoht ye-hah-leh-khoon, leev-yah-tahn zeh yah-tsah-re-tah le-sah-khehk boh: koo-lahm eh-ley-khah ye-sah-beh-roon, lah-teht ohkh-lahm be-ee-toh: tee-tehn lah-hehm yeel-koh-toon, teef-tahkh yah-DE-khah yees-be-oon tohv: tahs-teer pah-ney-khah yee-bah-heh-loon toh-sehf roo-khahm yeeg-vah-oon, ve-ehl ah-fah-rahm ye-shoo-voon: te-shah-lahkh roo-khah-khah yee-bah-reh-oon, oo-TE-khah-dehsh pe-ney ah-dah-mah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','he','יְהִי כְבוֹד יְהֹוָה לְעוֹלָם, יִשְׂמַח יְהֹוָה בְּמַעֲשָׂיו: הַמַּבִּיט לָאָֽרֶץ וַתִּרְעָד, יִגַּע בֶּהָרִים וְיֶעֱשָֽׁנוּ: אָשִֽׁירָה לַּיהוָֹה בְּחַיָּי, אֲזַמְּ֒רָה לֵאלֺהַי בְּעוֹדִי: יֶעֱרַב עָלָיו שִׂיחִי, אָנֹכִי אֶשְׂמַח בַּיהוָֹה: יִתַּֽמּוּ חַטָּאִים מִן־הָאָֽרֶץ וּרְ֒שָׁעִים עוֹד אֵינָם בָּרְ֒כִי נַפְשִׁי אֶת־יְהֹוָה הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','en','The glory of Adonoy will endure forever, Adonoy will rejoice in His works— Who gazes upon the earth and it trembles; Who touches the mountains and they erupt. I will sing to Adonoy with my life; I will offer hymns to my God as long as I am alive. May my words be pleasant to Him; I will rejoice in Adonoy. Sin will be excised from the earth, and the wicked will be no more; My soul bless Adonoy, Praise God.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','transliteration','ye-hee khe-vohd ah-doh-NAI le-oh-lahm, yees-mahkh ah-doh-NAI be-mah-ah-sahv: hah-mah-beet lah-ah-rehts vah-teer-ahd, yee-gah beh-hah-reem ve-yeh-eh-shah-noo: ah-shee-rah lah-ah-doh-NAI be-khah-yahy, ah-zah-ME-rah leh-loh-hahy be-oh-dee: yeh-eh-rahv ah-lahv see-khee, ah-noh-khee ehs-mahkh bah-ah-doh-NAI: yee-tah-moo khah-tah-eem meen hah-ah-rehts oo-RE-shah-eem ohd ey-nahm bah-RE-khee nahf-shee eht ah-doh-NAI hah-LE-loo-yahh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','he','(הושיענו וכו''. קדיש יתום.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','en','(Deliver us...; Mourner''s Kaddish.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','מנהג טוב לומר אחר כל תפלה מזמור לדוד ה׳‬ אורי וישעי. ובפרט מר״ח אלול עד הושענא רבא (מורה באצבע סי'' לז).','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','The following psalm (27) is recited at the conclusion of services, morning and evenings, from the first day of Elul, through Shemini Atzeres. Others say only until Hoasha''na Rabbah. The psalm voices our prayer that God will be our light on Rosh Hashana enabling us to repel the darkness of sin through true repentance, and that He will be our salvation on Yom Kippur, through His compassionate atonement of our sins.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','לְדָוִד יְהֹוָה אוֹרִי וְיִשְׁעִי מִמִּי אִירָא יְהֹוָה מָעוֹז חַיַּי מִמִּי אֶפְחָד: בִּקְ֒רֹב עָלַי מְרֵעִים לֶאֱכֹל אֶת בְּשָׂרִי צָרַי וְאֹיְ֒בַי לִי הֵֽמָּה כָשְׁ֒לוּ וְנָפָֽלוּ: אִם תַּחֲנֶה עָלַי מַחֲנֶה לֺא יִירָא לִבִּי אִם תָּקוּם עָלַי מִלְחָמָה בְּזֹאת אֲנִי בוֹטֵֽחַ: אַחַת שָׁאַֽלְתִּי מֵאֵת יְהֹוָה אוֹתָהּ אֲבַקֵּשׁ שִׁבְתִּי בְּבֵית יְהֹוָה כָּל יְמֵי חַיַּי לַחֲזוֹת בְּנֹֽעַם יְהֹוָה וּלְ֒בַקֵּר בְּהֵיכָלוֹ: כִּי יִצְפְּ֒נֵֽנִי בְּסֻכֹּה בְּיוֹם רָעָה יַסְתִּרֵֽנִי בְּסֵֽתֶר אָהֳלוֹ בְּצוּר יְרוֹמְ֒מֵֽנִי: וְעַתָּה יָרוּם רֹאשִׁי עַל אֹיְ֒בַי סְבִיבוֹתָי וְאֶזְבְּחָה בְאָהֳלוֹ זִבְחֵי תְרוּעָה אָשִֽׁירָה וַאֲזַמְּ֒רָה לַיהוָֹה: שְׁמַע יְהֹוָה קוֹלִי אֶקְרָא וְחָנֵּֽנִי וַעֲנֵֽנִי: לְךָ אָמַר לִבִּי בַּקְּ֒שׁוּ פָנָי אֶת פָּנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֲבַקֵּשׁ: אַל תַּסְתֵּר פָּנֶֽיךָ מִמֶּֽנִּי אַל תַּט בְּאַף עַבְדֶּֽךָ עֶזְרָתִי הָיִֽיתָ אַל תִּטְּ֒שֵֽׁנִי וְאַל תַּעַזְ֒בֵֽנִי אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׁעִי: כִּי אָבִי וְאִמִּי עֲזָבֽוּנִי וַיהוָֹה יַאַסְ֒פֵֽנִי: הוֹרֵֽנִי יְהֹוָה דַּרְכֶּֽךָ וּנְ֒חֵֽנִי בְּאֹֽרַח מִישׁוֹר לְמַֽעַן שׁוֹרְ֒רָי: אַל תִּתְּ֒נֵֽנִי בְּנֶֽפֶשׁ צָרָי כִּי קָֽמוּ בִי עֵֽדֵי שֶֽׁקֶר וִיפֵֽחַ חָמָס: לוּלֵא הֶאֱמַֽנְתִּי לִרְאוֹת בְּטוּב יְהֹוָה בְּאֶֽרֶץ חַיִּים: קַוֵּה אֶל יְהֹוָה חֲזַק וְיַאֲמֵץ לִבֶּךָ וְקַוֵּה אֶל יְהֹוָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','By David: Adonoy is my light and my salvation, whom shall I fear? Adonoy is the strength of my life, of whom shall I be afraid? When evildoers approach me to devour my flesh— my tormentors and my foes they stumble and fall. If an army should encamp against me, my heart would not fear; if war were to rise against me, in this I trust. One thing I request of Adonoy, [only] that shall I seek, that I may dwell in the House of Adonoy all the days of my life, to behold the pleasantness of Adonoy, and to meditate in His Sanctuary. For He will hide me in His Tabernacle on the day of distress, He will conceal me in the shelter of His Tent, upon a rock He will lift me. And now my head is raised high above my enemies around me; and I will offer in His Tent, sacrifices accompanied by trumpets of joy; I will sing and chant to Adonoy. Adonoy, hear my voice when I call; be gracious to me and answer me. Of You, my heart has said, Seek My Presence; Your Presence, Adonoy I will seek. Conceal not Your Presence from me, do not turn away Your servant in anger. You have been my help; neither cast me off nor abandon me, God of my deliverance. When my father and mother abandon me, Adonoy will gather me up. Adonoy, teach me Your way, and lead me in the path of uprightness, because of my watchers. Do not deliver me to the will of my tormentors, for false witnesses have risen against me, who breathe violence. Had I not believed that I would see the goodness of Adonoy in the land of living. Hope to Adonoy, be strong and He will give you courage; and hope to Adonoy.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','transliteration','le-dah-veed ah-doh-NAI oh-ree ve-yeesh-ee mee-mee ee-rah ah-doh-NAI mah-ohz khah-yahy mee-mee ehf-khahd: BEEK-rohv ah-lahy me-reh-eem leh-eh-khohl eht be-sah-ree tsah-rahy ve-oh-YE-vahy lee heh-mah khah-SHE-loo ve-nah-fah-loo: eem tah-khah-neh ah-lahy mah-khah-neh loh yee-rah lee-bee eem tah-koom ah-lahy meel-khah-mah be-zoht ah-nee voh-teh-ahkh: ah-khaht shah-ah-le-tee meh-eht ah-doh-NAI oh-tahh ah-vah-kehsh sheev-tee be-veyt ah-doh-NAI kohl ye-mey khah-yahy lah-khah-zoht be-noh-ahm ah-doh-NAI oo-LE-vah-kehr be-hey-khah-loh: kee yeets-PE-neh-nee be-soo-kohh be-yohm rah-ah yahs-tee-reh-nee be-seh-tehr oh-hoh-loh be-tsoor ye-roh-ME-meh-nee: ve-ah-tah yah-room roh-shee ahl oh-YE-vahy se-vee-voh-tahy ve-ehz-be-khah ve-oh-hoh-loh zeev-khey te-roo-ah ah-shee-rah vah-ah-zah-ME-rah lah-ah-doh-NAI: she-mah ah-doh-NAI koh-lee ehk-rah ve-khah-neh-nee vah-ah-neh-nee: le-khah ah-mahr lee-bee bah-KE-shoo fah-nahy eht pah-ney-khah ah-doh-NAI ah-vah-kehsh: ahl tahs-tehr pah-ney-khah mee-meh-nee ahl taht be-ahf ahv-deh-khah ehz-rah-tee hah-yee-tah ahl tee-TE-sheh-nee ve-ahl tah-AHZ-veh-nee eh-loh-hey yeesh-ee: kee ah-vee ve-ee-mee ah-zah-voo-nee vah-ah-doh-NAI yah-AHS-feh-nee: hoh-reh-nee ah-doh-NAI dahr-keh-khah oo-NE-kheh-nee be-oh-rahkh mee-shohr le-mah-ahn shoh-RE-rahy: ahl tee-TE-neh-nee be-neh-fehsh tsah-rahy kee kah-moo vee eh-dey sheh-kehr vee-feh-ahkh khah-mahs: loo-leh heh-ehmah-ne-tee leer-oht be-toov ah-doh-NAI be-eh-rehts khah-yeem: kah-veh ehl ah-doh-NAI khah-zahk ve-yah-ah-mehts lee-beh-khah ve-kah-veh ehl ah-doh-NAI:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','(קדיש יתום)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','(Mourner''s Kaddish.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','בבית האבל בבוקר אחר שיר של יום ואחר מנחה בימים שיש בהם תחנון אומרים זה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','It is customary to recite this psalm (49) in the house of a mourner during the week of mourning, following the morning and evening services. On weekdays when Tachanun is not said Psalm 16 (page 218) is substituted. This psalm, the final hymn of the psalms set down by the sons of Korach has significance for all mankind. Its message is that man must utilize all his material and physical resources to enhance his spiritual existence so that when his soul survives the body''s brief stay on earth it can ascend to immortality. If man fails to recognize his purpose in life and instead regards the acquisition of material wealth the primary aim of life, he forfeits his hope of immortality, and his existence will not continue beyond the grave.—S.R. Hirsch','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','לַמְנַצֵּֽחַ לִבְנֵי קֹֽרַח מִזְמוֹר: שִׁמְ֒עוּ זֹאת כָּל־הָעַמִּים הַאֲזִֽינוּ כָּל יֽשְׁ֒בֵי חָֽלֶד: גַּם בְּנֵי אָדָם גַּם בְּנֵי אִישׁ יַֽחַד עָשִׁיר וְאֶבְיוֹן: פִּי יְדַבֵּר חָכְמוֹת וְהָגוּת לִבִּי תְבוּנוֹת: אַטֶּה לְמָשָׁל אָזְנִי אֶפְתַּח בְּכִנּוֹר חִידָתִי: לָֽמָּה אִירָא בִּֽימֵי רָע עֲוֹן עֲקֵבַי יְסוּבֵּֽנִי: הַבֹּטְ֒חִים עַל חֵילָם וּבְ֒רֹב עָשְׁרָם יִתְהַלָּֽלוּ: אָח לֺא פָדֹה יִפְדֶּה אִישׁ לֺא יִתֵּן לֵאלֺהִים כָּפְרוֹ: וְיֵקַר פִּדְיוֹן נַפְשָׁם וְחָדַל לְעוֹלָם: וִיחִי עוֹד לָנֶֽצַח לֺא יִרְאֶה הַשָּֽׁחַת: כִּי יִרְאֶה חֲכָמִים יָמֽוּתוּ יַֽחַד כְּסִיל וָבַֽעַר יֹאבֵֽדוּ וְעָזְ֒בוּ לַאֲחֵרִים חֵילָם: קִרְבָּם בָּתֵּֽימוֹ לְעוֹלָם מִשְׁכְּ֒נֹתָם לְדוֹר וָדֹר קָרְ֒אוּ בִשְׁמוֹתָם עֲלֵי אֲדָמוֹת: וְאָדָם בִּיקָר בַּל־יָלִין נִמְשַׁל כַּבְּ֒הֵמוֹת נִדְמוּ: זֶה דַרְכָּם כֶּֽסֶל לָֽמוֹ וְאַחֲרֵיהֶם בְּפִיהֶם יִרְצוּ סֶֽלָה: כַּצֹּאן לִשְׁ֒אוֹל שַׁתּוּ מָֽוֶת יִרְעֵם וַיִּרְדּוּ בָם יְשָׁרִים לַבֹּֽקֶר וְצוּרָם לְבַלּוֹת שְׁאוֹל מִזְּ֒בֻל לוֹ: אַךְ־אֱלֺהִים יִפְדֶּה נַפְשִׁי מִיַּד שְׁאוֹל כִּי יִקָּחֵֽנִי סֶֽלָה: אַל־תִּירָא כִּי־יַעֲשִׁר אִישׁ כִּי־יִרְבֶּה כְּבוֹד בֵּיתוֹ: כִּי לֺא בְמוֹתוֹ יִקַּח הַכֹּל לֺא־יֵרֵד אַחֲרָיו כְּבוֹדוֹ: כִּי־נַפְשׁוֹ בְּחַיָּיו יְבָרֵךְ וְיוֹדֻֽךָ כִּי־תֵיטִיב לָךְ: תָּבוֹא עַד־דּוֹר אֲבוֹתָיו עַד־נֵֽצַח לֺא יִרְאוּ אוֹר: אָדָם בִּיקָר וְלֺא־יָבִין נִמְשַׁל כַּבְּ֒הֵמוֹת נִדְמוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','To Him Who grants victory, a psalm by the sons of Korach. Hear this all peoples, listen all inhabitants of the decaying world! Sons of Adam and sons of men, rich and poor together. My mouth shall speak wisdom, and the meditation of my heart shall be of understanding. I will incline my ear to a parable, I will begin to solve, to the accompaniment of a harp, my riddle. Why should I fear in the days of evil? The iniquity I trod upon surrounds me. Those who trust in their wealth and take pride in their great riches. A man will not redeem his brother neither can he give to God his ransom. The redemption of their soul is too costly and it shall cease to be forever. Shall he then live forever, shall he never see the grave? For he sees that wise men die, the fools and senseless perish equally and leave their wealth to others. Their inner thoughts are that their houses [will last] forever, their homes for generation after generation; (for) they have proclaimed their names throughout the lands. But man does not endure in his splendor, he is likened to the silenced animals. This is their way— their folly remains with them, and [yet] their descendants take pleasure in their speech, Selah. Like sheep—they are destined for the grave; death shall be their shepherd, and the upright shall dominate them at morning, their form will be consumed in the grave; [it will not remain] their dwelling-place. But God will redeem my soul from the [grasp of] the grave, for He will take me [to Himself] Selah. Fear not when a man grows rich, when the glory of his house is increased. For when he dies, he shall carry nothing away, his glory will not descend after him. Because while he lived, he blessed his soul. (saying): they will praise you because you have done well for yourself. He will join the generation of his fathers, they shall not see light, for all eternity. Man with [all] his splendor, [but] without understanding is likened to the silenced animals.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','transliteration','lahm-nah-tseh-ahkh leev-ney koh-rahkh meez-mohr: SHEEM-oo zoht kohl hah-ah-meem hah-ah-zee-noo kohl YSHE-vey khah-lehd: gahm be-ney ah-dahm gahm be-ney eesh yah-khahd ah-sheer ve-ehv-yohn: pee ye-dah-behr khohkh-moht ve-hah-goot lee-bee te-voo-noht: ah-teh le-mah-shahl ohz-nee ehf-tahkh be-khee-nohr khee-dah-tee: lah-mah ee-rah bee-mey rah ah-vohn ah-keh-vahy ye-soo-beh-nee: hah-boh-TE-kheem ahl khey-lahm oo-VE-rohv ohsh-rahm yeet-hah-lah-loo: ahkh loh fah-dohh yeef-deh eesh loh yee-tehn leh-loh-heem kah-fe-roh: ve-yeh-kahr peed-yohn nahf-shahm ve-khah-dahl le-oh-lahm: vee-khee ohd lah-neh-tsahkh loh yeer-eh hah-shah-khaht: kee yeer-eh khah-khah-meem yah-moo-too yah-khahd ke-seel vah-vah-ahr yoh-veh-doo ve-ah-ZE-voo lah-ah-kheh-reem khey-lahm: keer-bahm bah-tey-moh le-oh-lahm meesh-KE-noh-tahm le-dohr vah-dohr kah-RE-oo veesh-moh-tahm ah-ley ah-dah-moht: ve-ah-dahm bee-kahr bahl yah-leen neem-shahl kah-BE-heh-moht need-moo: zeh dahr-kahm keh-sehl lah-moh ve-ah-khah-rey-hehm be-fee-hehm yeer-tsoo seh-lah: kah-tsohn LEESH-ohl shah-too mah-veht yeer-ehm vah-yeer-doo vahm ye-shah-reem lah-boh-kehr ve-tsoo-rahm le-vah-loht she-ohl mee-ZE-vool loh: ahkh eh-loh-heem yeef-deh nahf-shee mee-yahd she-ohl kee yee-kah-kheh-nee seh-lah: ahl tee-rah kee yah-ah-sheer eesh kee yeer-beh ke-vohd bey-toh: kee loh ve-moh-toh yee-kahkh hah-kohl loh yeh-rehd ah-khah-rahv ke-voh-doh: kee nahf-shoh be-khah-yahv ye-vah-rehkh ve-yoh-doo-khah kee tey-teev lahkh: tah-voh ahd dohr ah-voh-tahv ahd neh-tsahkh loh yeer-oo ohr: ah-dahm bee-kahr ve-loh yah-veen neem-shahl kah-BE-heh-moht need-moo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
