('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','ובימים שאין בהם תחנון אומרים זה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','On weekdays when Tachanun is not said, the following is said in the house of a mourner.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','מִכְתָּם לְדָוִד שָׁמְרֵֽנִי אֵל כִּי־חָסִֽיתִי בָךְ: אָמַֽרְתְּ לַיהֺוָה אֲדֹנָי אָֽתָּה טוֹבָתִי בַּל־עָלֶֽיךָ: לִקְדוֹשִׁים אֲשֶׁר־בָּאָֽרֶץ הֵֽמָּה וְאַדִּירֵי כָּל־חֶפְצִי־בָם: יִרְבּוּ עַצְּבוֹתָם אַחֵר מָהָֽרוּ בַּל־אַסִּיךְ נִסְכֵּיהֶם מִדָּם וּבַל־אֶשָּׂא אֶת־שְׁמוֹתָם עַל־שְׂפָתָי: יְהֺוָה מְנָת־חֶלְקִי וְכוֹסִי אַתָּה תּוֹמִיךְ גּוֹרָלִי: חֲבָלִים נָֽפְלוּ־לִי בַּנְּעִמִים אַף־נַחֲלָת שָׁפְרָה עָלָי: אֲבָרֵךְ אֶת־יְהֺוָה אֲשֶׁר יְעָצָֽנִי אַף־לֵילוֹת יִסְּרֽוּנִי כִלְיוֹתָי: שִׁוִּיתִי יְהֺוָה לְנֶגְדִּי תָמִיד כִּי מִימִינִי בַּל־אֶמּוֹט: לָכֵן שָׂמַח לִבִּי וַיָּֽגֶל כְּבוֹדִי אַף־בְּשָׂרִי יִשְׁכֹּן לָבֶֽטַח: כִּי לֹא־תַעֲזֹב נַפְשִׁי לִשְׁאוֹל לֹא־תִתֵּן חֲסִידְךָ לִרְאוֹת שָֽׁחַת: תּוֹדִיעֵֽנִי אֹֽרַח חַיִּים שֽׂבַע שְׂמָחוֹת אֶת־פָּנֶֽיךָ נְעִימוֹת בִּימִינְךָ נֶֽצַח:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','A Michtam of David. Preserve me, Almighty, for I have taken refuge in You. You said to Adonoy, You are my Master, I have no well-being without You. Due to the holy that are in the earth, and the mighty, are all my desires [fulfilled]. Let their sufferings multiply, those who follow another [sovereignty]; I will not pour their libations of blood, nor carry their names upon my lips. Adonoy is the portion of my inheritance and of my cup; You guide my fate. The portions that have fallen to me are in pleasant places; a beautiful inheritance is mine. I will bless Adonoy Who has given me counsel; even for the nights in which my mind admonished me. I have set Adonoy before me always; for surely He is at my right hand, I will not be moved. Therefore my heart rejoiced and my soul exulted; also my flesh will dwell in safety. For You will not abandon my soul to the grave, nor will You allow Your devoted one to see the pit. You will make known to me the path of life; fullness of joy is in Your presence; pleasantness is at Your right hand, evermore.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','transliteration','meekh-tahm le-dah-veed shah-me-reh-nee ehl kee khah-see-tee vahkh: ah-mahrt lah-ah-doh-NAI ah-doh-nahy ah-tah toh-vah-tee bahl ah-ley-khah: leek-doh-sheem ah-shehr bah-ah-rehts heh-mah ve-ah-dee-rey kohl khehf-tsee vahm: yeer-boo ah-tse-voh-tahm ah-khehr mah-hah-roo bahl ah-seekh nees-key-hehm mee-dahm oo-vahl eh-sah eht she-moh-tahm ahl se-fah-tahy: ah-doh-NAI me-naht khehl-kee ve-khoh-see ah-tah toh-meekh goh-rah-lee: khah-vah-leem nah-fe-loo lee bah-ne-ee-meem ahf nah-khah-laht shah-fe-rah ah-lahy: ah-vah-rehkh eht ah-doh-NAI ah-shehr ye-ah-tsah-nee ahf ley-loht yee-se-roo-nee kheel-yoh-tahy: shee-vee-tee ah-doh-NAI le-nehg-dee tah-meed kee mee-mee-nee bahl eh-moht: lah-khehn sah-mahkh lee-bee vah-yah-gehl ke-voh-dee ahf be-sah-ree yeesh-kohn lah-veh-tahkh: kee loh tah-ah-zohv nahf-shee leesh-ohl loh tee-tehn khah-see-de-khah leer-oht shah-khaht: toh-dee-eh-nee oh-rahkh khah-yeem s-vah se-mah-khoht eht pah-ney-khah ne-ee-moht bee-mee-ne-khah neh-tsahkh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','קדיש יתום יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְ֒מָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְ֒קָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','Mourner''s Kaddish Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming if His Messiah in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','transliteration','kdysh ytvm yeet-gah-dahl ve-yeet-kah-dahsh she-meh rah-bah be-ah-LE-mah dee ve-rah kheer-oo-teh ve-yahm-leekh mahl-khoo-teh ve-yahts-mahkh poo-RE-kah-neh vee-kah-rehv (kehts) me-shee-kheh be-khah-yey-khohn oo-ve-yoh-mey-khohn oo-ve-khah-yey de-khahl beyt yees-rah-ehl, bah-ah-gah-lah oo-veez-mahn kah-reev ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','transliteration','ye-heh she-meh rah-bah me-vah-rahkh le-ah-lahm oo-le-ah-LE-mey ah-LE-mah-yah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְ֒עֵֽלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְ֒מָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן,','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','transliteration','yeet-bah-rahkh ve-yeesh-tah-bahkh ve-yeet-pah-ahr ve-yeet-roh-mahm ve-yeet-nah-seh ve-yeet-hah-dahr ve-yeet-ah-leh ve-yeet-hah-lahl she-meh de-koo-de-shah, be-reekh hoo le-eh-lah (vshyt" oo-LE-eh-lah mee-kahl) meen kohl beer-khah-tah ve-shee-rah-tah, toosh-be-khah-tah ve-neh-kheh-mah-tah, dah-ah-mee-rahn be-ah-LE-mah, ve-eem-roo ah-mehn,','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','May there be abundant peace from heaven and life for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','transliteration','ye-heh she-lah-mah rah-bah meen she-mah-yah ve-khah-yeem ah-ley-noo ve-ahl kohl yees-rah-ehl ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','עוֹשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם (בעשי"ת הַשָּׁלוֹם) בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא יַעֲשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם עָלֵינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','He Who makes peace (Ten Days of Penitence: the peace) in His high heavens may He, make peace for us and for all Israel, and say, Amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','transliteration','oh-seh shah-lohm (vshyt" hah-shah-lohm) beem-roh-mahv hoo yah-ah-seh shah-lohm ah-ley-noo ve-ahl kohl yees-rah-ehl ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','קַוֵּה אֶל יְהֹוָה חֲזַק וְיַאֲמֵץ לִבֶּךָ וְקַוֵּה אֶל יְהֹוָה: אֵין קָדוֹשׁ כַּיהֹוָה כִּי אֵין בִּלְתֶּךָ וְאֵין צוּר כֵּאלֹהֵינוּ: כִּי מִי אֱלוֹהַּ מִבַּלְעֲדֵי יְהֹוָה וּמִי צוּר זוּלָתִי אֱלֹהֵינוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','Hope to Adonoy; be strong and He will give you courage and hope to Adonoy. There is none holy like Adonoy for there is none beside You and there is no stronghold like our God. For who is a god other than Adonoy and who is a stronghold beside our God.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','kah-veh ehl ah-doh-NAI khah-zahk ve-yah-ah-mehts lee-beh-khah ve-kah-veh ehl ah-doh-NAI: eyn kah-dohsh kah-ah-doh-NAI kee eyn beel-teh-khah ve-eyn tsoor keh-loh-hey-noo: kee mee eh-loh-ahh mee-bahl-ah-dey ah-doh-NAI oo-mee tsoor zoo-lah-tee eh-loh-hey-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','אֵין כֵּאלֹהֵינוּ. אֵין כַּאדוֹנֵנוּ. אֵין כְּמַלְכֵּנוּ. אֵין כְּמוֹשִׁיעֵנוּ: מִי כֵאלֹהֵינוּ. מִי כַאדוֹנֵנוּ. מִי כְמַלְכֵּנוּ. מִי כְמוֹשִׁיעֵנוּ: נוֹדֶה לֵאלֹהֵינוּ. נוֹדֶה לַאדוֹנֵנוּ. נוֹדֶה לְמַלְכֵּנוּ. נוֹדֶה לְמוֹשִׁיעֵנוּ: בָּרוּךְ אֱלֹהֵינוּ. בָּרוּךְ אֲדוֹנֵנוּ. בָּרוּךְ מַלְכֵּנוּ. בָּרוּךְ מוֹשִׁיעֵנוּ: אַתָּה הוּא אֱלֹהֵינוּ. אַתָּה הוּא אֲדוֹנֵנוּ. אַתָּה הוּא מַלְכֵּנוּ. אַתָּה הוּא מוֹשִׁיעֵנוּ. אַתָּה תוֹשִׁיעֵנוּ. אַתָּה תָקוּם תְּרַחֵם צִיוֹן כִּי עֵת לְחֶנְנָה כִּי בָא מוֹעֵד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','There is none like our God. There is none like our Master. There is none like our King. There is none like our Deliverer. Who is like our God? Who is like our Master? Who is like our King? Who is like our Deliverer? Let us thank our God. Let us thank our Master. Let us thank our King. Let us thank our deliverer. Blessed is our God. Blesed is our Master. Blessed is our King. Blessed is our Deliverer. You are our God. You are our Master. You are our King. You are our Deliverer. You will deliver us You will arise and have mercy on Zion, for it is time to be gracious to her, for the appointed time has come.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','eyn keh-loh-hey-noo. eyn kah-doh-neh-noo. eyn ke-mahl-keh-noo. eyn ke-moh-shee-eh-noo: mee kheh-loh-hey-noo. mee khah-doh-neh-noo. mee khe-mahl-keh-noo. mee khe-moh-shee-eh-noo: noh-deh leh-loh-hey-noo. noh-deh lah-doh-neh-noo. noh-deh le-mahl-keh-noo. noh-deh le-moh-shee-eh-noo: bah-rookh eh-loh-hey-noo. bah-rookh ah-doh-neh-noo. bah-rookh mahl-keh-noo. bah-rookh moh-shee-eh-noo: ah-tah hoo eh-loh-hey-noo. ah-tah hoo ah-doh-neh-noo. ah-tah hoo mahl-keh-noo. ah-tah hoo moh-shee-eh-noo. ah-tah toh-shee-eh-noo. ah-tah tah-koom te-rah-khehm tsee-yohn kee eht le-khehn-nah kee vah moh-ehd:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','פִּטּוּם הַקְּ֒טֺרֶת הַצֳּרִי וְהַצִּפֹּרֶן הַחֶלְ֒בְּנָה וְהַלְּבוֹנָה מִשְׁקַל שִׁבְעִים שִׁבְעִים מָנָה. מוֹר וּקְ֒צִיעָה שִׁבֹּלֶת נֵרְדְּ וְכַרְכֹּם מִשְׁקַל שִׁשָּׁה עָשָׂר שִׁשָּׁה עָשָׂר מָנֶה. הַקּשְׁטְ שְׁנֵים עָשָׂר וְקִלּוּפָה שְׁלֹשָׁה וְקִנָּמוֹן תִּשְׁעָה. בֹּרִית כַּרְשִׁינָה תִּשְׁעָה קַבִּין. יֵין קַפְרִיסִין סְאִין תְּלָתָא וְקַבִּין תְּלָתָא. וְאִם אֵין לוֹ יֵין קַפְרִיסִין מֵבִיא חֲמַר חִוַּרְיָן עַתִּיק. מֶלַח סְדוֹמִית רֹבַע הַקָב. מַעֲלֶה עָשָׁן כָּל שֶׁהוּא. רַבִּי נָתָן הַבַּבְלִי אוֹמֵר אַף כִּפַּת הַיַּרְדֵּן כָּל שֶׁהוּא. וְאִם נָתַן בָּהּ דְּבַשׁ פְּסָלָהּ וְאִם חִסַּר אַחַת מִכָּל סַמָּנֶיהָ חַיָּב מִיתָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','The composition of the incense consisted of balm, onycha, galbanum, and frankincense— by weight, seventy maneh of each; myrrh, cassia, spikenard and saffron by weight— sixteen maneh of each; twelve maneh of costus, three maneh of aromatic bark, and nine maneh of cinnamon. [Also used in compounding the incense were:] Nine kabin of Carshina lye, Cyprus wine [measuring] three s''in and three kabin— if he had no Cyprus wine, he could used strong white wine— a fourth of a kab of Sodom salt, and a minute quantity of maaleh ashan. Rabbi Nosson of Babylonia says, Add a minute quantity of Jordan amber. If one added honey, the incense became unfit; and if one omitted any of its spices he was liable to the death penalty.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','pee-toom hah-KE-toh-reht hah-tsoh-ree ve-hah-tsee-poh-rehn hah-KHEHL-be-nah ve-hah-le-voh-nah meesh-kahl sheev-eem sheev-eem mah-nah. mohr oo-KE-tsee-ah shee-boh-leht nehrd ve-khahr-kohm meesh-kahl shee-shah ah-sahr shee-shah ah-sahr mah-neh. hahksht she-neym ah-sahr ve-kee-loo-fah she-loh-shah ve-kee-nah-mohn teesh-ah. boh-reet kahr-shee-nah teesh-ah kah-been. yeyn kahf-ree-seen se-een te-lah-tah ve-kah-been te-lah-tah. ve-eem eyn loh yeyn kahf-ree-seen meh-vee khah-mahr khee-vahr-yahn ah-teek. meh-lahkh se-doh-meet roh-vah hah-kahv. mah-ah-leh ah-shahn kohl sheh-hoo. rah-bee nah-tahn hah-bahv-lee oh-mehr ahf kee-paht hah-yahr-dehn kohl sheh-hoo. ve-eem nah-tahn bahh de-vahsh pe-sah-lahh ve-eem khee-sahr ah-khaht mee-kohl sah-mah-ney-hah khah-yahv mee-tah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','רַבָּן שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן גַּמְלִיאֵל אוֹמֵר הַצֳּרִי אֵינוֹ אֶלָּא שְׂרָף הַנּוֹטֵף מֵעֲצֵי הַקְּ֒טָף. בֹּרִית כַּרְשִׁינָה לָמָּה הִיא בָאָה כְּדֵי לְיַפּוֹת בָּהּ אֶת הַצִּפֹּרֶן כְּדֵי שֶׁתְּ֒הֵא נָאָה. יֵין קַפְרִיסִין לָמָּה הוּא בָא כְּדֵי לִשְׁרוֹת בּוֹ אֶת הַצִּפֹּרֶן כְּדֵי שֶׁתְּ֒הֵא עַזָּה. וַהֲלֹא מֵי רַגְלַיִם יָפִין לָהּ אֶלָּא שֶׁאֵין מַכְנִיסִין מֵי רַגְלַיִם בַּמִּקְדָּשׁ מִפְּ֒נֵי הַכָּבוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','Rabbi Shimon ben Gamliel says: The balm is nothing but sap which drips from the balsam tree. the lye of Carshina was used for rubbing the onycha in order to refine its appearance. The Cyprus wine was used to soak the onycha to give it a pungent odor. Though the water of Raglayim was well suited for that purpose, they did not bring the water of Raglayim into the Temple because it would be disrespectful.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','rah-bahn sheem-ohn behn gahm-lee-ehl oh-mehr hah-tsoh-ree ey-noh eh-lah se-rahf hah-noh-tehf meh-ah-tsey hah-KE-tahf. boh-reet kahr-shee-nah lah-mah hee vah-ah ke-dey le-yah-poht bahh eht hah-tsee-poh-rehn ke-dey sheh-TE-heh nah-ah. yeyn kahf-ree-seen lah-mah hoo vah ke-dey leesh-roht boh eht hah-tsee-poh-rehn ke-dey sheh-TE-heh ah-zah. vah-hah-loh mey rahg-lah-yeem yah-feen lahh eh-lah sheh-eyn mahkh-nee-seen mey rahg-lah-yeem bah-meek-dahsh mee-PE-ney hah-kah-vohd:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','תַּנְיָא רַבִּי נָתָן אוֹמֵר כְּשֶׁהוּא שׁוֹחֵק אוֹמֵר הָדֵק הֵיטֵב הֵיטֵב הָדֵק מִפְּ֒נֵי שֶׁהַקּוֹל יָפֶה לַבְּ֒שָׂמִים, פִּטְּ֒מָהּ לַחֲצָאִין כְּשֵׁרָה לִשְׁלִישׁ וְלִרְבִֽיעַ לֹא שָׁמַֽעְנוּ: אָמַר רַבִּי יְהוּדָה זֶה הַכְּ֒לָל אִם כְּמִדָּתָהּ כְּשֵׁרָה לַחֲצָאִין וְאִם חִסַּר אַחַת מִכָּל סַמָּנֶֽיהָ חַיָּב מִיתָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','It was taught in a Boraysa: Rabbi Nosson says, While [the Kohein] ground [the incense] he would say, ‘Hodeik heiteiv, heiteiv hodeik,'' because the sound is good for the spices. If half the quantity of incense was prepared it was acceptable, but if only a third or a fourth [of it was prepared] we have not heard [whether it was acceptable."] Rabbi Yehuda said, This is the general rule: If [it was prepared with all its ingredients] in the correct proportion, it is acceptable even if only half was prepared; but if he left out any of its spices, he was liable for the death penalty.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','tahn-yah rah-bee nah-tahn oh-mehr ke-sheh-hoo shoh-khehk oh-mehr hah-dehk hey-tehv hey-tehv hah-dehk mee-PE-ney sheh-hah-kohl yah-feh lah-BE-sah-meem, pee-TE-mahh lah-khah-tsah-een ke-sheh-rah leesh-leesh ve-leer-vee-ah loh shah-mah-e-noo: ah-mahr rah-bee ye-hoo-dah zeh hah-KE-lahl eem ke-mee-dah-tahh ke-sheh-rah lah-khah-tsah-een ve-eem khee-sahr ah-khaht mee-kohl sah-mah-ney-hah khah-yahv mee-tah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','תַּנְיָא בַּר קַפָּרָא אוֹמֵר אַחַת לְשִׁשִּׁים אוֹ לְשִׁבְעִים שָׁנָה הָיְ֒תָה בָאָה שֶׁל שִׁירַֽיִם לַחֲצָאִין: וְעוֹד תָּנֵי בַּר קַפָּרָא אִלּוּ הָיָה נוֹתֵן בָּהּ קוֹרְ֒טוֹב שֶׁל דְּבַשׁ אֵין אָדָם יָכוֹל לַעֲמֹד מִפְּ֒נֵי רֵיחָהּ וְלָֽמָּה אֵין מְעָרְ֒בִין בָּהּ דְּבַשׁ מִפְּ֒נֵי שֶׁהַתּוֹרָה אָמְ֒רָה כִּי כָל־שְׂאֹר וְכָל־דְּבַשׁ לֹא־תַקְטִֽירוּ מִמֶּֽנּוּ אִשֶּׁה לַיהוָֹה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','It was taught in a Boraysa: Bar Kappara says, Once in sixty or seventy years the accumulated surplus was sufficient to provide half [the yearly quantity of incense."] Bar Kappara also taught, If he would have put into it a minute quantity of honey, no one could have withstood [resisted] the scent. Why was no honey mixed with it? Because the Torah says, (Leviticus 2:11) For any leaven or honey, do not burn from them, [as] a fire-offering to Adonoy.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','tahn-yah bahr kah-pah-rah oh-mehr ah-khaht le-shee-sheem oh le-sheev-eem shah-nah hah-YE-tah vah-ah shehl shee-rah-yeem lah-khah-tsah-een: ve-ohd tah-ney bahr kah-pah-rah ee-loo hah-yah noh-tehn bahh koh-RE-tohv shehl de-vahsh eyn ah-dahm yah-khohl lah-ah-mohd mee-PE-ney rey-khahh ve-lah-mah eyn me-ah-RE-veen bahh de-vahsh mee-PE-ney sheh-hah-toh-rah ah-ME-rah kee khohl se-ohr ve-khohl de-vahsh loh tahk-tee-roo mee-meh-noo ee-sheh lah-ah-doh-NAI:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','אומר ג'' פעמים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','Recite each of these verses three times:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת עִמָּֽנוּ מִשְׂגַּב־לָֽנוּ אֱלֹהֵי יַעֲקֹב סֶֽלָה: יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת אַשְׁרֵי אָדָם בֹּטֵֽחַ בָּךְ: יְהֹוָה הוֹשִֽׁיעָה הַמֶּֽלֶךְ יַעֲנֵֽנוּ בְיוֹם־קָרְאֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','Adonoy of Hosts is with us, a stronghold for us is the God of Jacob, Selah! Adonoy of Hosts, fortunate is the man who trusts in You. Adonoy, deliver [us]! The King will answer us on the day we call.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','ah-doh-NAI tse-vah-oht ee-mah-noo mees-gahv lah-noo eh-loh-hey yah-ah-kohv seh-lah: ah-doh-NAI tse-vah-oht ahsh-rey ah-dahm boh-teh-ahkh bahkh: ah-doh-NAI hoh-shee-ah hah-meh-lehkh yah-ah-neh-noo ve-yohm kah-re-eh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','אַתָּה סֵֽתֶר לִי מִצַּר תִּצְּ֒רֵֽנִי רָנֵּי פַלֵּט תְּסוֹבְ֒בֵֽנִי סֶֽלָה: וְעָרְ֒בָה לַיהוָֹה מִנְחַת יְהוּדָה וִירוּשָׁלָֽםִ כִּימֵי עוֹלָם וּכְשָׁנִים קַדְמֹנִיּוֹת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','You are my shelter; from distress You preserve me; with glad song of rescue, You envelop me, Selah! Let Adonoy be pleased with the offerings of Judah and Jerusalem, as in the days of old and in earlier years.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','ah-tah seh-tehr lee mee-tsahr tee-TSE-reh-nee rah-ney fah-leht te-soh-VE-veh-nee seh-lah: ve-ah-RE-vah lah-ah-doh-NAI meen-khaht ye-hoo-dah vee-roo-shah-lah-mee kee-mey oh-lahm oo-khe-shah-neem kahd-moh-nee-yoht:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','תָּנָא דְבֵי אֵלִיָּֽהוּ כָּל הַשּׁוֹנֶה הֲלָכוֹת בְּכָל יוֹם מֻבְטָח לוֹ שֶׁהוּא בֶּן עוֹלָם הַבָּא שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר הֲלִיכוֹת עוֹלָם לוֹ אַל תִּקְרֵי הֲלִיכוֹת אֶלָּא הֲלָכוֹת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','It was taught in the school of Elijah; Whoever studies halachos every day, he is assured of life in the World-to-Come, for it is said, The ways (halichos) of the world are His." Do not read halichos, but halachos:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','tah-nah de-vey eh-lee-yah-hoo kohl hah-shoh-neh hah-lah-khoht be-khohl yohm moov-tahkh loh sheh-hoo behn oh-lahm hah-bah sheh-neh-eh-mahr hah-lee-khoht oh-lahm loh ahl teek-rey hah-lee-khoht eh-lah hah-lah-khoht:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','אָמַר רַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר אָמַר רַבִּי חֲנִינָא. תַּלְמִידֵי חֲכָמִים מַרְבִּים שָׁלוֹם בָּעוֹלָם. שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר וְכָל בָּנַֽיִךְ לִמּוּדֵי יְהֹוָה וְרַב שְׁלוֹם בָּנָֽיךְ: אַל תִּקְרֵי בָּנָֽיךְ אֶלָּא בּוֹנָֽיךְ: שָׁלוֹם רָב לְאֹהֲבֵי תוֹרָתֶֽךָ וְאֵין לָֽמוֹ מִכְשׁוֹל: יְהִי שָׁלוֹם בְּחֵילֵךְ שַׁלְוָה בְּאַרְמְּנוֹתָֽיךְ לְמַֽעַן אַחַי וְרֵעָי אֲדַבְּרָה נָא שָׁלוֹם בָּךְ: לְמַֽעַן בֵּית יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ אֲבַקְ֒שָׁה טוֹב לָךְ: יְהֹוָה עֹז לְעַמּוֹ יִתֵּן יְהֹוָה יְבָרֵךְ אֶת עַמּוֹ בַשָּׁלוֹם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','Rabbi Eliezer said on behalf of Rabbi Chanina: the disciples of the wise increase peace in the world, for it is said: ‘and all your children will be disciples of Adonoy''s [Torah]; and great will be the peace of your children.'' Do not read banayich [your children] but read bonayich [your builders]. Great is the peace of those who love Your Torah, and they will have no stumbling block [misfortune]. Let there be peace within your moats, serenity within your palaces. For the sake of my brethren and companions, I will say: ‘peace be with you.'' For the sake of the House of Adonoy, our God, I will seek [pray for] your good. Adonoy will give strength to His people, Adonoy will bless His people with peace.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','ah-mahr rah-bee ehl-ah-zahr ah-mahr rah-bee khah-nee-nah. tahl-mee-dey khah-khah-meem mahr-beem shah-lohm bah-oh-lahm. sheh-neh-eh-mahr ve-khohl bah-nah-yeekh lee-moo-dey ah-doh-NAI ve-rahv she-lohm bah-nahykh: ahl teek-rey bah-nahykh eh-lah boh-nahykh: shah-lohm rahv le-oh-hah-vey toh-rah-teh-khah ve-eyn lah-moh meekh-shohl: ye-hee shah-lohm be-khey-lehkh shahl-vah be-ahr-me-noh-tahykh le-mah-ahn ah-khahy ve-reh-ahy ah-dah-be-rah nah shah-lohm bahkh: le-mah-ahn beyt ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo ah-VAHK-shah tohv lahkh: ah-doh-NAI ohz le-ah-moh yee-tehn ah-doh-NAI ye-vah-rehkh eht ah-moh vah-shah-lohm:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','קדיש דרבנן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','Mourners say the following Kaddish d''Rabanan','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְ֒מָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְ֒קָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ. בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming of His Mashiach. In your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','yeet-gah-dahl ve-yeet-kah-dahsh she-meh rah-bah be-ah-LE-mah dee ve-rah kheer-oo-teh ve-yahm-leekh mahl-khoo-teh ve-yahts-mahkh poo-RE-kah-neh vee-kah-rehv (kehts) me-shee-kheh. be-khah-yey-khohn oo-ve-yoh-mey-khohn oo-ve-khah-yey de-khahl beyt yees-rah-ehl, bah-ah-gah-lah oo-veez-mahn kah-reev ve-eem-roo ah-mehn','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','ye-heh she-meh rah-bah me-vah-rahkh le-ah-lahm oo-le-ah-LE-mey ah-LE-mah-yah','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְ֒עֵֽלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְ֒מָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','yeet-bah-rahkh ve-yeesh-tah-bahkh ve-yeet-pah-ahr ve-yeet-roh-mahm ve-yeet-nah-seh ve-yeet-hah-dahr ve-yeet-ah-leh ve-yeet-hah-lahl she-meh de-koo-de-shah, be-reekh hoo le-eh-lah (vshyt" oo-LE-eh-lah mee-kahl) meen kohl beer-khah-tah ve-shee-rah-tah, toosh-be-khah-tah ve-neh-kheh-mah-tah, dah-ah-mee-rahn be-ah-LE-mah, ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','עַל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְעַל רַבָּנָן וְעַל תַלְמִידֵיהוֹן וְעַל כָּל תַּלְמִידֵי תַלְמִידֵיהוֹן, וְעַל כָּל מָאן דְּעָסְ֒קִין בְּאוֹרַיְתָא, דִּי בְאַתְרָא הָדֵין וְדִי בְכָל אֲתַר וַאֲתַר, יְהֵא לְהוֹן וּלְכוֹן שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא חִנָּא וְחִסְדָּא וְרַחֲמִין וְחַיִּין אֲרִיכִין וּמְזוֹנָא רְוִיחֵי וּפוּרְקָנָא מִן קֳדָם אֲבוּהוֹן דְבִשְׁמַיָּא וְאַרְעָא וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','Upon Israel, and upon our Sages, and upon their disciples, and upon all the disciples of their disciples, and upon all those who engage in Torah study in this land and in every land. May there be unto them and unto you abundant peace, favor, kindness, compassion, long life, ample sustenance and redemption from their Father Who is in heaven and on earth, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','ahl yees-rah-ehl ve-ahl rah-bah-nahn ve-ahl tahl-mee-dey-hohn ve-ahl kohl tahl-mee-dey tahl-mee-dey-hohn, ve-ahl kohl mahn de-ah-SE-keen be-oh-rahy-tah, dee ve-aht-rah hah-deyn ve-dee ve-khahl ah-tahr vah-ah-tahr, ye-heh le-hohn oo-le-khohn she-lah-mah rah-bah khee-nah ve-khees-dah ve-rah-khah-meen ve-khah-yeen ah-ree-kheen oo-me-zoh-nah re-vee-khey oo-foo-re-kah-nah meen koh-dahm ah-voo-hohn de-veesh-mah-yah ve-ahr-ah ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים טוֹבִים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','May there be abundant peace from heaven and a good life for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:16:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','ye-heh she-lah-mah rah-bah meen she-mah-yah ve-khah-yeem toh-veem ah-ley-noo ve-ahl kohl yees-rah-ehl ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','עוֹשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם (בעשי"ת הַשָּׁלוֹם) בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא בְּרַחֲמָיו יַעֲשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','He Who makes peace (Ten Days of Penitence: the peace) in His high heavens may He, in His mercy, make peace for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:17:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','oh-seh shah-lohm (vshyt" hah-shah-lohm) beem-roh-mahv hoo be-rah-khah-mahv yah-ah-seh shah-lohm ah-ley-noo ve-ahl kohl yees-rah-ehl ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','he','אחר כל התפלות אומר עלינו לשבח. בפרק ר׳ אליעזר אומר שבח גדול יש בעלינו לשבח על כן צריך לאומרו מעומד ותמצא עלינו עולה בגימטריא ומעומד. ושמעתי שיהושע תקנו בשעה שכבש יריחו וחתם בו שם קטנותו למפרע. (כל בו)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','en','Kol Bo writes that Joshua authored this prayer when he captured Jericho. Taken from the Musaf service of Rosh Hashana, it serves as the closing prayer of all the daily services. As ruled by Tur (Orach Chaim 133), it is said while standing.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','he','עָלֵֽינוּ לְשַׁבֵּֽחַ לַאֲדוֹן הַכֹּל לָתֵת גְּדֻלָּה לְיוֹצֵר בְּרֵאשִׁית שֶׁלֺּא עָשָֽׂנוּ כְּגוֹיֵי הָאֲרָצוֹת וְלֺא שָׂמָֽנוּ כְּמִשְׁפְּחוֹת הָאֲדָמָה שֶׁלֺּא שָׂם חֶלְקֵֽנוּ כָּהֶם וְגוֹרָלֵֽנוּ כְּכָל הֲמוֹנָם: שֶׁהֵם מִשְׁתַּחֲוִים לָהֶֽבֶל וָרִיק וּמִתְפַּלְּ֒לִים אֶל אֵל לֹא יוֹשִֽׁיעַ, וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ כּוֹרְ֒עִים וּמִשְׁתַּחֲוִים וּמוֹדִים לִפְנֵי מֶֽלֶךְ מַלְ֒כֵי הַמְּ֒לָכִים הַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא, שֶׁהוּא נוֹטֶה שָׁמַֽיִם וְיוֹסֵד אָֽרֶץ, וּמוֹשַׁב יְקָרוֹ בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם מִמַּֽעַל, וּשְׁ֒כִינַת עֻזּוֹ בְּגָבְ֒הֵי מְרוֹמִים, הוּא אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ אֵין עוֹד, אֱמֶת מַלְכֵּֽנוּ אֶֽפֶס זוּלָתוֹ כַּכָּתוּב בְּתוֹרָתוֹ וְיָדַעְתָּ הַיּוֹם וַהֲשֵׁבֹתָ אֶל לְבָבֶֽךָ כִּי יְהֹוָה הוּא הָאֱלֺהִים בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם מִמַּֽעַל וְעַל הָאָֽרֶץ מִתָּֽחַת אֵין עוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','en','It is our obligation to praise the Master of all, to ascribe greatness to the Creator of the [world in the] beginning: that He has not made us like the nations of the lands, and has not positioned us like the families of the earth; that He has not assigned our portion like theirs, nor our lot like that of all their multitudes. For they prostrate themselves to vanity and nothingness, and pray to a god that cannot deliver. But we bow, prostrate ourselves, and offer thanks before the Supreme King of Kings, the Holy One blessed is He, Who spreads the heavens, and establishes the earth, and the seat of His glory is in heaven above, and the abode of His invincible might is in the loftiest heights. He is our God, there is nothing else. Our King is true, all else is insignificant, as it is written in His Torah: And You shall know this day and take into Your heart that Adonoy is God in the heavens above and upon the earth below; there is nothing else.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','transliteration','ah-ley-noo le-shah-beh-ahkh lah-ah-dohn hah-kohl lah-teht ge-doo-lah le-yoh-tsehr be-reh-sheet sheh-loh ah-sah-noo ke-goh-yey hah-ah-rah-tsoht ve-loh sah-mah-noo ke-meesh-pe-khoht hah-ah-dah-mah sheh-loh sahm khehl-keh-noo kah-hehm ve-goh-rah-leh-noo ke-khahl hah-moh-nahm: sheh-hehm meesh-tah-khah-veem lah-heh-vehl vah-reek oo-meet-pah-LE-leem ehl ehl loh yoh-shee-ah, vah-ahnah-khe-noo koh-RE-eem oo-meesh-tah-khah-veem oo-moh-deem leef-ney meh-lehkh MAHL-khey hah-ME-lah-kheem hah-kah-dohsh bah-rookh hoo, sheh-hoo noh-teh shah-mah-yeem ve-yoh-sehd ah-rehts, oo-moh-shahv ye-kah-roh bah-shah-mah-yeem mee-mah-ahl, oo-SHE-khee-naht oo-zoh be-GOHV-hey me-roh-meem, hoo eh-loh-hey-noo eyn ohd, eh-meht mahl-keh-noo eh-fehs zoo-lah-toh kah-kah-toov be-toh-rah-toh ve-yah-dah-tah hah-yohm vah-hah-sheh-voh-tah ehl le-vah-veh-khah kee ah-doh-NAI hoo hah-eh-loh-heem bah-shah-mah-yeem mee-mah-ahl ve-ahl hah-ah-rehts mee-tah-khaht eyn ohd:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','he','(וְ)עַל כֵּן נְקַוֶּה לְךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ לִרְאוֹת מְהֵרָה בְּתִפְאֶֽרֶת עֻזֶּֽךָ לְהַעֲבִיר גִּלּוּלִים מִן הָאָֽרֶץ וְהָאֱלִילִים כָּרוֹת יִכָּרֵתוּן לְתַקֵּן עוֹלָם בְּמַלְכוּת שַׁדַּי וְכָל בְּנֵי בָשָׂר יִקְרְאוּ בִשְׁ֒מֶֽךָ, לְהַפְנוֹת אֵלֶֽיךָ כָּל רִשְׁ֒עֵי אָֽרֶץ, יַכִּֽירוּ וְיֵדְ֒עוּ כָּל יוֹשְׁ֒בֵי תֵבֵל כִּי לְךָ תִכְרַע כָּל בֶּֽרֶךְ תִּשָּׁבַע כָּל לָשׁוֹן: לְפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ יִכְרְעוּ וְיִפֹּֽלוּ, וְלִכְ֒בוֹד שִׁמְךָ יְקָר יִתֵּֽנוּ, וִיקַבְּ֒לוּ כֻלָּם אֶת עֹל מַלְכוּתֶֽךָ, וְתִמְלֺךְ עֲלֵיהֶם מְהֵרָה לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד, כִּי הַמַּלְ֒כוּת שֶׁלְּ֒ךָ הִיא וּלְ֒עֽוֹלְ֒מֵי עַד תִּמְלוֹךְ בְּכָבוֹד, כַּכָּתוּב בְּתוֹרָתֶֽךָ יְהֹוָה יִמְלֺךְ לְעֹלָם וָעֶד: וְנֶאֱמַר וְהָיָה יְהֹוָה לְמֶֽלֶךְ עַל כָּל הָאָֽרֶץ בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא יִהְיֶה יְהֹוָה אֶחָד וּשְׁמוֹ אֶחָד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','en','We therefore put our hope in You, Adonoy our God, to soon behold the glory of Your might in banishing idolatry from the earth, and the false gods will be utterly exterminated to perfect the world as the kingdom of Shadai. And all mankind will invoke Your Name, to turn back to You, all the wicked of the earth. They will realize and know, all the inhabitants of the world, that to You, every knee must bend, every tongue must swear [allegiance to You]. Before You, Adonoy, our God, they will bow and prostrate themselves, and to the glory of Your Name give honor. And they will all accept [upon themselves] the yoke of Your kingdom, and You will reign over them, soon, forever and ever. For the kingdom is Yours, and to all eternity You will reign in glory, as it is written in Your Torah: Adonoy will reign forever and ever. And it is said: And Adonoy will be King over the whole earth; on that day Adonoy will be One and His Name One.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','transliteration','(ve-ahl) kehn ne-kah-veh le-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo leer-oht me-heh-rah be-teef-eh-reht oo-zeh-khah le-hah-ah-veer gee-loo-leem meen hah-ah-rehts ve-hah-eh-lee-leem kah-roht yee-kah-reh-toon le-tah-kehn oh-lahm be-mahl-khoot shah-dahy ve-khohl be-ney vah-sahr yeek-re-oo VEESH-meh-khah, le-hahf-noht eh-ley-khah kohl REESH-ey ah-rehts, yah-kee-roo ve-yeh-DE-oo kohl yoh-SHE-vey teh-vehl kee le-khah teekh-rah kohl beh-rehkh tee-shah-vah kohl lah-shohn: le-fah-ney-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo yeekh-re-oo ve-yee-poh-loo, ve-LEEKH-vohd sheem-khah ye-kahr yee-teh-noo, vee-kah-BE-loo khoo-lahm eht ohl mahl-khoo-teh-khah, ve-teem-lohkh ah-ley-hehm me-heh-rah le-oh-lahm vah-ehd, kee hah-MAHL-khoot sheh-LE-khah hee oo-LE-oh-LE-mey ahd teem-lohkh be-khah-vohd, kah-kah-toov be-toh-rah-teh-khah ah-doh-NAI yeem-lohkh le-oh-lahm vah-ehd: ve-neh-eh-mahr ve-hah-yah ah-doh-NAI le-meh-lehkh ahl kohl hah-ah-rehts bah-yohm hah-hoo yeeh-yeh ah-doh-NAI eh-khahd oo-she-moh eh-khahd:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','he','אַל תִּירָא מִפַּחַד פִּתאֹם וּמִשֹׁאַת רְשָׁעִים כִּי תָבֹא עֻֽצוּ עֵצָה וְתֻפָר דַּבְּ֒רוּ דָבָר וְלֹא יָקוּם כִּי עִמָּנוּ אֵל: וְעַד זִקְנָה אֲנִי הוּא וְעַד שֵׂיבָה אֲנִי אֶסְבֹּל: אֲנִי עָשִֽׂיתִי וַאֲנִי אֶשָׂא וַאֲנִי אֶסְבֹּל וַאֲמַלֵּט:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','en','Do not fear sudden terror nor the destruction of the wicked when it comes take counsel together but it will be foiled speak the word and it will not stand for God is with us. To Your old age I am [with You], to Your older years I will sustain You, I have made You, and I will carry You, I will sustain You and save You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','transliteration','ahl tee-rah mee-pah-khahd pee-t-ohm oo-mee-shoh-aht re-shah-eem kee tah-voh oo-tsoo eh-tsah ve-too-fahr dah-BE-roo dah-vahr ve-loh yah-koom kee ee-mah-noo ehl: ve-ahd zeek-nah ah-nee hoo ve-ahd sey-vah ah-nee ehs-bohl: ah-nee ah-see-tee vah-ah-nee eh-sah vah-ah-nee ehs-bohl vah-ah-mah-leht:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','he','כתב הלבוש בסי קל"ג אחר עלינו אומרים קדיש יתום. ואפילו אין יתום של תוך י"ב חודש בבית הכנסת יאמר אותו אחר מי שאין לו אב ואם. והטעם שהרי לעולם צריכין לומר קדיש אחר שאמרו פסוקים. ובעלינו יש גם כן פסוקים וצריכים קדיש אחריו. אלא שנהגו בקדיש זה להניחו ליתום שמת אביו ואמו תוך שנה זו. מפני שיש יתומים קטנים או אפילו גדולים שאינם יכולין להיות שלוחי ציבור ולומר קדיש וברכו אחר אביו ואמו. וכבר ידענו ממעשה דרבי עקיבא [במס'' כלה רבתי פ"ב] תועלת הגדולה שיש למתים כשיש להם בן האומר קדיש וברכו ויותר בתוך שנה ראשונה. לכך תקנו והניחו קדיש זה. שאין צריך שום דבר יותר ליתומים הן קטנים הן גדולים. ומפני שתקנוהו ליתומים אין נוהגין לאמרו כלל מי שיש לו אב או אם שמא אביו או אמו יקפידו בכך משום אל יפתח אדם פיו לשטן ויאמר אתה מקוה למיתתנו. לפיכך אם אין אביו או אמו מקפידין בכך יכול לאומרו אפילו מי שיש לו אב ואם. ע"כ.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','en','Although the Kaddish contains no reference to the dead, it has been recited by mourners for many centuries. The tradition of the mourner''s Kaddish began with the following incident: Once, while walking, Rabbi Akiva met a man who had died some time before and was suffering the torments of Purgatory. He pleaded with Rabbi Akiva to go to his home town and teach his son to recite the Kaddish and Borechu, for this would save him from the terrible punishments. Rabbi Akiva and his Court then instituted the practice of mourners reciting the Kaddish, for until then it had been limited to the Chazzan''s reciting it only after the services or after a sermon (See Tana D''vei Eliyahu Zuta, 17: Zohar Parshas Noach).','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְ֒מָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְ֒קָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming if His Messiah in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','transliteration','yeet-gah-dahl ve-yeet-kah-dahsh she-meh rah-bah be-ah-LE-mah dee ve-rah kheer-oo-teh ve-yahm-leekh mahl-khoo-teh ve-yahts-mahkh poo-RE-kah-neh vee-kah-rehv (kehts) me-shee-kheh be-khah-yey-khohn oo-ve-yoh-mey-khohn oo-ve-khah-yey de-khahl beyt yees-rah-ehl, bah-ah-gah-lah oo-veez-mahn kah-reev ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','transliteration','ye-heh she-meh rah-bah me-vah-rahkh le-ah-lahm oo-le-ah-LE-mey ah-LE-mah-yah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְ֒עֵֽלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְ֒מָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן, יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein. May there be abundant peace from heaven and life for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','transliteration','yeet-bah-rahkh ve-yeesh-tah-bahkh ve-yeet-pah-ahr ve-yeet-roh-mahm ve-yeet-nah-seh ve-yeet-hah-dahr ve-yeet-ah-leh ve-yeet-hah-lahl she-meh de-koo-de-shah, be-reekh hoo le-eh-lah (vshyt" oo-LE-eh-lah mee-kahl) meen kohl beer-khah-tah ve-shee-rah-tah, toosh-be-khah-tah ve-neh-kheh-mah-tah, dah-ah-mee-rahn be-ah-LE-mah, ve-eem-roo ah-mehn, ye-heh she-lah-mah rah-bah meen she-mah-yah ve-khah-yeem ah-ley-noo ve-ahl kohl yees-rah-ehl ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','he','עוֹשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם (בעשי"ת הַשָּׁלוֹם) בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא יַעֲשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם עָלֵינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','en','He Who makes peace (Ten Days of Penitence: the peace) in His high heavens may He, make peace for us and for all Israel, and say, Amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','transliteration','oh-seh shah-lohm (vshyt" hah-shah-lohm) beem-roh-mahv hoo yah-ah-seh shah-lohm ah-ley-noo ve-ahl kohl yees-rah-ehl ve-eem-roo ah-mehn','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god','he','וְעַתָּה֙ יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל מָ֚ה יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ שֹׁאֵ֖ל מֵעִמָּ֑ךְ כִּ֣י אִם־לְ֠יִרְאָה אֶת־יְהוָ֨ה אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ לָלֶ֤כֶת בְּכָל־דְּרָכָיו֙ וּלְאַהֲבָ֣ה אֹת֔וֹ וְלַֽעֲבֹד֙ אֶת־יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ בְּכָל־לְבָבְךָ֖ וּבְכָל־נַפְשֶֽׁךָ׃ לִשְׁמֹ֞ר אֶת־מִצְוֺ֤ת יְהוָה֙ וְאֶת־חֻקֹּתָ֔יו אֲשֶׁ֛ר אָנֹכִ֥י מְצַוְּךָ֖ הַיּ֑וֹם לְט֖וֹב לָֽךְ׃ הֵ֚ן לַיהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם וּשְׁמֵ֣י הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם הָאָ֖רֶץ וְכָל־אֲשֶׁר־בָּֽהּ׃ רַ֧ק בַּאֲבֹתֶ֛יךָ חָשַׁ֥ק יְהוָ֖ה לְאַהֲבָ֣ה אוֹתָ֑ם וַיִּבְחַ֞ר בְּזַרְעָ֣ם אַחֲרֵיהֶ֗ם בָּכֶ֛ם מִכָּל־הָעַמִּ֖ים כַּיּ֥וֹם הַזֶּה׃ וּמַלְתֶּ֕ם אֵ֖ת עָרְלַ֣ת לְבַבְכֶ֑ם וְעָ֨רְפְּכֶ֔ם לֹ֥א תַקְשׁ֖וּ עֽוֹד׃ כִּ֚י יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם ה֚וּא אֱלֹהֵ֣י הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים וַאֲדֹנֵ֖י הָאֲדֹנִ֑ים הָאֵ֨ל הַגָּדֹ֤ל הַגִּבֹּר֙ וְהַנּוֹרָ֔א אֲשֶׁר֙ לֹא־יִשָּׂ֣א פָנִ֔ים וְלֹ֥א יִקַּ֖ח שֹֽׁחַד׃ עֹשֶׂ֛ה מִשְׁפַּ֥ט יָת֖וֹם וְאַלְמָנָ֑ה וְאֹהֵ֣ב גֵּ֔ר לָ֥תֶת ל֖וֹ לֶ֥חֶם וְשִׂמְלָֽה׃ וַאֲהַבְתֶּ֖ם אֶת־הַגֵּ֑ר כִּֽי־גֵרִ֥ים הֱיִיתֶ֖ם בְּאֶ֥רֶץ מִצְרָֽיִם׃ אֶת־יְהוָ֧ה אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ תִּירָ֖א אֹת֣וֹ תַעֲבֹ֑ד וּב֣וֹ תִדְבָּ֔ק וּבִשְׁמ֖וֹ תִּשָּׁבֵֽעַ׃ ה֥וּא תְהִלָּתְךָ֖ וְה֣וּא אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ אֲשֶׁר־עָשָׂ֣ה אִתְּךָ֗ אֶת־הַגְּדֹלֹ֤ת וְאֶת־הַנּֽוֹרָאֹת֙ הָאֵ֔לֶּה אֲשֶׁ֥ר רָא֖וּ עֵינֶֽיךָ׃ בְּשִׁבְעִ֣ים נֶ֔פֶשׁ יָרְד֥וּ אֲבֹתֶ֖יךָ מִצְרָ֑יְמָהּ וְעַתָּ֗ה שָֽׂמְךָ֙ יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ כְּכוֹכְבֵ֥י הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם לָרֹֽב׃ וְאָ֣הַבְתָּ֔ אֵ֖ת יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ וְשָׁמַרְתָּ֣ מִשְׁמַרְתּ֗וֹ וְחֻקֹּתָ֧יו וּמִשְׁפָּטָ֛יו וּמִצְוֺתָ֖יו כָּל־הַיָּמִֽים׃ וִֽידַעְתֶּם֮ הַיּוֹם֒ כִּ֣י ׀ לֹ֣א אֶת־בְּנֵיכֶ֗ם אֲשֶׁ֤ר לֹֽא־יָדְעוּ֙ וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר לֹא־רָא֔וּ אֶת־מוּסַ֖ר יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֑ם אֶת־גָּדְל֕וֹ אֶת־יָדוֹ֙ הַחֲזָקָ֔ה וּזְרֹע֖וֹ הַנְּטוּיָֽה׃ וְאֶת־אֹֽתֹתָיו֙ וְאֶֽת־מַעֲשָׂ֔יו אֲשֶׁ֥ר עָשָׂ֖ה בְּת֣וֹךְ מִצְרָ֑יִם לְפַרְעֹ֥ה מֶֽלֶךְ־מִצְרַ֖יִם וּלְכָל־אַרְצֽוֹ׃ וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר עָשָׂה֩ לְחֵ֨יל מִצְרַ֜יִם לְסוּסָ֣יו וּלְרִכְבּ֗וֹ אֲשֶׁ֨ר הֵצִ֜יף אֶת־מֵ֤י יַם־סוּף֙ עַל־פְּנֵיהֶ֔ם בְּרָדְפָ֖ם אַחֲרֵיכֶ֑ם וַיְאַבְּדֵ֣ם יְהוָ֔ה עַ֖ד הַיּ֥וֹם הַזֶּֽה׃ וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר עָשָׂ֛ה לָכֶ֖ם בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר עַד־בֹּאֲכֶ֖ם עַד־הַמָּק֥וֹם הַזֶּֽה׃ וַאֲשֶׁ֨ר עָשָׂ֜ה לְדָתָ֣ן וְלַאֲבִירָ֗ם בְּנֵ֣י אֱלִיאָב֮ בֶּן־רְאוּבֵן֒ אֲשֶׁ֨ר פָּצְתָ֤ה הָאָ֙רֶץ֙ אֶת־פִּ֔יהָ וַתִּבְלָעֵ֥ם וְאֶת־בָּתֵּיהֶ֖ם וְאֶת־אָהֳלֵיהֶ֑ם וְאֵ֤ת כָּל־הַיְקוּם֙ אֲשֶׁ֣ר בְּרַגְלֵיהֶ֔ם בְּקֶ֖רֶב כָּל־יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ כִּ֤י עֵֽינֵיכֶם֙ הָֽרֹאֹ֔ת אֶת־כָּל־מַעֲשֵׂ֥ה יְהוָ֖ה הַגָּדֹ֑ל אֲשֶׁ֖ר עָשָֽׂה׃ וּשְׁמַרְתֶּם֙ אֶת־כָּל־הַמִּצְוָ֔ה אֲשֶׁ֛ר אָנֹכִ֥י מְצַוְּךָ֖ הַיּ֑וֹם לְמַ֣עַן תֶּחֶזְק֗וּ וּבָאתֶם֙ וִֽירִשְׁתֶּ֣ם אֶת־הָאָ֔רֶץ אֲשֶׁ֥ר אַתֶּ֛ם עֹבְרִ֥ים שָׁ֖מָּה לְרִשְׁתָּֽהּ׃ וּלְמַ֨עַן תַּאֲרִ֤יכוּ יָמִים֙ עַל־הָ֣אֲדָמָ֔ה אֲשֶׁר֩ נִשְׁבַּ֨ע יְהוָ֧ה לַאֲבֹתֵיכֶ֛ם לָתֵ֥ת לָהֶ֖ם וּלְזַרְעָ֑ם אֶ֛רֶץ זָבַ֥ת חָלָ֖ב וּדְבָֽשׁ׃','Siddur Sefard, Additional Prayers , Chapter of Fear of God'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god','en','Deuteronomy 10:12-11:9 And now Israel, what does Adonoy, your God, require of you, but to fear Adonoy, your God, to walk in all His ways, and to love Him and to serve Adonoy, your God, with all your heart and with all your soul. To keep the commandments of Adonoy and His decrees, which I command you this day. Behold, the heaven and the highest of heavens belong to Adonoy, your God, the earth and all that is in it. Yet only in your fathers did Adonoy delight, to love them, and He chose their offspring after them, even you among all the peoples as [it is] this day. Circumcise the barrier of your heart, and be stiffnecked no longer. For Adonoy, your God, is God of all powers and the Master of all masters, the Almighty, the Great, the Powerful, the Awesome, Who has no regard for personages and takes no bribes. Who does justice for the orphan and the widow, and loves the stranger, giving him food and clothing. You must love the stranger for you were strangers in the land of Egypt. You must fear Adonoy, your God, serve Him, cleave to Him, and swear by His Name. He is your praise, and He is your God, Who did with you all these great and awesome things that your eyes have seen. With seventy people your fathers descended to Egypt, and now Adonoy, your God, has made you as abundant as the stars of heaven. [Therefore] you shall love Adonoy, your God, and keep His trust, His decrees, His statutes, and His commandments all the days. And you should know this day, that it is not with your children who have not known and who did not experience the chastisement of Adonoy, your God, His mighty hand, and His outstretched arm. His signs and His deeds that He performed in the midst of Egypt, to Pharaoh, the king of Egypt, and to all his land. And what He did to the army of Egypt, to their horses, and to their chariots; how He made the water of the Sea of Reeds drown them as they pursued you, and Adonoy destroyed them to this very day. And what He did for you in the wilderness, until you came into this place. And what He did unto Dathan and Aviram, the sons of Eliav, son of Reuben, when the earth opened her mouth, and swallowed them, and their households, their tents and all the substance that was in their possession in the midst of all Israel. But your eyes have seen all the great deeds of Adonoy, that He performed. You should [therefore] keep all the commandments which I command you this day, so you will be strong, and go in and possess the land, to which you are passing over to possess it. And in order to prolong your days upon the land Adonoy swore to your fathers to give to them and to their offspring; a land flowing with milk and honey.','Siddur Sefard, Additional Prayers , Chapter of Fear of God'),
