('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:42:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! remember, that we are dust.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:42:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo zah-khohr kee ah-fahr ah-nah-khe-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:43:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ נָא אַל תְּשִׁיבֵֽנוּ רֵיקָם מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:43:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! Please do not turn us away empty-handed from You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:43:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo nah ahl te-shee-veh-noo rey-kahm mee-LE-fah-ney-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:44:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ תְּהֵא הַשָּׁעָה הַזֹּאת שְׁעַת רַחֲמִים וְעֵת רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:44:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! let this hour be an hour of compassion and a time of favor before You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:44:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo te-heh hah-shah-ah hah-zoht she-aht rah-khah-meem ve-eht rah-tsohn mee-LE-fah-ney-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:45:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ חֲמוֹל עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל עוֹלָלֵֽינוּ וְטַפֵּֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:45:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! have compassion upon us, and upon our children and infants.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:45:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo khah-mohl ah-ley-noo ve-ahl oh-lah-ley-noo ve-tah-peh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:46:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן הֲרוּגִים עַל שֵׁם קָדְשֶֽׁךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:46:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of those who were slain for Your holy Name.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:46:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo ah-seh le-mah-ahn hah-roo-geem ahl shehm kohd-sheh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:47:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן טְבוּחִים עַל יִחוּדֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:47:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of those who were slaughtered for [proclaiming] Your Unity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:47:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo ah-seh le-mah-ahn te-voo-kheem ahl yee-khoo-deh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:48:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן בָּאֵי בָאֵשׁ וּבַמַּֽיִם עַל קִדּוּשׁ שְׁמֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:48:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of those who went through fire and water for the sanctification of Your Name.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:48:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo ah-seh le-mah-ahn bah-ey vah-ehsh oo-vah-mah-yeem ahl kee-doosh she-meh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:49:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ נְקוֹם לְעֵינֵֽינוּ נִקְ֒מַת דַּם עֲבָדֶֽיךָ הַשָּׁפוּךְ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:49:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! avenge before our eyes the spilled blood of Your servants.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:49:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo ne-kohm le-ey-ney-noo NEEK-maht dahm ah-vah-dey-khah hah-shah-fookh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:50:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַעַנְ֒ךָ אִם לֺא לְמַעֲנֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:50:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for Your sake if not for ours.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:50:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo ah-seh le-mah-AHN-khah eem loh le-mah-ah-neh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:51:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַעַנְ֒ךָ וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:51:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for Your sake and deliver us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:51:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo ah-seh le-mah-AHN-khah ve-hoh-shee-eh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:52:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן רַחֲמֶֽיךָ הָרַבִּים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:52:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of Your great mercy.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:52:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo ah-seh le-mah-ahn rah-khah-mey-khah hah-rah-beem:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:53:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן שִׁמְךָ הַגָּדוֹל הַגִּבּוֹר וְהַנּוֹרָא שֶׁנִּקְרָא עָלֵֽינוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:53:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of Your great, mighty, and awesome Name which is proclaimed upon us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:53:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo ah-seh le-mah-ahn sheem-khah hah-gah-dohl hah-gee-bohr ve-hah-noh-rah sheh-neek-rah ah-ley-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:54:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ חָנֵּֽנוּ וַעֲנֵֽנוּ כִּי אֵין בָּֽנוּ מַעֲשִׂים עֲשֵׂה עִמָּֽנוּ צְדָקָה וָחֶֽסֶד וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:54:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! favor us and answer us for we have no accomplishments; deal with us charitably and kindly with us and deliver us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:54:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','ah-vee-noo mahl-keh-noo khah-neh-noo vah-ah-neh-noo kee eyn bah-noo mah-ah-seem ah-seh ee-mah-noo tse-dah-kah vah-kheh-sehd ve-hoh-shee-eh-noo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְמָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְ֒קָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ. בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל. בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב. וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming of His Mashiach. In your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','yeet-gah-dahl ve-yeet-kah-dahsh she-meh rah-bah be-ah-le-mah dee ve-rah kheer-oo-teh ve-yahm-leekh mahl-khoo-teh ve-yahts-mahkh poo-RE-kah-neh vee-kah-rehv (kehts) me-shee-kheh. be-khah-yey-khohn oo-ve-yoh-mey-khohn oo-ve-khah-yey de-khahl beyt yees-rah-ehl. bah-ah-gah-lah oo-veez-mahn kah-reev. ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','ye-heh she-meh rah-bah me-vah-rahkh le-ah-lahm oo-le-ah-LE-mey ah-LE-mah-yah','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְעֵֽלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְ֒מָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','yeet-bah-rahkh ve-yeesh-tah-bahkh ve-yeet-pah-ahr ve-yeet-roh-mahm ve-yeet-nah-seh ve-yeet-hah-dahr ve-yeet-ah-leh ve-yeet-hah-lahl she-meh de-koo-de-shah, be-reekh hoo le-eh-lah (vshyt" oo-le-eh-lah mee-kahl) meen kohl beer-khah-tah ve-shee-rah-tah, toosh-be-khah-tah ve-neh-kheh-mah-tah, dah-ah-mee-rahn be-ah-LE-mah, ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','וִיהִי נֹֽעַם אֲדֹנָי אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ עָלֵֽינוּ וּמַעֲשֵׂה יָדֵֽינוּ כּוֹנְנָה עָלֵֽינוּ וּמַעֲשֵׂה יָדֵֽינוּ כּוֹנְנֵֽהוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','May the pleasantness of my Master our God be upon us, and the work of our hands established for us, and the work of our hands—establish it.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','vee-hee noh-ahm ah-doh-nahy eh-loh-hey-noo ah-ley-noo oo-mah-ah-seh yah-dey-noo koh-ne-nah ah-ley-noo oo-mah-ah-seh yah-dey-noo koh-ne-neh-hoo:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','ישֵׁב בְּסֵֽתֶר עֶלְיוֹן בְּצֵל שַׁדַּי יִתְלוֹנָן: אֹמַר לַיהֹוָה מַחְסִי וּמְצוּדָתִי אֱלֹהַי אֶבְטַח־בּוֹ: כִּי הוּא יַצִּילְךָ מִפַּח יָקוּשׁ מִדֶּֽבֶר הַוּֽוֹת: בְּאֶבְרָתוֹ יָֽסֶךְ לָךְ וְתַֽחַת־כְּנָפָיו תֶּחְסֶה צִנָּה וְסֹחֵרָה אֲמִתּוֹ: לֹא־תִירָא מִפַּֽחַד לָֽיְלָה מֵחֵץ יָעוּף יוֹמָם: מִדֶּֽבֶר בָּאֹֽפֶל יַהֲלֹךְ מִקֶּֽטֶב יָשׁוּד צָהֳרָֽיִם: יִפֹּל מִצִּדְּךָ אֶֽלֶף וּרְבָבָה מִימִינֶֽךָ אֵלֶֽיךָ לֹא יִגָּשׁ: רַק בְּעֵינֶֽיךָ תַבִּיט וְשִׁלֻּמַת רְשָׁעִים תִּרְאֶה: כִּי־אַתָּה יְהֹוָה מַחְסִי עֶלְיוֹן שַֽׂמְתָּ מְעוֹנֶֽךָ: לֹא־תְאֻנֶּה אֵלֶֽיךָ רָעָה וְנֶֽגַע לֹא־יִקְרַב בְּאָהֳלֶֽךָ: כִּי מַלְאָכָיו יְצַוֶּה־לָּךְ לִשְׁמָרְךָ בְּכָל־דְּרָכֶֽיךָ: עַל־כַּפַּֽיִם יִשָּׂאֽוּנְךָ פֶּן־תִּגֹּף בָּאֶֽבֶן רַגְלֶֽךָ: עַל־שַֽׁחַל וָפֶֽתֶן תִּדְרֹךְ תִּרְמֹס כְּפִיר וְתַנִּין: כִּי בִי חָשַׁק וַאֲפַלְּטֵֽהוּ אֲשַׂגְּבֵֽהוּ כִּי־יָדַע שְׁמִי: יִקְרָאֵֽנִי וְאֶעֱנֵֽהוּ עִמּוֹ־אָנֹכִי בְצָרָה אֲחַלְּצֵֽהוּ וַאֲכַבְּדֵֽהוּ: אֹֽרֶךְ יָמִים אַשְׂבִּיעֵֽהוּ וְאַרְאֵֽהוּ בִּישׁוּעָתִי: אֹֽרֶךְ יָמִים אַשְׂבִּיעֵֽהוּ וְאַרְאֵֽהוּ בִּישׁוּעָתִי:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','He who dwells in the shelter of the Supreme One, under the protection of Shadai he will abide. I say of Adonoy, [He is] my refuge and my stronghold, my God in Whom I trust. For He will save you from the snare-trap, from destructive pestilence. With His wings He will cover you and beneath His wings, you will find refuge; His truth is a shield, a full shield. You will not fear the terror of night, nor the arrow that flies by day. The pestilence that prowls in darkness, nor the deadly plague that ravages at noon. A thousand will fall at your [left] side, and ten thousand at your [right] side but it shall not come near you. Only with your eyes will you behold and see the punishment of the wicked. For you [have proclaimed]: “Adonoy is my refuge,” the Supreme One you have made your dwelling. No evil shall befall you, and no plague shall come near your tent. For His angels He will command on your behalf— to guard you in all your ways. They will carry you upon their hands, lest you hurt your foot on a rock. You will tread upon lion and snake, you will trample young lion and serpent. Because he clings to Me with desire, I will save him; I will strengthen him, for he knows My Name. When he calls upon Me, I will answer him; I am with him in distress, I will free him and honor him. I will satiate him with longevity, and will let him see My deliverance. I will satiate him with longevity, and will let him see My deliverance.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','y-shehv be-seh-tehr ehl-yohn be-tsehl shah-dahy yeet-loh-nahn: oh-mahr lah-ah-doh-NAI mahkh-see oo-me-tsoo-dah-tee eh-loh-hahy ehv-tahkh boh: kee hoo yah-tsee-le-khah mee-pahkh yah-koosh mee-deh-vehr hah-voht: be-ehv-rah-toh yah-sehkh lahkh ve-tah-khaht ke-nah-fahv tehkh-seh tsee-nah ve-soh-kheh-rah ah-mee-toh: loh tee-rah mee-pah-khahd lah-ye-lah meh-khehts yah-oof yoh-mahm: mee-deh-vehr bah-oh-fehl yah-hah-lohkh mee-keh-tehv yah-shood tsoh-hoh-rah-yeem: yee-pohl mee-tsee-de-khah eh-lehf oo-re-vah-vah mee-mee-neh-khah eh-ley-khah loh yee-gahsh: rahk be-ey-ney-khah tah-beet ve-shee-loo-maht re-shah-eem teer-eh: kee ah-tah ah-doh-NAI mahkh-see ehl-yohn sah-me-tah me-oh-neh-khah: loh te-oo-neh eh-ley-khah rah-ah ve-neh-gah loh yeek-rahv be-oh-hoh-leh-khah: kee mahl-ah-khahv ye-tsah-veh lahkh leesh-mah-re-khah be-khohl de-rah-khey-khah: ahl kah-pah-yeem yee-sah-oo-ne-khah pehn tee-gohf bah-eh-vehn rahg-leh-khah: ahl shah-khahl vah-feh-tehn teed-rohkh teer-mohs ke-feer ve-tah-neen: kee vee khah-shahk vah-ah-fah-le-teh-hoo ah-sah-ge-veh-hoo kee yah-dah she-mee: yeek-rah-eh-nee ve-eh-eh-neh-hoo ee-moh ah-noh-khee ve-tsah-rah ah-khah-le-tseh-hoo vah-ah-khah-be-deh-hoo: oh-rehkh yah-meem ahs-bee-eh-hoo ve-ahr-eh-hoo bee-shoo-ah-tee: oh-rehkh yah-meem ahs-bee-eh-hoo ve-ahr-eh-hoo bee-shoo-ah-tee:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','וְאַתָּה קָדוֹשׁ יוֹשֵׁב תְּהִלּוֹת יִשְׂרָאֵל: וְקָרָא זֶה אֶל זֶה וְאָמַר','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','And You, Holy One, are enthroned upon the praises of Israel. And [the angels] call one to another and say:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','ve-ah-tah kah-dohsh yoh-shehv te-hee-loht yees-rah-ehl: ve-kah-rah zeh ehl zeh ve-ah-mahr','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','קָדוֹשׁ קָדוֹשׁ קָדוֹשׁ יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת מְלֹא כָל הָאָֽרֶץ כְּבוֹדוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','“Holy, holy, holy is Adonoy of Hosts: the fullness of all the earth is His glory.”','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','kah-dohsh kah-dohsh kah-dohsh ah-doh-NAI tse-vah-oht me-loh khohl hah-ah-rehts ke-voh-doh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','וּמְקַבְּ֒לִין דֵּין מִן דֵּין וְאָמְרִין קַדִּישׁ בִּשְׁמֵי מְרוֹמָא עִלָּאָה בֵּית שְׁכִינְתֵּהּ קַדִּישׁ עַל אַרְעָא עוֹבַד גְּבוּרְתֵּהּ קַדִּישׁ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְמֵי עָלְמַיָּא יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת. מַלְיָא כָל אַרְעָא זִיו יְקָרֵהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','And they receive [sanction] one from another, and say, “Holy in the highest heights of heaven, the abode of His Divine Presence; holy upon earth, the work of His mighty power; holy forever and to all eternity— is Adonoy of Hosts; the whole earth is filled with the radiance of His glory.”','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','oo-me-kah-BE-leen deyn meen deyn ve-ah-me-reen kah-deesh beesh-mey me-roh-mah ee-lah-ah beyt she-khee-ne-teh kah-deesh ahl ahr-ah oh-vahd ge-voo-re-teh kah-deesh le-ah-lahm oo-le-ah-le-mey ah-le-mah-yah ah-doh-NAI tse-vah-oht. mahl-yah khohl ahr-ah zeev ye-kah-reh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','וַתִּשָּׂאֵֽנִי רֽוּחַ וָאֶשְׁמַע אַחֲרַי קוֹל רַֽעַשׁ גָּדוֹל','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','And a wind lifted me; and I heard behind me the sound of a great rushing;','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','vah-tee-sah-eh-nee roo-ahkh vah-ehsh-mah ah-khah-rahy kohl rah-ahsh gah-dohl','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','בָּרוּךְ כְּבוֹד יְהֹוָה מִמְּ֒קוֹמוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','“Blessed is the glory of Adonoy from His place.”','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','bah-rookh ke-vohd ah-doh-NAI mee-ME-koh-moh:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','וּנְטָלַתְנִי רוּחָא וּשְׁמָעִית בַּתְרַי קָל זִֽיעַ סַגִּיא דִּמְשַׁבְּ֒חִין וְאָמְרִין בְּרִיךְ יְקָרָא דַיהֹוָה מֵאֲתַר בֵּית שְׁכִינְתֵּהּ: יְהֹוָה יִמְלֹךְ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד: יְהֹוָה מַלְכוּתֵהּ קָאֵים לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְמֵי עָלְמַיָּא: יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵי אַבְרָהָם יִצְחָק וְיִשְׂרָאֵל אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ שָׁמְרָה זֹאת לְעֹלָם לְיֵֽצֶר מַחְשְׁ֒בוֹת לְבַב עַמֶּֽךָ וְהָכֵן לְבָבָם אֵלֶֽיךָ: וְהוּא רַחוּם יְכַפֵּר עָוֹן וְלֹא יַשְׁחִית וְהִרְבָּה לְהָשִׁיב אַפּוֹ וְלֹא יָעִיר כָּל חֲמָתוֹ: כִּי אַתָּה אֲדֹנָי טוֹב וְסַלָּח וְרַב חֶֽסֶד לְכָל קֹרְ֒אֶֽיךָ: צִדְקָתְ֒ךָ צֶֽדֶק לְעוֹלָם וְתוֹרָתְ֒ךָ אֱמֶת: תִּתֵּן אֱמֶת לְיַעֲקֹב חֶֽסֶד לְאַבְרָהָם אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּֽעְתָּ לַאֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ מִֽימֵי קֶֽדֶם: בָּרוּךְ אֲדֹנָי יוֹם יוֹם יַעֲמָס לָֽנוּ הָאֵל יְשׁוּעָתֵֽנוּ סֶֽלָה: יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת עִמָּֽנוּ מִשְׂגָּב לָֽנוּ אֱלֹהֵי יַעֲקֹב סֶֽלָה: יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת אַשְׁרֵי אָדָם בֹּטֵֽחַ בָּךְ: יְהֹוָה הוֹשִֽׁיעָה הַמֶּֽלֶךְ יַעֲנֵֽנוּ בְיוֹם קָרְאֵֽנוּ: בָּרוּךְ הוּא אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ שֶׁבְּ֒רָאָֽנוּ לִכְבוֹדוֹ וְהִבְדִּילָֽנוּ מִן הַתּוֹעִים וְנָֽתַן לָֽנוּ תּוֹרַת אֱמֶת וְחַיֵּי עוֹלָם נָטַע בְּתוֹכֵֽנוּ הוּא יִפְתַּח לִבֵּֽנוּ בְּתוֹרָתוֹ וְיָשֵׂם בְּלִבֵּֽנוּ אַהֲבָתוֹ וְיִרְאָתוֹ וְלַעֲשׂוֹת רְצוֹנוֹ וּלְעָבְדוֹ בְּלֵבָב שָׁלֵם לְמַֽעַן לֹא נִיגַע לָרִיק וְלֹא נֵלֵד לַבֶּהָלָה: יְהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ שֶׁנִּשְׁמֹר חֻקֶּֽיךָ בָּעוֹלָם הַזֶּה וְנִזְכֶּה וְנִחְיֶה וְנִרְאֶה וְנִירַשׁ טוֹבָה וּבְרָכָה לִשְׁנֵי יְמוֹת הַמָּשִֽׁיחַ וּלְחַיֵּי הָעוֹלָם הַבָּא: לְמַֽעַן יְזַמֶּרְךָ כָבוֹד וְלֹא יִדֹּם יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהַי לְעוֹלָם אוֹדֶֽךָ: בָּרוּךְ הַגֶּֽבֶר אֲשֶׁר יִבְטַח בַּיהֹוָה וְהָיָה יְהֹוָה מִבְטַחוֹ: בִּטְחוּ בַיהֹוָה עֲדֵי עַד כִּי בְּיָהּ יְהֹוָה צוּר עוֹלָמִים: וְיִבְטְ֒חוּ בְךָ יוֹדְ֒עֵי שְׁמֶֽךָ כִּי לֹא עָזַֽבְתָּ דֹרְ֒שֶֽׁיךָ יְהֹוָה: יְהֹוָה חָפֵץ לְמַֽעַן צִדְקוֹ יַגְדִּיל תּוֹרָה וְיַאְדִּיר:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','“And a wind lifted me and I heard behind me a sound of a great rushing of those who uttered praises and said, “Blessed is the glory of Adonoy from the place, the abode of His Divine Presence.” Adonoy will reign forever and ever. Adonoy, His kingdom is established forever and to all eternity. Adonoy, God of Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, our fathers, keep this forever as the intention of the hearts of Your people, and direct their hearts to You. And He, the merciful One, atons iniquity and does ot destroy; He frequently withdraws His anger and does not arouse all His rage. For You, my Master, are good and forgiving, and abounding in kindness to all who call upon You. Your righteousness is everlasting and Your Torah is truth. You will grant truth to Jacob kindliness to Abraham, as You have sworn to our fathers from the days of old. Blessed is my Master day by day; He loads us, the Almighty Who is our deliverance, forever. Adonoy of Hosts is with us a stronghold for us is the God of Jacob, selah. Adonoy of Hosts, fortunate is the man who trusts in You. Adonoy, deliver [us]; the King will answer us on the day we call. Blessed is He, our God, Who created us for His glory, and set us apart from those who go astray; and gave us the Torah of truth, and eternal life He implanted within us. May He open our heart to His Torah, and instill in our heart love and awe of Him, to do His will and serve Him with a perfect heart, so that we shall not labor in vain nor bring forth that which causes dismay. May it be Your will, Adonoy, our God, and God of our fathers, that we keep Your statutes in this world, and [thus] be privileged to live and behold, and to inherit the goodness and blessing of the Messianic days and in the life of the World to Come. In order that my soul sing to You and not be stilled; Adonoy, my God, forever will I thank You. Blessed is the man who trusts in Adonoy, so that Adonoy is his security. Trust in Adonoy until the end of days, for in God, Adonoy, is the strength of the worlds. Those who know your Name will trust in You, for You have never forsaken those who seek You, Adonoy. Adonoy desired, for the sake of His righteousness, to make the Torah great and to glorify it.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','oo-ne-tah-laht-nee roo-khah oo-she-mah-eet baht-rahy kahl zee-ah sah-gee deem-shah-BE-kheen ve-ah-me-reen be-reekh ye-kah-rah dah-ah-doh-NAI meh-ah-tahr beyt she-khee-ne-teh: ah-doh-NAI yeem-lohkh le-oh-lahm vah-ehd: ah-doh-NAI mahl-khoo-teh kah-eym le-ah-lahm oo-le-ah-le-mey ah-le-mah-yah: ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey ahv-rah-hahm yeets-khahk ve-yees-rah-ehl ah-voh-tey-noo shah-me-rah zoht le-oh-lahm le-yeh-tsehr mahkh-SHE-voht le-vahv ah-meh-khah ve-hah-khehn le-vah-vahm eh-ley-khah: ve-hoo rah-khoom ye-khah-pehr ah-vohn ve-loh yahsh-kheet ve-heer-bah le-hah-sheev ah-poh ve-loh yah-eer kohl khah-mah-toh: kee ah-tah ah-doh-nahy tohv ve-sah-lahkh ve-rahv kheh-sehd le-khohl koh-RE-ey-khah: tseed-kah-TE-khah tseh-dehk le-oh-lahm ve-toh-rah-TE-khah eh-meht: tee-tehn eh-meht le-yah-ah-kohv kheh-sehd le-ahv-rah-hahm ah-shehr neesh-bah-e-tah lah-ah-voh-tey-noo mee-mey keh-dehm: bah-rookh ah-doh-nahy yohm yohm yah-ah-mahs lah-noo hah-ehl ye-shoo-ah-teh-noo seh-lah: ah-doh-NAI tse-vah-oht ee-mah-noo mees-gahv lah-noo eh-loh-hey yah-ah-kohv seh-lah: ah-doh-NAI tse-vah-oht ahsh-rey ah-dahm boh-teh-ahkh bahkh: ah-doh-NAI hoh-shee-ah hah-meh-lehkh yah-ah-neh-noo ve-yohm kah-re-eh-noo: bah-rookh hoo eh-loh-hey-noo sheh-BE-rah-ah-noo leekh-voh-doh ve-heev-dee-lah-noo meen hah-toh-eem ve-nah-tahn lah-noo toh-raht eh-meht ve-khah-yey oh-lahm nah-tah be-toh-kheh-noo hoo yeef-tahkh lee-beh-noo be-toh-rah-toh ve-yah-sehm be-lee-beh-noo ah-hah-vah-toh ve-yeer-ah-toh ve-lah-ah-soht re-tsoh-noh oo-le-ah-ve-doh be-leh-vahv shah-lehm le-mah-ahn loh nee-gah lah-reek ve-loh neh-lehd lah-beh-hah-lah: ye-hee rah-tsohn mee-le-fah-ney-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo veh-loh-hey ah-voh-tey-noo sheh-neesh-mohr khoo-key-khah bah-oh-lahm hah-zeh ve-neez-keh ve-neekh-yeh ve-neer-eh ve-nee-rahsh toh-vah oo-ve-rah-khah leesh-ney ye-moht hah-mah-shee-ahkh oo-le-khah-yey hah-oh-lahm hah-bah: le-mah-ahn ye-zah-mehr-khah khah-vohd ve-loh yee-dohm ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hahy le-oh-lahm oh-deh-khah: bah-rookh hah-geh-vehr ah-shehr yeev-tahkh bah-ah-doh-NAI ve-hah-yah ah-doh-NAI meev-tah-khoh: beet-khoo vah-ah-doh-NAI ah-dey ahd kee be-yahh ah-doh-NAI tsoor oh-lah-meem: ve-yeev-TE-khoo ve-khah yoh-DE-ey she-meh-khah kee loh ah-zah-ve-tah doh-RE-shey-khah ah-doh-NAI: ah-doh-NAI khah-fehts le-mah-ahn tseed-koh yahg-deel toh-rah ve-yah-deer:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְמָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְקָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ. בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל. בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming of His Mashiach in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','yeet-gah-dahl ve-yeet-kah-dahsh she-meh rah-bah be-ah-le-mah dee ve-rah kheer-oo-teh ve-yahm-leekh mahl-khoo-teh ve-yahts-mahkh poo-re-kah-neh vee-kah-rehv (kehts) me-shee-kheh. be-khah-yey-khohn oo-ve-yoh-mey-khohn oo-ve-khah-yey de-khahl beyt yees-rah-ehl. bah-ah-gah-lah oo-veez-mahn kah-reev ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְמֵי עָלְמַיָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','ye-heh she-meh rah-bah me-vah-rahkh le-ah-lahm oo-le-ah-le-mey ah-le-mah-yah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקֻדְשָׁא. בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְעֵֽלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא. תֻּשְׁבְּ֒חָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא. דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְמָא. וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','yeet-bah-rahkh ve-yeesh-tah-bahkh ve-yeet-pah-ahr ve-yeet-roh-mahm ve-yeet-nah-seh ve-yeet-hah-dahr ve-yeet-ah-leh ve-yeet-hah-lahl she-meh de-kood-shah. be-reekh hoo le-eh-lah (vshyt" oo-le-eh-lah mee-kahl) meen kohl beer-khah-tah ve-shee-rah-tah. toosh-BE-khah-tah ve-neh-kheh-mah-tah. dah-ah-mee-rahn be-ah-le-mah. ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','תִּתְקַבֵּל צְלוֹתְ֒הוֹן וּבָעוּתְ֒הוֹן דְּכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל קֳדָם אֲבוּהוֹן דִּי בִשְׁמַיָּא וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','May there be acceptance of the prayers and supplications of the entire House of Israel before their Father in heaven. And say, Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','teet-kah-behl tse-loh-TE-hohn oo-vah-oo-TE-hohn de-khahl beyt yees-rah-ehl koh-dahm ah-voo-hohn dee veesh-mah-yah ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','May there be abundant peace from heaven and life for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','ye-heh she-lah-mah rah-bah meen she-mah-yah ve-khah-yeem ah-ley-noo ve-ahl kohl yees-rah-ehl ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','עוֹשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא יַעֲשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','He Who makes peace in His high heavens may He, make peace for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:16:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','oh-seh shah-lohm beem-roh-mahv hoo yah-ah-seh shah-lohm ah-ley-noo ve-ahl kohl yees-rah-ehl ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','עָלֵֽינוּ לְשַׁבֵּֽחַ לַאֲדוֹן הַכֹּל לָתֵת גְּדֻלָּה לְיוֹצֵר בְּרֵאשִׁית שֶׁלֹּא עָשָֽׂנוּ כְּגוֹיֵי הָאֲרָצוֹת וְלֹא שָׂמָֽנוּ כְּמִשְׁפְּ֒חוֹת הָאֲדָמָה שֶׁלֹּא שָׂם חֶלְקֵֽנוּ כָּהֶם וְגוֹרָלֵֽנוּ כְּכָל הֲמוֹנָם: שֶׁהֵם מִשְׁתַּחֲוִים לַהֶֽבֶל וָרִיק וּמִתְפַּלְּ֒לִים אֶל אֵל לֹא יוֹשִֽׁיעַ. וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ כּוֹרְ֒עִים וּמִשְׁתַּחֲוִים וּמוֹדִים לִפְנֵי מֶֽלֶךְ מַלְכֵי הַמְּ֒לָכִים הַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא. שֶׁהוּא נוֹטֶה שָׁמַֽיִם וְיוֹסֵד אָֽרֶץ. וּמוֹשַׁב יְקָרוֹ בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם מִמַּֽעַל. וּשְׁכִינַת עֻזּוֹ בְּגָבְהֵי מְרוֹמִים. הוּא אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ אֵין עוֹד. אֱמֶת מַלְכֵּֽנוּ אֶֽפֶס זוּלָתוֹ כַּכָּתוּב בְּתוֹרָתוֹ וְיָדַעְתָּ הַיּוֹם וַהֲשֵׁבֹתָ אֶל לְבָבֶֽךָ כִּי יְהֹוָה הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם מִמַּֽעַל וְעַל הָאָֽרֶץ מִתָּֽחַת אֵין עוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','It is our obligation to praise the Master of all, to ascribe greatness to the Creator of the [world in the] beginning: that He has not made us like the nations of the lands, and has not positioned us like the families of the earth; that He has not assigned our portion like theirs, nor our lot like that of all their multitudes. For they prostrate themselves to vanity and nothingness, and pray to a god that cannot deliver. But we bow, prostrate ourselves, and offer thanks before the Supreme King of kings, the Holy One blessed is He, Who spreads the heavens, and establishes the earth, and the Seat of His glory is in heaven above, and the abode of His invincible might is in the loftiest heights. He is our God, there is nothing else. Our King is true, all else is insignificant, as it is written in His Torah: “And you shall know this day and take into your heart that Adonoy is God in the heavens above and upon the earth below; there is nothing else.”','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:17:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','ah-ley-noo le-shah-beh-ahkh lah-ah-dohn hah-kohl lah-teht ge-doo-lah le-yoh-tsehr be-reh-sheet sheh-loh ah-sah-noo ke-goh-yey hah-ah-rah-tsoht ve-loh sah-mah-noo ke-meesh-PE-khoht hah-ah-dah-mah sheh-loh sahm khehl-keh-noo kah-hehm ve-goh-rah-leh-noo ke-khahl hah-moh-nahm: sheh-hehm meesh-tah-khah-veem lah-heh-vehl vah-reek oo-meet-pah-LE-leem ehl ehl loh yoh-shee-ah. vah-ahnah-khe-noo koh-RE-eem oo-meesh-tah-khah-veem oo-moh-deem leef-ney meh-lehkh mahl-khey hah-ME-lah-kheem hah-kah-dohsh bah-rookh hoo. sheh-hoo noh-teh shah-mah-yeem ve-yoh-sehd ah-rehts. oo-moh-shahv ye-kah-roh bah-shah-mah-yeem mee-mah-ahl. oo-she-khee-naht oo-zoh be-gohv-hey me-roh-meem. hoo eh-loh-hey-noo eyn ohd. eh-meht mahl-keh-noo eh-fehs zoo-lah-toh kah-kah-toov be-toh-rah-toh ve-yah-dah-tah hah-yohm vah-hah-sheh-voh-tah ehl le-vah-veh-khah kee ah-doh-NAI hoo hah-eh-loh-heem bah-shah-mah-yeem mee-mah-ahl ve-ahl hah-ah-rehts mee-tah-khaht eyn ohd:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','עַל כֵּן נְקַוֶּה לְךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ לִרְאוֹת מְהֵרָה בְּתִפְאֶֽרֶת עֻזֶּֽךָ לְהַעֲבִיר גִּלּוּלִים מִן הָאָֽרֶץ וְהָאֱלִילִים כָּרוֹת יִכָּרֵתוּן לְתַקֵּן עוֹלָם בְּמַלְכוּת שַׁדַּי וְכָל בְּנֵי בָשָׂר יִקְרְ֒אוּ בִשְׁמֶֽךָ. לְהַפְנוֹת אֵלֶֽיךָ כָּל רִשְׁעֵי אָֽרֶץ. יַכִּֽירוּ וְיֵדְ֒עוּ כָּל יוֹשְׁ֒בֵי תֵבֵל כִּי לְךָ תִכְרַע כָּל בֶּֽרֶךְ תִּשָּׁבַע כָּל לָשׁוֹן: לְפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ יִכְרְ֒עוּ וְיִפֹּֽלוּ. וְלִכְבוֹד שִׁמְךָ יְקָר יִתֵּֽנוּ. וִיקַבְּ֒לוּ כֻלָּם אֶת עֹל מַלְכוּתֶֽךָ. וְתִמְלֹךְ עֲלֵיהֶם מְהֵרָה לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד. כִּי הַמַּלְכוּת שֶׁלְּ֒ךָ הִיא וּלְעֽוֹלְ֒מֵי עַד תִּמְלוֹךְ בְּכָבוֹד. כַּכָּתוּב בְּתוֹרָתֶֽךָ יְהֹוָה יִמְלֹךְ לְעֹלָם וָעֶד: וְנֶאֱמַר וְהָיָה יְהֹוָה לְמֶֽלֶךְ עַל כָּל הָאָֽרֶץ בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא יִהְיֶה יְהֹוָה אֶחָד וּשְׁמוֹ אֶחָד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','We therefore put our hope in You, Adonoy our God, to soon behold the glory of Your might in banishing idolatry from the earth and the false gods will be utterly exterminated to perfect the world as the kingdom of Shadai. And all mankind will invoke Your Name, to turn back to You, all the wicked of the earth. They will realize and know, all the inhabitants of the world, that to You, every knee must bend, every tongue must swear [allegiance to You]. Before You, Adonoy, our God, they will bow and prostrate themselves, and to the glory of Your Name give honor. And they will all accept [upon themselves] the yoke of Your kingdom, and You will reign over them, soon, forever and ever. For the kingdom is Yours, and to all eternity You will reign in glory, as it is written in Your Torah: “Adonoy will reign forever and ever.” And it is said: “And Adonoy will be King over the whole earth; on that day Adonoy will be One and His Name One.”','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:18:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','ahl kehn ne-kah-veh le-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo leer-oht me-heh-rah be-teef-eh-reht oo-zeh-khah le-hah-ah-veer gee-loo-leem meen hah-ah-rehts ve-hah-eh-lee-leem kah-roht yee-kah-reh-toon le-tah-kehn oh-lahm be-mahl-khoot shah-dahy ve-khohl be-ney vah-sahr yeek-RE-oo veesh-meh-khah. le-hahf-noht eh-ley-khah kohl reesh-ey ah-rehts. yah-kee-roo ve-yeh-DE-oo kohl yoh-SHE-vey teh-vehl kee le-khah teekh-rah kohl beh-rehkh tee-shah-vah kohl lah-shohn: le-fah-ney-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo yeekh-RE-oo ve-yee-poh-loo. ve-leekh-vohd sheem-khah ye-kahr yee-teh-noo. vee-kah-BE-loo khoo-lahm eht ohl mahl-khoo-teh-khah. ve-teem-lohkh ah-ley-hehm me-heh-rah le-oh-lahm vah-ehd. kee hah-mahl-khoot sheh-LE-khah hee oo-le-oh-LE-mey ahd teem-lohkh be-khah-vohd. kah-kah-toov be-toh-rah-teh-khah ah-doh-NAI yeem-lohkh le-oh-lahm vah-ehd: ve-neh-eh-mahr ve-hah-yah ah-doh-NAI le-meh-lehkh ahl kohl hah-ah-rehts bah-yohm hah-hoo yeeh-yeh ah-doh-NAI eh-khahd oo-she-moh eh-khahd:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','אַל תִּירָא מִפַּֽחַד פִּתְאֹם וּמִשֹּׁאַת רְשָׁעִים כִּי תָבֹא: עֻֽצוּ עֵצָה וְתֻפָר דַּבְּ֒רוּ דָבָר וְלֹא יָקוּם כִּי עִמָּֽנוּ אֵל: וְעַד זִקְנָה אֲנִי הוּא וְעַד שֵׂיבָה אֲנִי אֶסְבֹּל: אֲנִי עָשִֽׂיתִי וַאֲנִי אֶשָּׂא וַאֲנִי אֶסְבֹּל וַאֲמַלֵּט:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','Do not fear sudden terror nor the destruction of the wicked when it comes. Take counsel together and it will be foiled speak the word and it will not stand for God is with us. To your old age I am [with you], to your older years I will sustain you, I have made you, and I will carry you, I will sustain you and save you.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','ahl tee-rah mee-pah-khahd peet-ohm oo-mee-shoh-aht re-shah-eem kee tah-voh: oo-tsoo eh-tsah ve-too-fahr dah-BE-roo dah-vahr ve-loh yah-koom kee ee-mah-noo ehl: ve-ahd zeek-nah ah-nee hoo ve-ahd sey-vah ah-nee ehs-bohl: ah-nee ah-see-tee vah-ah-nee eh-sah vah-ah-nee ehs-bohl vah-ah-mah-leht:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְמָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְ֒קָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ. בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל. בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב. וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming of His Mashiach in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:20:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','yeet-gah-dahl ve-yeet-kah-dahsh she-meh rah-bah be-ah-le-mah dee ve-rah kheer-oo-teh ve-yahm-leekh mahl-khoo-teh ve-yahts-mahkh poo-RE-kah-neh vee-kah-rehv (kehts) me-shee-kheh. be-khah-yey-khohn oo-ve-yoh-mey-khohn oo-ve-khah-yey de-khahl beyt yees-rah-ehl. bah-ah-gah-lah oo-veez-mahn kah-reev. ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְמֵי עָלְמַיָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:21:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','ye-heh she-meh rah-bah me-vah-rahkh le-ah-lahm oo-le-ah-le-mey ah-le-mah-yah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקֻדְשָׁא. בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְעֵלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא. תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא. דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְמָא. וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:22:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','yeet-bah-rahkh ve-yeesh-tah-bahkh ve-yeet-pah-ahr ve-yeet-roh-mahm ve-yeet-nah-seh ve-yeet-hah-dahr ve-yeet-ah-leh ve-yeet-hah-lahl she-meh de-kood-shah. be-reekh hoo le-eh-lah (vshyt" oo-le-eh-lah mee-kahl) meen kohl beer-khah-tah ve-shee-rah-tah. toosh-be-khah-tah ve-neh-kheh-mah-tah. dah-ah-mee-rahn be-ah-le-mah. ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל. וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','May there be abundant peace from heaven and life for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:23:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','ye-heh she-lah-mah rah-bah meen she-mah-yah ve-khah-yeem ah-ley-noo ve-ahl kohl yees-rah-ehl. ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','עוֹשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא יַעֲשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','He Who makes peace in His high heavens may He, make peace for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:24:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','oh-seh shah-lohm beem-roh-mahv hoo yah-ah-seh shah-lohm ah-ley-noo ve-ahl kohl yees-rah-ehl ve-eem-roo ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','רִבּוֹנוֹ שֶׁל־עוֹלָם הֲרֵינִי מוֹחֵל לְכָל־מִי שֶׁהִכְעִיס וְהִקְנִיט אוֹתִי אוֹ שֶׁחָטָא כְּנֶגְדִי בֵּין בְּגוּפִי בֵּין בְּמֶמוֹנִי בֵין בִּכְבוֹדִי בֵין בְכָל אֲשֶׁר לִי בֵין בְּאוֹנֶס בֵּין בְּרָצוֹן בֵּין בְּשׁוֹגֵג בֵּין בְּמֵזִיד בֵין בְּדִבּוּר בֵּין בְּמַעֲשֶׂה בֵּין בְּגִלְגוּל זֶה בֵּין בְּגִלְגּוּל אַחֵר לְכָל־בַּר יִשְׂרָאֵל וְלֹא יֵעָנֵשׁ שׁוּם אָדָם בְסִבָּתִי יְהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהַי וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתַי שֶׁלֹּא אֶחְטֶא עוֹד וְלֹא אֶחֱזוֹר בָּהֶם וְלֹא אָשׁוּב עוֹד לְהַכְעִיסֶךָ וְלֹא אֶעֱשֶׂה הָרַע בְּעֵינֶֽיךָ וּמַה־שֶׁחָטָֽאתִי מְחוֹק בְּרַחֲמֶֽיךָ הָרַבִּים וְלֹא עַל יְדֵי יִסּוּרִים וָחֳלֶיִם רָעִים: יִהְיוּ לְרָצוֹן אִמְרֵי־פִי וְהֶגְיוֹן לִבִּי לְפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה צוּרִי וְגֹאֲלִי:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Master of the universe! I hearby forgive anyone who has angered me, or sinned against me, either physically or financially, against my honor or anything that is mine, whether accidentally or intentionally, inadvertently or deliberately, by speech or by deed, in this incarnation or in any other any Israelite [is forgiven], may no man be punished on my account. May it be Your will, Adonoy, my God and God of my fathers, that I shall sin no more nor repeat my sins, neither shall I again anger You nor do what is wrong in Your eyes. The sins I have committed, erase in your abounding mercies, but not through suffering or severe illnesses. May they be acceptable the words of my mouth and the thoughts of my heart, before You Adonoy, my Rock and my Redeemer.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','ree-boh-noh shehl oh-lahm hah-rey-nee moh-khehl le-khohl mee sheh-heekh-ees ve-heek-neet oh-tee oh sheh-khah-tah ke-nehg-dee beyn be-goo-fee beyn be-meh-moh-nee veyn beekh-voh-dee veyn ve-khahl ah-shehr lee veyn be-oh-nehs beyn be-rah-tsohn beyn be-shoh-gehg beyn be-meh-zeed veyn be-dee-boor beyn be-mah-ah-seh beyn be-geel-gool zeh beyn be-geel-gool ah-khehr le-khohl bahr yees-rah-ehl ve-loh yeh-ah-nehsh shoom ah-dahm ve-see-bah-tee ye-hee rah-tsohn mee-le-fah-ney-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hahy veh-loh-hey ah-voh-tahy sheh-loh ehkh-teh ohd ve-loh eh-kheh-zohr bah-hehm ve-loh ah-shoov ohd le-hahkh-ee-seh-khah ve-loh eh-eh-seh hah-rah be-ey-ney-khah oo-mahh sheh-khah-tah-tee me-khohk be-rah-khah-mey-khah hah-rah-beem ve-loh ahl ye-dey yee-soo-reem voh-khoh-leh-yeem rah-eem: yeeh-yoo le-rah-tsohn eem-rey fee ve-hehg-yohn lee-bee le-fah-ney-khah ah-doh-NAI tsoo-ree ve-goh-ah-lee:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם הַמַּפִּיל חֶבְלֵי שֵׁנָה עַל עֵינָי וּתְנוּמָה עַל עַפְעַפָּי: וּמֵאִיר לְאִישׁוֹן בַּת עָיִן. וִיהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהַי וֵאלֺהֵי אֲבוֹתַי שֶׁתַּשְׁכִּיבֵֽנִי לְשָׁלוֹם וְתַעֲמִידֵֽנִי לְחַיִים טוֹבִים וּלְשָׁלוֹם וְתֵן חֶלְקֵי בְּתוֹרָתֶךָ וְתַרְגִילֵנוּ לִדְבַר מִצְוָה וְאַל תַּרְגִילֵנוּ לִדְבַר עַבֵרָה וְאַל תְּבִיאֵֽנוּ לֹא לִידֵי חֵטְא וְלֹא לִידֵי נִסָּיוֹן וְלֹא לִידֵי בִזָּיוֹן וְיִשְׁלֹט בִּי יֵצֵר הַטוֹב וְאַל יִשְׁלֹט בִּי יֵֽצֶר הָרָע וְתַצִילֵנוּ מִשָׂטָן וּמִפֶגַע רָע וּמֵחָלָיִם רָעִים וְאַל יְבַהֲלֽוּנִי רַעְיוֹנַי וַחֲלוֹמוֹת רָעִים וְהַרְהוֹרִים רָעִים וּתְהֵא מִטָּתִי שְׁלֵמָה לְפָנֶֽיךָ: וְהָאֵר עֵינַי פֶּן אִישַׁן הַמָּֽוֶת. בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה הַמֵּאִיר לָעוֹלָם כֻּלּוֹ בִּכְבוֹדוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy, our God, King of the Universe, Who causes the fetters of sleep to fall upon my eyes, and slumber upon my eyelids. And illuminates the pupil of the eye. May it be Your will, Adonoy, my God and God of my fathers to make me lie down in peace, and to raise me (again) to good life and peace, and grant me my portion in Your Torah, make us accustomed to do Your commands, and let us not become accustomed to sin, Do not bring us into the grasp of sin, Do not cause us to be tested, or brought to disgrace. May I be ruled by the Good Inclination and let me not be ruled over by the Evil Inclination. Protect me from Satan, from an evil mishap and from illnesses. Let my thoughts not terrify me— nor evil dreams or evil fancies (disturb me), and may my bed be perfect before You. And light up my eyes lest I sleep the sleep of death, Blessed are You, Adonoy, Who illuminates the whole world with His glory.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','bah-rookh ah-tah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo meh-lehkh hah-oh-lahm hah-mah-peel khehv-ley sheh-nah ahl ey-nahy oo-te-noo-mah ahl ahf-ah-pahy: oo-meh-eer le-ee-shohn baht ah-yeen. vee-hee rah-tsohn mee-LE-fah-ney-khah ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hahy veh-loh-hey ah-voh-tahy sheh-tahsh-kee-veh-nee le-shah-lohm ve-tah-ah-mee-deh-nee le-khah-yeem toh-veem oo-le-shah-lohm ve-tehn khehl-key be-toh-rah-teh-khah ve-tahr-gee-leh-noo leed-vahr meets-vah ve-ahl tahr-gee-leh-noo leed-vahr ah-veh-rah ve-ahl te-vee-eh-noo loh lee-dey kheht ve-loh lee-dey nee-sah-yohn ve-loh lee-dey vee-zah-yohn ve-yeesh-loht bee yeh-tsehr hah-tohv ve-ahl yeesh-loht bee yeh-tsehr hah-rah ve-tah-tsee-leh-noo mee-sah-tahn oo-mee-feh-gah rah oo-meh-khah-lah-yeem rah-eem ve-ahl ye-vah-hah-loo-nee rah-yoh-nahy vah-khah-loh-moht rah-eem ve-hahr-hoh-reem rah-eem oo-te-heh mee-tah-tee she-leh-mah le-fah-ney-khah: ve-hah-ehr ey-nahy pehn ee-shahn hah-mah-veht. bah-rookh ah-tah ah-doh-NAI hah-meh-eer lah-oh-lahm koo-loh beekh-voh-doh:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','מי שאינו מדקדק לקרות ק"ש בבהכ"נ בזמנה צריך לקרות ק"ש על מטתו שתי פרשיות שמע והיה אם שמוע. אבל פ'' ויאמר שהוא משום הזכרת יצ"מ אין צריך לחזור ולקרות על מטתו כיון שכבר הזכיר בבהכ"נ. אבל מי שקורא ק"ש בזמנה אין צריך לקרות על מטתו רק פרשה ראשונה לבד. ורי"ו כתב על פי המדרש לומר כל שלש פרשיות על מטתו משום שהוא רמ"ח תיבות לשמור רמ"ח איבריו. (דה"ח ומ"א)','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','If one has prayed Ma''ariv and with it recited Sh''ma earlier than the ideal time for the evening Sh''ma, he should repeat all of it here. Some people have the custom of reciting all three paragraphs here every night.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','אֵל מֶֽלֶךְ נֶאֱמָן:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Almighty, faithful King','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','ehl meh-lehkh neh-eh-mahn:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ יְהֹוָה אֶחָד:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Hear, Israel Adonoy is our God Adonoy is One','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','she-mah yees-rah-ehl ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo ah-doh-NAI eh-khahd:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','יש להפסיק מעט בין אחד לברוך כי עיקר קבול עול מלכות שמים היא פסוק ראשון. ויאמר בלחש:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','The following three lines are to be said silently:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','בָּרוּךְ שֵׁם כְּבוֹד מַלְכוּתוֹ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Blessed [is His] Name, Whose glorious Kingdom is forever and ever.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','bah-rookh shehm ke-vohd mahl-khoo-toh le-oh-lahm vah-ehd:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וְאָהַבְתָּ אֵת יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ בְּכָל֯־לְ֯בָבְ֒ךָ וּבְכָל־נַפְשְׁךָ וּבְכָל־מְאֹדֶֽךָ: וְהָיוּ הַדְּ֒בָרִים הָאֵֽלֶּה אֲשֶׁר֯ אָ֯נֹכִי מְצַוְּ֒ךָ הַיּוֹם עַל֯־לְ֯בָבֶֽךָ: וְשִׁנַּנְתָּם לְבָנֶֽיךָ וְדִבַּרְתָּ בָּם בְּשִׁבְתְּ֒ךָ בְּבֵיתֶֽךָ וּבְ֒לֶכְתְּךָ בַדֶּֽרֶךְ וּבְ֒שָׁכְבְּךָ וּבְ֒קוּמֶֽךָ: וּקְ֒שַׁרְתָּם לְאוֹת עַל֯־יָ֯דֶֽךָ וְהָיוּ לְטֹטָפֹת בֵּין עֵינֶֽיךָ: וּכְ֒תַבְתָּם עַל־מְזֻזוֹת בֵּיתֶֽךָ וּבִשְׁ֒עָרֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','And you shall love Adonoy, your God with all your heart and with all your soul and with all your possessions. And these words which I command you today shall be upon your heart. And you shall teach them sharply to your children, and you shall discuss them when you sit in your house, and when you travel on the road, and when you lie down and when you rise. And you shall bind them for a sign upon your hand, and they shall be for totafos between your eyes. And you shall write them upon the doorposts of your house and upon your gateways.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','ve-ah-hahv-tah eht ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-khah be-khahl le-vah-VE-khah oo-ve-khohl nahf-she-khah oo-ve-khohl me-oh-deh-khah: ve-hah-yoo hah-DE-vah-reem hah-eh-leh ah-SHEHR ah-noh-KHEE me-tsah-VE-khah hah-yohm ahl le-vah-veh-KHAH: ve-shee-nahn-tahm le-vah-ney-khah ve-dee-bahr-tah bahm be-sheev-TE-khah be-vey-teh-khah oo-VE-lehkh-te-khah vah-deh-rehkh oo-VE-shah-khe-be-khah oo-VE-koo-meh-khah: oo-KE-shahr-tahm le-oht ahl yah-deh-KHAH ve-hah-yoo le-toh-tah-foht beyn ey-ney-khah: oo-KHE-tahv-tahm ahl me-zoo-zoht bey-teh-khah oo-VEESH-ah-rey-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וִיהִי נֹֽעַם אֲדֹנָי אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ עָלֵֽינוּ וּמַעֲשֵׂה יָדֵֽינוּ כּוֹנְנָה עָלֵֽינוּ וּמַעֲשֵׂה יָדֵֽינוּ כּוֹנְנֵֽהוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','May the pleasantness of my Master, our God, be upon us, and the work of our hands establish for us and the work of our hands may He establish.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','vee-hee noh-ahm ah-doh-nahy eh-loh-hey-noo ah-ley-noo oo-mah-ah-seh yah-dey-noo koh-ne-nah ah-ley-noo oo-mah-ah-seh yah-dey-noo koh-ne-neh-hoo:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','ישֵׁב בְּסֵֽתֶר עֶלְיוֹן בְּצֵל שַׁדַּי יִתְלוֹנָן: אֹמַר לַיהֹוָה מַחְסִי וּמְצוּדָתִי אֱלֹהַי אֶבְטַח־בּוֹ: כִּי הוּא יַצִּילְךָ מִפַּח יָקוּשׁ מִדֶּֽבֶר הַוָּוֹת: בְּאֶבְרָתוֹ יָֽסֶךְ לָךְ וְתַֽחַת־כְּנָפָיו תֶּחְסֶה צִנָּה וְסֹחֵרָה אֲמִתּוֹ: לֹא־תִירָא מִפַּֽחַד לָֽיְלָה מֵחֵץ יָעוּף יוֹמָם: מִדֶּֽבֶר בָּאֹֽפֶל יַהֲלֹךְ מִקֶּֽטֶב יָשׁוּד צָהֳרָֽיִם: יִפֹּל מִצִּדְּךָ אֶֽלֶף וּרְבָבָה מִימִינֶֽךָ אֵלֶֽיךָ לֹא יִגָּשׁ: רַק בְּעֵינֶֽיךָ תַבִּיט וְשִׁלֻּמַת רְשָׁעִים תִּרְאֶה: כִּי־אַתָּה יְהֹוָה מַחְסִי עֶלְיוֹן שַֽׂמְתָּ מְעוֹנֶֽךָ: לֹא־תְאֻנֶּה אֵלֶֽיךָ רָעָה וְנֶֽגַע לֹא־יִקְרַב בְּאָהֳלֶֽךָ: כִּי מַלְאָכָיו יְצַוֶּה־לָּךְ לִשְׁמָרְךָ בְּכָל־דְּרָכֶֽיךָ: עַל־כַּפַּֽיִם יִשָּׂאֽוּנְךָ פֶּן־תִּגֹּף בָּאֶֽבֶן רַגְלֶֽךָ: עַל־שַֽׁחַל וָפֶֽתֶן תִּדְרֹךְ תִּרְמֹס כְּפִיר וְתַנִּין: כִּי בִי חָשַׁק וַאֲפַלְּטֵֽהוּ אֲשַׂגְּבֵֽהוּ כִּי־יָדַע שְׁמִי: יִקְרָאֵֽנִי וְאֶעֱנֵֽהוּ עִמּוֹ־אָנֹכִי בְצָרָה אֲחַלְּצֵֽהוּ וַאֲכַבְּדֵֽהוּ: אֹֽרֶךְ יָמִים אַשְׂבִּיעֵֽהוּ וְאַרְאֵֽהוּ בִּישׁוּעָתִי: אֹֽרֶךְ יָמִים אַשְׂבִּיעֵֽהוּ וְאַרְאֵֽהוּ בִּישׁוּעָתִי:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','He who dwells in the shelter of the Supreme One, under the protection of Shadai He will abide. I say of Adonoy, [He is] my refuge and my stronghold, my God in Whom I trust. For He will save you from the snare-trap, from destructive pestilence. With His wings He will cover you and beneath His wings, you will find refuge; His truth is a shield, a full shield. You will not fear the terror of night, nor the arrow that flies by day, the pestilence that prowls in darkness, nor the deadly plague that ravages at noon. A thousand will fall at your [left] side, and ten thousand at your [right] side but it shall not come near you. Only with your eyes will you behold and see the punishment of the wicked. For you [have proclaimed]: Adonoy is my refuge, the Supreme One you have made your dwelling No evil shall befall you, and no plague shall come near your tent. For His angels He will command on your behalf— to guard you in all your ways. They will carry you upon their hands, lest you hurt your foot on a rock. You will tread upon lion and snake, you will trample young lion and serpent. Because he clings to Me with desire, I will save him; I will strengthen him, for he knows My Name. When he calls upon Me, I will answer him; I am with him in distress, I will free him and honor him. I will satiate him with longevity, and will let him see My deliverance. I will satiate him with longevity and will let him see My deliverance.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','y-shehv be-seh-tehr ehl-yohn be-tsehl shah-dahy yeet-loh-nahn: oh-mahr lah-ah-doh-NAI mahkh-see oo-me-tsoo-dah-tee eh-loh-hahy ehv-tahkh boh: kee hoo yah-tsee-le-khah mee-pahkh yah-koosh mee-deh-vehr hah-vah-voht: be-ehv-rah-toh yah-sehkh lahkh ve-tah-khaht ke-nah-fahv tehkh-seh tsee-nah ve-soh-kheh-rah ah-mee-toh: loh tee-rah mee-pah-khahd lah-ye-lah meh-khehts yah-oof yoh-mahm: mee-deh-vehr bah-oh-fehl yah-hah-lohkh mee-keh-tehv yah-shood tsoh-hoh-rah-yeem: yee-pohl mee-tsee-de-khah eh-lehf oo-re-vah-vah mee-mee-neh-khah eh-ley-khah loh yee-gahsh: rahk be-ey-ney-khah tah-beet ve-shee-loo-maht re-shah-eem teer-eh: kee ah-tah ah-doh-NAI mahkh-see ehl-yohn sah-me-tah me-oh-neh-khah: loh te-oo-neh eh-ley-khah rah-ah ve-neh-gah loh yeek-rahv be-oh-hoh-leh-khah: kee mahl-ah-khahv ye-tsah-veh lahkh leesh-mah-re-khah be-khohl de-rah-khey-khah: ahl kah-pah-yeem yee-sah-oo-ne-khah pehn tee-gohf bah-eh-vehn rahg-leh-khah: ahl shah-khahl vah-feh-tehn teed-rohkh teer-mohs ke-feer ve-tah-neen: kee vee khah-shahk vah-ah-fah-le-teh-hoo ah-sah-ge-veh-hoo kee yah-dah she-mee: yeek-rah-eh-nee ve-eh-eh-neh-hoo ee-moh ah-noh-khee ve-tsah-rah ah-khah-le-tseh-hoo vah-ah-khah-be-deh-hoo: oh-rehkh yah-meem ahs-bee-eh-hoo ve-ahr-eh-hoo bee-shoo-ah-tee: oh-rehkh yah-meem ahs-bee-eh-hoo ve-ahr-eh-hoo bee-shoo-ah-tee:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','יְהֹוָה מָה־רַבּוּ צָרָי רַבִּים קָמִים עָלָי: רַבִּים אֹמְ֒רִים לְנַפְשִׁי אֵין יְשׁוּעָֽתָה לוֹ בֵאלֺהִים סֶֽלָה: וְאַתָּה יְהֹוָה מָגֵן בַּעֲדִי כְּבוֹדִי וּמֵרִים רֹאשִׁי: קוֹלִי אֶל־יְהֹוָה אֶקְרָא וַיַּעֲנֵֽנִי מֵהַר קָדְשׁוֹ סֶֽלָה: אֲנִי שָׁכַֽבְתִּי וָאִישָֽׁנָה הֱקִיצֽוֹתִי כִּי יְהֹוָה יִסְמְ֒כֵֽנִי: לֺא אִירָא מֵרִבְבוֹת עָם אֲשֶׁר סָבִיב שָֽׁתוּ עָלָי: קוּמָה יְהֹוָה הוֹשִׁיעֵֽנִי אֱלֺהַי כִּי־הִכִּֽיתָ אֶת־כָּל אֹיְ֒בַי לֶֽחִי שִׁנֵּי רְשָׁעִים שִׁבַּֽרְתָּ: לַיהוָֹה הַיְ֒שׁוּעָה עַל־עַמְּ֒ךָ בִרְכָתֶֽךָ סֶֽלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','(Psalms 3:2-9) Adonoy, how many are my tormentors; many rise up against me. Many say of my soul: There is no deliverance for him through God, forever. But You, Adonoy, are a shield for me; my glory and Raiser of my head. With my voice, I call out to Adonoy, and He answers me from His holy mountain, forever. I lay down and slept; I awake for Adonoy supports me. I fear not the tens of thousands of people deployed against me from every side. Rise Adonoy, deliver me, my God, for You have struck all my enemies on the cheek; You have broken the teeth of the wicked. Deliverance is Adonoy''s; upon Your people is Your blessing, selah.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','ah-doh-NAI mah rah-boo tsah-rahy rah-beem kah-meem ah-lahy: rah-beem oh-ME-reem le-nahf-shee eyn ye-shoo-ah-tah loh veh-loh-heem seh-lah: ve-ah-tah ah-doh-NAI mah-gehn bah-ah-dee ke-voh-dee oo-meh-reem roh-shee: koh-lee ehl ah-doh-NAI ehk-rah vah-yah-ah-neh-nee meh-hahr kohd-shoh seh-lah: ah-nee shah-khah-ve-tee vah-ee-shah-nah heh-kee-tsoh-tee kee ah-doh-NAI yees-ME-kheh-nee: loh ee-rah meh-reev-voht ahm ah-shehr sah-veev shah-too ah-lahy: koo-mah ah-doh-NAI hoh-shee-eh-nee eh-loh-hahy kee hee-kee-tah eht kohl oh-YE-vahy leh-khee shee-ney re-shah-eem shee-bah-re-tah: lah-ah-doh-NAI hah-YE-shoo-ah ahl ah-ME-khah veer-khah-teh-khah seh-lah:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','הַשְׁכִּיבֵֽנוּ יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ לְשָׁלוֹם וְהַעֲמִידֵֽנוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ לְחַיִּים טוֹבִים וּלשָׁלוֹם. וּפְרוֹשׂ עָלֵֽינוּ סֻכַּת שְׁלוֹמֶֽךָ וְתַקְּ֒נֵֽנוּ בְּעֵצָה טוֹבָה מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ מְהֵרָה לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ. וְהָגֵן בַּעֲדֵֽנוּ וְהָסֵר מֵעָלֵֽינוּ אוֹיֵב דֶּֽבֶר וְחֶֽרֶב וְרָעָב וְיָגוֹן וְהָסֵר שָׂטָן מִלְּ֒פָנֵֽינוּ וּמֵאַחֲרֵֽינוּ וּבְצֵל כְּנָפֶֽיךָ תַּסְתִּירֵֽנוּ. כִּי אֵל שׁוֹמְ֒רֵֽנוּ וּמַצִּילֵֽנוּ אָֽתָּה כִּי אֵל מֶֽלֶךְ חַנּוּן וְרַחוּם אָֽתָּה. וּשְׁמוֹר צֵאתֵֽנוּ וּבוֹאֵֽנוּ לְחַיִּים וּלְשָׁלוֹם מֵעַתָּה וְעַד עוֹלָם:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Adonoy, our God, make us lie down in peace, our King, raise us [again] to good life and peace. Spread over us the shelter of Your peace, and direct us to better ourselves through Your good counsel; and deliver us speedily for Your Name''s sake. Shield us, and remove from us enemies, pestilence, sword, famine and sorrow. Remove the adversary from before us and from behind us, and in the shadow of Your wings shelter us. For You are the Almighty Who is our protector and rescuer. For You are the Almighty Who is King, Gracious, and Merciful. Guard our going out and our coming in for life and peace from now, forever.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','hahsh-kee-veh-noo ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo le-shah-lohm ve-hah-ah-mee-deh-noo mahl-keh-noo le-khah-yeem toh-veem oo-l-shah-lohm. oo-fe-rohs ah-ley-noo soo-kaht she-loh-meh-khah ve-tah-KE-neh-noo be-eh-tsah toh-vah mee-LE-fah-ney-khah ve-hoh-shee-eh-noo me-heh-rah le-mah-ahn she-meh-khah. ve-hah-gehn bah-ah-deh-noo ve-hah-sehr meh-ah-ley-noo oh-yehv deh-vehr ve-kheh-rehv ve-rah-ahv ve-yah-gohn ve-hah-sehr sah-tahn mee-LE-fah-ney-noo oo-meh-ah-khah-rey-noo oo-ve-tsehl ke-nah-fey-khah tahs-tee-reh-noo. kee ehl shoh-ME-reh-noo oo-mah-tsee-leh-noo ah-tah kee ehl meh-lehkh khah-noon ve-rah-khoom ah-tah. oo-she-mohr tseh-teh-noo oo-voh-eh-noo le-khah-yeem oo-le-shah-lohm meh-ah-tah ve-ahd oh-lahm:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','בָּרוּךְ יְהֹוָה בַּיּוֹם בָּרוּךְ יְהֹוָה בַּלָּֽיְלָה בָּרוּךְ יְהֹוָה בְּשָׁכְבֵֽנוּ בָּרוּךְ יְהֹוָה בְּקוּמֵֽנוּ. כִּי בְיָדְ֒ךָ נַפְשׁוֹת הַחַיִּים וְהַמֵּתִים אֲשֶׁר בְּיָדוֹ נֶֽפֶשׁ כָּל חָי וְרֽוּחַ כָּל בְּשַׂר אִישׁ. בְּיָדְ֒ךָ אַפְקִיד רוּחִי פָּדִֽיתָה אוֹתִי יְהֹוָה אֵל אֱמֶת. אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ שֶׁבַּשָּׁמַֽיִם יַחֵד שִׁמְךָ וְקַיֵּם מַלְכוּתְ֒ךָ תָּמִיד וּמְלֺךְ עָלֵֽינוּ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Blessed is Adonoy by day, Blessed is Adonoy by night. Blessed is Adonoy when we lie down Blessed is Adonoy when we rise. For in Your hand are the souls of the living and the dead, (as it is written): For in His hand is the soul of every living thing and the spirit of every human being. In Your hand, I commit my spirit; You have liberated me, Adonoy, Almighty of truth. Our God in heaven, reveal the unity of Your Name, preserve Your kingdom always, and reign over us forever and ever.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','bah-rookh ah-doh-NAI bah-yohm bah-rookh ah-doh-NAI bah-lah-ye-lah bah-rookh ah-doh-NAI be-shah-khe-veh-noo bah-rookh ah-doh-NAI be-koo-meh-noo. kee ve-yah-DE-khah nahf-shoht hah-khah-yeem ve-hah-meh-teem ah-shehr be-yah-doh neh-fehsh kohl khahy ve-roo-ahkh kohl be-sahr eesh. be-yah-DE-khah ahf-keed roo-khee pah-dee-tah oh-tee ah-doh-NAI ehl eh-meht. eh-loh-hey-noo sheh-bah-shah-mah-yeem yah-khehd sheem-khah ve-kah-yehm mahl-khoo-TE-khah tah-meed oo-me-lohkh ah-ley-noo le-oh-lahm vah-ehd:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','יִרְאוּ עֵינֵֽינוּ וְיִשְׂמַח לִבֵּֽנוּ וְתָגֵל נַפְשֵֽׁנוּ בִּישׁוּעָתְ֒ךָ בֶּאֱמֶת בֶּאֱמוֹר לְצִיּוֹן מָלַךְ אֱלֺהָֽיִךְ. יְהֹוָה מֶֽלֶךְ יְהֹוָה מָלָךְ יְהֹוָה יִמְלֹךְ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד: כִּי הַמַּלְכוּת שֶׁלְּ֒ךָ הִיא וּלְעֽוֹלְ֒מֵי עַד תִּמְלוֹךְ בְּכָבוֹד כִּי אֵין לָֽנוּ מֶֽלֶךְ אֶלָּא אָֽתָּה:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','May our eyes behold, may our heart rejoice and our soul exalt in Your true deliverance, when it will be said to Zion: Your God has begun His reign Adonoy is King, Adonoy was King, Adonoy will reign forever and ever For the Kingdom is Yours and to all eternity, You will reign in glory, for we have no king except You.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','yeer-oo ey-ney-noo ve-yees-mahkh lee-beh-noo ve-tah-gehl nahf-sheh-noo bee-shoo-ah-TE-khah beh-eh-meht beh-eh-mohr le-tsee-yohn mah-lahkh eh-loh-hah-yeekh. ah-doh-NAI meh-lehkh ah-doh-NAI mah-lahkh ah-doh-NAI yeem-lohkh le-oh-lahm vah-ehd: kee hah-mahl-khoot sheh-LE-khah hee oo-le-oh-LE-mey ahd teem-lohkh be-khah-vohd kee eyn lah-noo meh-lehkh eh-lah ah-tah:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','הַמַּלְאָךְ הַגֹּאֵל אֹתִי מִכָּל רָע יְבָרֵךְ אֶת הַנְּ֒עָרִים וְיִקָּרֵא בָהֶם שְׁמִי וְשֵׁם אֲבוֹתַי אַבְרָהָם וְיִצְחָק וְיִדְגּוּ לָרֹב בְּקֶֽרֶב הָאָֽרֶץ:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','The angel who redeemed me from all evil May he bless the lads; and may they be called by my name and the names of my fathers, Abraham and Isaac; and may they multiply like fish within the land.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','hah-mahl-ahkh hah-goh-ehl oh-tee mee-kohl rah ye-vah-rehkh eht hah-NE-ah-reem ve-yee-kah-reh vah-hehm she-mee ve-shehm ah-voh-tahy ahv-rah-hahm ve-yeets-khahk ve-yeed-goo lah-rohv be-keh-rehv hah-ah-rehts:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וַיֹּֽאמֶר אִם שָׁמֽוֹעַ תִּשְׁמַע לְקוֹל יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֶֽיךָ וְהַיָּשָׁר בְּעֵינָיו תַּעֲשֶׂה וְהַאֲזַנְתָּ לְמִצְוֹתָיו וְשָׁמַרְתָּ כָּל חֻקָּיו כָּל הַמַּחֲלָה אֲשֶׁר שַֽׂמְתִּי בְמִצְרַֽיִם לֺא אָשִׂים עָלֶֽיךָ כִּי אֲנִי יְהֹוָה רֹפְ֒אֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','And He said, "If you will diligently heed the voice of Adonoy, your God, and do what is upright in His eyes, and listen carefully to His commandments, and guard all His statutes— [then] every sickness that I put in Egypt, I will not put upon you, for I am Adonoy, your Healer.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','vah-yoh-mehr eem shah-moh-ah teesh-mah le-kohl ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-khah ve-hah-yah-shahr be-ey-nahv tah-ah-seh ve-hah-ah-zahn-tah le-meets-voh-tahv ve-shah-mahr-tah kohl khoo-kahv kohl hah-mah-khah-lah ah-shehr sah-me-tee ve-meets-rah-yeem loh ah-seem ah-ley-khah kee ah-nee ah-doh-NAI roh-FE-eh-khah:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וַיֹּֽאמֶר יְהֹוָה אֶל הַשָּׂטָן יִגְעַר יְהֹוָה בְּךָ הַשָּׂטָן וְיִגְעַר יְהֹוָה בְּךָ הַבֹּחֵר בִּירוּשָׁלָֽםִ הֲלֺא זֶה אוּד מֻצָּל מֵאֵשׁ','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','And Adonoy said to Satan: Adonoy rebukes you, Satan, Adonoy rebukes you, He Who chose Jerusalem; for is this one not a firebrand plucked out of the fire?','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:16:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','vah-yoh-mehr ah-doh-NAI ehl hah-sah-tahn yeeg-ahr ah-doh-NAI be-khah hah-sah-tahn ve-yeeg-ahr ah-doh-NAI be-khah hah-boh-khehr bee-roo-shah-lah-mee hah-loh zeh ood moo-tsahl meh-ehsh','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','הִנֵּה מִטָּתוֹ שֶׁלִּשְׁלֺמֹה שִׁשִּׁים גִּבֹּרִים סָבִיב לָהּ מִגִּבֹּרֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל כֻּלָּם אֲחֻֽזֵי חֶֽרֶב מְלֻמְּ֒דֵי מִלְחָמָה אִישׁ חַרְבּוֹ עַל יְרֵכוֹ מִפַּֽחַד בַּלֵּילוֹת','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Behold the bed of Solomon! Sixty mighty men [are set] around it, of the mighty men of Israel. All of them armed with swords, trained in warfare; each man has his sword at his side, because of the dread of the night.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:17:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','hee-neh mee-tah-toh sheh-leesh-loh-mohh shee-sheem gee-boh-reem sah-veev lahh mee-gee-boh-rey yees-rah-ehl koo-lahm ah-khoo-zey kheh-rehv me-loo-ME-dey meel-khah-mah eesh khahr-boh ahl ye-reh-khoh mee-pah-khahd bah-ley-loht','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','יאמר כל פסוק ג"פ:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Each unit is said three times:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','יְבָרֶכְךָ יְהֹוָה וְיִשְׁמְרֶֽךָ יָאֵר יְהֹוָה פָּנָיו אֵלֶֽיךָ וִיחֻנֶּֽךָּ: יִשָּׂא יְהֹוָה פָּנָיו אֵלֶֽיךָ וְיָשֵׂם לְךָ שָׁלוֹם:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Adonoy bless you and guard you! Adonoy shine His countenance upon you and be gracious unto You! Adonoy turn His countenance toward you and grant you peace!','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','ye-vah-rehkh-khah ah-doh-NAI ve-yeesh-me-reh-khah yah-ehr ah-doh-NAI pah-nahv eh-ley-khah vee-khoo-neh-kah: yee-sah ah-doh-NAI pah-nahv eh-ley-khah ve-yah-sehm le-khah shah-lohm:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','הִנֵּה לֺא יָנוּם וְלֺא יִישָׁן שׁוֹמֵר יִשְׂרָאֵל:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Behold, He neither slumbers nor sleeps! the Guardian of Israel.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:20:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','hee-neh loh yah-noom ve-loh yee-shahn shoh-mehr yees-rah-ehl:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','לִישׁוּעָתְ֒ךָ קִוִּיתִי יְהֹוָה קִוִּיתִי יְהֹוָה לִישׁוּעָתְ֒ךָ יְהֹוָה לִישׁוּעָתְ֒ךָ קִוִּיתִי','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','For your deliverance, I hope, Adonoy; I hope, Adonoy, for Your deliverance; Adonoy, for Your deliverance I hope.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:21:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','lee-shoo-ah-TE-khah kee-vee-tee ah-doh-NAI kee-vee-tee ah-doh-NAI lee-shoo-ah-TE-khah ah-doh-NAI lee-shoo-ah-TE-khah kee-vee-tee','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','בְּשֵׁם יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל מִימִינִי מִיכָאֵל וּמִשְּׂ֒מֹאלִי גַבְרִיאֵל וּמִלְּ֒פָנַי אוֹרִיאֵל וּמֵאֲחוֹרַי רְפָאֵל וְעַל רֹאשִי שְׁכִינַת אֵל:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','In the Name of Adonoy, God of Israel: at my right [hand] Michael, at my left [hand] Gabriel, before me Uriel, behind me Raphael, and above my head, the Presence of Almighty.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:22:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','be-shehm ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey yees-rah-ehl mee-mee-nee mee-khah-ehl oo-mee-SE-moh-lee gahv-ree-ehl oo-mee-LE-fah-nahy oh-ree-ehl oo-meh-ah-khoh-rahy re-fah-ehl ve-ahl roh-shee she-khee-naht ehl:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','שִׁיר הַמַּעֲלוֹת אַשְׁרֵי כָּל־יְרֵא יְהֹוָה הַהֹלֵךְ בִּדְרָכָיו: יְגִֽיעַ כַּפֶּֽיךָ כִּי תֹאכֵל אַשְׁרֶֽיךָ וְטוֹב לָךְ: אֶשְׁתְּ֒ךָ כְּגֶֽפֶן פֹּרִיָּה בְּיַרְכְּ֒תֵי בֵיתֶֽךָ בָּנֶֽיךָ כִּשְׁתִלֵי זֵיתִים סָבִיב לְשֻׁלְחָנֶֽךָ: הִנֵּה כִי־כֵן יְבֹֽרַךְ גָּֽבֶר יְרֵא יְהֹוָה: יְבָרֶכְךָ יְהֹוָה מִצִּיּוֹן וּרְאֵה בְּטוּב יְרוּשָׁלָֽםִ כֹּל יְמֵי חַיֶּֽיךָ: וּרְאֵה־ בָנִים לְבָנֶֽיךָ שָׁלוֹם עַל־יִשְׂרָאֵל:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','A song of ascents Fortunate are all who fear Adonoy, who walk in His ways. When you eat of the toil of your hands you are fortunate and it is good with you. Your wife will be like a fruitful vine in the innermost parts of your house; your children like olive plants around your table. Behold! thus shall be blessed the man who fears Adonoy. Adonoy bless you from Zion! and [may you] see the good of Jerusalem all the days of your life! May you [live to] see your children''s children! Peace upon Israel!','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:23:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','sheer hah-mah-ah-loht ahsh-rey kohl ye-reh ah-doh-NAI hah-hoh-lehkh beed-rah-khahv: ye-gee-ah kah-pey-khah kee toh-khehl ahsh-rey-khah ve-tohv lahkh: ehsh-TE-khah ke-geh-fehn poh-ree-yah be-yahr-KE-tey vey-teh-khah bah-ney-khah keesh-tee-ley zey-teem sah-veev le-shool-khah-neh-khah: hee-neh khee khehn ye-voh-rahkh gah-vehr ye-reh ah-doh-NAI: ye-vah-rehkh-khah ah-doh-NAI mee-tsee-yohn oo-re-eh be-toov ye-roo-shah-lah-mee kohl ye-mey khah-yey-khah: oo-re-eh vah-neem le-vah-ney-khah shah-lohm ahl yees-rah-ehl:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','יאמר כל פסוק ג"פ:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','To be said three times:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:25:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','רִגְזוּ וְאַל תֶּחֱטָֽאוּ אִמְרוּ בִלְבַבְכֶם עַל מִשְׁכַּבְכֶם וְדֹֽמּוּ סֶֽלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:25:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Tremble and do not sin; commune with your hearts upon your bed, and be silent, selah!','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:25:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','reeg-zoo ve-ahl teh-kheh-tah-oo eem-roo veel-vahv-khehm ahl meesh-kahv-khehm ve-doh-moo seh-lah:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:26:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','אֲדוֹן עוֹלָם אֲשֶׁר מָלַךְ, בְּטֶֽרֶם כָּל יְצִיר נִבְרָא:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:26:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Master of the Universe Who reigned before any creature was created.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:26:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','ah-dohn oh-lahm ah-shehr mah-lahkh, be-teh-rehm kohl ye-tseer neev-rah:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:27:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','לְעֵת נַעֲשָׂה בְחֶפְצוֹ כֹּל, אֲזַי מֶֽלֶךְ שְׁמוֹ נִקְרָא:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:27:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','At the time when all was made by His will, then was His Name proclaimed King.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:27:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','le-eht nah-ah-sah ve-khehf-tsoh kohl, ah-zahy meh-lehkh she-moh neek-rah:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:28:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וְאַחֲרֵי כִּכְ֒לוֹת הַכֹּל, לְבַדּוֹ יִמְלֹךְ נוֹרָא:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:28:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','And after all things shall cease to be the Awesome One will reign alone.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:28:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','ve-ah-khah-rey KEEKH-loht hah-kohl, le-vah-doh yeem-lohkh noh-rah:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:29:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וְהוּא הָיָה וְהוּא הֹוֶה, וְהוּא יִהְיֶה בְּתִפְאָרָה:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:29:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','He was, He is, and He shall be in glory.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:29:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','ve-hoo hah-yah ve-hoo hoh-veh, ve-hoo yeeh-yeh be-teef-ah-rah:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:30:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וְהוּא אֶחָד וְאֵין שֵׁנִי, לְהַמְשִׁיל לוֹ לְהַחְבִּֽירָה:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:30:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','He is One, and there is no second to compare to Him, to associate [with Him].','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:30:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','ve-hoo eh-khahd ve-eyn sheh-nee, le-hah-me-sheel loh le-hahkh-bee-rah:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:31:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','בְּלִי רֵאשִׁית בְּלִי תַכְלִית, וְלוֹ הָעֹז וְהַמִּשְׂרָה:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:31:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Without beginning, without end, power and dominion are His.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:31:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','be-lee reh-sheet be-lee tahkh-leet, ve-loh hah-ohz ve-hah-mees-rah:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:32:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וְהוּא אֵלִי וְחַי גּוֹאֲלִי, וְצוּר חֶבְלִי בְּעֵת צָרָה:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:32:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','He is my God and my ever-living Redeemer, the Rock of my destiny in times of distress.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:32:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','ve-hoo eh-lee ve-khahy goh-ah-lee, ve-tsoor khehv-lee be-eht tsah-rah:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:33:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וְהוּא נִסִּי וּמָנוֹס לִי, מְנָת כּוֹסִי בְּיוֹם אֶקְרָא:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:33:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','He is my flag and my refuge; He is the portion of my cup on the day I call.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:33:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','ve-hoo nee-see oo-mah-nohs lee, me-naht koh-see be-yohm ehk-rah:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:34:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','בְּיָדוֹ אַפְקִיד רוּחִי, בְּעֵת אִישַׁן וְאָעִֽירָה:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:34:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Into His hand I entrust my spirit [both] when I sleep and when I awaken.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:34:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','be-yah-doh ahf-keed roo-khee, be-eht ee-shahn ve-ah-ee-rah:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:35:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וְעִם רוּחִי גְּוִיָּתִי, יְהֹוָה לִי וְלֹא אִירָא:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:35:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','And with my spirit my body [too], Adonoy is with me, I shall not fear.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:35:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','ve-eem roo-khee ge-vee-yah-tee, ah-doh-NAI lee ve-loh ee-rah:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','אֵשֶׁת חַיִל מִי יִמְצָא וְרָחֹק מִפְּנִינִים מִכְרָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Whoever finds a valorous wife— far greater than that of pearls is her value.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','eh-sheht khah-yeel mee yeem-tsah ve-rah-khohk mee-pe-nee-neem meekh-rahh:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','בָּטַח בָּהּ לֵב בַּעְלָהּ וְשָׁלָל לֹא יֶחְסָר:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','The heart of her husband trusts in her, and he lacks no gain.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','bah-tahkh bahh lehv bah-lahh ve-shah-lahl loh yehkh-sahr:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','גְּמָלַתְהוּ טוֹב וְלֹא רָע כָּל יְמֵי חַיֶּיה:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She repays him good and not evil all the days of her life.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','ge-mah-laht-hoo tohv ve-loh rah kohl ye-mey khah-yeyh:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','דָּרְשָׁה צֶמֶר וּפִשְׁתִּים וַתַּעַשׂ בְּחֵפֶץ כַּפֶּיהָ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She seeks wool and linen, and works them willingly with her hands.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','dah-re-shah tseh-mehr oo-feesh-teem vah-tah-ahs be-kheh-fehts kah-pey-hah:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','הָיְתָה כָּאֳנִיּוֹת סוֹחֵר מִמֶּרְחָק תָּבִיא לַחְמָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She is like the merchant ships; from afar, she brings her food.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','hah-ye-tah koh-oh-nee-yoht soh-khehr mee-mehr-khahk tah-vee lahkh-mahh:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','וַתָּקָם בְּעוֹד לַיְלָה וַתִּתֵּן טֶרֶף לְבֵיתָהּ וְחֹק לְנַעֲרֹתֶיהָ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She rises while it is still night and gives food to her household, and tasks to her maids.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','vah-tah-kohm be-ohd lahy-lah vah-tee-tehn teh-rehf le-vey-tahh ve-khohk le-nah-ah-roh-tey-hah:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','זָמְמָה שָׂדֶה וַתִּקָּחֵהוּ מִפְּרִי כַפֶּיהָ נָטְעָה כָּרֶם:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She considers a field and buys it; from the fruit of her hand, she plants a vineyard.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','zah-me-mah sah-deh vah-tee-kah-kheh-hoo mee-pe-ree khah-pey-hah nah-te-ah kah-rehm:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','חָגְרָה בְעוֹז מָתְנֶיהָ וַתְּאַמֵּץ זְרֹעוֹתֶיהָ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She girds herself with might and strengthens her arms.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','khah-ge-rah ve-ohz moht-ney-hah vah-te-ah-mehts ze-roh-oh-tey-hah:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','טָעֲמָה כִּי טוֹב סַחְרָהּ לֹא יִכְבֶּה בַלַּיְלָה נֵרָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She senses that her business is good, [so] her lamp is not extinguished at night.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','tah-ah-mah kee tohv sahkh-rahh loh yeekh-beh vah-lahy-lah neh-rahh:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','יָדֶיהָ שִׁלְּחָה בַכִּישׁוֹר וְכַפֶּיהָ תָּמְכוּ פָלֶךְ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She puts her hand to the spindle, and her palms support the distaff.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','yah-dey-hah shee-le-khah vah-kee-shohr ve-khah-pey-hah tah-me-khoo fah-lehkh:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','כַּפָּהּ פָּרְשָׂה לֶעָנִי וְיָדֶיהָ שִׁלְּחָה לָאֶבְיוֹן:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Her palm she spreads out to the poor and her hands she extends to the needy.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','kah-pahh pah-re-sah leh-ah-nee ve-yah-dey-hah shee-le-khah lah-ehv-yohn:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','לֹא תִירָא לְבֵיתָהּ מִשָּׁלֶג כִּי כָל בֵּיתָהּ לָבֻשׁ שָׁנִים:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She has no fear for her household because of snow, for her entire household is clothed with scarlet [wool].','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','loh tee-rah le-vey-tahh mee-shah-lehg kee khohl bey-tahh lah-voosh shah-neem:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','מַרְבַדִּים עָשְׂתָה לָּהּ שֵׁשׁ וְאַרְגָּמָן לְבוּשָׁהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Bedspreads, she makes herself fine linen and purple [wool] are her clothing.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','mahr-vah-deem ah-se-tah lahh shehsh ve-ahr-gah-mahn le-voo-shahh:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','נוֹדָע בַּשְּׁעָרִים בַּעְלָהּ בְּשִׁבְתּוֹ עִם זִקְנֵי אָרֶץ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Well-known at the gates is her husband as he sits among the elders of the land.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','noh-dah bah-she-ah-reem bah-lahh be-sheev-toh eem zeek-ney ah-rehts:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','סָדִין עָשְׂתָה וַתִּמְכֹּר וַחֲגוֹר נָתְנָה לַכְּנַעֲנִי:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Garments she makes and sells them, and belts, she provides for the merchants.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','sah-deen ah-se-tah vah-teem-kohr vah-khah-gohr nah-te-nah lah-ke-nah-ah-nee:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','עֹז וְהָדָר לְבוּשָׁהּ וַתִּשְׂחַק לְיוֹם אַחֲרוֹן:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Strength and splendor are her clothing, and smilingly [she awaits her] last day.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','ohz ve-hah-dahr le-voo-shahh vah-tees-khahk le-yohm ah-khah-rohn:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','פִּיהָ פָּתְחָה בְחָכְמָה וְתוֹרַת חֶסֶד עַל לְשׁוֹנָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Her mouth she opens with wisdom, and the teaching of kindness is on her tongue.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:16:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','pee-hah pah-te-khah ve-khohkh-mah ve-toh-raht kheh-sehd ahl le-shoh-nahh:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','צוֹפִיָּה הֲלִיכוֹת בֵּיתָהּ וְלֶחֶם עַצְלוּת לֹא תֹאכֵל:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She anticipates the ways of her household, and the bread of idleness, she does not eat.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:17:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','tsoh-fee-yah hah-lee-khoht bey-tahh ve-leh-khehm ahts-loot loh toh-khehl:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','קָמוּ בָנֶיהָ וַיְאַשְּׁרוּהָ בַּעְלָהּ וַיְהַלְלָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Her children rise16 and make her fortunate; her husband—and he praises her:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:18:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','kah-moo vah-ney-hah vah-ye-ah-she-roo-hah bah-lahh vah-ye-hah-le-lahh:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','רַבּוֹת בָּנוֹת עָשׂוּ חָיִל וְאַתְּ עָלִית עַל כֻּלָּנָה:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Many daughters have attained valor but you surpassed them all.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','rah-boht bah-noht ah-soo khah-yeel ve-aht ah-leet ahl koo-lah-nah:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','שֶׁקֶר הַחֵן וְהֶבֶל הַיֹּפִי אִשָּׁה יִרְאַת יְהֹוָה הִיא תִתְהַלָּל:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Favor is deceptive and beauty is vain; a God-fearing woman— —she should be praised.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:20:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','sheh-kehr hah-khehn ve-heh-vehl hah-yoh-fee ee-shah yeer-aht ah-doh-NAI hee teet-hah-lahl:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','תְּנוּ לָהּ מִפְּרִי יָדֶיהָ וִיהַלְלוּהָ בַשְּׁעָרִים מַעֲשֶׂיהָ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Give her the fruit of her hand, and let her deeds praise her in the gates.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:21:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','te-noo lahh mee-pe-ree yah-dey-hah vee-hah-le-loo-hah vah-she-ah-reem mah-ah-sey-hah:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva','he','אם קראו לספר תורה נער שנעשה בר מצוה אחר שבירך ברכה אחרונה. יאמר אביו:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Bar Mitzva'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva','en','The following blessing is said by the father of a Bar Mitzvah, after the lad has been called to the Torah and has recited the blessing following the reading:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Bar Mitzva'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva','he','בָּרוּךְ שֶׁפְּטָרַנִי מֵעָנְשׁוֹ שֶׁלָזֶה:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Bar Mitzva'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy our God, King of the Universe, Who has released me from the punishment of this [boy].','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Bar Mitzva'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva','transliteration','bah-rookh sheh-pe-tah-rah-nee meh-ah-ne-shoh sheh-lah-zeh:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Bar Mitzva'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah','he','מגביהין את הספר ואומרים:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Hagbahah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah','en','When the reading of the Torah is concluded, the Half Kaddish is recited by the Reader. The Maftir is read and then the Torah is raised so that the congregation can see the script, and the congregation exclaims:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Hagbahah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah','he','וְזֹאת הַתּוֹרָה אֲשֶׁר שָׂם מֹשֶׁה לִפְנֵי בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל: עַל פִּי יְהֹוָה בְּיַד מֹשֶׁה: תּוֹרָה צִוָה לָנוּ מֹשֶׁה מוֹרָשָׁה קְהִלַּת יַעֲקֹב: עֵץ חַיִּים הִיא לַמַּחֲזִיקִים בָּהּ וְתוֹמְכֶיהָ מְאֻשָּׁר: דְּרָכֶיהָ דַרְכֵי נֹעַם וְכָל נְתִיבוֹתֶיהָ שָׁלוֹם: אֹרֶךְ יָמִים בִּימִינָה, בִּשְׂמֹאלָה עֹשֶׁר וְכָבוֹד: יְהֹוָה חָפֵץ לְמַעַן צִדְקוֹ, יַגְדִּיל תּוֹרָה וְיַאְדִּיר:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Hagbahah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah','en','This is the Torah which Moses placed before the children of Israel. at Adonoy''s command by the hand of Moses. It is a tree of life to those who grasp to it, and those who support it are fortunate. Its ways are ways of pleasantness, and all its paths are peace. Long life is at its right, at its left, riches and honor. Adonoy desired, for the sake of His righteousness, to make the Torah great and to glorify it.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Hagbahah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah','transliteration','ve-zoht hah-toh-rah ah-shehr sahm moh-sheh leef-ney be-ney yees-rah-ehl: ahl pee ah-doh-NAI be-yahd moh-sheh: toh-rah tsee-vah lah-noo moh-sheh moh-rah-shah ke-hee-laht yah-ah-kohv: ehts khah-yeem hee lah-mah-khah-zee-keem bahh ve-toh-me-khey-hah me-oo-shahr: de-rah-khey-hah dahr-khey noh-ahm ve-khohl ne-tee-voh-tey-hah shah-lohm: oh-rehkh yah-meem bee-mee-nah, bees-moh-lah oh-shehr ve-khah-vohd: ah-doh-NAI khah-fehts le-mah-ahn tseed-koh, yahg-deel toh-rah ve-yah-deer:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Hagbahah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','he','נהגו להזכיר נשמות המת אחר קריאת התורה בכל שבת שאומרים אב הרחמים:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','en','Yizkor may be recited following the Torah reading.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','he','לזכר:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','en','In memory of a father:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','he','אֵל מָלֵא רַחֲמִים שׁוֹכֵן בַּמְּרוֹמִים הַמְצֵא מְנוּחָה נְכוֹנָה עַל כַּנְפֵי הַשְּׁכִינָה בְּמַעֲלוֹת קְדוֹשִׁים וּטְהוֹרִים כְּזֹהַר הָרָקִיעַ מַזְהִירִים אֶת נִשְׁמַת (פב"פ) שֶׁהָלַךְ לְעוֹלָמוֹ בַּעֲבוּר (שפלוני) נָדַב לִצְדָקָה בְּעַד הַזְכָּרַת נִשְׁמָתוֹ, לָכֵן בַּעַל הָרַחֲמִים יַסְתִּירֵהוּ בְּסֵתֶר כְּנָפָיו לְעוֹלָמִים וְיִצְרֹר בִּצְרוֹר הַחַיִּים אֶת נִשְׁמָתוֹ יְהֹוָה הוּא נַחֲלָתוֹ וְיָנוּחַ בְּשָּׁלוֹם עַל מִשְׁכָּבוֹ וְנֹאמַר אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','en','May God remember the soul of my father, my teacher, (Mention his Hebrew name and that of his father) son of who has gone to his world, because I pledge [without vowing] to donate charity for his sake In this merit, may his soul be bound up in the bond of life, with the souls of Avraham, Yitzchak, and Yaakov, Sarah, Rivkah, Rachel, and Leah, and with the other righteous men and women who are in the Gan Eden (Paradise) and let us say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','transliteration','ehl mah-leh rah-khah-meem shoh-khehn bah-me-roh-meem hah-me-tseh me-noo-khah ne-khoh-nah ahl kahn-fey hah-she-khee-nah be-mah-ah-loht ke-doh-sheem oo-te-hoh-reem ke-zoh-hahr hah-rah-kee-ah mahz-hee-reem eht neesh-maht (fvf") sheh-hah-lahkh le-oh-lah-moh bah-ah-voor (shflvny) nah-dahv leets-dah-kah be-ahd hahz-kah-raht neesh-mah-toh, lah-khehn bah-ahl hah-rah-khah-meem yahs-tee-reh-hoo be-seh-tehr ke-nah-fahv le-oh-lah-meem ve-yeets-rohr beets-rohr hah-khah-yeem eht neesh-mah-toh ah-doh-NAI hoo nah-khah-lah-toh ve-yah-noo-ahkh be-shah-lohm ahl meesh-kah-voh ve-noh-mahr ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','he','לנקבה:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','en','In memory of a mother:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','he','אֵל מָלֵא רַחֲמִים שׁוֹכֵן בַּמְּרוֹמִים הַמְצֵא מְנוּחָה נְכוֹנָה עַל כַּנְפֵי הַשְּׁכִינָה בְּמַעֲלוֹת קְדוֹשִׁים וּטְהוֹרִים כְּזֹהַר הָרָקִיעַ מַזְהִירִים אֶת נִשְׁמַת (פב"פ) שֶׁהָלְכָה לְעוֹלָמָהּ בַּעֲבוּר (שפלוני) נָדַב לִצְדָקָה בְּעַד הַזְכָּרַת נִשְׁמָתָהּ, לָכֵן בַּעַל הָרַחֲמִים יַסְתִּירָהּ בְּסֵתֶר כְּנָפָיו לְעוֹלָמִים וְיִצְרֹר בִּצְרוֹר הַחַיִּים אֶת נִשְׁמָתָהּ יְהֹוָה הוּא נַחֲלָתָהּ וְתָנוּחַ בְּשָּׁלוֹם עַל מִשְׁכָּבָהּ וְנֹאמַר אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','en','May God remember the soul of my mother, my teacher, (Mention her Hebrew name and that of her father) daughter of who has gone to her world. because I pledge [without vowing] to donate charity for her sake. In this merit, may her soul be bound up in the bond of life, with the souls of Avraham, Yitzchak, and Yaakov, Sarah, Rivkah, Rachel, and Leah, and with the other righteous men and women who are in Gan Eden (Paradise) and let us say, Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','transliteration','ehl mah-leh rah-khah-meem shoh-khehn bah-me-roh-meem hah-me-tseh me-noo-khah ne-khoh-nah ahl kahn-fey hah-she-khee-nah be-mah-ah-loht ke-doh-sheem oo-te-hoh-reem ke-zoh-hahr hah-rah-kee-ah mahz-hee-reem eht neesh-maht (fvf") sheh-hah-le-khah le-oh-lah-mahh bah-ah-voor (shflvny) nah-dahv leets-dah-kah be-ahd hahz-kah-raht neesh-mah-tahh, lah-khehn bah-ahl hah-rah-khah-meem yahs-tee-rahh be-seh-tehr ke-nah-fahv le-oh-lah-meem ve-yeets-rohr beets-rohr hah-khah-yeem eht neesh-mah-tahh ah-doh-NAI hoo nah-khah-lah-tahh ve-tah-noo-ahkh be-shah-lohm ahl meesh-kah-vahh ve-noh-mahr ah-mehn:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','הושענות ליו"ט ראשון ולחוה"מ','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Hoshanot for the First Day Holiday and the Intermediate Days','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','הוֹשַׁע נָא','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Please save!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','hoh-shah nah','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','לְמַעַנְךָ אֱלֹהֵינוּ הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','For Your sake, our God, please save;','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','le-mah-ahn-khah eh-loh-hey-noo hoh-shah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','לְמַעַנְךָ בּוֹרְאֵנוּ הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','for Your sake, our Creator, please save;','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','le-mah-ahn-khah boh-re-eh-noo hoh-shah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','לְמַעַנְךָ גּוֹאֲלֵנוּ הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','for Your sake, our Redeemer, please save;','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','le-mah-ahn-khah goh-ah-leh-noo hoh-shah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','לְמַעַנְךָ דּוֹרְשֵׁנוּ הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','for Your sake, our Seeker, please save!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','le-mah-ahn-khah doh-re-sheh-noo hoh-shah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','ליו"ט ראשון למעט כשחל בשבת שאז אומרים זה ביום א'', א'' דחוה"מ:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','For the first day holiday, except when it falls out on Shabbat. In that case, we say this on Sunday, the first day of the intermediate days of the festival:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','לְמַעַן אֲמִתָּךְ. לְמַעַן בְרִיתָךְ. לְמַעַן גָּדְלָךְ וְתִפְאַרְתָּךְ. לְמַעַן דָּתָךְ. לְמַעַן הוֹדָךְ. לְמַעַן וִעוּדָךְ. לְמַעַן זִכְרָךְ. לְמַעַן חַסְדָּךְ. לְמַעַן טוּבָךְ. לְמַעַן יִחוּדָךְ. לְמַעַן כְּבוֹדָךְ. לְמַעַן לִמּוּדָךְ. לְמַעַן מַלְכוּתָךְ. לְמַעַן נִצְחָךְ. לְמַעַן סוֹדָךְ. לְמַעַן עֻזָךְ. לְמַעַן פְּאֵרָךְ. לְמַעַן צִדְקָתָךְ. לְמַעַן קְדֻשָּׁתָךְ. לְמַעַן רַחֲמֶיךָ הָרַבִּים. לְמַעַן שְׁכִינָתָךְ. הוֹשַׁע נָא: לְמַעַן תְּהִלָּתָךְ. הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','For the sake of Your truth; for the sake of Your covenant; for the sake of Your greatness and harmony; for the sake of Your doctrine; for the sake of Your majesty; for the sake of Your assembly; for the sake of Your mention; for the sake of Your kindness; for the sake of Your goodness; for the sake of Your unity; for the sake of Your glory; for the sake of Your teaching; for the sake of Your kingdom; for the sake of Your eternity; for the sake of Your secret; for the sake of Your might; for the sake of Your splendor; for the sake of Your righteousness; for the sake of Your holiness; for the sake of Your great mercy; for the sake of Your Divine Presence, please save! For the sake of Your praise, please save!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','le-mah-ahn ah-mee-tahkh. le-mah-ahn ve-ree-tahkh. le-mah-ahn gohd-lahkh ve-teef-ahr-tahkh. le-mah-ahn dah-tahkh. le-mah-ahn hoh-dahkh. le-mah-ahn vee-oo-dahkh. le-mah-ahn zeekh-rahkh. le-mah-ahn khahs-dahkh. le-mah-ahn too-vahkh. le-mah-ahn yee-khoo-dahkh. le-mah-ahn ke-voh-dahkh. le-mah-ahn lee-moo-dahkh. le-mah-ahn mahl-khoo-tahkh. le-mah-ahn neets-khahkh. le-mah-ahn soh-dahkh. le-mah-ahn oo-zahkh. le-mah-ahn pe-eh-rahkh. le-mah-ahn tseed-kah-tahkh. le-mah-ahn ke-doo-shah-tahkh. le-mah-ahn rah-khah-mey-khah hah-rah-beem. le-mah-ahn she-khee-nah-tahkh. hoh-shah nah: le-mah-ahn te-hee-lah-tahkh. hoh-shah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','ah-nee vah-hoh hoh-shee-ah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ אֵלִים בְּלוּד עִמָּךְ. בְּצֵאתְךָ לְיֵשַׁע עַמָּךְ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ גּוֹי וֵאלֹהִים. דְרוּשִׁים לְיֵשַׁע אֱלֹהִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ הֲמוֹן צִבְאוֹת. וְעִמָּם מַלְאֲכֵי צְבָאוֹת. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ זַכִּים מִבֵּית עֲבָדִים. חַנּוּן בְּיָדָם מַעֲבִידִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ טְבוּעִים בְּצוּל גְּזָרִים. יְקָרְךָ עִמָּם מַעֲבִירִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ כַּנָּה מְשׁוֹרֶרֶת וַיּוֹשַׁע. לְגוֹחָהּ מְצֻיֶּנֶת וַיִּוָּשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ מַאֲמַר וְהוֹצֵאתִי אֶתְכֶם. נָקוּב וְהוּצֵאתִי אִתְּכֶם. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ סוֹבְבֵי מִזְבֵּחַ. עוֹמְסֵי עֲרָבָה לְהַקִּיף מִזְבֵּחַ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ פִּלְאֵי אָרוֹן כְּהֻפְשַׁע. צִעֵר פְּלֶשֶׁת בַּחֲרוֹן אַף וְנוֹשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ קְהִלּוֹת בָּבֶלָה שָׁלַחְתָּ. רַחוּם לְמַעֲנָם שֻׁלַּחְתָּ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שְׁבוּת שִׁבְטֵי יַעֲקֹב. תָּשׁוּב וְתָשִׁיב שְׁבוּת אָהֳלֵי יַעֲקֹב וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא. כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שׁוֹמְרֵי מִצְוֹת וְחוֹכֵי יְשׁוּעוֹת אֵל לְמוֹשָׁעוֹת. וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא: אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Like You saved the great ones in Lud (the son of Mitzrayim, Egypt''s namesake) with You, when You went out to save Your people, so too please save! Like You saved ''a nation and its leaders'' needing the salvation of God, so too please save! Like You saved many legions and, with them, hosts of angels, so too please save! Like You saved the pure ones from a house of bondage [when] they subjugated the Compassionate One with their hands, so too please save! Like You saved the drowning ones in the depths of the shreds [when] they were transporting Your glory with them, so too please save! Like You saved the base, singing (Exodus 13:40), "and He saved," [when] the One bursting out was indicated as saved, so too please save! Like You saved [with] the statement (Exodus 6:6), "and I will take you (etchem)," [but] it is designated, ''and I will go out with you (itchem),'' so too please save! Like You saved the ones that went around the altar, loaded with the willow to circle the altar, so too please save! Like You saved the wonders of the ark when it was sullied - He distraught Philistia with burning anger and it was saved - so too please save! Like You saved the congregations You sent to Babylonia - Merciful One, You [too] were sent for their sake - so too please save! You saved the return of the tribes of Jacob - return and bring back the return of the tents of Jacob and, so too, please save! Like You saved the keepers of the commandments and those awaiting salvations - You are the ''God of salvations'' - so, so too please bring salvation! Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','ke-hoh-shah-tah eh-leem be-lood ee-mahkh. be-tseh-te-khah le-yeh-shah ah-mahkh. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah gohy veh-loh-heem. de-roo-sheem le-yeh-shah eh-loh-heem. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah hah-mohn tseev-oht. ve-ee-mahm mahl-ah-khey tse-vah-oht. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah zah-keem mee-beyt ah-vah-deem. khah-noon be-yah-dahm mah-ah-vee-deem. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah te-voo-eem be-tsool ge-zah-reem. ye-kah-re-khah ee-mahm mah-ah-vee-reem. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah kah-nah me-shoh-reh-reht vah-yoh-shah. le-goh-khahh me-tsoo-yeh-neht vah-yee-vah-shah. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah mah-ah-mahr ve-hoh-tseh-tee eht-khehm. nah-koov ve-hoo-tseh-tee ee-te-khehm. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah soh-ve-vey meez-beh-ahkh. oh-me-sey ah-rah-vah le-hah-keef meez-beh-ahkh. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah peel-ey ah-rohn ke-hoof-shah. tsee-ehr pe-leh-sheht bah-khah-rohn ahf ve-noh-shah. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah ke-hee-loht bah-veh-lah shah-lahkh-tah. rah-khoom le-mah-ah-nahm shoo-lahkh-tah. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah she-voot sheev-tey yah-ah-kohv. tah-shoov ve-tah-sheev she-voot oh-hoh-ley yah-ah-kohv ve-hoh-shee-ah nah. ke-hoh-shah-tah shoh-me-rey meets-voht ve-khoh-khey ye-shoo-oht ehl le-moh-shah-oht. ve-hoh-shee-ah nah: ah-nee vah-hoh hoh-shee-ah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','הוֹשִׁיעָה אֶת עַמֶּךָ וּבָרֵךְ אֶת נַחֲלָתֶךָ וּרְעֵם וְנַשְּׂאֵם עַד הָעוֹלָם: וְיִהְיוּ דְּבָרַי אֵלֶּה אֲשֶׁר הִתְחַנַּנְתִּי לִפְנֵי יְהֹוָה קְרוֹבִים אֶל יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵינוּ יוֹמָם וָלָיְלָה לַעֲשׂוֹת מִשְׁפַּט עַבְדּוֹ וּמִשְׁפַּט עַמּוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל דְּבַר יוֹם בְּיוֹמוֹ: לְמַעַן דַּעַת כָּל עַמֵּי הָאָרֶץ כִּי יְהֹוָה הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים אֵין עוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Deliver and bless Your people; tend them and sustain them forever (Psalms 28:9). And may these words of mine, which I have offered in supplication before the Lord, be close to the Lord our God day and night, that He may provide for His servant and for His people Israel, according to each day’s needs. In order that all the peoples of the earth may know that the Lord alone is God, there is no other (I Kings 8:59-60).','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','hoh-shee-ah eht ah-meh-khah oo-vah-rehkh eht nah-khah-lah-teh-khah oo-re-ehm ve-nah-se-ehm ahd hah-oh-lahm: ve-yeeh-yoo de-vah-rahy eh-leh ah-shehr heet-khah-nahn-tee leef-ney ah-doh-NAI ke-roh-veem ehl ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo yoh-mahm vah-lah-ye-lah lah-ah-soht meesh-paht ahv-doh oo-meesh-paht ah-moh yees-rah-ehl de-vahr yohm be-yoh-moh: le-mah-ahn dah-aht kohl ah-mey hah-ah-rehts kee ah-doh-NAI hoo hah-eh-loh-heem eyn ohd:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','ליום א'' דחוה"מ למעט כשיו"ט חל בשבת אז יאמרו זה ביום ג'', ג'' דחוה"מ','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','For the first day of the intermediate days of the festival, except when the holiday falls out on Shabbat. In that case, we say this on Tuesday, the third day of the intermediate days:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אֶבֶן שְׁתִיָּה. בֵּית הַבְּחִירָה. גּוֹרֶן אָרְנָן. דְּבִיר הַמּוּצְנָע. הַר הַמּוֹרִיָּה. וְהַר יֵרָאֶה. זְבוּל תִּפְאַרְתֶּךָ. חָנָה דָוִד. טוֹב הַלְּבָנוֹן. יְפֵה נוֹף מְשׂוֹשׂ כָּל הָאָרֶץ. כְּלִילַת יוֹפִי. לִינַת הַצֶּדֶק. מָכוֹן לְשִׁבְתֶּךָ. נָוֶה שַׁאֲנָן. סֻכַּת שָׁלֵם. עֲלִיַּת שְׁבָטִים. פִּנַת יִקְרַת. צִיּוֹן הַמְצֻיֶּנֶת. קֹדֶשׁ הַקֳּדָשִׁים. רָצוּף אַהֲבָה. שְׁכִינַת כְּבוֹדֶךָ. תֵּל תַּלְפִּיּוֹת. הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Foundation stone, chosen house, threshing floor of Ornan, hidden sanctuary, Mount Moriah, Mount of He is Seen, palace of Your splendor, residence of David, goodly ridge, beautifully placed, joy of all the earth, most beautiful bride, resting place of justice, place of Your dwelling, tranquil habitation, complete sukkah, pilgrimage of the tribes, precious corner, excellent Zion, holy of holies, inlaid with love, dwelling place of Your glory - please save! Hill of magnificence, please save!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','eh-vehn she-tee-yah. beyt hah-be-khee-rah. goh-rehn ah-re-nahn. de-veer hah-moo-tse-nah. hahr hah-moh-ree-yah. ve-hahr yeh-rah-eh. ze-vool teef-ahr-teh-khah. khah-nah dah-veed. tohv hah-le-vah-nohn. ye-feh nohf me-sohs kohl hah-ah-rehts. ke-lee-laht yoh-fee. lee-naht hah-tseh-dehk. mah-khohn le-sheev-teh-khah. nah-veh shah-ah-nahn. soo-kaht shah-lehm. ah-lee-yaht she-vah-teem. pee-naht yeek-raht. tsee-yohn hah-me-tsoo-yeh-neht. koh-dehsh hah-koh-dah-sheem. rah-tsoof ah-hah-vah. she-khee-naht ke-voh-deh-khah. tehl tahl-pee-yoht. hoh-shah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','ah-nee vah-hoh hoh-shee-ah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ אֵלִים בְּלוּד עִמָּךְ. בְּצֵאתְךָ לְיֵשַׁע עַמָּךְ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ גּוֹי וֵאלֹהִים. דְרוּשִׁים לְיֵשַׁע אֱלֹהִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ הֲמוֹן צִבְאוֹת. וְעִמָּם מַלְאֲכֵי צְבָאוֹת. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ זַכִּים מִבֵּית עֲבָדִים. חַנּוּן בְּיָדָם מַעֲבִידִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ טְבוּעִים בְּצוּל גְּזָרִים. יְקָרְךָ עִמָּם מַעֲבִירִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ כַּנָּה מְשׁוֹרֶרֶת וַיּוֹשַׁע. לְגוֹחָהּ מְצֻיֶּנֶת וַיִּוָּשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ מַאֲמַר וְהוֹצֵאתִי אֶתְכֶם. נָקוּב וְהוּצֵאתִי אִתְּכֶם. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ סוֹבְבֵי מִזְבֵּחַ. עוֹמְסֵי עֲרָבָה לְהַקִּיף מִזְבֵּחַ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ פִּלְאֵי אָרוֹן כְּהֻפְשַׁע. צִעֵר פְּלֶשֶׁת בַּחֲרוֹן אַף וְנוֹשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ קְהִלּוֹת בָּבֶלָה שָׁלַחְתָּ. רַחוּם לְמַעֲנָם שֻׁלַּחְתָּ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שְׁבוּת שִׁבְטֵי יַעֲקֹב. תָּשׁוּב וְתָשִׁיב שְׁבוּת אָהֳלֵי יַעֲקֹב וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא. כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שׁוֹמְרֵי מִצְוֹת וְחוֹכֵי יְשׁוּעוֹת אֵל לְמוֹשָׁעוֹת. וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא: אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Like You saved the great ones in Lud (the son of Mitzrayim, Egypt''s namesake) with You, when You went out to save Your people, so too please save! Like You saved ''a nation and its leaders'' needing the salvation of God, so too please save! Like You saved many legions and, with them, hosts of angels, so too please save! Like You saved the pure ones from a house of bondage [when] they subjugated the Compassionate One with their hands, so too please save! Like You saved the drowning ones in the depths of the shreds [when] they were transporting Your glory with them, so too please save! Like You saved the base, singing (Exodus 13:40), "and He saved," [when] the One bursting out was indicated as saved, so too please save! Like You saved [with] the statement (Exodus 6:6), "and I will take you (etchem)," [but] it is designated, ''and I will go out with you (itchem),'' so too please save! Like You saved the ones that went around the altar, loaded with the willow to circle the altar, so too please save! Like You saved the wonders of the ark when it was sullied - He distraught Philistia with burning anger and it was saved - so too please save! Like You saved the congregations You sent to Babylonia - Merciful One, You [too] were sent for their sake - so too please save! You saved the return of the tribes of Jacob - return and bring back the return of the tents of Jacob and, so too, please save! Like You saved the keepers of the commandments and those awaiting salvations - You are the ''God of salvations'' - so, so too please bring salvation! Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','ke-hoh-shah-tah eh-leem be-lood ee-mahkh. be-tseh-te-khah le-yeh-shah ah-mahkh. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah gohy veh-loh-heem. de-roo-sheem le-yeh-shah eh-loh-heem. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah hah-mohn tseev-oht. ve-ee-mahm mahl-ah-khey tse-vah-oht. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah zah-keem mee-beyt ah-vah-deem. khah-noon be-yah-dahm mah-ah-vee-deem. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah te-voo-eem be-tsool ge-zah-reem. ye-kah-re-khah ee-mahm mah-ah-vee-reem. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah kah-nah me-shoh-reh-reht vah-yoh-shah. le-goh-khahh me-tsoo-yeh-neht vah-yee-vah-shah. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah mah-ah-mahr ve-hoh-tseh-tee eht-khehm. nah-koov ve-hoo-tseh-tee ee-te-khehm. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah soh-ve-vey meez-beh-ahkh. oh-me-sey ah-rah-vah le-hah-keef meez-beh-ahkh. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah peel-ey ah-rohn ke-hoof-shah. tsee-ehr pe-leh-sheht bah-khah-rohn ahf ve-noh-shah. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah ke-hee-loht bah-veh-lah shah-lahkh-tah. rah-khoom le-mah-ah-nahm shoo-lahkh-tah. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah she-voot sheev-tey yah-ah-kohv. tah-shoov ve-tah-sheev she-voot oh-hoh-ley yah-ah-kohv ve-hoh-shee-ah nah. ke-hoh-shah-tah shoh-me-rey meets-voht ve-khoh-khey ye-shoo-oht ehl le-moh-shah-oht. ve-hoh-shee-ah nah: ah-nee vah-hoh hoh-shee-ah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','הוֹשִׁיעָה אֶת עַמֶּךָ וּבָרֵךְ אֶת נַחֲלָתֶךָ וּרְעֵם וְנַשְּׂאֵם עַד הָעוֹלָם: וְיִהְיוּ דְּבָרַי אֵלֶּה אֲשֶׁר הִתְחַנַּנְתִּי לִפְנֵי יְהֹוָה קְרוֹבִים אֶל יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵינוּ יוֹמָם וָלָיְלָה לַעֲשׂוֹת מִשְׁפַּט עַבְדּוֹ וּמִשְׁפַּט עַמּוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל דְּבַר יוֹם בְּיוֹמוֹ: לְמַעַן דַּעַת כָּל עַמֵּי הָאָרֶץ כִּי יְהֹוָה הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים אֵין עוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Deliver and bless Your people; tend them and sustain them forever (Psalms 28:9). And may these words of mine, which I have offered in supplication before the Lord, be close to the Lord our God day and night, that He may provide for His servant and for His people Israel, according to each day’s needs. In order that all the peoples of the earth may know that the Lord alone is God, there is no other (I Kings 8:59-60).','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','hoh-shee-ah eht ah-meh-khah oo-vah-rehkh eht nah-khah-lah-teh-khah oo-re-ehm ve-nah-se-ehm ahd hah-oh-lahm: ve-yeeh-yoo de-vah-rahy eh-leh ah-shehr heet-khah-nahn-tee leef-ney ah-doh-NAI ke-roh-veem ehl ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo yoh-mahm vah-lah-ye-lah lah-ah-soht meesh-paht ahv-doh oo-meesh-paht ah-moh yees-rah-ehl de-vahr yohm be-yoh-moh: le-mah-ahn dah-aht kohl ah-mey hah-ah-rehts kee ah-doh-NAI hoo hah-eh-loh-heem eyn ohd:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','ליום ה'', ג'' דחוה"מ רק כשיו"ט חל ביום שני','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','For Thursday, the third day of the intermediate days of the festival, only when the holiday falls out on Monday:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אוֹם אֲנִי חוֹמָה. בָּרָה כַּחַמָּה. גּוֹלָה וְסוּרָה. דָּמְתָה לְתָמָר. הַהֲרוּגָה עָלֶיךָ. וְנֶחֱשֶׁבֶת כְּצֹאן טִבְחָה. זְרוּיָה בֵּין מַכְעִיסֶיהָ. חֲבוּקָה וּדְבוּקָה בָּךְ. טוֹעֶנֶת עֻלָּךְ. יְחִידָה לְיַחֲדָךְ. כְּבוּשָׁה בַגּוֹלָה. לוֹמֶדֶת יִרְאָתָךְ. מְרוּטַת לֶחִי. נְתוּנָה לְמַכִּים. סוֹבֶלֶת סִבְלָךְ. עֲנִיָּה סֹעֲרָה. פְּדוּיַת טוֹבִיָּה. צֹאן קָדָשִׁים. קְהִלּוֹת יַעֲקֹב. רְשׁוּמִים בִּשְׁמֶךָ. שׁוֹאֲגִים הוֹשַׁע נָא: תְּמוּכִים עָלֶיךָ. הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','The nation - ''I am a wall,'' bright as the sun, exiled and turned away, compared to a date palm, the one killed for You and considered like sheep for slaughter; scattered among its angerers, hugging and clinging to You, seeking Your yoke, alone to unify You, trampled in the exile, studying Your awe, pulled of cheek, given to be paupers, bearing Your burden, ship in a storm, redeemed of Tuviah (Moses), holy sheep, congregations of Jacob, marked with Your name - roars, "Please save!" [They are] dependent upon You, please save!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:17:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','ohm ah-nee khoh-mah. bah-rah kah-khah-mah. goh-lah ve-soo-rah. dah-me-tah le-tah-mahr. hah-hah-roo-gah ah-ley-khah. ve-neh-kheh-sheh-veht ke-tsohn teev-khah. ze-roo-yah beyn mahkh-ee-sey-hah. khah-voo-kah oo-de-voo-kah bahkh. toh-eh-neht oo-lahkh. ye-khee-dah le-yah-khah-dahkh. ke-voo-shah vah-goh-lah. loh-meh-deht yeer-ah-tahkh. me-roo-taht leh-khee. ne-too-nah le-mah-keem. soh-veh-leht seev-lahkh. ah-nee-yah soh-ah-rah. pe-doo-yaht toh-vee-yah. tsohn kah-dah-sheem. ke-hee-loht yah-ah-kohv. re-shoo-meem beesh-meh-khah. shoh-ah-geem hoh-shah nah: te-moo-kheem ah-ley-khah. hoh-shah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:18:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','ah-nee vah-hoh hoh-shee-ah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ אֵלִים בְּלוּד עִמָּךְ. בְּצֵאתְךָ לְיֵשַׁע עַמָּךְ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ גּוֹי וֵאלֹהִים. דְרוּשִׁים לְיֵשַׁע אֱלֹהִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ הֲמוֹן צִבְאוֹת. וְעִמָּם מַלְאֲכֵי צְבָאוֹת. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ זַכִּים מִבֵּית עֲבָדִים. חַנּוּן בְּיָדָם מַעֲבִידִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ טְבוּעִים בְּצוּל גְּזָרִים. יְקָרְךָ עִמָּם מַעֲבִירִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ כַּנָּה מְשׁוֹרֶרֶת וַיּוֹשַׁע. לְגוֹחָהּ מְצֻיֶּנֶת וַיִּוָּשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ מַאֲמַר וְהוֹצֵאתִי אֶתְכֶם. נָקוּב וְהוּצֵאתִי אִתְּכֶם. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ סוֹבְבֵי מִזְבֵּחַ. עוֹמְסֵי עֲרָבָה לְהַקִּיף מִזְבֵּחַ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ פִּלְאֵי אָרוֹן כְּהֻפְשַׁע. צִעֵר פְּלֶשֶׁת בַּחֲרוֹן אַף וְנוֹשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ קְהִלּוֹת בָּבֶלָה שָׁלַחְתָּ. רַחוּם לְמַעֲנָם שֻׁלַּחְתָּ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שְׁבוּת שִׁבְטֵי יַעֲקֹב. תָּשׁוּב וְתָשִׁיב שְׁבוּת אָהֳלֵי יַעֲקֹב וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא. כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שׁוֹמְרֵי מִצְוֹת וְחוֹכֵי יְשׁוּעוֹת אֵל לְמוֹשָׁעוֹת. וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא: אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Like You saved the great ones in Lud (the son of Mitzrayim, Egypt''s namesake) with You, when You went out to save Your people, so too please save! Like You saved ''a nation and its leaders'' needing the salvation of God, so too please save! Like You saved many legions and, with them, hosts of angels, so too please save! Like You saved the pure ones from a house of bondage [when] they subjugated the Compassionate One with their hands, so too please save! Like You saved the drowning ones in the depths of the shreds [when] they were transporting Your glory with them, so too please save! Like You saved the base, singing (Exodus 13:40), "and He saved," [when] the One bursting out was indicated as saved, so too please save! Like You saved [with] the statement (Exodus 6:6), "and I will take you (etchem)," [but] it is designated, ''and I will go out with you (itchem),'' so too please save! Like You saved the ones that went around the altar, loaded with the willow to circle the altar, so too please save! Like You saved the wonders of the ark when it was sullied - He distraught Philistia with burning anger and it was saved - so too please save! Like You saved the congregations You sent to Babylonia - Merciful One, You [too] were sent for their sake - so too please save! You saved the return of the tribes of Jacob - return and bring back the return of the tents of Jacob and, so too, please save! Like You saved the keepers of the commandments and those awaiting salvations - You are the ''God of salvations'' - so, so too please bring salvation! Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','ke-hoh-shah-tah eh-leem be-lood ee-mahkh. be-tseh-te-khah le-yeh-shah ah-mahkh. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah gohy veh-loh-heem. de-roo-sheem le-yeh-shah eh-loh-heem. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah hah-mohn tseev-oht. ve-ee-mahm mahl-ah-khey tse-vah-oht. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah zah-keem mee-beyt ah-vah-deem. khah-noon be-yah-dahm mah-ah-vee-deem. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah te-voo-eem be-tsool ge-zah-reem. ye-kah-re-khah ee-mahm mah-ah-vee-reem. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah kah-nah me-shoh-reh-reht vah-yoh-shah. le-goh-khahh me-tsoo-yeh-neht vah-yee-vah-shah. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah mah-ah-mahr ve-hoh-tseh-tee eht-khehm. nah-koov ve-hoo-tseh-tee ee-te-khehm. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah soh-ve-vey meez-beh-ahkh. oh-me-sey ah-rah-vah le-hah-keef meez-beh-ahkh. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah peel-ey ah-rohn ke-hoof-shah. tsee-ehr pe-leh-sheht bah-khah-rohn ahf ve-noh-shah. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah ke-hee-loht bah-veh-lah shah-lahkh-tah. rah-khoom le-mah-ah-nahm shoo-lahkh-tah. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah she-voot sheev-tey yah-ah-kohv. tah-shoov ve-tah-sheev she-voot oh-hoh-ley yah-ah-kohv ve-hoh-shee-ah nah. ke-hoh-shah-tah shoh-me-rey meets-voht ve-khoh-khey ye-shoo-oht ehl le-moh-shah-oht. ve-hoh-shee-ah nah: ah-nee vah-hoh hoh-shee-ah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','הוֹשִׁיעָה אֶת עַמֶּךָ וּבָרֵךְ אֶת נַחֲלָתֶךָ וּרְעֵם וְנַשְּׂאֵם עַד הָעוֹלָם: וְיִהְיוּ דְּבָרַי אֵלֶּה אֲשֶׁר הִתְחַנַּנְתִּי לִפְנֵי יְהֹוָה קְרוֹבִים אֶל יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵינוּ יוֹמָם וָלָיְלָה לַעֲשׂוֹת מִשְׁפַּט עַבְדּוֹ וּמִשְׁפַּט עַמּוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל דְּבַר יוֹם בְּיוֹמוֹ: לְמַעַן דַּעַת כָּל עַמֵּי הָאָרֶץ כִּי יְהֹוָה הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים אֵין עוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Deliver and bless Your people; tend them and sustain them forever (Psalms 28:9). And may these words of mine, which I have offered in supplication before the Lord, be close to the Lord our God day and night, that He may provide for His servant and for His people Israel, according to each day’s needs. In order that all the peoples of the earth may know that the Lord alone is God, there is no other (I Kings 8:59-60).','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:20:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','hoh-shee-ah eht ah-meh-khah oo-vah-rehkh eht nah-khah-lah-teh-khah oo-re-ehm ve-nah-se-ehm ahd hah-oh-lahm: ve-yeeh-yoo de-vah-rahy eh-leh ah-shehr heet-khah-nahn-tee leef-ney ah-doh-NAI ke-roh-veem ehl ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo yoh-mahm vah-lah-ye-lah lah-ah-soht meesh-paht ahv-doh oo-meesh-paht ah-moh yees-rah-ehl de-vahr yohm be-yoh-moh: le-mah-ahn dah-aht kohl ah-mey hah-ah-rehts kee ah-doh-NAI hoo hah-eh-loh-heem eyn ohd:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','כשחל יו"ט ביום ג'' יאמרו זה ביום א'', ה'' דחוה"מ. כשחל יו"ט ביום ה'' יאמרו זה ביום ג'', ה'' דחוה"מ. כשחל יו"ט בש"ק יאמרו זה ביום ה'', ה'' דחוה"מ.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','When the holiday falls out on Tuesday, we say this on Sunday, the fifth day of the intermediate days. When the holiday comes out on Thursday, we say this on Tuesday, the fifth day of the intermediate days. When the holiday comes out on Shabbat, we say this on Thursday, the fifth day of the intermediate days.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אָדוֹן הַמּוֹשִׁיעַ. בִּלְתְּךָ אֵין לְהוֹשִׁיעַ. גִּבּוֹר וְרַב לְהוֹשִׁיעַ. דַּלּוֹתִי וְלִי יְהוֹשִׁיעַ. הָאֵל הַמּוֹשִׁיעַ. וּמַצִּיל וּמוֹשִׁיעַ. זוֹעֲקֶיךָ תּוֹשִׁיעַ. חוֹכֶיךָ הוֹשִׁיעַ. טְלָאֶיךָ תַּשְׂבִּיעַ. יְבוּל לְהַשְׁפִּיעַ. כָּל שִׂיחַ תַּדְשֵׁא וְתוֹשִׁיעַ. לְגֵיא בַּל תַּרְשִׁיעַ. מְגָדִים תַּמְתִּיק וְתוֹשִׁיעַ. נְשִׂיאִים לְהַסִּיעַ. שְׂעִירִים לְהָנִיעַ. עֲנָנִים מִלְּהַמְנִיעַ. פּוֹתֵחַ יָד וּמַשְׂבִּיעַ. צְמֵאֶיךָ תַּשְׂבִּיעַ. קוֹרְאֶיךָ תּוֹשִׁיעַ. רְחוּמֶיךָ תּוֹשִׁיעַ. שׁוֹחֲרֶיךָ הוֹשִׁיעַ. הוֹשַׁע נָא: תְּמִימֶיךָ תּוֹשִׁיעַ. הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','The Master who brings salvation - without You there is no salvation, mighty One and great in saving, ''I became indigent and He will bring me salvation,'' the saving God who rescues and brings salvation - bring salvation to those who cry to You; bring salvation to those that wait for You, to satiate your sheep, to give produce bountifully, make every shrub grow, and bring salvation. Do not do bad to the valley - sweeten the delicacies and bring salvation, to carry the clouds, to move the rains. Restrain the clouds, open the hand and satiate - satiate Your thirsty ones. Bring salvation to those that call to You, bring salvation to the ones You pity, bring salvation to the ones who seek You, please save! Bring salvation to Your blameless ones, please save!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:22:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','ah-dohn hah-moh-shee-ah. beel-te-khah eyn le-hoh-shee-ah. gee-bohr ve-rahv le-hoh-shee-ah. dah-loh-tee ve-lee ye-hoh-shee-ah. hah-ehl hah-moh-shee-ah. oo-mah-tseel oo-moh-shee-ah. zoh-ah-key-khah toh-shee-ah. khoh-khey-khah hoh-shee-ah. te-lah-ey-khah tahs-bee-ah. ye-vool le-hahsh-pee-ah. kohl see-ahkh tahd-sheh ve-toh-shee-ah. le-gey bahl tahr-shee-ah. me-gah-deem tahm-teek ve-toh-shee-ah. ne-see-eem le-hah-see-ah. se-ee-reem le-hah-nee-ah. ah-nah-neem mee-le-hah-me-nee-ah. poh-teh-ahkh yahd oo-mahs-bee-ah. tse-meh-ey-khah tahs-bee-ah. koh-re-ey-khah toh-shee-ah. re-khoo-mey-khah toh-shee-ah. shoh-khah-rey-khah hoh-shee-ah. hoh-shah nah: te-mee-mey-khah toh-shee-ah. hoh-shah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:23:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','ah-nee vah-hoh hoh-shee-ah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ אֵלִים בְּלוּד עִמָּךְ. בְּצֵאתְךָ לְיֵשַׁע עַמָּךְ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ גּוֹי וֵאלֹהִים. דְרוּשִׁים לְיֵשַׁע אֱלֹהִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ הֲמוֹן צִבְאוֹת. וְעִמָּם מַלְאֲכֵי צְבָאוֹת. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ זַכִּים מִבֵּית עֲבָדִים. חַנּוּן בְּיָדָם מַעֲבִידִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ טְבוּעִים בְּצוּל גְּזָרִים. יְקָרְךָ עִמָּם מַעֲבִירִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ כַּנָּה מְשׁוֹרֶרֶת וַיּוֹשַׁע. לְגוֹחָהּ מְצֻיֶּנֶת וַיִּוָּשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ מַאֲמַר וְהוֹצֵאתִי אֶתְכֶם. נָקוּב וְהוּצֵאתִי אִתְּכֶם. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ סוֹבְבֵי מִזְבֵּחַ. עוֹמְסֵי עֲרָבָה לְהַקִּיף מִזְבֵּחַ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ פִּלְאֵי אָרוֹן כְּהֻפְשַׁע. צִעֵר פְּלֶשֶׁת בַּחֲרוֹן אַף וְנוֹשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ קְהִלּוֹת בָּבֶלָה שָׁלַחְתָּ. רַחוּם לְמַעֲנָם שֻׁלַּחְתָּ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שְׁבוּת שִׁבְטֵי יַעֲקֹב. תָּשׁוּב וְתָשִׁיב שְׁבוּת אָהֳלֵי יַעֲקֹב וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא. כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שׁוֹמְרֵי מִצְוֹת וְחוֹכֵי יְשׁוּעוֹת אֵל לְמוֹשָׁעוֹת. וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא: אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Like You saved the great ones in Lud (the son of Mitzrayim, Egypt''s namesake) with You, when You went out to save Your people, so too please save! Like You saved ''a nation and its leaders'' needing the salvation of God, so too please save! Like You saved many legions and, with them, hosts of angels, so too please save! Like You saved the pure ones from a house of bondage [when] they subjugated the Compassionate One with their hands, so too please save! Like You saved the drowning ones in the depths of the shreds [when] they were transporting Your glory with them, so too please save! Like You saved the base, singing (Exodus 13:40), "and He saved," [when] the One bursting out was indicated as saved, so too please save! Like You saved [with] the statement (Exodus 6:6), "and I will take you (etchem)," [but] it is designated, ''and I will go out with you (itchem),'' so too please save! Like You saved the ones that went around the altar, loaded with the willow to circle the altar, so too please save! Like You saved the wonders of the ark when it was sullied - He distraught Philistia with burning anger and it was saved - so too please save! Like You saved the congregations You sent to Babylonia - Merciful One, You [too] were sent for their sake - so too please save! You saved the return of the tribes of Jacob - return and bring back the return of the tents of Jacob and, so too, please save! Like You saved the keepers of the commandments and those awaiting salvations - You are the ''God of salvations'' - so, so too please bring salvation! Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:24:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','ke-hoh-shah-tah eh-leem be-lood ee-mahkh. be-tseh-te-khah le-yeh-shah ah-mahkh. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah gohy veh-loh-heem. de-roo-sheem le-yeh-shah eh-loh-heem. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah hah-mohn tseev-oht. ve-ee-mahm mahl-ah-khey tse-vah-oht. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah zah-keem mee-beyt ah-vah-deem. khah-noon be-yah-dahm mah-ah-vee-deem. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah te-voo-eem be-tsool ge-zah-reem. ye-kah-re-khah ee-mahm mah-ah-vee-reem. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah kah-nah me-shoh-reh-reht vah-yoh-shah. le-goh-khahh me-tsoo-yeh-neht vah-yee-vah-shah. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah mah-ah-mahr ve-hoh-tseh-tee eht-khehm. nah-koov ve-hoo-tseh-tee ee-te-khehm. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah soh-ve-vey meez-beh-ahkh. oh-me-sey ah-rah-vah le-hah-keef meez-beh-ahkh. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah peel-ey ah-rohn ke-hoof-shah. tsee-ehr pe-leh-sheht bah-khah-rohn ahf ve-noh-shah. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah ke-hee-loht bah-veh-lah shah-lahkh-tah. rah-khoom le-mah-ah-nahm shoo-lahkh-tah. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah she-voot sheev-tey yah-ah-kohv. tah-shoov ve-tah-sheev she-voot oh-hoh-ley yah-ah-kohv ve-hoh-shee-ah nah. ke-hoh-shah-tah shoh-me-rey meets-voht ve-khoh-khey ye-shoo-oht ehl le-moh-shah-oht. ve-hoh-shee-ah nah: ah-nee vah-hoh hoh-shee-ah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:25:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','הוֹשִׁיעָה אֶת עַמֶּךָ וּבָרֵךְ אֶת נַחֲלָתֶךָ וּרְעֵם וְנַשְּׂאֵם עַד הָעוֹלָם: וְיִהְיוּ דְּבָרַי אֵלֶּה אֲשֶׁר הִתְחַנַּנְתִּי לִפְנֵי יְהֹוָה קְרוֹבִים אֶל יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵינוּ יוֹמָם וָלָיְלָה לַעֲשׂוֹת מִשְׁפַּט עַבְדּוֹ וּמִשְׁפַּט עַמּוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל דְּבַר יוֹם בְּיוֹמוֹ: לְמַעַן דַּעַת כָּל עַמֵּי הָאָרֶץ כִּי יְהֹוָה הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים אֵין עוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:25:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Deliver and bless Your people; tend them and sustain them forever (Psalms 28:9). And may these words of mine, which I have offered in supplication before the Lord, be close to the Lord our God day and night, that He may provide for His servant and for His people Israel, according to each day’s needs. In order that all the peoples of the earth may know that the Lord alone is God, there is no other (I Kings 8:59-60).','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:25:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','hoh-shee-ah eht ah-meh-khah oo-vah-rehkh eht nah-khah-lah-teh-khah oo-re-ehm ve-nah-se-ehm ahd hah-oh-lahm: ve-yeeh-yoo de-vah-rahy eh-leh ah-shehr heet-khah-nahn-tee leef-ney ah-doh-NAI ke-roh-veem ehl ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo yoh-mahm vah-lah-ye-lah lah-ah-soht meesh-paht ahv-doh oo-meesh-paht ah-moh yees-rah-ehl de-vahr yohm be-yoh-moh: le-mah-ahn dah-aht kohl ah-mey hah-ah-rehts kee ah-doh-NAI hoo hah-eh-loh-heem eyn ohd:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:26:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','כשחל יו"ט ביום ב'' יאמרו זה ביום ד'', ב'' דחוה"מ. כשחל יו"ט ביום ג'' יאמרו זה ביום ה'', ב'' דחוה"מ. כשחל יו"ט ביום ה'' יאמרו זה ביום א'', ג'' דחוה"מ. כשחל יו"ו בש"ק יאמרו זה ביום ב'', ב'' דחוה"מ','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:26:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','When the holiday falls out on Monday, we say this on Thursday, the second day of the intermediate days. When the holiday falls out on Tuesday, we say this on Thursday, the second day of the intermediate days.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:27:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אֶעֱרוֹךְ שׁוּעִי. בְּבֵית שַׁוְעִי. גִּלִּיתִי בַצּוֹם פִּשְׁעִי. דְּרַשְׁתִּיךָ בּוֹ לְהוֹשִׁיעִי. הַקְשִׁיבָה לְקוֹל שַׁוְעִי. וְקוּמָה וְהוֹשִׁיעִי. זְכוֹר וְרַחֵם מוֹשִׁיעִי. חַי כֵּן תְּשַׁעְשְׁעִי. טוֹב בְּאֶנֶק שְׁעִי. יוּחַשׁ מוֹשִׁיעִי. כַּלֵּה מַרְשִׁיעִי. לְבַל עוֹד תַּרְשִׁיעִי. מַהֵר אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׁעִי. נֶצַח לְהוֹשִׁיעִי. שָׂא נָא עֲוֹן רִשְׁעִי. עֲבוֹר עַל פִּשְׁעִי. פְּנֵה נָא לְהוֹשִׁיעִי. צוּר צַדִּיק מוֹשִׁיעִי. קַבֵּל נָא שַׁוְעִי. רוֹמֵם קֶרֶן יִשְׁעִי. שַׁדַּי מוֹשִׁיעִי. הוֹשַׁע נָא: תּוֹפִיעַ וְתוֹשִׁיעִי. הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:27:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','I shall set up my prayer in the house of my prayer: I have revealed my rebellion on the fast (Yom Kippur); I sought You then to save me. Listen to the voice of my prayer, and arise and bring me salvation. My Savior, remember and have mercy. Living One, indeed make me rejoice; Goodly One, in groaning, answer me - may my Savior be quick. Destroy the one who does evil to me (Satan), so that he not continue to make me evil. Quickly, God of my salvation, eternally to save me. Please lift up the iniquity of my evil, pass over my rebellion; please turn to me to bring me salvation. Rock, my righteous Savior, please accept my prayer. Lift up the horn of my salvation; Omnipresent, my Savior, please save! Appear and bring me salvation, please save!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:27:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','eh-eh-rohkh shoo-ee. be-veyt shahv-ee. gee-lee-tee vah-tsohm peesh-ee. de-rahsh-tee-khah boh le-hoh-shee-ee. hahk-shee-vah le-kohl shahv-ee. ve-koo-mah ve-hoh-shee-ee. ze-khohr ve-rah-khehm moh-shee-ee. khahy kehn te-shah-she-ee. tohv be-eh-nehk she-ee. yoo-khahsh moh-shee-ee. kah-leh mahr-shee-ee. le-vahl ohd tahr-shee-ee. mah-hehr eh-loh-hey yeesh-ee. neh-tsahkh le-hoh-shee-ee. sah nah ah-vohn reesh-ee. ah-vohr ahl peesh-ee. pe-neh nah le-hoh-shee-ee. tsoor tsah-deek moh-shee-ee. kah-behl nah shahv-ee. roh-mehm keh-rehn yeesh-ee. shah-dahy moh-shee-ee. hoh-shah nah: toh-fee-ah ve-toh-shee-ee. hoh-shah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:28:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:28:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:28:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','ah-nee vah-hoh hoh-shee-ah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:29:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ אֵלִים בְּלוּד עִמָּךְ. בְּצֵאתְךָ לְיֵשַׁע עַמָּךְ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ גּוֹי וֵאלֹהִים. דְרוּשִׁים לְיֵשַׁע אֱלֹהִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ הֲמוֹן צִבְאוֹת. וְעִמָּם מַלְאֲכֵי צְבָאוֹת. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ זַכִּים מִבֵּית עֲבָדִים. חַנּוּן בְּיָדָם מַעֲבִידִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ טְבוּעִים בְּצוּל גְּזָרִים. יְקָרְךָ עִמָּם מַעֲבִירִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ כַּנָּה מְשׁוֹרֶרֶת וַיּוֹשַׁע. לְגוֹחָהּ מְצֻיֶּנֶת וַיִּוָּשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ מַאֲמַר וְהוֹצֵאתִי אֶתְכֶם. נָקוּב וְהוּצֵאתִי אִתְּכֶם. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ סוֹבְבֵי מִזְבֵּחַ. עוֹמְסֵי עֲרָבָה לְהַקִּיף מִזְבֵּחַ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ פִּלְאֵי אָרוֹן כְּהֻפְשַׁע. צִעֵר פְּלֶשֶׁת בַּחֲרוֹן אַף וְנוֹשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ קְהִלּוֹת בָּבֶלָה שָׁלַחְתָּ. רַחוּם לְמַעֲנָם שֻׁלַּחְתָּ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שְׁבוּת שִׁבְטֵי יַעֲקֹב. תָּשׁוּב וְתָשִׁיב שְׁבוּת אָהֳלֵי יַעֲקֹב וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא. כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שׁוֹמְרֵי מִצְוֹת וְחוֹכֵי יְשׁוּעוֹת אֵל לְמוֹשָׁעוֹת. וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא: אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:29:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Like You saved the great ones in Lud (the son of Mitzrayim, Egypt''s namesake) with You, when You went out to save Your people, so too please save! Like You saved ''a nation and its leaders'' needing the salvation of God, so too please save! Like You saved many legions and, with them, hosts of angels, so too please save! Like You saved the pure ones from a house of bondage [when] they subjugated the Compassionate One with their hands, so too please save! Like You saved the drowning ones in the depths of the shreds [when] they were transporting Your glory with them, so too please save! Like You saved the base, singing (Exodus 13:40), "and He saved," [when] the One bursting out was indicated as saved, so too please save! Like You saved [with] the statement (Exodus 6:6), "and I will take you (etchem)," [but] it is designated, ''and I will go out with you (itchem),'' so too please save! Like You saved the ones that went around the altar, loaded with the willow to circle the altar, so too please save! Like You saved the wonders of the ark when it was sullied - He distraught Philistia with burning anger and it was saved - so too please save! Like You saved the congregations You sent to Babylonia - Merciful One, You [too] were sent for their sake - so too please save! You saved the return of the tribes of Jacob - return and bring back the return of the tents of Jacob and, so too, please save! Like You saved the keepers of the commandments and those awaiting salvations - You are the ''God of salvations'' - so, so too please bring salvation! Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:29:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','ke-hoh-shah-tah eh-leem be-lood ee-mahkh. be-tseh-te-khah le-yeh-shah ah-mahkh. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah gohy veh-loh-heem. de-roo-sheem le-yeh-shah eh-loh-heem. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah hah-mohn tseev-oht. ve-ee-mahm mahl-ah-khey tse-vah-oht. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah zah-keem mee-beyt ah-vah-deem. khah-noon be-yah-dahm mah-ah-vee-deem. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah te-voo-eem be-tsool ge-zah-reem. ye-kah-re-khah ee-mahm mah-ah-vee-reem. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah kah-nah me-shoh-reh-reht vah-yoh-shah. le-goh-khahh me-tsoo-yeh-neht vah-yee-vah-shah. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah mah-ah-mahr ve-hoh-tseh-tee eht-khehm. nah-koov ve-hoo-tseh-tee ee-te-khehm. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah soh-ve-vey meez-beh-ahkh. oh-me-sey ah-rah-vah le-hah-keef meez-beh-ahkh. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah peel-ey ah-rohn ke-hoof-shah. tsee-ehr pe-leh-sheht bah-khah-rohn ahf ve-noh-shah. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah ke-hee-loht bah-veh-lah shah-lahkh-tah. rah-khoom le-mah-ah-nahm shoo-lahkh-tah. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah she-voot sheev-tey yah-ah-kohv. tah-shoov ve-tah-sheev she-voot oh-hoh-ley yah-ah-kohv ve-hoh-shee-ah nah. ke-hoh-shah-tah shoh-me-rey meets-voht ve-khoh-khey ye-shoo-oht ehl le-moh-shah-oht. ve-hoh-shee-ah nah: ah-nee vah-hoh hoh-shee-ah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:30:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','הוֹשִׁיעָה אֶת עַמֶּךָ וּבָרֵךְ אֶת נַחֲלָתֶךָ וּרְעֵם וְנַשְּׂאֵם עַד הָעוֹלָם: וְיִהְיוּ דְּבָרַי אֵלֶּה אֲשֶׁר הִתְחַנַּנְתִּי לִפְנֵי יְהֹוָה קְרוֹבִים אֶל יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵינוּ יוֹמָם וָלָיְלָה לַעֲשׂוֹת מִשְׁפַּט עַבְדּוֹ וּמִשְׁפַּט עַמּוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל דְּבַר יוֹם בְּיוֹמוֹ: לְמַעַן דַּעַת כָּל עַמֵּי הָאָרֶץ כִּי יְהֹוָה הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים אֵין עוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:30:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Deliver and bless Your people; tend them and sustain them forever (Psalms 28:9). And may these words of mine, which I have offered in supplication before the Lord, be close to the Lord our God day and night, that He may provide for His servant and for His people Israel, according to each day’s needs. In order that all the peoples of the earth may know that the Lord alone is God, there is no other (I Kings 8:59-60).','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:30:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','hoh-shee-ah eht ah-meh-khah oo-vah-rehkh eht nah-khah-lah-teh-khah oo-re-ehm ve-nah-se-ehm ahd hah-oh-lahm: ve-yeeh-yoo de-vah-rahy eh-leh ah-shehr heet-khah-nahn-tee leef-ney ah-doh-NAI ke-roh-veem ehl ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo yoh-mahm vah-lah-ye-lah lah-ah-soht meesh-paht ahv-doh oo-meesh-paht ah-moh yees-rah-ehl de-vahr yohm be-yoh-moh: le-mah-ahn dah-aht kohl ah-mey hah-ah-rehts kee ah-doh-NAI hoo hah-eh-loh-heem eyn ohd:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:31:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','כשחל יו"ט ביום ב'' יאמרו זה ביום ו'', ד'' דחוה"מ. כשחל יו"ט ביום ג'' יאמרו זה ביום ו'', ג'' דחוה"מ. כשחל יו"ט ביום ה'' יאמרו זה ביום ב'', ד'' דחוה"מ, כשחל יו"ט בש"ק יאמרו זה ביום ד'', ד'' דחוה"מ.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:31:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','When the holiday falls out on Monday, we say this on Friday, the fourth day of the intermediate days. When the holiday falls out on Tuesday, we say this on Friday, the third day of the intermediate days. When the holiday falls out on Thursday, we say this on Monday, the fourth day of the intermediate days. When the holiday falls out on Shabbat, we say this on Wednesday the fourth day of the intermediate days.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:32:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אֵל לְמוֹשָׁעוֹת. בְּאַרְבַּע שָׁבוּעוֹת. גָּשִׁים בְּשַׁוְעוֹת. דּוֹפְקֵי עֶרֶךְ שׁוּעוֹת. (נ"א שְׁעוֹת) הוֹגֵי שַׁעְשְׁעוֹת. וְחִידוֹתָם מִשְׁתַּעְשְׁעוֹת. זוֹעֲקִים לְהַשְׁעוֹת. חוֹכֵי יְשׁוּעוֹת. טְפוּלִים בְּךָ שְׁעוֹת. יוֹדְעֵי בִין שָׁעוֹת. כּוֹרְעֶיךָ בְּשַׁוְעוֹת. לְהָבִין שְׁמוּעוֹת. מִפִּיךָ נִשְׁמָעוֹת. נוֹתֵן תְּשׁוּעוֹת. סְפוּרוֹת מַשְׁמָעוֹת. (נ"א מְשַׁמְעוֹת) עֵדוּת מַשְׁמִיעוֹת. פּוֹעֵל יְשׁוּעוֹת. צַדִּיק נוֹשָׁעוֹת. קִרְיַת (נ"א קָרֵב) תְּשׁוּעוֹת. רֶגֶשׁ תְּשׁוּאוֹת. שָׁלשׁ שָׁעוֹת. הוֹשַׁע נָא: תָּחִישׁ לִתְשׁוּעוֹת. הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:32:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','''God of salvations'' - with four oaths, they approach with prayers, knock with the arrangement of prayers, meditate upon the enjoyments (the Torah) and enjoy their riddles; they yell out for salvations, those that await salvations with You in their prayers, knowing the understanding of the hours, bending down in their prayers to understand the traditions that were heard from Your mouth - Giver of salvations - recounters of heard things, the ones that give over [the] testimony - Doer of salvations, Righteous One of salvation - the town of salvation, [with] emotional cheers [in] three hours, please save! Be quick for salvations, please save!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:32:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','ehl le-moh-shah-oht. be-ahr-bah shah-voo-oht. gah-sheem be-shahv-oht. doh-fe-key eh-rehkh shoo-oht. (n" she-oht) hoh-gey shah-she-oht. ve-khee-doh-tahm meesh-tah-she-oht. zoh-ah-keem le-hahsh-oht. khoh-khey ye-shoo-oht. te-foo-leem be-khah she-oht. yoh-de-ey veen shah-oht. koh-re-ey-khah be-shahv-oht. le-hah-veen she-moo-oht. mee-pee-khah neesh-mah-oht. noh-tehn te-shoo-oht. se-foo-roht mahsh-mah-oht. (n" me-shahm-oht) eh-doot mahsh-mee-oht. poh-ehl ye-shoo-oht. tsah-deek noh-shah-oht. keer-yaht (n" kah-rehv) te-shoo-oht. reh-gehsh te-shoo-oht. shahlsh shah-oht. hoh-shah nah: tah-kheesh leet-shoo-oht. hoh-shah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:33:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:33:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:33:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','ah-nee vah-hoh hoh-shee-ah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:34:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ אֵלִים בְּלוּד עִמָּךְ. בְּצֵאתְךָ לְיֵשַׁע עַמָּךְ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ גּוֹי וֵאלֹהִים. דְרוּשִׁים לְיֵשַׁע אֱלֹהִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ הֲמוֹן צִבְאוֹת. וְעִמָּם מַלְאֲכֵי צְבָאוֹת. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ זַכִּים מִבֵּית עֲבָדִים. חַנּוּן בְּיָדָם מַעֲבִידִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ טְבוּעִים בְּצוּל גְּזָרִים. יְקָרְךָ עִמָּם מַעֲבִירִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ כַּנָּה מְשׁוֹרֶרֶת וַיּוֹשַׁע. לְגוֹחָהּ מְצֻיֶּנֶת וַיִּוָּשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ מַאֲמַר וְהוֹצֵאתִי אֶתְכֶם. נָקוּב וְהוּצֵאתִי אִתְּכֶם. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ סוֹבְבֵי מִזְבֵּחַ. עוֹמְסֵי עֲרָבָה לְהַקִּיף מִזְבֵּחַ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ פִּלְאֵי אָרוֹן כְּהֻפְשַׁע. צִעֵר פְּלֶשֶׁת בַּחֲרוֹן אַף וְנוֹשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ קְהִלּוֹת בָּבֶלָה שָׁלַחְתָּ. רַחוּם לְמַעֲנָם שֻׁלַּחְתָּ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שְׁבוּת שִׁבְטֵי יַעֲקֹב. תָּשׁוּב וְתָשִׁיב שְׁבוּת אָהֳלֵי יַעֲקֹב וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא. כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שׁוֹמְרֵי מִצְוֹת וְחוֹכֵי יְשׁוּעוֹת אֵל לְמוֹשָׁעוֹת. וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא: אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:34:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Like You saved the great ones in Lud (the son of Mitzrayim, Egypt''s namesake) with You, when You went out to save Your people, so too please save! Like You saved ''a nation and its leaders'' needing the salvation of God, so too please save! Like You saved many legions and, with them, hosts of angels, so too please save! Like You saved the pure ones from a house of bondage [when] they subjugated the Compassionate One with their hands, so too please save! Like You saved the drowning ones in the depths of the shreds [when] they were transporting Your glory with them, so too please save! Like You saved the base, singing (Exodus 13:40), "and He saved," [when] the One bursting out was indicated as saved, so too please save! Like You saved [with] the statement (Exodus 6:6), "and I will take you (etchem)," [but] it is designated, ''and I will go out with you (itchem),'' so too please save! Like You saved the ones that went around the altar, loaded with the willow to circle the altar, so too please save! Like You saved the wonders of the ark when it was sullied - He distraught Philistia with burning anger and it was saved - so too please save! Like You saved the congregations You sent to Babylonia - Merciful One, You [too] were sent for their sake - so too please save! You saved the return of the tribes of Jacob - return and bring back the return of the tents of Jacob and, so too, please save! Like You saved the keepers of the commandments and those awaiting salvations - You are the ''God of salvations'' - so, so too please bring salvation! Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:34:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','ke-hoh-shah-tah eh-leem be-lood ee-mahkh. be-tseh-te-khah le-yeh-shah ah-mahkh. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah gohy veh-loh-heem. de-roo-sheem le-yeh-shah eh-loh-heem. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah hah-mohn tseev-oht. ve-ee-mahm mahl-ah-khey tse-vah-oht. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah zah-keem mee-beyt ah-vah-deem. khah-noon be-yah-dahm mah-ah-vee-deem. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah te-voo-eem be-tsool ge-zah-reem. ye-kah-re-khah ee-mahm mah-ah-vee-reem. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah kah-nah me-shoh-reh-reht vah-yoh-shah. le-goh-khahh me-tsoo-yeh-neht vah-yee-vah-shah. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah mah-ah-mahr ve-hoh-tseh-tee eht-khehm. nah-koov ve-hoo-tseh-tee ee-te-khehm. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah soh-ve-vey meez-beh-ahkh. oh-me-sey ah-rah-vah le-hah-keef meez-beh-ahkh. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah peel-ey ah-rohn ke-hoof-shah. tsee-ehr pe-leh-sheht bah-khah-rohn ahf ve-noh-shah. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah ke-hee-loht bah-veh-lah shah-lahkh-tah. rah-khoom le-mah-ah-nahm shoo-lahkh-tah. kehn hoh-shah nah: ke-hoh-shah-tah she-voot sheev-tey yah-ah-kohv. tah-shoov ve-tah-sheev she-voot oh-hoh-ley yah-ah-kohv ve-hoh-shee-ah nah. ke-hoh-shah-tah shoh-me-rey meets-voht ve-khoh-khey ye-shoo-oht ehl le-moh-shah-oht. ve-hoh-shee-ah nah: ah-nee vah-hoh hoh-shee-ah nah:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:35:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','הוֹשִׁיעָה אֶת עַמֶּךָ וּבָרֵךְ אֶת נַחֲלָתֶךָ וּרְעֵם וְנַשְּׂאֵם עַד הָעוֹלָם: וְיִהְיוּ דְּבָרַי אֵלֶּה אֲשֶׁר הִתְחַנַּנְתִּי לִפְנֵי יְהֹוָה קְרוֹבִים אֶל יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵינוּ יוֹמָם וָלָיְלָה לַעֲשׂוֹת מִשְׁפַּט עַבְדּוֹ וּמִשְׁפַּט עַמּוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל דְּבַר יוֹם בְּיוֹמוֹ: לְמַעַן דַּעַת כָּל עַמֵּי הָאָרֶץ כִּי יְהֹוָה הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים אֵין עוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:35:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Deliver and bless Your people; tend them and sustain them forever (Psalms 28:9). And may these words of mine, which I have offered in supplication before the Lord, be close to the Lord our God day and night, that He may provide for His servant and for His people Israel, according to each day’s needs. In order that all the peoples of the earth may know that the Lord alone is God, there is no other (I Kings 8:59-60).','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:35:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','hoh-shee-ah eht ah-meh-khah oo-vah-rehkh eht nah-khah-lah-teh-khah oo-re-ehm ve-nah-se-ehm ahd hah-oh-lahm: ve-yeeh-yoo de-vah-rahy eh-leh ah-shehr heet-khah-nahn-tee leef-ney ah-doh-NAI ke-roh-veem ehl ah-doh-NAI eh-loh-hey-noo yoh-mahm vah-lah-ye-lah lah-ah-soht meesh-paht ahv-doh oo-meesh-paht ah-moh yees-rah-ehl de-vahr yohm be-yoh-moh: le-mah-ahn dah-aht kohl ah-mey hah-ah-rehts kee ah-doh-NAI hoo hah-eh-loh-heem eyn ohd:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:36:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','קדיש שלם, שיר של יום, לדוד, קריאת התורה, אשרי ובא לציון, מוסף, קוה ועלינו:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:36:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Full Kaddish, the Song of the Day, Le''David (Psalms 27), Reading of the Torah, Ashrei, Uva Letzion, the additional prayer, Kaveh and Aleinu.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
